       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Flood forecast bias account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型水庫調度先把預報入流與可控制出流分開。入流偏差會隨時間積分成庫容偏差，即使瞬時流量差看似不大，也可能持續耗用預留空間。模型必須以相同時間窗對齊雨量預報、支流到達與下游限制，不能把更新前後的預報當成兩股來水。 逐時正負誤差可能在期末抵消，但最大累積偏差仍決定需要保留的暫時空間，應同時報告兩種量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洪峰預報偏差帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Reservoir scheduling separates forecast inflow from controllable release. Inflow bias integrates over time into storage error, so a modest flow discrepancy can consume reserved space when it persists. Rainfall predictions, tributary arrival and downstream restrictions must share a time window; forecast revisions are alternative estimates, not additional streams of water. Positive and negative hourly errors may cancel at the endpoint, while the maximum cumulative error still determines temporary space requirements; report both quantities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flood forecast bias account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=1500 m3/s; dt=6 h; dS=dQ*dt*3600=32400000 m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「每次預報更新都應另加一筆來水」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every forecast revision should be counted as an additional inflow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
