       "objective": "說明「分段庫容積分」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Piecewise storage integration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水位與庫容通常不是固定面積的線性關係，山谷展寬會讓同一水位增量對應不同體積。用相鄰高程的水面面積做梯形積分，是資料稀疏時可檢查的近似；但支流庫灣及回水的空間差異仍須另外處理，不能把單站水位當成全庫水平面的證明。 若測深採用的水位基準與岸線高程不同，整張容量曲線會偏移，因此測量基準屬於模型輸入的一部分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分段庫容積分」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Water level and storage are rarely related by one constant surface area. A widening valley gives different volumes for equal level increments. Trapezoidal integration between surveyed areas provides a transparent approximation when data are sparse, but tributary bays and backwater remain spatial effects that a single gauge cannot resolve. A mismatch between bathymetric water-level datum and shoreline elevations shifts the capacity curve; reference control is therefore part of the model input. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Piecewise storage integration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A1=380 km2; A2=420 km2; dz=2 m; dV=(A1+A2)/2*1e6*dz=800000000 m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「分段庫容積分」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Piecewise storage integration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "three-gorges-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "分段庫容積分",
         "titleEn": "Piecewise storage integration",
         "text": "水位與庫容通常不是固定面積的線性關係，山谷展寬會讓同一水位增量對應不同體積。用相鄰高程的水面面積做梯形積分，是資料稀疏時可檢查的近似；但支流庫灣及回水的空間差異仍須另外處理，不能把單站水位當成全庫水平面的證明。",
         "textEn": "Water level and storage are rarely related by one constant surface area. A widening valley gives different volumes for equal level increments.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v5-place-c445157198d7",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "three-gorges-v15-05-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：相同水位增量必定增加相同庫容 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Equal level increments always add equal reservoir storage. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
