       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Sediment mass and deposition” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "懸浮泥砂先以乾質量守恆，沉積後再透過乾容重轉成體積，兩個步驟不可混用水的密度。流量、濃度與攔砂比例共同控制入庫及留庫質量；細粒壓密會隨時間改變體積，因此一次估算的體積不能直接當成永久損失曲線。 乾容重包含沉積孔隙的體積效應，壓密後即使乾質量不變，對應占據庫容仍可能減少，需明示測量齡期。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泥砂質量與淤積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Suspended sediment is first conserved as dry mass and then converted to deposited volume using dry bulk density, not water density. Discharge, concentration and trapping fraction jointly control incoming and retained mass. Fine material consolidates over time, so one volume estimate does not establish a permanent capacity-loss curve. Dry bulk density includes pore-volume effects, so consolidation can reduce occupied storage without changing dry mass; specify the age of the surveyed deposit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment mass and deposition” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
