       "instructionEn": "Sample concentration at several depths, check whether turbidity calibration spans changing grain sizes, and obtain dry bulk density from cores. Compare mass and bathymetric volume over the same period; otherwise consolidation after a flood may be mistaken for sediment leaving the reservoir. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：以兩種乾容重重算同一留庫質量，再令洪水濃度隨流量先升後降，繪出質量輸入曲線，說明單一平均濃度會遺失哪些時序資訊。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Recalculate one retained mass using two dry bulk densities, then make concentration rise and fall around the flood peak. Plot incoming mass and identify timing information lost by one average concentration.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：只用表層濃度容易漏掉近底高濃度流，低估留庫質量；若直接用顆粒實體密度換算，還會忽略孔隙而低估沉積體積，兩項誤差可能同向疊加。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
