       "objective": "說明「升船機平衡偏差」如何影響長江三峽大壩工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Ship lift balance imbalance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水槽式升船裝置的理想平衡取決於槽內總重量，而非只看船重。浮船進槽時通常排出相應水量，若槽內水位維持不變，載船前後總重近似不變。教材把殘餘不平衡質量與摩擦分開，藉此辨認驅動功率、制動及結構載重是不同問題。 船仍漂浮時排水質量與船重相等，若船體接觸槽底則浮力條件改變，不能再使用原先重量替代關係。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「升船機平衡偏差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A water-filled ship lift is balanced by total trough weight, not vessel weight alone. A floating vessel displaces approximately its own weight of water when the trough level is maintained. Separate residual imbalance from friction to distinguish driving power, braking requirements and structural load, which are different engineering questions. Displaced water mass equals vessel mass while the vessel floats; grounding changes that buoyancy condition and invalidates the original weight-substitution relationship for the trough. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ship lift balance imbalance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dm=18000 kg; g=9.81 m/s2; v=0.08 m/s; eta=0.80 (dimensionless); P=dm*g*v/eta=17658 W.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「升船機平衡偏差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ship lift balance imbalance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "three-gorges-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "升船機平衡偏差",
         "titleEn": "Ship lift balance imbalance",
         "text": "水槽式升船裝置的理想平衡取決於槽內總重量，而非只看船重。浮船進槽時通常排出相應水量，若槽內水位維持不變，載船前後總重近似不變。",
         "textEn": "A water-filled ship lift is balanced by total trough weight, not vessel weight alone. A floating vessel displaces approximately its own weight of water when the trough level is maintained.",
         "sourceIds": [
