       "objective": "從症狀倒推「升船機平衡偏差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Ship lift balance imbalance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "水位控制失準會改變槽內總重，造成原先平衡假設不成立；導輪卡阻也會提高電流，但不會以相同方式改變靜態重量，兩者需靠停機稱重與方向試驗區分。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Incorrect level control changes total trough weight and invalidates the balance assumption. A binding guide also raises current without the same static weight change, allowing weighing and direction tests to distinguish the two mechanisms. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：船仍漂浮時排水質量與船重相等，若船體接觸槽底則浮力條件改變，不能再使用原先重量替代關係。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Displaced water mass equals vessel mass while the vessel floats; grounding changes that buoyancy condition and invalidates the original weight-substitution relationship for the trough.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「大船入槽一定等量增加升降總重」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A heavier floating vessel always adds its full weight to the lifted total.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "three-gorges-v15-24-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
