       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Long reservoir backwater difference” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges Dam Engineering”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "有持續流量通過的長庫區並非處處靜水面，水面坡度同時受斷面、摩阻與下游控制影響。教材先以已量測平均坡度換算兩站高差，建立空間尺度感；真正回水分析仍需能量方程及各斷面資料，不能用一條坡線外推所有支流。 水面坡度與能量坡度並不總相等，流速水頭沿程改變時需要補入能量方程，尤其在斷面突變附近。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「長庫區回水高差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A long reservoir carrying flow does not have a level surface everywhere. Section geometry, friction and downstream control jointly influence the water-surface slope. A measured mean slope can estimate the difference between two stations, but actual backwater analysis requires energy equations and cross sections rather than one line extrapolated through every tributary. Water-surface slope and energy slope are not always equal; changing velocity head requires an energy correction, particularly near abrupt changes in cross-sectional geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long reservoir backwater difference” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
