       "objective": "從症狀倒推「拱座相容與分力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Abutment compatibility and load sharing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere. Calibrating only one crest displacement may reproduce overall stiffness while completely misrepresenting local stress concentrations and the distribution of support reactions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：平行彈簧共同位移來自相容條件，若兩岸支承本身移動，需把支承位移加入，分力比例就不再只由剛度決定。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Equal spring displacement follows compatibility; moving supports introduce imposed displacements, after which stiffness ratios alone no longer determine the force shares between the paths.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「只知道壩高就能決定拱向分力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Dam height alone determines the arch load share.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "拱座節理張開會使承載路徑變軟並把荷載移向其他部位；若只校準壩頂單點位移，可能得到看似正確的總剛度，卻完全錯判局部應力集中。",
         "textEn": "Opening abutment joints soften one load path and transfer force elsewhere. Calibrating only one crest displacement may reproduce overall stiffness while completely misrepresenting local stress concentrations and the distribution of support reactions.",
         "sourceIds": [
