       ],
       "objective": "說明「裂縫連通與揚壓」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Crack connectivity and uplift” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "基礎裂縫是否與上游水連通，會改變揚壓分布而不只是減少受壓面積。教材把已假設的壓力分布積分成向上合力，再討論裂縫開口與排水能力對分布的影響。裂縫長度不能獨立決定壓力，因流動阻力、下游水位與排水孔都參與控制。 排水點可能讓壓力圖出現折線，積分時應按各段面積相加，作用點也必須用各段力矩求得。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂縫連通與揚壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Whether a foundation crack connects to upstream water changes uplift distribution as well as contact area. Integrating an explicitly assumed pressure diagram gives the upward resultant; crack aperture and drainage then explain possible changes to that diagram. Crack length alone cannot determine pressure because flow resistance, tailwater and drains also control it. A drain may introduce a breakpoint in the pressure diagram; sum segment areas for force and segment moments for the resultant location on the base. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Crack connectivity and uplift” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pu=900 kPa; pd=100 kPa; B=60 m; w=1 m; U=(pu+pd)/2*B*w=30000 kN.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要量得裂縫長度就知道全部揚壓」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Crack length alone determines the complete uplift pressure distribution.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「裂縫連通與揚壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Crack connectivity and uplift”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "裂縫連通與揚壓",
         "titleEn": "Crack connectivity and uplift",
         "text": "基礎裂縫是否與上游水連通，會改變揚壓分布而不只是減少受壓面積。教材把已假設的壓力分布積分成向上合力，再討論裂縫開口與排水能力對分布的影響。",
         "textEn": "Whether a foundation crack connects to upstream water changes uplift distribution as well as contact area. Integrating an explicitly assumed pressure diagram gives the upward resultant; crack aperture and drainage then explain possible changes to that diagram.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v6-hoover-dam",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
