       "instructionEn": "Convert piezometer readings to pressure heads on one datum and compare their response and lag at different reservoir levels. Pair pressure with drainage flow: rising pressure with falling flow supports blockage, while simultaneous increases require investigation of a newly connected seepage path. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
