       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Concrete cooling heat account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大體積混凝土降溫同時涉及熱量移除與空間溫差，兩者不可互相代替。比熱模型能估算均勻降溫所需移除的顯熱，但表面冷得過快可能提高內外約束應力。需把水化熱產生、冷卻水帶走熱量與周邊散熱分列，才能判斷熱量帳是否閉合。 熱擴散時間隨特徵長度平方變化，縮小試件的冷卻曲線不能直接按時間等比例搬到大體積壩塊。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土冷卻熱量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Cooling mass concrete involves both heat removal and spatial gradients, which are not interchangeable. Heat capacity estimates sensible energy for uniform cooling, while rapid surface cooling can increase restraint stresses. Separate hydration heat, heat carried by cooling water and environmental exchange to establish whether the thermal account actually closes. Thermal diffusion time scales with characteristic length squared, so cooling observations from small specimens cannot be transferred to massive blocks by simple linear time scaling. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concrete cooling heat account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=5000 m3; rho=2400 kg/m3; c=900 J/(kg*K); dT=8 K; E=V*rho*c*dT/1e9=86.4 GJ.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「平均降溫達標就表示沒有梯度風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Meeting an average cooling target proves there is no gradient risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「混凝土冷卻熱量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Concrete cooling heat account”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
