    {
     "id": "b202-v15-s3",
     "title": "施工方法與施工階段控制",
     "titleEn": "Construction methods and stage control",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「壓力鋼管水錘」與「溢洪面汽蝕指標」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Penstock water hammer\" and \"Spillway cavitation indicator\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b202-v15-17",
       "title": "壓力鋼管水錘：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Penstock water hammer: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v6-hoover-dam",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments",
        "v15s-usace-catalog"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b202-v15-16"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「壓力鋼管水錘」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Penstock water hammer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "導葉或閥門快速變動使水流動量轉為壓力波，波速同時受水的可壓縮性與管壁彈性影響。焦科夫斯基關係適合估計快速速度改變的首波幅度；反射、分岔與調壓設施會改變後續波形，因此單一首波不能取代整段管路的暫態包絡。 反射的符號取決於邊界阻抗，水庫端與封閉閥端可能產生不同反射，因此應在時空圖標明每個邊界。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力鋼管水錘」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rapid guide-vane or valve movement converts flow momentum into a pressure wave whose speed depends on water compressibility and pipe elasticity. The Joukowsky relation estimates the first wave from a rapid velocity change. Reflections, branches and surge facilities alter later waves, so one first-wave estimate is not a full transient envelope. Reflection sign depends on boundary impedance; reservoir and closed-valve ends can reflect differently, so every boundary must be identified on the space-time diagram. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Penstock water hammer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=0.7 m/s; dp=rho*a*dv/1e6=0.63 MPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「壓力鋼管水錘」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Penstock water hammer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-17-k1",
         "title": "壓力鋼管水錘",
         "titleEn": "Penstock water hammer",
         "text": "導葉或閥門快速變動使水流動量轉為壓力波，波速同時受水的可壓縮性與管壁彈性影響。焦科夫斯基關係適合估計快速速度改變的首波幅度；反射、分岔與調壓設施會改變後續波形，因此單一首波不能取代整段管路的暫態包絡。",
         "textEn": "Rapid guide-vane or valve movement converts flow momentum into a pressure wave whose speed depends on water compressibility and pipe elasticity. The Joukowsky relation estimates the first wave from a rapid velocity change.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v6-hoover-dam",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-17-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
