       "objective": "從症狀倒推「壓力鋼管水錘」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Penstock water hammer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave. Column separation on the low-pressure side can generate a larger impact when the separated liquid columns rejoin. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：反射的符號取決於邊界阻抗，水庫端與封閉閥端可能產生不同反射，因此應在時空圖標明每個邊界。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Reflection sign depends on boundary impedance; reservoir and closed-valve ends can reflect differently, so every boundary must be identified on the space-time diagram.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「首波壓升必定是所有暫態最大壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The first pressure rise is always the maximum of the whole transient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-20-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "延遲關閉或不協調的保護動作可能形成多次反射峰值，最大壓力不一定在首波；低壓端的液柱分離也可能在重新接合時產生更大衝擊。",
         "textEn": "Delayed or uncoordinated protective actions can produce repeated reflected peaks, with the maximum occurring after the first wave. Column separation on the low-pressure side can generate a larger impact when the separated liquid columns rejoin.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v6-hoover-dam",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-20-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
