      },
      {
       "id": "b202-v15-21",
       "title": "溢洪面汽蝕指標：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Spillway cavitation indicator: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v6-hoover-dam",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments",
        "v15s-usace-catalog"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b202-v15-20"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「溢洪面汽蝕指標」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Spillway cavitation indicator” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "高速溢洪流在不平整表面附近會產生局部低壓，是否形成汽穴要比較局部絕對壓力與水的蒸氣壓。汽蝕數把可用壓力差除以動壓，便於比較流況，但臨界值仍依表面幾何、含氣與尺度而異。以平均壓力計算只能作初步篩查。 蒸氣壓取決於水溫，而局部絕對壓也受大氣壓影響，兩者均應使用與事件同時的條件比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溢洪面汽蝕指標」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "High-speed spillway flow can create local low pressure near surface irregularities. Vapor formation depends on absolute pressure relative to vapor pressure. A cavitation number normalizes available pressure by dynamic pressure, but its critical value depends on geometry, aeration and scale. A value based on mean pressure is therefore a preliminary indicator only. Vapor pressure depends on water temperature and absolute local pressure depends on atmospheric conditions; both should represent the same event rather than unrelated reference conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Spillway cavitation indicator” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pabs=85000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=25 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5*rho*v*v)=0.264.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「所有表面可採同一汽蝕數界線」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"One cavitation-number threshold applies to every spillway surface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「溢洪面汽蝕指標」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Spillway cavitation indicator”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "溢洪面汽蝕指標",
         "titleEn": "Spillway cavitation indicator",
         "text": "高速溢洪流在不平整表面附近會產生局部低壓，是否形成汽穴要比較局部絕對壓力與水的蒸氣壓。汽蝕數把可用壓力差除以動壓，便於比較流況，但臨界值仍依表面幾何、含氣與尺度而異。",
         "textEn": "High-speed spillway flow can create local low pressure near surface irregularities. Vapor formation depends on absolute pressure relative to vapor pressure.",
