       "objective": "從症狀倒推「低水頭機組出力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low head generating output” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "為補償低水頭而增加流量，可能提高損失與不穩定流動，使預期增益落空；若流量計受流態改變影響，也會出現虛假的效率提升，需用獨立量測核對。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Increasing flow to compensate for low head may raise losses and unstable-flow effects enough to defeat the expected gain. A meter affected by altered flow patterns can also indicate a false efficiency improvement, requiring independent verification. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：導葉開度與流量的關係隨水頭改變，固定開度不等於固定流量，比較模型時必須明確哪一項受到控制。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: The relation between guide-vane opening and discharge changes with head; fixed opening is not fixed flow, so the controlled quantity must be stated explicitly.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「低水頭可藉無限增加流量完全補償」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Any low head can be fully compensated by unlimited discharge.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
