       "objective": "說明「沉積三角洲前移」如何影響胡佛壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Sediment delta advance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "入庫流速降低使較粗顆粒優先沉降，三角洲前緣位置影響取水與通道幾何。簡化的體積除以橫截面積只能估算平均前移距離，不能描述底坡、粒徑分選及潛流。應把泥砂供給與可容納空間分開，避免把局部淤高等同全庫均勻填滿。 沉積前緣可能沿舊河槽形成狹長分支，使用全庫平均寬度會稀釋這種集中前移，需要保留局部地形。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沉積三角洲前移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Deceleration at reservoir entry deposits coarse material preferentially, and delta position affects intake and channel geometry. Deposited volume divided by a representative cross-sectional area estimates mean advance only; it omits bed slope, sorting and density currents. Sediment supply and accommodation space must be distinguished from uniform filling of the reservoir. A depositional front may advance as a narrow lobe along the old channel; reservoir-average width conceals that concentration and should not replace local geometry. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment delta advance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: V=240000 m3; B=600 m; h=8 m; dx=V/(B*h)=50 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「沉積三角洲前移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment delta advance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
