       "objective": "從症狀倒推「沉積三角洲前移」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment delta advance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake. Conversely, level-driven shoreline movement may be mistaken for deposition; submerged topography referenced to a fixed elevation is needed to distinguish them. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：沉積前緣可能沿舊河槽形成狹長分支，使用全庫平均寬度會稀釋這種集中前移，需要保留局部地形。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: A depositional front may advance as a narrow lobe along the old channel; reservoir-average width conceals that concentration and should not replace local geometry.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「岸線移動距離就是沉積前緣移動距離」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Shoreline movement equals the movement of the sediment front.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-32-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "只追蹤表面岸線可能漏掉水下前緣逼近取水區；反之，水位變化造成的岸線位移也可能被誤作淤積，應以固定高程下的水下地形辨識。",
         "textEn": "Tracking only the visible shoreline can miss an underwater front approaching an intake. Conversely, level-driven shoreline movement may be mistaken for deposition; submerged topography referenced to a fixed elevation is needed to distinguish them.",
         "sourceIds": [
