       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "垂線觀測相對位置時，量測支架與讀數裝置也會受到溫度影響。把已校準的儀器溫度係數乘溫差，可估算需扣除的儀器漂移，但不能順便移除壩體真正熱變形。兩種效應必須以獨立基準、內部溫度與不同原理位移儀共同辨識。 溫漂係數具有量測軸向與安裝條件，儀器移位或更換支架後須重新檢查，不能沿用舊校準而未記錄。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「垂線監測溫漂」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Pendulum observations include temperature effects in mounting and readout hardware as well as movement of the structure. A calibrated instrument coefficient estimates instrumental drift, but must not remove genuine thermal deformation of the dam. Independent reference control, internal temperature and another displacement principle are needed to separate the effects. A drift coefficient belongs to a measurement axis and mounting arrangement; relocation or replacement of the support requires renewed checks and documented calibration continuity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pendulum monitoring thermal drift” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
