       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Drainage redundancy common causes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Hoover Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "備援只有在失效機制足夠獨立時才能降低同時失效機率。兩部泵可能共用電源、進水池或控制器，因此把單機失效機率直接相乘會過度樂觀。教材先建立明示獨立的基準，再加入共同原因事件，強調可靠度數值取決於系統邊界與資料期間。 故障機率須附需求期間與成功功能定義，短時啟動成功與長時持續抽水成功是兩個不同的事件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水備援共同原因」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Redundancy reduces simultaneous failure only when failure mechanisms are sufficiently independent. Two pumps may share power, a sump or controls, making a simple product of individual probabilities optimistic. Establish an explicitly independent baseline before adding a common-cause event, and define the system boundary and observation period for every probability. A probability needs a demand interval and a defined success function; successful starting and sustained pumping throughout a long event are different reliability questions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drainage redundancy common causes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: pA=0.03 (dimensionless); pB=0.04 (dimensionless); pBoth=pA*pB=0.0012.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「排水備援共同原因」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drainage redundancy common causes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
