       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水備援共同原因」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Drainage redundancy common causes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "用設備接線圖與管線圖找出共同電源、閥件與吸入口，逐項核對測試是否真正涵蓋切換。把無需求時停機與有需求時失效分開統計；若兩泵常在同一事件失效，就不能保留獨立假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Trace shared power, valves and suction paths on electrical and hydraulic diagrams, then check whether tests actually exercise transfer. Distinguish planned idle states from failures on demand. Repeated simultaneous failures during one event invalidate the independence assumption used by the simple probability product. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：加入一個共同電源失效事件，畫故障樹並計算條件機率，指出何種改造可切斷共同原因，以及需要哪些需求紀錄才能更新估計。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Add a common power-failure event, draw a fault tree and calculate conditional probabilities. Identify a modification that removes the shared cause and the demand records needed to update the estimate.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
