       "objective": "從症狀倒推「排水備援共同原因」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Drainage redundancy common causes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. Testing unloaded motor starts does not reveal a blocked common intake, so the actual drainage path and electrical separation must be verified together. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：故障機率須附需求期間與成功功能定義，短時啟動成功與長時持續抽水成功是兩個不同的事件。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: A probability needs a demand interval and a defined success function; successful starting and sustained pumping throughout a long event are different reliability questions.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「每增加一台備用設備就多一個獨立備援」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every additional spare device provides another fully independent backup.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-40-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "淹水可能同時淹沒兩部泵的控制設備，使機械備援失去作用；只測馬達空載啟動不會揭露共同吸入口堵塞，需驗證實際抽排路徑與電力隔離。",
         "textEn": "Flooding can disable controls for both pumps and defeat mechanical redundancy. Testing unloaded motor starts does not reveal a blocked common intake, so the actual drainage path and electrical separation must be verified together.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v6-hoover-dam",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b202-v15-40-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v6-hoover-dam",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「排水備援共同原因」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Drainage redundancy common causes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
