       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Irrigation pumping energy account” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grand Coulee Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "發電廠與抽水站共用水資源時，抽水所需能量不能從發電流量直接相減。抽水揚程包含上下游能量高程差與管路損失，電端輸入還需除以泵及馬達效率。先把取水量、提高的位能與耗電分列，才能比較不同灌溉時程的水能代價。 若以每立方米耗電比較方案，應將功率除流量並正確換算能量單位，才能消除單純抽水規模不同的影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「灌溉抽水能量帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "When generation and irrigation pumping share a water resource, pumping energy cannot be subtracted directly from generating discharge. Pump head includes the difference in energy elevations and conveyance losses, while electrical input divides hydraulic power by pump and motor efficiency. Separate water volume, gained potential energy and electricity before comparing irrigation schedules. Comparing energy per cubic metre requires dividing power by flow with consistent energy units, separating scale of pumping from the underlying hydraulic and efficiency effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Irrigation pumping energy account” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
