       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b203-v15-03"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「灌溉抽水能量帳」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Irrigation pumping energy account” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "進水柵堵塞會提高損失且可能降低吸入壓力，單靠增加馬達功率不一定恢復流量；電表和流量計時間窗不同也會偽造效率變化，需先檢查資料對齊。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "An obstructed intake raises losses and may reduce suction pressure, so increasing motor input need not restore discharge. Different meter integration windows can also create a false efficiency change and must be checked before diagnosing the pump. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若以每立方米耗電比較方案，應將功率除流量並正確換算能量單位，才能消除單純抽水規模不同的影響。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Comparing energy per cubic metre requires dividing power by flow with consistent energy units, separating scale of pumping from the underlying hydraulic and efficiency effects.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「抽水電端功率等於水力功率乘效率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pump electrical input equals hydraulic power multiplied by efficiency.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b203-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "進水柵堵塞會提高損失且可能降低吸入壓力，單靠增加馬達功率不一定恢復流量；電表和流量計時間窗不同也會偽造效率變化，需先檢查資料對齊。",
         "textEn": "An obstructed intake raises losses and may reduce suction pressure, so increasing motor input need not restore discharge. Different meter integration windows can also create a false efficiency change and must be checked before diagnosing the pump.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-coulee-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b203-v15-04-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
