       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Forebay level buffering” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qin=80 m3/s; Qout=95 m3/s; dt=600 s; A=300000 m2; dz=(Qin-Qout)*dt/A=-0.03 m。模型邊界：面積固定且忽略波浪與側向取水；負號表示水位下降。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qin=80 m3/s; Qout=95 m3/s; dt=600 s; A=300000 m2; dz=(Qin-Qout)*dt/A=-0.03 m. Model boundary: constant surface area, no waves or lateral withdrawals; negative sign denotes falling level. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：以同時段入出流積分預測水位，再比較多站平均水位與單點波動。",
