       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Irrigation return flow accounting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grand Coulee Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "從水庫取出的水不全等於流域消耗，部分可能在不同時間和位置回到河道。課程把取水、作物蒸散、渠道蒸發、地下儲存與回歸流分開，先建立明確邊界的日帳。回歸水水質與到達時間也可能限制再利用，不能只靠體積差評價灌溉效益。 回歸水若跨越原先劃定邊界，需改列外部輸出而非區內儲存，控制體選擇會改變各項名稱但不改守恆。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「灌溉回歸流水帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Water withdrawn from a reservoir is not identical to basin consumption because some returns at another time and location. Separate withdrawal, crop evapotranspiration, canal evaporation, subsurface storage and return flow within a declared daily boundary. Return-water quality and arrival time can constrain reuse even when the volume account closes. Return water crossing the chosen boundary is an external output rather than internal storage; control-volume choice changes labels while preserving the conservation requirement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Irrigation return flow accounting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：W=1200000 m3/day; ET=650000 m3/day; E=50000 m3/day; dS=100000 m3/day; R=W-ET-E-dS=400000 m3/day。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: W=1200000 m3/day; ET=650000 m3/day; E=50000 m3/day; dS=100000 m3/day; R=W-ET-E-dS=400000 m3/day.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「水庫取水量就是流域總消耗量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Reservoir withdrawal volume equals total basin consumptive use.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
