       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「混凝土分塊溫差」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Concrete block temperature mismatch” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "以埋入式溫度量測還原各塊核心歷程，配對接縫計及澆置日期，避免用外氣溫代表內部。若應變差預測與接縫方向相反，先核對正負號、感測軸向及塊體約束，再研究材料異常。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Reconstruct core temperature histories from embedded sensors and pair them with joint gauges and placement dates. If predicted strain difference has the opposite sign to joint movement, check sign conventions, sensor orientation and block restraint before investigating an unusual material response. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：改變兩塊溫度歷程使最終溫度相同但降溫速率不同，畫出自由應變差隨時間的變化，指出徐變試驗及約束模型需要補充的資料。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Give two blocks the same final temperature but different cooling rates. Plot their free-strain difference over time and identify the creep-test and restraint-model information needed to assess the consequences.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：只按相同日曆時間比較不同齡期混凝土，會忽略剛度及徐變發展；量測點離冷卻管太近也可能把局部溫度當成整塊平均，導致錯估相容差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Comparing blocks only by calendar time ignores age-dependent stiffness and creep. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
