       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Foundation drainage resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grand Coulee Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排水孔降低基礎孔隙水壓的能力取決於連通路徑及排水阻力，流量大並不必然表示排水效果較好。簡化的導水率乘水頭差模型可描述一段線性滲流路徑，但岩體裂隙網絡可能隨壓力改變。壓力與流量必須成對觀察，才可區分堵塞及新增滲流。 導水率的單位是面積每時間，與材料滲透係數的長度每時間不同，兩者還差流路幾何因子。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基礎排水阻力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Drain effectiveness depends on hydraulic connectivity and resistance, so a larger discharge does not automatically mean better pressure relief. Conductance times head difference describes one linear seepage path, while a fractured-rock network may change with pressure. Pressure and flow must be observed together to distinguish blockage from newly connected seepage. Hydraulic conductance has area-per-time units, unlike conductivity in length per time; a flow-path geometry factor is required before one can be converted into the other. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Foundation drainage resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：C=0.00025 m2/s; dh=32 m; Q=C*dh=0.008 m3/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: C=0.00025 m2/s; dh=32 m; Q=C*dh=0.008 m3/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「排水量下降必定證明滲漏改善」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A decrease in drain flow always proves improved seepage control.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
