       ],
       "objective": "說明「停機容量與水量」如何影響大古力水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Outage capacity and water allocation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grand Coulee Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型機組檢修會降低可用發電通道，但不一定同比例降低河道總出流，因其他機組及放流設施可能分擔水量。教材先用可用機組數乘假定單機出力估算容量，再把水頭、流量與共同輸電限制另列。設備容量是上限條件之一，不能單獨預測實際電量。 未被發電利用的水可能仍履行必要河道放流，因此旁通量應記入水量帳，而非自動視為可避免的浪費。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「停機容量與水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A major-unit outage reduces available generating paths without necessarily reducing total river release proportionally, because other units and outlets may carry water. Count available units at an assumed unit output first, then consider head, discharge and shared transmission constraints. Equipment capacity is only one limit and cannot independently predict energy production. Water bypassing turbines may still satisfy required river release; account for its volume without automatically treating all bypass as an avoidable operational waste. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Outage capacity and water allocation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N=8 units; nout=2 units; Pu=120 MW/unit; Pav=(N-nout)*Pu=720 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: N=8 units; nout=2 units; Pu=120 MW/unit; Pav=(N-nout)*Pu=720 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「可用機組台數足以保證同時滿載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Available unit count alone guarantees simultaneous full-load operation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「停機容量與水量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Outage capacity and water allocation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b203-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "停機容量與水量",
         "titleEn": "Outage capacity and water allocation",
         "text": "大型機組檢修會降低可用發電通道，但不一定同比例降低河道總出流，因其他機組及放流設施可能分擔水量。教材先用可用機組數乘假定單機出力估算容量，再把水頭、流量與共同輸電限制另列。",
         "textEn": "A major-unit outage reduces available generating paths without necessarily reducing total river release proportionally, because other units and outlets may carry water. Count available units at an assumed unit output first, then consider head, discharge and shared transmission constraints.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-coulee-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments",
          "v15s-usace-catalog"
         ]
