       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Level reference closure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grand Coulee Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "壩體沉陷、庫水位與設備高程若使用不同基準，量測之間會出現看似物理的差異。水準閉合差用來檢查測線一致性，卻不能證明所有基準點都穩定；整組點共同移動時，內部閉合仍可能良好，因此必須連到獨立且可追溯的控制點。 觀測線長度與視距不平衡會影響誤差來源，配賦方式應依量測品質而非僅按測段數平均處理。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水準基準閉合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Dam settlement, reservoir level and equipment elevation can appear inconsistent when different reference datums are used. Level-loop closure tests internal consistency but cannot establish that every benchmark is stable. A group of points moving together can still close well, so an independent traceable control point is needed to interpret movement. Line length and unequal sight distances affect survey errors; adjustment weights should reflect observation quality rather than distributing every closure equally by number of legs. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level reference closure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dh1=1.245 m; dh2=-0.630 m; dh3=-0.612 m; e=(dh1+dh2+dh3)*1000=3 mm。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dh1=1.245 m; dh2=-0.630 m; dh3=-0.612 m; e=(dh1+dh2+dh3)*1000=3 mm.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「水準閉合良好就證明所有基準穩定」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Good level-loop closure proves every benchmark is stable.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水準基準閉合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
