      {
       "id": "b203-v15-39",
       "title": "更新效率比較：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Post renewal efficiency comparison: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-coulee-owner",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments",
        "v15s-usace-catalog"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b203-v15-38"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「更新效率比較」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Post renewal efficiency comparison” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "在更新前後選取可比工況，校驗流量與功率儀表並重複測試，將不確定度與效率差並列。若差值小於量測解析能力，應報告未能辨識改善，而非把四捨五入後的正值當成確定收益。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Select comparable conditions before and after renewal, calibrate discharge and power instruments, and repeat measurements. Report uncertainty beside the efficiency difference. If the difference is below measurement resolution, state that improvement was not resolved rather than presenting a rounded positive value as a demonstrated gain. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：以三組水頭流量建立更新前後比較表，先計算同工況功率差，再加入流量偏差，討論何種精度才能辨識假定的效率增益。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Build before-and-after comparisons at three head-flow combinations. Calculate matched-condition power differences, then introduce flow bias and determine what measurement precision is needed to resolve the assumed efficiency gain.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：更新後恰逢較高水頭會讓功率增加，即使效率不變；流量儀表重新校正也可能改變計算效率，需保留原始校準與一致的比較邊界，避免把量測變動列為設備成效。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Higher head after renewal can increase power without any efficiency gain. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
