       "objective": "從症狀倒推「更新效率比較」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Post renewal efficiency comparison” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "更新後恰逢較高水頭會讓功率增加，即使效率不變；流量儀表重新校正也可能改變計算效率，需保留原始校準與一致的比較邊界，避免把量測變動列為設備成效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Higher head after renewal can increase power without any efficiency gain. Recalibrating a flow meter can also change calculated efficiency, so original calibration records and a consistent comparison boundary are needed to avoid crediting measurement changes to the equipment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：全年收益需以各工況停留時間加權，單一最佳效率點的改善不能代表全年不同水頭流量下的平均成效。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Annual benefit requires weighting operating points by their duration; improvement at one best-efficiency point does not represent average performance across a year of varying conditions.",
