       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「頻率極數與轉速」如何影響伊泰普水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Frequency poles and speed” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "同步發電機的電氣頻率由機械轉速與磁極數共同決定，並非只靠水輪機轉得更快。比較兩種頻率時應先寫清楚總極數而非極對數，再檢查轉輪水力設計所允許的轉速。電網頻率不同不表示兩台機組的轉輪幾何可以不經分析直接互換。 磁極數選擇也影響發電機幾何與轉輪匹配，因此頻率介面應由機械與電氣團隊共同確認，不能只改控制設定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「頻率極數與轉速」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Synchronous electrical frequency depends on mechanical speed and magnetic pole count, rather than simply making a turbine rotate faster. State total poles rather than pole pairs when comparing frequencies, then check the speed allowed by the hydraulic design. Different grid frequencies do not make runner geometries interchangeable without analysis. Pole selection also affects generator geometry and runner matching, so mechanical and electrical teams must jointly verify a frequency interface rather than merely changing control settings. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Frequency poles and speed” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：f=50 Hz; poles=60; n=120*f/poles=100 rpm。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: f=50 Hz; poles=60; n=120*f/poles=100 rpm.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要電壓相同就能忽略頻率直接並聯」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal voltage permits direct paralleling regardless of frequency.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「頻率極數與轉速」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Frequency poles and speed”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b204-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "頻率極數與轉速",
         "titleEn": "Frequency poles and speed",
