       "objective": "從症狀倒推「頻率極數與轉速」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Frequency poles and speed” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "總極數與極對數混用會產生兩倍轉速誤差，影響後續轉矩及離心力估算；同步關係只適用已同步狀態，啟動或解列後的暫態不能照此強制代入。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Mixing poles with pole pairs creates a factor-of-two speed error that propagates into torque and centrifugal calculations. The synchronous relation applies after synchronization; startup and disconnected transients cannot be forced to follow it. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：磁極數選擇也影響發電機幾何與轉輪匹配，因此頻率介面應由機械與電氣團隊共同確認，不能只改控制設定。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Pole selection also affects generator geometry and runner matching, so mechanical and electrical teams must jointly verify a frequency interface rather than merely changing control settings.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「只要電壓相同就能忽略頻率直接並聯」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal voltage permits direct paralleling regardless of frequency.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b204-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "總極數與極對數混用會產生兩倍轉速誤差，影響後續轉矩及離心力估算；同步關係只適用已同步狀態，啟動或解列後的暫態不能照此強制代入。",
         "textEn": "Mixing poles with pole pairs creates a factor-of-two speed error that propagates into torque and centrifugal calculations. The synchronous relation applies after synchronization; startup and disconnected transients cannot be forced to follow it.",
         "sourceIds": [
