      {
       "id": "b204-v15-05",
       "title": "異頻換流能量：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Asynchronous conversion energy: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-itaipu-owner",
        "v6-science-itaipu-history",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b204-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「異頻換流能量」如何影響伊泰普水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Asynchronous conversion energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "不同頻率的交流系統可藉電力電子換流傳輸能量，但換流站會產生損失並受控制及設備限制。教材以輸入電量乘總效率求接收電量，只描述能量帳，不把它當成電壓穩定或故障穿越分析。每個效率都要附邊界，避免把線路損失同時算入兩次。 換流損失可包含固定輔助耗電及隨負載改變的部分，低負載效率因此未必與額定點相同，需保留負載曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「異頻換流能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Power-electronic conversion can transfer energy between AC systems of different frequencies, with losses and equipment constraints. Multiplying input energy by overall efficiency describes the energy account only, not voltage stability or fault behavior. Each efficiency needs a boundary so that line losses are not included twice in the same transfer estimate. Conversion losses can include fixed auxiliaries and load-dependent components, making low-load efficiency differ from the rated point; retain the load curve in comparisons. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Asynchronous conversion energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Pin=900 MW; t=4 h; eta=0.965 (dimensionless); Eout=Pin*t*eta=3474 MWh。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Pin=900 MW; t=4 h; eta=0.965 (dimensionless); Eout=Pin*t*eta=3474 MWh.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「不同頻率換流後必定沒有能量損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Conversion between different frequencies necessarily has no energy loss.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「異頻換流能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Asynchronous conversion energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b204-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "異頻換流能量",
         "titleEn": "Asynchronous conversion energy",
         "text": "不同頻率的交流系統可藉電力電子換流傳輸能量，但換流站會產生損失並受控制及設備限制。教材以輸入電量乘總效率求接收電量，只描述能量帳，不把它當成電壓穩定或故障穿越分析。",
         "textEn": "Power-electronic conversion can transfer energy between AC systems of different frequencies, with losses and equipment constraints. Multiplying input energy by overall efficiency describes the energy account only, not voltage stability or fault behavior.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-itaipu-owner",
          "v6-science-itaipu-history",
