       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Reactive power and apparent capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "發電機與變壓器的電流負擔同時受實功與無功影響，因此兆伏安額定值不能直接改寫成兆瓦。功率三角形可在平衡正弦穩態下關聯三者，但熱限制與勵磁限制形成的實際能力曲線更複雜。教材先分清量綱，再討論何者是真正限制。 視在功率描述電壓電流乘積，實功才對應平均能量轉移，無功方向則需明示供應或吸收的符號慣例。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「無功與視在容量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Generator and transformer current loading depends on both active and reactive power, so an MVA rating cannot simply be relabeled as MW. The power triangle connects the quantities for balanced sinusoidal steady operation, while thermal and excitation limits make the actual capability curve more complex. Identify quantities before deciding which limit controls. Apparent power describes the voltage-current product, active power represents mean energy transfer, and reactive direction needs an explicit convention for supply versus absorption. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Reactive power and apparent capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
