       "objective": "從症狀倒推「無功與視在容量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Reactive power and apparent capacity” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "將視在額定值全部當實功，會忽略供應無功時的電流負擔；即使實功低於名目值，過勵磁或冷卻不足仍可能形成限制，需要核對能力曲線與溫度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating the apparent rating entirely as active power ignores current loading while supplying reactive power. Overexcitation or inadequate cooling can constrain operation even below nominal active output, requiring checks of the capability curve and temperatures. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：視在功率描述電壓電流乘積，實功才對應平均能量轉移，無功方向則需明示供應或吸收的符號慣例。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Apparent power describes the voltage-current product, active power represents mean energy transfer, and reactive direction needs an explicit convention for supply versus absorption.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「兆伏安額定值可直接當成同數字兆瓦」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An MVA rating can directly be treated as the same numerical MW rating.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
