       "objective": "說明「尾水抬升耦合」如何影響伊泰普水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Tailwater rise coupling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "多台機組向共同尾水河段排放時，增加總流量可能抬高尾水並降低每台機組淨水頭。單機功率因此不一定能線性相加到任意總流量。教材以量測的局部尾水敏感度估算水頭損失，提醒學員同一河段的各機組不是完全獨立的水力設備。 共同尾水河段形成水力耦合，即使電氣母線分開仍會互相影響；模型拓撲應同時保留水路與電路的差異。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「尾水抬升耦合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Units releasing into a common tailwater reach can raise its level as total discharge increases, reducing net head for each machine. Individual outputs therefore cannot be added linearly at arbitrary aggregate flow. A measured local tailwater sensitivity estimates the head effect and illustrates why machines sharing a reach are not hydraulically independent. A shared tailwater creates hydraulic coupling even with separate electrical buses; model topology should preserve the different connections of the water and electrical systems. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tailwater rise coupling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dQ=500 m3/s; k=0.0012 s/m2; dH=k*dQ=0.6 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dQ=500 m3/s; k=0.0012 s/m2; dH=k*dQ=0.6 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「每台機組出力永遠與其他機組無關」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Each unit output is always independent of the other units.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「尾水抬升耦合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tailwater rise coupling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
