       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「尾水抬升耦合」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tailwater rise coupling” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "以同步總出流與尾水位建立上升及下降兩條散點路徑，並檢查下游來水是否另有影響。若同流量出現不同尾水，應保留遲滯或邊界條件，不以一條平均直線宣稱機組效率異常。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Plot rising and falling total-flow paths against synchronized tailwater level and check downstream influences. Different levels at the same discharge require retaining hysteresis or boundary conditions rather than forcing one mean line and interpreting the residual as a turbine-efficiency fault. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：以兩種尾水敏感度比較增加機組後的總功率，指出為何加機組的邊際收益可能下降，再列出需要河道模型處理的情境。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Compare aggregate power after adding units under two tailwater sensitivities. Explain diminishing marginal benefit and identify conditions where a river model is required instead of a local linear relation.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：洪水期間下游控制抬升可能主導尾水，原先低流量線性係數就不再有效；若仍沿用該係數，會高估可用水頭並誤排機組負載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: During flooding, downstream control can dominate tailwater and invalidate a coefficient fitted at low discharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
