       "objective": "從症狀倒推「尾水抬升耦合」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tailwater rise coupling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "洪水期間下游控制抬升可能主導尾水，原先低流量線性係數就不再有效；若仍沿用該係數，會高估可用水頭並誤排機組負載。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "During flooding, downstream control can dominate tailwater and invalidate a coefficient fitted at low discharge. Continuing to use that coefficient overstates available head and can lead to an inappropriate allocation of generating load among units. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：共同尾水河段形成水力耦合，即使電氣母線分開仍會互相影響；模型拓撲應同時保留水路與電路的差異。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: A shared tailwater creates hydraulic coupling even with separate electrical buses; model topology should preserve the different connections of the water and electrical systems.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「每台機組出力永遠與其他機組無關」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Each unit output is always independent of the other units.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
