       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Spillway jet momentum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "洩洪水舌轉向時，其動量改變需要由導流構造與水體承受反力。教材只取一個水平分量，以質量流率乘速度差建立尺度；實際衝擊力還受壓力、重力及含氣影響。把動量通量與水舌動能分開，才能避免用能量單位直接當載重。 控制體出口角度決定速度分量，速度大小相同而方向改變仍有動量差，應先做向量解析再計算反力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溢洪水舌動量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Turning a spillway jet requires a reaction associated with momentum change. One horizontal component is estimated from mass flow times velocity difference, while real impact also involves pressure, gravity and entrained air. Distinguish momentum flux from kinetic energy so that energy units are not incorrectly treated as structural force. Outlet direction determines velocity components; unchanged speed with a changed direction still produces momentum change, requiring vector resolution before calculating the associated reaction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Spillway jet momentum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
