       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Spillway jet momentum” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "水舌偏流會把反力集中在局部邊牆，總水平力不變也可能增加局部損傷；含氣及脈動又會改變瞬時峰值，因此平均動量不能代替動態載重評估。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "A skewed jet concentrates reaction on a sidewall even when total horizontal force is unchanged. Aeration and pulsation also modify instantaneous peaks, so mean momentum does not replace assessment of spatially concentrated dynamic loading. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：控制體出口角度決定速度分量，速度大小相同而方向改變仍有動量差，應先做向量解析再計算反力。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Outlet direction determines velocity components; unchanged speed with a changed direction still produces momentum change, requiring vector resolution before calculating the associated reaction.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「水舌動能數值可以直接當結構反力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The numerical jet kinetic energy can directly be used as structural reaction force.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b204-v15-20-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "水舌偏流會把反力集中在局部邊牆，總水平力不變也可能增加局部損傷；含氣及脈動又會改變瞬時峰值，因此平均動量不能代替動態載重評估。",
         "textEn": "A skewed jet concentrates reaction on a sidewall even when total horizontal force is unchanged. Aeration and pulsation also modify instantaneous peaks, so mean momentum does not replace assessment of spatially concentrated dynamic loading.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-itaipu-owner",
          "v6-science-itaipu-history",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
