       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Unit cooling water temperature rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "發電機及軸承損失最終多以熱形式排出，冷卻水流量和溫升共同決定帶走的熱量。教材由已知熱負荷反求理想混合溫升，並區分換熱器端差與水的熱容量。增加冷卻流量不一定解除所有熱點，因接觸熱阻或局部流道堵塞仍可能控制溫度。 量測水溫差通常遠小於絕對溫度，因此成對感測器的差值校準可能比各自絕對精度更影響熱量帳。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「機組冷卻水熱升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Generator and bearing losses largely leave as heat, and cooling-water flow together with temperature rise determines heat removal. Infer an ideal mixed temperature rise from a stated thermal load, distinguishing exchanger approach temperature from water heat capacity. More cooling flow may not remove a hotspot controlled by contact resistance or a blocked local passage. The water temperature rise is often small relative to absolute temperature, so paired differential calibration can matter more than each sensor absolute accuracy for heat accounting. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unit cooling water temperature rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qheat=8000000 W; mdot=400 kg/s; cp=4180 J/(kg*K); dT=Qheat/(mdot*cp)=4.784688995 K。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qheat=8000000 W; mdot=400 kg/s; cp=4180 J/(kg*K); dT=Qheat/(mdot*cp)=4.784688995 K.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「冷卻水流量正常就保證所有熱點安全」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Normal cooling-water flow guarantees that every local hotspot is safe.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「機組冷卻水熱升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Unit cooling water temperature rise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
