       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rotor excitation frequency” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "轉子每轉出現的週期作用會在頻譜形成轉速的整數倍，葉片通過與電磁作用可能具有不同階次。辨識激振頻率先把每分鐘轉數換成每秒，再乘作用次數；頻率接近結構模態只是需要調查的條件，振幅仍取決於激振強度、阻尼及量測方向。 階次追蹤應使用同步轉速訊號，轉速掃描時固定頻率分析窗可能把峰值展寬，造成誤判阻尼增加。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉子激振頻率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Periodic forces per rotor revolution appear at integer orders of rotational frequency, with blade passage and electromagnetic forces having different orders. Convert revolutions per minute to per second before multiplying by events per turn. Proximity to a structural mode warrants investigation, while amplitude still depends on forcing, damping and measurement direction. Order tracking needs a synchronized speed reference; during a speed sweep, a fixed-frequency analysis window can smear a peak and falsely suggest greater damping. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rotor excitation frequency” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
