       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Unit rotation available hours” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Itaipu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "定期檢修以台時表示能區分停機數量與時間，卻不能直接等同失去的發電量。機組輪替可能在水量不足期間安排，部分停機因而不減少實際出力；相反地，共同設備停機可能影響所有機組。先算可用台時，再與逐時可用水量和輸電能力配對。 計畫停機與強迫停機可有不同管理目的，但在某時段都會限制可用設備；比較前應把分類與物理狀態分開。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「機組輪替可用時數」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Unit-hours distinguish outage count from duration but do not directly equal lost energy. Maintenance during water-limited periods may leave actual output unchanged, whereas shared-equipment outages can affect every unit. Calculate available unit-hours first and then pair them with hourly water availability and transmission capability. Planned and forced outages have different management meanings but both constrain equipment in an interval; separate classification from physical availability before comparing schedules. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Unit rotation available hours” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
