       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Unit rotation available hours” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "用事件紀錄核對每部機組停機開始與恢復時間，區分計畫檢修、故障及外部限制。再與逐時發電和來水比較，若可用台時減少而能量不變，需檢查原本是否受水量限制，而非假定紀錄錯誤。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Reconcile each unit outage and restoration with event logs, distinguishing maintenance, failures and external restrictions. Compare hourly generation and inflow. Reduced available unit-hours with unchanged energy may indicate water-limited operation rather than an error in the equipment records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：比較同樣損失十二台時但安排在高流量與低流量時段的情境，建立簡化發電表，指出哪種條件下兩者實際能量損失不同。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Compare two schedules losing twelve unit-hours during high-flow and low-flow periods. Build a simplified generation table and identify conditions under which the schedules produce different actual energy losses.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把待命未發電記為設備故障會低估可用率，反之只看機械可動也會漏掉電氣外送限制；不同可用率定義不能在未說明邊界時直接排名。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Treating idle standby as equipment failure understates availability, while mechanical readiness alone overlooks electrical export restrictions. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
