       "objective": "從症狀倒推「機組輪替可用時數」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Unit rotation available hours” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把待命未發電記為設備故障會低估可用率，反之只看機械可動也會漏掉電氣外送限制；不同可用率定義不能在未說明邊界時直接排名。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating idle standby as equipment failure understates availability, while mechanical readiness alone overlooks electrical export restrictions. Availability metrics with different definitions cannot be ranked directly without explaining their boundaries and what each unavailable state includes. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：計畫停機與強迫停機可有不同管理目的，但在某時段都會限制可用設備；比較前應把分類與物理狀態分開。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Planned and forced outages have different management meanings but both constrain equipment in an interval; separate classification from physical availability before comparing schedules.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「可用台時減少一定等比例減少發電量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reduced available unit-hours always reduce generation by the same proportion.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
