      {
       "id": "b205-v15-03",
       "title": "效率試驗不確定度：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Efficiency test uncertainty: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-guri-andritz",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b205-v15-02"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「效率試驗不確定度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Efficiency test uncertainty” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "查閱各儀表校準的標準不確定度及共同來源，將不同工況的重複試驗分開統計。若改善幅度與不確定度相近，應報告分辨能力不足，再研究增加樣本能否降低隨機項，而非期待它消除系統偏差。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Review standard calibration uncertainties and shared causes, keeping repeated tests at different operating points separate. If the claimed improvement is comparable to uncertainty, report limited resolution and assess whether more samples reduce random components rather than expecting them to remove systematic bias. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：為三個量測項建立不確定度表，再加入流量與水頭正相關情境，重算效率不確定度，指出改善哪一項儀表最能提高辨識能力。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Build an uncertainty budget for the three measurements, add positive correlation between head and flow, and recompute efficiency uncertainty. Identify the instrument improvement that most increases the ability to resolve a performance change.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：水頭與流量共用錯誤時間窗會造成相關偏差，直接平方和會低估或高估結果；更新前後若換了儀表量程，也可能製造看似效率改善的校準差。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Head and discharge using the same incorrect time window can have correlated errors, invalidating a simple sum of squares. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-03-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "查閱各儀表校準的標準不確定度及共同來源，將不同工況的重複試驗分開統計。若改善幅度與不確定度相近，應報告分辨能力不足，再研究增加樣本能否降低隨機項，而非期待它消除系統偏差。",
         "textEn": "Review standard calibration uncertainties and shared causes, keeping repeated tests at different operating points separate. If the claimed improvement is comparable to uncertainty, report limited resolution and assess whether more samples reduce random components rather than expecting them to remove systematic bias.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
