       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b205-v15-03"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「效率試驗不確定度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Efficiency test uncertainty” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "水頭與流量共用錯誤時間窗會造成相關偏差，直接平方和會低估或高估結果；更新前後若換了儀表量程，也可能製造看似效率改善的校準差。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Head and discharge using the same incorrect time window can have correlated errors, invalidating a simple sum of squares. Changing instrument ranges between tests may also create an apparent efficiency improvement that is actually a calibration difference. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：標準不確定度與擴充不確定度不能直接相混，若資料給涵蓋因子，應先換成同一層級再進行傳播。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Standard and expanded uncertainties cannot be mixed directly; when a coverage factor is supplied, convert every input to the same uncertainty level before propagation.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「重複測試足夠多次就能消除所有偏差」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Enough repeated tests eliminate every systematic measurement bias.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "水頭與流量共用錯誤時間窗會造成相關偏差，直接平方和會低估或高估結果；更新前後若換了儀表量程，也可能製造看似效率改善的校準差。",
         "textEn": "Head and discharge using the same incorrect time window can have correlated errors, invalidating a simple sum of squares. Changing instrument ranges between tests may also create an apparent efficiency improvement that is actually a calibration difference.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-04-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
