       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Available cavitation head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Guri Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "法蘭西斯轉輪低壓區受尾水淹沒、當地大氣壓與水溫蒸氣壓共同影響，不能只由水庫水位判定汽蝕條件。教材把壓力全部換成水頭，再用機組淨水頭標準化，取得可用汽蝕係數。所需係數依轉輪與工況改變，必須另由試驗或經驗資料取得。 轉輪基準高於尾水時吸出高度為正，淹沒時則可能為負，符號定義會直接改變可用水頭帳。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「汽蝕可用水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Low pressure around a Francis runner depends on tailwater submergence, atmospheric pressure and temperature-dependent vapor pressure, not reservoir level alone. Convert pressures to head and normalize by net machine head to obtain an available cavitation coefficient. The required coefficient varies with runner and operating point and needs separate test evidence. Runner setting above tailwater is positive under this convention, while submergence can be negative; that sign definition directly changes the available-head account. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Available cavitation head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Hatm=9.8 m; Hvap=0.3 m; Hs=1.1 m; H=70 m; sigmaA=(Hatm-Hvap-Hs)/H=0.12。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Hatm=9.8 m; Hvap=0.3 m; Hs=1.1 m; H=70 m; sigmaA=(Hatm-Hvap-Hs)/H=0.12.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「相同淨水頭必定具有相同汽蝕餘量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal net head always provides equal cavitation margin.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
