       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「汽蝕可用水頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Available cavitation head” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "同步量測尾水高程、大氣壓與水溫，核對轉輪基準點定義，再將壓力脈動及表面檢查與運轉工況配對。若水溫上升時問題加重，應檢查蒸氣壓變化，而不只調整淹沒深度假設。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Measure tailwater elevation, atmospheric pressure and water temperature together, checking the runner reference definition. Pair pressure pulsation and surface inspection with operating condition. Deterioration at warmer water calls for investigating vapor-pressure changes rather than modifying only the assumed submergence depth. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：固定機組淨水頭，分別降低大氣壓水頭與提高蒸氣壓水頭，重算可用係數，並說明還缺哪張試驗曲線才能比較所需餘量。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: At fixed net head, lower atmospheric head and raise vapor-pressure head separately. Recalculate the available coefficient and identify the test curve still required to compare it with the necessary margin.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：高海拔較低大氣壓會減少可用壓力餘量，溫水又提高蒸氣壓；若誤用海平面常數及固定水溫，可能在相同淨水頭下錯判汽蝕條件。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Lower atmospheric pressure reduces available margin, and warmer water raises vapor pressure. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
