       "objective": "從症狀倒推「汽蝕可用水頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Available cavitation head” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "高海拔較低大氣壓會減少可用壓力餘量，溫水又提高蒸氣壓；若誤用海平面常數及固定水溫，可能在相同淨水頭下錯判汽蝕條件。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Lower atmospheric pressure reduces available margin, and warmer water raises vapor pressure. Using sea-level pressure and a fixed temperature can therefore misrepresent cavitation conditions even when the net generating head remains unchanged during comparison. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：轉輪基準高於尾水時吸出高度為正，淹沒時則可能為負，符號定義會直接改變可用水頭帳。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Runner setting above tailwater is positive under this convention, while submergence can be negative; that sign definition directly changes the available-head account.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「相同淨水頭必定具有相同汽蝕餘量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Equal net head always provides equal cavitation margin.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
