       "objective": "說明「轉子不平衡力」如何影響古里水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rotor unbalance force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Guri Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "轉子不平衡量可用質量乘偏心距表示，旋轉時產生隨角速度平方增加的週期力。平衡修正需知道相位與支承反應，而不是只測振幅。教材估算激振力尺度後，要求區分軸彎曲、對心偏差與水力不對稱，因它們也可能在轉頻附近產生訊號。 不平衡力是隨軸旋轉的向量，固定方向感測器看到其投影，量測相位可提供配重位置而振幅單獨不能。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉子不平衡力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rotor unbalance is expressed as mass times eccentricity and generates a periodic force proportional to angular speed squared. Correction requires phase and support response, not amplitude alone. After estimating excitation scale, distinguish bent shafts, misalignment and hydraulic asymmetry, which can also produce signals near rotational frequency. Unbalance force rotates as a vector; a fixed sensor observes its projection, making phase information essential for locating a correction mass rather than amplitude alone. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rotor unbalance force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：U=500 kg*m; n=100 rpm; F=U*(2*pi*n/60)**2=54831.13556 N。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: U=500 kg*m; n=100 rpm; F=U*(2*pi*n/60)**2=54831.13556 N.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「出現轉頻振動就一定是轉子不平衡」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A vibration at rotational frequency always proves rotor unbalance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「轉子不平衡力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rotor unbalance force”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
