      {
       "id": "b205-v15-23",
       "title": "局部熱阻與熱點：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Local thermal resistance and hotspots: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-guri-andritz",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b205-v15-22"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「局部熱阻與熱點」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Local thermal resistance and hotspots” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "在熱源附近與冷卻端同時量溫，透過不同負載下的溫差斜率估算熱阻，再比較停機冷卻曲線。若穩態溫差增大但熱源功率未變，應研究接觸劣化或結垢；若只有時間常數改變，需另查熱容量與流量分配。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Measure temperatures near the source and cooling end, infer resistance from temperature difference over several loads, and compare cooldown curves. A larger steady difference at unchanged heat load suggests contact degradation or fouling, while changed response time also requires considering thermal capacity and flow distribution. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：把等效熱阻增加一半並保持熱負荷，計算新溫差，再建立兩條並聯散熱路徑，說明新增旁路如何改變局部熱流而非只改變總流量。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Increase resistance by half at fixed heat load and calculate the new temperature difference. Then build two parallel heat paths and explain how a bypass changes local heat flow rather than only total coolant flow.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：接觸面鬆動會增加熱阻並形成局部高溫，平均出口水溫可能仍正常；若感測器離熱點太遠，訊號會被導熱平滑，延後發現絕緣或潤滑問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: A loose contact increases thermal resistance and local temperature while average outlet water can remain normal. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-23-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "在熱源附近與冷卻端同時量溫，透過不同負載下的溫差斜率估算熱阻，再比較停機冷卻曲線。若穩態溫差增大但熱源功率未變，應研究接觸劣化或結垢；若只有時間常數改變，需另查熱容量與流量分配。",
         "textEn": "Measure temperatures near the source and cooling end, infer resistance from temperature difference over several loads, and compare cooldown curves. A larger steady difference at unchanged heat load suggests contact degradation or fouling, while changed response time also requires considering thermal capacity and flow distribution.",
         "sourceIds": [
