       "objective": "從症狀倒推「局部熱阻與熱點」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Local thermal resistance and hotspots” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "接觸面鬆動會增加熱阻並形成局部高溫，平均出口水溫可能仍正常；若感測器離熱點太遠，訊號會被導熱平滑，延後發現絕緣或潤滑問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "A loose contact increases thermal resistance and local temperature while average outlet water can remain normal. A sensor far from the hotspot smooths the signal through conduction and can delay recognition of insulation or lubrication deterioration. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：串聯熱阻相加而並聯導熱能力相加，選錯連接方式會錯判熱流方向及熱點，應先畫熱路圖。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Series thermal resistances add, while parallel conductances add; choosing the wrong connection misrepresents heat paths and hotspots, so draw the thermal network first.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「總冷卻流量正常就代表局部熱阻正常」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Normal total cooling flow proves that local thermal resistance is normal.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-24-k1",
