       "objective": "說明「疲勞循環累積」如何影響古里水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Fatigue cycle accumulation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Guri Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "轉輪與軸系承受的交變荷載需要按幅值及循環次數整理，平均功率相同可能具有不同疲勞歷程。線性損傷和可作教材尺度分析，但材料曲線、平均應力與荷載先後次序會影響真實壽命。計算值不能直接當成剩餘年限，尤其缺少裂紋狀態時。 每一組疲勞壽命必須對應同一應力幅定義，範圍與振幅差一倍，混用會嚴重改變材料曲線取值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「疲勞循環累積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Alternating runner and shaft loads require cycle counts by amplitude; equal mean power can hide different fatigue histories. A linear damage sum provides a teaching scale, while material curves, mean stress and sequence affect actual life. The calculated fraction cannot directly be converted into remaining years, particularly without crack-state information. Every fatigue life must use the same stress definition; stress range and amplitude differ by a factor of two, strongly affecting the selected material-curve value. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fatigue cycle accumulation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：n1=200000 cycles; N1=1000000 cycles; n2=1000000 cycles; N2=5000000 cycles; D=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.4。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: n1=200000 cycles; N1=1000000 cycles; n2=1000000 cycles; N2=5000000 cycles; D=n1/N1+n2/N2=0.4.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「相同平均功率就保證相同疲勞壽命」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal mean power guarantees equal fatigue life.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「疲勞循環累積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fatigue cycle accumulation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
