      {
       "id": "b205-v15-27",
       "title": "疲勞循環累積：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Fatigue cycle accumulation: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-guri-andritz",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b205-v15-26"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「疲勞循環累積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Fatigue cycle accumulation” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "對應變時序進行循環計數，核對高低幅值分類與材料試驗的應力定義一致。再以非破壞檢查追蹤裂紋或缺陷；若累積指標低而裂紋成長，應查局部集中及模型遺漏，而不是否定檢查結果。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Count cycles from strain histories and ensure amplitude definitions match the material test data. Track cracks or defects with nondestructive inspection. Crack growth despite a low damage index calls for investigating local concentration and omitted mechanisms rather than dismissing the inspection evidence. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：保持總循環數，將一部分低幅循環改為高幅循環，重算損傷和，再列出平均應力與腐蝕環境會如何限制這個簡化比較。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Keep total cycle count fixed while replacing some low-amplitude cycles with high-amplitude cycles. Recalculate the damage sum and explain how mean stress and corrosion constrain the simplified comparison.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：少量高幅值事件可能主導疲勞，低頻平均紀錄會把它們抹平；若將不同應力集中位置混成一張循環表，也會使線性損傷值失去物理意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: A few high-amplitude events can dominate fatigue and disappear in low-frequency averages. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-27-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "對應變時序進行循環計數，核對高低幅值分類與材料試驗的應力定義一致。再以非破壞檢查追蹤裂紋或缺陷；若累積指標低而裂紋成長，應查局部集中及模型遺漏，而不是否定檢查結果。",
         "textEn": "Count cycles from strain histories and ensure amplitude definitions match the material test data. Track cracks or defects with nondestructive inspection. Crack growth despite a low damage index calls for investigating local concentration and omitted mechanisms rather than dismissing the inspection evidence.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
