       ],
       "objective": "說明「表面磨耗質量」如何影響古里水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Surface wear mass loss” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Guri Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "轉輪表面損失的體積可由面積與平均厚度變化估算，再用材料密度換成質量，但磨耗通常高度不均勻。局部坑蝕深度對應力集中及水力形狀的影響，可能比總失重更重要。量測必須追蹤同一坐標區域，修補材料也需從原材損失中分開。 平均厚度須按面積加權，不能把不同大小區塊的厚度直接算術平均，否則質量帳會與表面幾何不一致。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「表面磨耗質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Surface loss can be estimated from area and mean thickness change and converted to mass with density, but wear is rarely uniform. Local pit depth may matter more than total mass for stress concentration and hydraulic shape. Repeat measurements must track the same coordinates and distinguish repair material from original material loss. Mean thickness requires area weighting; a simple mean of unequal patch sizes gives a mass account inconsistent with the measured surface geometry and affected area. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Surface wear mass loss” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：A=12 m2; dt=0.0008 m; rho=7800 kg/m3; dm=A*dt*rho=74.88 kg。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: A=12 m2; dt=0.0008 m; rho=7800 kg/m3; dm=A*dt*rho=74.88 kg.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「總失重量小就表示局部磨耗無害」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Small total mass loss proves that local wear is harmless.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「表面磨耗質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Surface wear mass loss”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "表面磨耗質量",
         "titleEn": "Surface wear mass loss",
         "text": "轉輪表面損失的體積可由面積與平均厚度變化估算，再用材料密度換成質量，但磨耗通常高度不均勻。局部坑蝕深度對應力集中及水力形狀的影響，可能比總失重更重要。",
         "textEn": "Surface loss can be estimated from area and mean thickness change and converted to mass with density, but wear is rarely uniform. Local pit depth may matter more than total mass for stress concentration and hydraulic shape.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-29-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：總失重量小就表示局部磨耗無害 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Small total mass loss proves that local wear is harmless. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
