      {
       "id": "b205-v15-31",
       "title": "表面磨耗質量：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Surface wear mass loss: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-guri-andritz",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b205-v15-30"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「表面磨耗質量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Surface wear mass loss” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "將三維掃描對準固定控制點，建立厚度損失分布而不只報平均值，並用已知厚度區域檢查掃描偏差。對最大坑深另作局部檢查，若總失重很小但形狀尖銳，仍需評估應力與流場。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Register three-dimensional scans to fixed controls and map thickness loss rather than reporting only its mean. Check scan bias against known-thickness regions and inspect maximum pit depth separately. Small total mass loss with sharp local geometry still requires stress and flow assessment. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：設計兩個失重量相同但坑深分布不同的表面，計算平均厚度並比較最大深度，再提出哪些掃描解析度與檢查方法能區分其風險。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Construct two surfaces with equal mass loss but different pit-depth distributions. Calculate mean thickness and compare maximum depth, then choose scan resolution and inspection methods that distinguish their implications.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：掃描對位誤差可在整片表面製造假磨耗，修補塗層又可能掩蓋下方缺陷；如果只以總重量驗收，會漏掉局部形狀造成的水力性能及疲勞問題。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Registration error can create apparent wear over a large surface, while a repair layer can conceal underlying defects. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-31-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "將三維掃描對準固定控制點，建立厚度損失分布而不只報平均值，並用已知厚度區域檢查掃描偏差。對最大坑深另作局部檢查，若總失重很小但形狀尖銳，仍需評估應力與流場。",
         "textEn": "Register three-dimensional scans to fixed controls and map thickness loss rather than reporting only its mean. Check scan bias against known-thickness regions and inspect maximum pit depth separately. Small total mass loss with sharp local geometry still requires stress and flow assessment.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-31-k2",
         "title": "現場實務",
         "titleEn": "Site practice",
         "text": "設計兩個失重量相同但坑深分布不同的表面，計算平均厚度並比較最大深度，再提出哪些掃描解析度與檢查方法能區分其風險。",
         "textEn": "Construct two surfaces with equal mass loss but different pit-depth distributions. Calculate mean thickness and compare maximum depth, then choose scan resolution and inspection methods that distinguish their implications.",
         "sourceIds": [
