       "objective": "從症狀倒推「表面磨耗質量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Surface wear mass loss” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "掃描對位誤差可在整片表面製造假磨耗，修補塗層又可能掩蓋下方缺陷；如果只以總重量驗收，會漏掉局部形狀造成的水力性能及疲勞問題。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Registration error can create apparent wear over a large surface, while a repair layer can conceal underlying defects. Acceptance based only on total weight can miss local geometry effects on hydraulic performance and fatigue behavior. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：平均厚度須按面積加權，不能把不同大小區塊的厚度直接算術平均，否則質量帳會與表面幾何不一致。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Mean thickness requires area weighting; a simple mean of unequal patch sizes gives a mass account inconsistent with the measured surface geometry and affected area.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「總失重量小就表示局部磨耗無害」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small total mass loss proves that local wear is harmless.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-32-k1",
