       "objective": "說明「檢測陽性與基率」如何影響古里水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Inspection positives and base rates” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Guri Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "非破壞檢測的陽性訊號不等於缺陷已被確認，解讀還需要靈敏度、特異度與受檢群的缺陷基率。貝氏帳可把真陽性與假陽性分開，說明低基率時為何需要第二種方法確認。教材機率均為假設，不代表任何現場檢測程序的認證能力。 陽性預測值回答已出現訊號後的缺陷機率，靈敏度回答已知有缺陷時能否檢出，兩者條件方向相反。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「檢測陽性與基率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A positive nondestructive indication is not a confirmed defect; interpretation also requires sensitivity, specificity and defect prevalence in the inspected population. A Bayesian account separates true and false positives and explains the value of a second confirmation method at low prevalence. Teaching probabilities do not certify any actual inspection procedure. Positive predictive value asks about a defect after an indication, while sensitivity asks about detection given a defect; the conditioning direction is different in these questions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Inspection positives and base rates” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：prev=0.02 (dimensionless); sens=0.90 (dimensionless); spec=0.95 (dimensionless); PPV=prev*sens/(prev*sens+(1-prev)*(1-spec))=0.2686567164。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: prev=0.02 (dimensionless); sens=0.90 (dimensionless); spec=0.95 (dimensionless); PPV=prev*sens/(prev*sens+(1-prev)*(1-spec))=0.2686567164.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「檢測靈敏度就是陽性結果的確診機率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Inspection sensitivity equals the probability that a positive result is a true defect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「檢測陽性與基率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Inspection positives and base rates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "檢測陽性與基率",
         "titleEn": "Inspection positives and base rates",
         "text": "非破壞檢測的陽性訊號不等於缺陷已被確認，解讀還需要靈敏度、特異度與受檢群的缺陷基率。貝氏帳可把真陽性與假陽性分開，說明低基率時為何需要第二種方法確認。",
         "textEn": "A positive nondestructive indication is not a confirmed defect; interpretation also requires sensitivity, specificity and defect prevalence in the inspected population. A Bayesian account separates true and false positives and explains the value of a second confirmation method at low prevalence.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-33-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：檢測靈敏度就是陽性結果的確診機率 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Inspection sensitivity equals the probability that a positive result is a true defect. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
