       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「檢測陽性與基率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Inspection positives and base rates” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "將靈敏度直接當成陽性可信度會高估低基率群的確診比例；第二次檢查若使用同樣缺陷敏感性與共同誤差，也不能當成完全獨立的確認。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating sensitivity as positive predictive value overstates confirmed defects in a low-prevalence population. A second inspection sharing the same blind spots and error sources cannot automatically be counted as independent confirmation of the first indication. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：陽性預測值回答已出現訊號後的缺陷機率，靈敏度回答已知有缺陷時能否檢出，兩者條件方向相反。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Positive predictive value asks about a defect after an indication, while sensitivity asks about detection given a defect; the conditioning direction is different in these questions.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「檢測靈敏度就是陽性結果的確診機率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Inspection sensitivity equals the probability that a positive result is a true defect.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-36-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "將靈敏度直接當成陽性可信度會高估低基率群的確診比例；第二次檢查若使用同樣缺陷敏感性與共同誤差，也不能當成完全獨立的確認。",
         "textEn": "Treating sensitivity as positive predictive value overstates confirmed defects in a low-prevalence population. A second inspection sharing the same blind spots and error sources cannot automatically be counted as independent confirmation of the first indication.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b205-v15-36-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-guri-andritz",
