       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「更新停機能量機會」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Renewal outage energy opportunity” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "將檢修時程與逐時來水、其他機組餘裕及水庫可用空間配對，核對實際旁通水量。若停機期間水被儲存，需追蹤後續發電而不能在停機當日把全部潛在電量列為永久損失。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Pair the outage schedule with hourly inflow, spare unit capacity and available storage, checking actual bypassed water. If water is retained during the outage, follow its later generation rather than booking the entire potential energy difference as a permanent loss on that day. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：比較立即更新與延後更新兩個時程，設定可儲存水量及替代機組容量，分別計算潛在與實際未利用電量，列出決策仍需的可靠度資料。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Compare immediate and delayed renewal schedules with stated storage space and substitute-unit capacity. Calculate potential and actually unused energy separately, then identify reliability information still needed for the decision.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：檢修延誤若跨入高流量期間，原可儲存的水可能轉為旁通，損失機制因而改變；只用全年平均功率估算，會漏掉停機時序與其他設備限制的關聯。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: An outage delay into a high-flow period can turn storable water into bypassed release and change the loss mechanism. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
