       "objective": "說明「開挖卸荷彈性回復」如何影響小灣水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Elastic rebound after excavation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "深谷壩肩開挖改變原先岩體應力，部分變形是彈性回復，部分可能來自節理張開或損傷。先以應力變化除彈性模數估計一維應變尺度，便於檢查量測大小；但岩體模數須與方向、尺度及卸載路徑相符，不能拿完整岩芯數值代表全部邊坡。 卸載曲線與初次載入曲線未必一致，回復應變應使用相符的路徑模數，才能保留不可逆變形的意義。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「開挖卸荷彈性回復」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Abutment excavation changes the original rock stress, producing elastic rebound as well as possible joint opening or damage. Stress change divided by modulus provides a one-dimensional strain scale for checking observations. Rock-mass modulus must match direction, scale and unloading path rather than being replaced indiscriminately by an intact-core value. Unloading and first-loading curves need not coincide; rebound strain requires a path-appropriate modulus so that irreversible deformation remains distinguishable from elastic recovery. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Elastic rebound after excavation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：dsigma=2 MPa; E=15000 MPa; strain=dsigma/E*1e6=133.3333333 microstrain。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: dsigma=2 MPa; E=15000 MPa; strain=dsigma/E*1e6=133.3333333 microstrain.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「完整岩芯彈性模數可直接代表整座岩坡」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"An intact-core modulus directly represents the entire rock slope.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「開挖卸荷彈性回復」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Elastic rebound after excavation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "開挖卸荷彈性回復",
         "titleEn": "Elastic rebound after excavation",
         "text": "深谷壩肩開挖改變原先岩體應力，部分變形是彈性回復，部分可能來自節理張開或損傷。先以應力變化除彈性模數估計一維應變尺度，便於檢查量測大小；但岩體模數須與方向、尺度及卸載路徑相符，不能拿完整岩芯數值代表全部邊坡。",
         "textEn": "Abutment excavation changes the original rock stress, producing elastic rebound as well as possible joint opening or damage. Stress change divided by modulus provides a one-dimensional strain scale for checking observations.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiaowan-huaneng",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-01-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：完整岩芯彈性模數可直接代表整座岩坡 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: An intact-core modulus directly represents the entire rock slope. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
