       "objective": "從症狀倒推「開挖卸荷彈性回復」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Elastic rebound after excavation” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "開挖擾動可能形成方向性鬆弛帶，若仍用開挖前模數會低估位移；測點支架受爆破振動鬆動也可能造成跳值，需用深部與地表量測互相確認。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Excavation can produce a directional loosened zone, making the pre-excavation modulus underpredict movement. Blast-induced loosening of a sensor mounting can also cause a jump, requiring comparison of deep and surface measurements before attributing it to rock response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：卸載曲線與初次載入曲線未必一致，回復應變應使用相符的路徑模數，才能保留不可逆變形的意義。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Unloading and first-loading curves need not coincide; rebound strain requires a path-appropriate modulus so that irreversible deformation remains distinguishable from elastic recovery.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「完整岩芯彈性模數可直接代表整座岩坡」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An intact-core modulus directly represents the entire rock slope.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "開挖擾動可能形成方向性鬆弛帶，若仍用開挖前模數會低估位移；測點支架受爆破振動鬆動也可能造成跳值，需用深部與地表量測互相確認。",
         "textEn": "Excavation can produce a directional loosened zone, making the pre-excavation modulus underpredict movement. Blast-induced loosening of a sensor mounting can also cause a jump, requiring comparison of deep and surface measurements before attributing it to rock response.",
         "sourceIds": [
