       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Directional stiffness and load transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "高拱壩向岩體傳力時，節理方向會使不同方向的等效剛度不同。教材以一個受壓岩柱的軸向變形建立尺度，不將岩柱當成實際三維拱座。受力面積與傳力長度是模型假設，需要地質與位移場支持；方向性被忽略時，總變形可能吻合而局部反力錯誤。 等效面積代表模型傳力範圍而非任意外觀面積，需與荷載方向和觀察尺度一起定義，才可比較剛度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「方向剛度與傳力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Joint orientation gives an abutment different effective stiffness in different directions. An axially loaded rock prism establishes a deformation scale without representing the actual three-dimensional support. Loaded area and transfer length are assumptions requiring geological and displacement evidence. Ignoring anisotropy can match overall motion while assigning incorrect local reactions. Effective area represents the modeled load-transfer region, not an arbitrary visible surface; define it with load direction and observation scale before comparing stiffness estimates. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Directional stiffness and load transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F=90 MN; L=12 m; E=18000 MPa; A=12 m2; u=F*1e6*L/(E*1e6*A)*1000=5 mm。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: F=90 MN; L=12 m; E=18000 MPa; A=12 m2; u=F*1e6*L/(E*1e6*A)*1000=5 mm.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「拱座各方向都可使用相同等效剛度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every abutment direction can use the same effective stiffness.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
