       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rock wedge effective normal force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "邊坡岩楔沿既有面滑動時，水壓會降低有效正向力而削弱摩擦抗力。教材把已解析到滑面的正向、切向及黏聚合力分開，避免把岩楔總重量直接當成正向力。真實三維岩楔可能沿兩個面共同運動，仍需節理方位與出口條件判斷運動學可行性。 若水壓大到使接觸面張開，摩擦抗力不能繼續按負有效正向力延伸，必須改變接觸狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩楔有效正向力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Water pressure reduces effective normal force on a potential rock-wedge sliding surface and weakens frictional resistance. Separate resolved normal force, driving shear and cohesive resultant rather than treating total weight as normal force. Real three-dimensional wedges may move along two planes and require orientation and daylighting checks before force balance is meaningful. If pressure opens the contact, friction cannot be extrapolated using a negative effective normal force; the model must change its contact state and load path. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rock wedge effective normal force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：N=20 MN; U=4 MN; mu=0.65 (dimensionless); C=2 MN; Tdrive=9 MN; FS=(mu*(N-U)+C)/Tdrive=1.377777778。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: N=20 MN; U=4 MN; mu=0.65 (dimensionless); C=2 MN; Tdrive=9 MN; FS=(mu*(N-U)+C)/Tdrive=1.377777778.",
