       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Pore pressure lag during drawdown” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水庫下降後，岸坡內孔壓可能因排水速度有限而仍偏高，外部水體支撐卻已減少。單一指數模型用來表示一個假想鬆弛時間，幫助比較降水位速度與內部反應；裂隙多路徑及飽和帶移動可能產生多個時間尺度，不能把擬合常數當成土性常數。 鬆弛時間描述系統幾何與排水路徑的綜合反應，增設排水後需要重新識別，不能直接沿用處理前數值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「降水位孔壓滯後」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "After reservoir drawdown, internal slope pressure may remain high because drainage is slow while external water support has already diminished. A single exponential illustrates an assumed relaxation time for comparing drawdown and response. Multiple fracture paths and moving saturation boundaries can produce several time scales, so a fitted constant is not a universal material property. Relaxation time combines geometry and drainage pathways; adding drains changes that system, so the parameter must be identified again rather than inherited unchanged from earlier conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pore pressure lag during drawdown” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：h0=10 m; t=24 h; tau=24 h; hExcess=h0*exp(-t/tau)=3.678794412 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: h0=10 m; t=24 h; tau=24 h; hExcess=h0*exp(-t/tau)=3.678794412 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「水庫水位下降時岸坡孔壓必定同步下降」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Slope pore pressure always falls simultaneously with reservoir level.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「降水位孔壓滯後」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pore pressure lag during drawdown”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
