       "objective": "從症狀倒推「地震慣性力尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Seismic inertia force scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "不同方向地震分量的峰值未必同時發生，任意相加可能扭曲載重組合；忽略庫水與基礎互制也會錯估頻率，表面上保守的力值不保證反應保守。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Peaks of different earthquake components need not coincide, so arbitrary addition distorts combinations. Omitting reservoir and foundation interaction can also misplace natural frequencies; an apparently conservative force does not guarantee conservative dynamic response. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：等效質量須說明對應方向與模態參與程度，壩體總質量不一定等於單一反應模態可使用的有效質量。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: An equivalent mass needs a direction and modal participation definition; total structural mass is not automatically the effective mass appropriate for one response mode.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「等效靜力較大就保證所有動力反應保守」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A larger equivalent static force guarantees conservative dynamic response in every mode.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-20-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "不同方向地震分量的峰值未必同時發生，任意相加可能扭曲載重組合；忽略庫水與基礎互制也會錯估頻率，表面上保守的力值不保證反應保守。",
         "textEn": "Peaks of different earthquake components need not coincide, so arbitrary addition distorts combinations. Omitting reservoir and foundation interaction can also misplace natural frequencies; an apparently conservative force does not guarantee conservative dynamic response.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiaowan-huaneng",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
