       "objective": "說明「受約束溫升應力」如何影響小灣水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Restrained heating stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "混凝土升溫希望自由膨脹，若沿一方向完全受約束，就會產生與自由熱應變相反的機械應變。教材用彈性模數乘熱應變估算壓應力幅度，並明確限制為單軸完全約束。實際早齡期材料會徐變，接縫也可能開合，必須避免把理想上界直接當成現場應力。 完全約束的總應變為零，但自由熱應變與機械應變各自非零，這個分解是辨認應力符號的關鍵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「受約束溫升應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Heating concrete creates free thermal expansion; complete restraint along one direction requires an opposing mechanical strain. Modulus times thermal strain estimates the compressive stress magnitude under a uniaxial fully restrained assumption. Early-age creep and joint movement alter real stress, so this idealized bound is not a field stress measurement. Total strain is zero under complete restraint, while thermal and mechanical strains are individually nonzero; their decomposition is essential for assigning the correct stress sign. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained heating stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：E=25000 MPa; alpha=0.00001 1/K; dT=12 K; sigmaC=E*alpha*dT=3 MPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: E=25000 MPa; alpha=0.00001 1/K; dT=12 K; sigmaC=E*alpha*dT=3 MPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「混凝土目前溫度高就必定承受拉應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Concrete at a high current temperature must be in thermal tension.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「受約束溫升應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained heating stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
