      {
       "id": "b206-v15-29",
       "title": "梯級變流到達：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Cascade release wave arrival: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-xiaowan-huaneng",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b206-v15-28"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「梯級變流到達」如何影響小灣水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Cascade release wave arrival” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "上游電站改變出流後，下游收到的是沿河傳播並被地形調制的水位流量波，不是整團水瞬間移動。教材用假定波速估算訊息到達時間，並區分波速與水粒子平均流速。分岔、回水與儲存會展寬波形，因此到達時間不能直接代表可用調節容量。 到達時間應區分波前、峰值與整體波形中心，三者在展寬河段可能不同，需先界定調度需要哪種時標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「梯級變流到達」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "An upstream release change reaches downstream as a wave modified by channel geometry rather than an instant movement of all water. An assumed wave celerity estimates signal travel time and is distinguished from average particle velocity. Branching, backwater and reach storage broaden the waveform, so arrival time is not regulating capacity. Arrival can mean the front, peak or center of a wave; these differ in a dispersive reach, so define the timing quantity relevant to coordination. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cascade release wave arrival” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：L=80000 m; c=2 m/s; t=L/c/3600=11.11111111 h。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: L=80000 m; c=2 m/s; t=L/c/3600=11.11111111 h.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「洪水波速必定等於水粒子的平均流速」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A release-wave celerity always equals mean water-particle velocity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「梯級變流到達」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cascade release wave arrival”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "梯級變流到達",
         "titleEn": "Cascade release wave arrival",
         "text": "上游電站改變出流後，下游收到的是沿河傳播並被地形調制的水位流量波，不是整團水瞬間移動。教材用假定波速估算訊息到達時間，並區分波速與水粒子平均流速。",
         "textEn": "An upstream release change reaches downstream as a wave modified by channel geometry rather than an instant movement of all water. An assumed wave celerity estimates signal travel time and is distinguished from average particle velocity.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiaowan-huaneng",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-29-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：洪水波速必定等於水粒子的平均流速 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: A release-wave celerity always equals mean water-particle velocity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiaowan-huaneng",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "關於「梯級變流到達」，下列哪一項敘述正確？",
        "questionEn": "Which statement about \"Cascade release wave arrival\" is correct?",
        "options": [
         "洪水波速必定等於水粒子的平均流速",
         "分層界面恢復力一律使用完整重力加速度",
         "上游電站改變出流後，下游收到的是沿河傳播並被地形調制的水位流量波，不是整團水瞬間移動。"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
