       "objective": "從症狀倒推「梯級變流到達」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cascade release wave arrival” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把平均流速當波速可能錯配下游調度時機，忽略支流洪峰又可能讓波形疊加；若只看最高水位時間，會漏掉較早開始的流量變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Using mean particle velocity as celerity can mistime downstream coordination, while ignoring a tributary peak can miss superposition. Tracking only the highest level also overlooks the earlier onset of a release-related flow change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：到達時間應區分波前、峰值與整體波形中心，三者在展寬河段可能不同，需先界定調度需要哪種時標。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Arrival can mean the front, peak or center of a wave; these differ in a dispersive reach, so define the timing quantity relevant to coordination.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「洪水波速必定等於水粒子的平均流速」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A release-wave celerity always equals mean water-particle velocity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-32-k1",
