       "objective": "說明「密度界面流態」如何影響小灣水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Density interface flow regime” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水庫分層使界面恢復力取決於密度差而非完整重力加速度。密度福祿數比較流速與內部重力波尺度，可幫助判斷取水或入流對界面的擾動，但實際捲吸受剪切、混合及幾何控制。教材不把某個比值當成所有水庫通用的分層破壞界線。 密度差符號反映穩定或不穩定排列，若重水在上則原先穩定內波尺度不適用，需改研究翻轉混合。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密度界面流態」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Reservoir stratification gives an interface a restoring force based on density contrast rather than full gravity. A densimetric Froude number compares flow speed with an internal-wave scale and helps characterize disturbance, while entrainment depends on shear, mixing and geometry. No single ratio is treated as a universal interface-breakdown threshold. The density-contrast sign identifies stable or unstable layering; dense water above light water invalidates the stable internal-wave scale and calls for an overturning analysis. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Density interface flow regime” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：v=0.2 m/s; drho=2 kg/m3; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; h=8 m; Fr=v/(g*drho/rho*h)**0.5=0.504818777。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: v=0.2 m/s; drho=2 kg/m3; rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; h=8 m; Fr=v/(g*drho/rho*h)**0.5=0.504818777.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「分層界面恢復力一律使用完整重力加速度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The restoring force at a stratified interface always uses full gravity without density contrast.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「密度界面流態」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Density interface flow regime”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "密度界面流態",
         "titleEn": "Density interface flow regime",
         "text": "水庫分層使界面恢復力取決於密度差而非完整重力加速度。密度福祿數比較流速與內部重力波尺度，可幫助判斷取水或入流對界面的擾動，但實際捲吸受剪切、混合及幾何控制。",
         "textEn": "Reservoir stratification gives an interface a restoring force based on density contrast rather than full gravity. A densimetric Froude number compares flow speed with an internal-wave scale and helps characterize disturbance, while entrainment depends on shear, mixing and geometry.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiaowan-huaneng",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b206-v15-33-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：分層界面恢復力一律使用完整重力加速度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: The restoring force at a stratified interface always uses full gravity without density contrast. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
