       "objective": "說明「岸坡位移速率」如何影響小灣水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Abutment slope movement rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiaowan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "邊坡位移速率由相鄰觀測差除時間取得，必須保留方向與正負號。較短時間窗能顯示快速變化，卻也放大量測噪音；較長時間窗則可能掩蓋加速。課程先算平均速率，再要求與降雨、孔壓及施工事件配對，避免把一個斜率直接當成通用失穩預報。 速率差分的兩次位移若有共同基準誤差，部分偏差可能相消，但不同日期的基準跳動反而會放大假速率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岸坡位移速率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Movement rate is displacement change divided by elapsed time with direction and sign retained. Short windows reveal rapid change but amplify noise, while long windows can conceal acceleration. Calculate the mean rate, then compare rainfall, pressure and construction events rather than treating one slope of a time series as a universal instability forecast. A shared reference bias can partly cancel in displacement differencing, while a reference jump between dates can create a large false rate; distinguish the two errors. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Abutment slope movement rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：x1=12 mm; x2=17 mm; dt=8 day; v=(x2-x1)/dt=0.625 mm/day。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: x1=12 mm; x2=17 mm; dt=8 day; v=(x2-x1)/dt=0.625 mm/day.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「任何正位移速率都能直接推算破壞日期」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Any positive movement rate can directly predict the date of failure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「岸坡位移速率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Abutment slope movement rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
