       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「岸坡位移速率」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Abutment slope movement rate” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "核對每次量測的基準穩定性與時間戳，將原始位移、速率及不確定度共同作圖。若速率增加只來自單次跳值，先查儀器；若多種獨立量測都持續加速，再研究水壓與岩體機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Check reference stability and timestamps, plotting displacement, rate and uncertainty together. An apparent increase caused by one jump calls for instrument checks. Sustained acceleration across independent measurements justifies investigating pore pressure and rock-mass mechanisms rather than relying on a single processed channel. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：用相同起訖位移製作等速與後期加速兩條曲線，比較八日平均及兩日速率，說明需要何種量測精度才可辨識其差異。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Create constant-rate and late-accelerating histories with identical endpoints. Compare eight-day and two-day rates and determine what measurement precision is required to distinguish the two movement patterns.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：將長時間平均速率外推會漏掉近期加速，過度平滑也可能延後辨識；反之，差分噪音能製造假加速度，必須用原始位移及獨立測點支持解釋。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Extrapolating a long-term mean can miss recent acceleration, and heavy smoothing can delay recognition. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
