       "objective": "從症狀倒推「高壩水壓投影」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “High dam pressure projection” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate. Ignoring curved-surface normal components can also omit vertical action, so a horizontal projected-force account does not constitute the complete loading of the dam. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：合力作用點由壓力一階矩決定，不是幾何深度中點；分段壓力圖改變時，力與力矩都需重新積分。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: The resultant location follows the first pressure moment, not the geometric midpoint; changing a piecewise pressure diagram requires recalculating both force and moment.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Crest elevation above sea level can directly replace water depth in pressure integration.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "使用壩頂高程代替水深會把基準誤差平方放大，造成外力嚴重失真；忽略曲面法向分量也可能漏掉垂直作用，不能由水平投影帳宣稱全壩荷載已完整。",
         "textEn": "Substituting crest elevation for depth squares a datum error in the load estimate. Ignoring curved-surface normal components can also omit vertical action, so a horizontal projected-force account does not constitute the complete loading of the dam.",
         "sourceIds": [
