       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Two plane wedge resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "深谷岩楔可能同時受兩組節理面約束，各面的有效正向力與摩擦係數都會影響可用抗力。教材在已給定法向反力的前提下加總沿假想運動方向的摩擦，避免用單一坡角代表全部三維幾何。真正反力須由向量平衡求得，不能憑重量任意平均分配。 兩面抗力在真實空間須按向量合成，本例同方向相加是額外假設，不能直接轉用到不同交線方位。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙滑面岩楔抗力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A canyon wedge may be constrained by two joint planes, each with its own effective normal force and friction. Given resolved reactions, sum the assumed friction contributions along a movement direction rather than representing all geometry by one slope angle. Actual reactions must follow vector equilibrium, not arbitrary equal division of wedge weight. Resistance contributions require vector combination in real space; adding them along one direction is an extra assumption here and cannot transfer unchanged to other intersection geometries. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Two plane wedge resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
