       "objective": "從症狀倒推「雙滑面岩楔抗力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Two plane wedge resistance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values. If a plane separates, its previous friction contribution cannot remain in the account; kinematics and equilibrium must be recalculated for the changed contact state. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：兩面抗力在真實空間須按向量合成，本例同方向相加是額外假設，不能直接轉用到不同交線方位。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Resistance contributions require vector combination in real space; adding them along one direction is an extra assumption here and cannot transfer unchanged to other intersection geometries.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「兩滑面反力可以一律把總重量平分」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reactions on two sliding planes can always be obtained by dividing weight equally.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-12-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "一面節理連通高水壓會重新分配接觸反力，原先固定反力假設可能失效；若某面脫開，其摩擦不能繼續按原正向力計入，需重新求運動學與平衡。",
         "textEn": "High pressure connected to one plane can redistribute contact reactions and invalidate their assumed fixed values. If a plane separates, its previous friction contribution cannot remain in the account; kinematics and equilibrium must be recalculated for the changed contact state.",
         "sourceIds": [
