       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Long term anchor force retention” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "預應力錨索鎖定後可能因鋼材鬆弛、岩體變形及接頭就位而損失拉力，各效應的參考狀態必須說清楚。若後一比例作用於已減少的力，應連乘而非把百分率任意相加。教材只建立保留力帳，實際錨固區承載及防蝕完整性仍要獨立評估。 保留力與可承受最大力不同，前者描述目前預應力，後者還需要鋼材截面、錨頭與岩體黏結能力等證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「錨索長期力保留」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "After lock-off, anchor force can decrease through steel relaxation, rock movement and seating, with each loss needing a stated reference state. If a later percentage acts on the remaining force, multiply retention factors rather than casually adding percentages. This account does not establish anchorage capacity or the integrity of corrosion protection. Retained force describes current prestress rather than maximum capacity; capacity additionally needs evidence about steel section, anchor head and rock-bond resistance along the system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Long term anchor force retention” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: F0=3000 kN; r1=0.05 (dimensionless); r2=0.08 (dimensionless); F=F0*(1-r1)*(1-r2)=2622 kN.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
