       "objective": "從症狀倒推「錨索長期力保留」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Long term anchor force retention” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay. Corroded wire breaks can reduce redundancy without a large change in mean measured force, so one force history cannot demonstrate integrity of the complete anchoring system. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：保留力與可承受最大力不同，前者描述目前預應力，後者還需要鋼材截面、錨頭與岩體黏結能力等證據。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Retained force describes current prestress rather than maximum capacity; capacity additionally needs evidence about steel section, anchor head and rock-bond resistance along the system.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「所有錨索損失百分率都可不看基準直接相加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All anchor-loss percentages can be added without checking their reference states.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-16-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "接頭滑移可能造成突降而非平滑比例衰減，鏽蝕斷絲又可能在平均拉力變化不大時削弱冗餘；只追蹤一條力曲線不能證明錨固系統完整。",
         "textEn": "Connection slip can cause a sudden drop rather than smooth proportional decay. Corroded wire breaks can reduce redundancy without a large change in mean measured force, so one force history cannot demonstrate integrity of the complete anchoring system.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-jinping-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-16-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-jinping-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
