       "objective": "說明「挑流水舌射程」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Ski jump jet travel” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "挑流水舌離開鼻坎後同時具有水平及垂直速度，重力使其軌跡彎曲。教材使用水平射出的拋體模型估算射程，只用來檢查尺度及方向；真實水舌會含氣、破碎並受尾水與風影響，不能以理想落點直接決定沖刷坑位置或岩體穩定。 水平射出時下落時間由高差決定，但若鼻坎提供向上速度，需解完整垂向方程，不能沿用相同飛行時間。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「挑流水舌射程」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A ski-jump jet has horizontal and vertical velocity components and follows a gravity-curved trajectory. A horizontally launched projectile estimates travel scale and direction only. Real jets aerate, break up and interact with wind and tailwater, so an ideal impact point does not directly locate scour or establish rock stability. For horizontal launch, drop determines flight time; an upward launch component requires the full vertical equation and cannot retain the same time of flight. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ski jump jet travel” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: vx=25 m/s; drop=120 m; g=9.81 m/s2; x=vx*(2*drop/g)**0.5=123.6548417 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「理想拋體落點就是實際沖刷坑中心」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The ideal projectile landing point is the actual center of the scour hole.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「挑流水舌射程」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ski jump jet travel”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
