       "objective": "說明「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Jet impact pressure scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水舌速度在撞擊區轉成壓力與湍流，動壓提供一個能量密度尺度，但瞬時壓力分布取決於水舌破碎、尾水深度和岩面形狀。動壓不是整片底床均勻承受的壓力，亦不能直接乘任意面積得到設計合力。需同時掌握受力面積與時間統計。 動壓的帕斯卡與每立方米焦耳量綱相同，代表能量密度而非總能量，乘體積或面積後才得到不同物理量。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Jet velocity is converted into pressure and turbulence at impact. Dynamic pressure supplies an energy-density scale, while instantaneous distribution depends on breakup, tailwater depth and bed geometry. It is not uniform over the whole bed and cannot be multiplied by an arbitrary area to obtain a design resultant without spatial and temporal evidence. Pascals share dimensions with joules per cubic metre, expressing energy density rather than total energy; multiplying by volume or area produces different physical quantities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet impact pressure scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; v=35 m/s; q=0.5*rho*v*v/1000=612.5 kPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「所有測點最大壓力可直接同時相加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Maximum pressures from all sensors can always be added as simultaneous loads.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水舌衝擊壓力尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet impact pressure scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
