      {
       "id": "b207-v15-29",
       "title": "分層交換位能：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Stratified exchange potential energy: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-jinping-owner",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b207-v15-28"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「分層交換位能」如何影響錦屏一級水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Stratified exchange potential energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Jinping-I Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。教材以兩等體積水團交換高程的位能差說明密度影響，不把此值當成實際混合所需總功。湍流耗散、界面厚度及連續剖面會改變能量路徑，取水溫度控制仍需觀察真正吸入水層。 兩水團交換時各自有位能變化，將兩者相加才留下密度差項，不能把完整水密度直接代入浮力差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分層交換位能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Exchanging upper and lower reservoir layers works against buoyancy associated with density contrast. The potential-energy change for equal exchanged volumes illustrates that effect but is not the total work required for actual mixing. Turbulent dissipation, interface thickness and continuous density profiles alter the energy pathway and withdrawal behavior. Both exchanged parcels change potential energy; adding their contributions leaves the density-contrast term, rather than permitting full water density to represent the buoyancy difference. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Stratified exchange potential energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: drho=2 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; V=1000000 m3; dz=20 m; dE=drho*g*V*dz/1e6=392.4 MJ.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「分層交換位能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Stratified exchange potential energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "分層交換位能",
         "titleEn": "Stratified exchange potential energy",
         "text": "分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。教材以兩等體積水團交換高程的位能差說明密度影響，不把此值當成實際混合所需總功。",
         "textEn": "Exchanging upper and lower reservoir layers works against buoyancy associated with density contrast. The potential-energy change for equal exchanged volumes illustrates that effect but is not the total work required for actual mixing.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-jinping-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-29-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: A changed outlet temperature proves that stratification has disappeared throughout the reservoir. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-jinping-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "關於「分層交換位能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？",
        "questionEn": "Which statement about \"Stratified exchange potential energy\" is correct?",
        "options": [
         "出口溫度改變就證明全庫分層消失",
         "相同庫容在任何水頭下都代表相同電能",
         "分層水庫上下層交換需要克服密度差產生的浮力恢復作用。"
