       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「相關監測聯合殘差」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Correlated monitoring residuals” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization. A drifting shared reference can also create high correlation between instruments without providing evidence of consistent structural behavior across the monitored locations. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：相關係數接近一時矩陣可能病態，小量測差異會被大幅放大，應檢查基線品質與數值穩定性再解讀。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: A correlation near one makes the covariance matrix ill-conditioned and can amplify small differences; assess baseline quality and numerical stability before interpreting the joint distance.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「兩個相關感測器就是兩份獨立異常證據」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two correlated sensors provide two independent confirmations of an anomaly.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-40-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。",
         "textEn": "Long-term movement within the baseline inflates variance and correlation, shrinking new anomalies after standardization. A drifting shared reference can also create high correlation between instruments without providing evidence of consistent structural behavior across the monitored locations.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-jinping-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b207-v15-40-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-jinping-owner",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「相關監測聯合殘差」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Correlated monitoring residuals\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。",
         "基線中混入長期變形會放大變異與相關，讓真正新異常被標準化後縮小；兩感測器共用漂移基準也可能製造高度相關，並非結構反應一致的證據。",
         "壩頂海拔可直接代替壓力積分水深"
