       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Low heat cement adiabatic rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Baihetan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "低熱水泥減少或延緩水化放熱，但大體積混凝土仍可能累積顯著溫升。教材以膠結料用量乘單位放熱量，再除混凝土體積熱容量估算絕熱上升尺度。放熱隨齡期改變，骨材與摻料也影響熱容量，因此材料名稱本身不能替代實測溫升曲線。 單位膠結料放熱量必須附齡期，早期與最終放熱不能混用，否則低熱材料延遲放熱的特徵會被抹平。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低熱水泥絕熱溫升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Low-heat cement reduces or delays hydration heat, but mass concrete can still accumulate a substantial temperature rise. Binder content times specific heat release divided by concrete volumetric heat capacity estimates an adiabatic scale. Age-dependent hydration, aggregates and supplementary materials alter the response, so a material name cannot replace a measured temperature-rise curve. Specific binder heat release requires an age; mixing early and final heat values erases the delayed-release behavior that matters when comparing low-heat materials. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low heat cement adiabatic rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
