       "objective": "從症狀倒推「低熱水泥絕熱溫升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Low heat cement adiabatic rise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "低熱不等於無熱，若忽略保溫邊界仍可能低估核心溫升；過快表面降溫又可能提高梯度，所以降低總熱量不能單獨保證沒有溫度裂縫。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Low heat is not zero heat, and an insulating boundary can still permit a high core temperature. Rapid surface cooling can increase gradients, so a reduced total heat release alone cannot guarantee the absence of thermal cracking. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：單位膠結料放熱量必須附齡期，早期與最終放熱不能混用，否則低熱材料延遲放熱的特徵會被抹平。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Specific binder heat release requires an age; mixing early and final heat values erases the delayed-release behavior that matters when comparing low-heat materials.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「使用低熱水泥就不需要量測核心溫度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Using low-heat cement eliminates the need to measure core temperature.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b208-v15-08-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "低熱不等於無熱，若忽略保溫邊界仍可能低估核心溫升；過快表面降溫又可能提高梯度，所以降低總熱量不能單獨保證沒有溫度裂縫。",
         "textEn": "Low heat is not zero heat, and an insulating boundary can still permit a high core temperature. Rapid surface cooling can increase gradients, so a reduced total heat release alone cannot guarantee the absence of thermal cracking.",
