       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Ventilation cooling volume flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Baihetan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "以空氣帶走發電機熱量時，體積流量須先乘密度轉成質量流率，再乘比熱與溫升。海拔、溫度和壓力會改變密度，因此相同風量不一定帶走相同熱量。教材求理想需求流量後，還要檢查風路分配、壓降與局部熱點，不能只看風機銘牌。 空氣密度應對應量測斷面的壓力與溫度，標準風量和實際風量需要換算後才能放進同一熱量帳。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通風散熱體積流」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Air cooling requires converting volume flow to mass flow with density before applying heat capacity and temperature rise. Altitude, temperature and pressure change density, so equal volume flow may remove different heat. After estimating ideal demand, examine distribution, pressure drop and hotspots rather than relying on a fan nameplate alone. Air density must match pressure and temperature at the measurement section; standard and actual volume flows require conversion before they belong in one thermal account. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ventilation cooling volume flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
