       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “High frequency signal aliasing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：ftrue=360 Hz; fs=500 Hz; falias=abs(ftrue-fs)=140 Hz。模型邊界：此頻率位於第一個折返區間且無有效防混疊濾波，非一般多區間公式。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: ftrue=360 Hz; fs=500 Hz; falias=abs(ftrue-fs)=140 Hz. Model boundary: this signal lies in the first folding interval without effective anti-alias filtering; not a general multi-band formula. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：查原始取樣率、類比濾波截止及感測器頻寬，再以較高取樣率重測同一工況。",
