       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Aeration volume fraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Baihetan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "洩洪摻氣使水氣混合流的密度與可壓縮性改變，空氣體積流量必須附壓力和溫度條件。以同一位置的氣水體積流量求表觀體積分率，可作供氣尺度帳，但氣液滑移會讓局部空隙率不同。不能把入口空氣比例直接當成底板表面的保護效果。 氣液滑移意味兩相停留時間不同，流量比例與瞬時體積占比因此可能不同，應先定義所需含氣指標。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「摻氣體積分率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Aeration changes mixture density and compressibility, and air volume flow needs a pressure-temperature reference. Gas and liquid volume rates at one location give a superficial fraction for supply accounting, while phase slip can produce a different local void fraction. Inlet air proportion does not directly establish protective conditions at the floor. Phase slip gives gas and liquid different residence times, so flow-rate fraction can differ from instantaneous occupied-volume fraction; define the required aeration measure first. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Aeration volume fraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：Qa=90 m3/s; Qw=510 m3/s; beta=Qa/(Qa+Qw)=0.15。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: Qa=90 m3/s; Qw=510 m3/s; beta=Qa/(Qa+Qw)=0.15.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「入口空氣分率就是底板局部空隙率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The inlet air-flow fraction equals the local void fraction at the floor.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「摻氣體積分率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Aeration volume fraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
