       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Hydraulic model scaling law” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Baihetan Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "重力主導的自由水面模型常以福祿相似配對流速與長度，流量尺度因此是長度比的二分之五次方，而非線性放大。模型能呈現某些水面與慣性作用，卻未必同時保持雷諾數、表面張力及汽蝕相似。每項結論應對應其被保留的物理機制。 福祿尺度下時間比為長度比平方根，影像播放速度若未換算，會錯判原型水舌波動與閘門變動的時序。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水工模型尺度律」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Gravity-dominated free-surface models often preserve Froude similarity, linking velocity and length and giving discharge a length-ratio exponent of five halves. Such a model can represent selected surface and inertial behavior without simultaneously preserving Reynolds, surface-tension or cavitation similarity. Every interpretation should identify the physical mechanism actually preserved. Under Froude scaling, time ratio is the square root of length ratio; unconverted video speed can misrepresent prototype jet fluctuations and gate-motion timing. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydraulic model scaling law” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：lambdaL=40 (dimensionless); Qm=0.12 m3/s; Qp=Qm*lambdaL**2.5=1214.3146215 m3/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: lambdaL=40 (dimensionless); Qm=0.12 m3/s; Qp=Qm*lambdaL**2.5=1214.3146215 m3/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「福祿相似會自動保證所有水力現象相似」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Froude similarity automatically preserves every hydraulic phenomenon.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水工模型尺度律」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydraulic model scaling law”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
