         "textEn": "Gravity-dominated free-surface models often preserve Froude similarity, linking velocity and length and giving discharge a length-ratio exponent of five halves. Such a model can represent selected surface and inertial behavior without simultaneously preserving Reynolds, surface-tension or cavitation similarity.",
