       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「水工模型尺度律」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hydraulic model scaling law” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "先核對幾何縮尺與所有測具位置，再用速度、水深及流量三種尺度互相驗算。比較不同模型尺寸的含氣與表面現象，若結果隨尺寸改變，應辨認尺度效應，不把較細緻照片當作更準確的原型預測。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Verify geometric scale and sensor positions, then cross-check velocity, depth and discharge scaling. Compare aeration and surface behavior in different model sizes. Size-dependent results require identifying scale effects rather than treating more detailed photographs as inherently more accurate prototype predictions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：用兩種長度縮尺計算相同原型流量所需模型流量，並列出速度與時間尺度，說明如何選尺寸兼顧供水能力及重要尺度效應。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: For two length scales, calculate model flows representing one prototype flow and list velocity and time scales. Explain how model size balances laboratory supply capability against important scale effects.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：小模型表面張力及黏性可能相對放大，含氣與小尺度破碎不再保持相似；直接把模型汽穴或侵蝕量按幾何比例放大，會超出福祿相似能支持的結論。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Surface tension and viscosity can be relatively stronger in a small model, preventing similarity of aeration and fine breakup. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
