       "objective": "說明「視在容量與無功」如何影響溪洛渡水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Apparent capacity and reactive power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiluodu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "溪洛渡供應商資料中的兆伏安額定值提醒學員，發電機電流容量同時支援實功與無功。功率三角形以平方和關聯三者，不能把視在功率減實功當無功。教材只在平衡正弦穩態下求尺度，實際勵磁、定子電流及端部發熱限制需要能力曲線。 功率三角形的無功大小仍需配合符號慣例，供應與吸收可有相同幅值，卻對電壓控制造成不同作用。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「視在容量與無功」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The supplier MVA rating illustrates that generator current capacity supports both active and reactive power. Their power triangle uses a sum of squares; reactive power is not apparent power minus active power. The calculation applies to balanced sinusoidal steady state, while excitation, stator current and end-region heating require an actual capability curve. Reactive magnitude from the triangle still needs a sign convention; supply and absorption can share magnitude while having different consequences for voltage control at the connection. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Apparent capacity and reactive power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：S=800 MVA; P=640 MW; Qreactive=(S*S-P*P)**0.5=480 Mvar。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: S=800 MVA; P=640 MW; Qreactive=(S*S-P*P)**0.5=480 Mvar.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「無功等於視在功率直接減去實功」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Reactive power equals apparent power minus active power.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「視在容量與無功」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Apparent capacity and reactive power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
