       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「視在容量與無功」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Apparent capacity and reactive power” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "核對功率表的無功正負定義與三相電流，再把實功無功工作點放到設備能力圖上。若低實功時電流仍高，應檢查無功輸出與諧波，而不能只憑發電兆瓦較低判斷設備熱負擔較低。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Check the meter reactive-sign convention and phase currents, then place active-reactive operating points on the machine capability diagram. High current at low active power calls for checking reactive output and harmonics rather than assuming that lower generated megawatts imply lower thermal loading. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：固定視在容量並增加實功，計算剩餘無功尺度，畫出兩個工作點，再說明為何真正可用無功仍可能受勵磁或冷卻限制。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Increase active power at fixed apparent capacity and calculate the remaining reactive scale. Plot both operating points and explain why actual reactive capability may still be constrained by excitation or cooling.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：以視在減實功估算無功會破壞向量關係，造成錯誤容量判斷；若系統含顯著諧波，簡單三角形本身也可能不足，需明確區分基波及總功率定義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Subtracting active from apparent power violates the vector relationship and misstates capacity. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
