      {
       "id": "b209-v15-04",
       "title": "視在容量與無功：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Apparent capacity and reactive power: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b209-v15-03"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「視在容量與無功」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Apparent capacity and reactive power” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "以視在減實功估算無功會破壞向量關係，造成錯誤容量判斷；若系統含顯著諧波，簡單三角形本身也可能不足，需明確區分基波及總功率定義。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Subtracting active from apparent power violates the vector relationship and misstates capacity. Significant harmonics can also make the simple triangle inadequate, requiring explicit distinction between fundamental-frequency and total-power definitions before interpreting the result. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：功率三角形的無功大小仍需配合符號慣例，供應與吸收可有相同幅值，卻對電壓控制造成不同作用。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Reactive magnitude from the triangle still needs a sign convention; supply and absorption can share magnitude while having different consequences for voltage control at the connection.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「無功等於視在功率直接減去實功」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Reactive power equals apparent power minus active power.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "以視在減實功估算無功會破壞向量關係，造成錯誤容量判斷；若系統含顯著諧波，簡單三角形本身也可能不足，需明確區分基波及總功率定義。",
         "textEn": "Subtracting active from apparent power violates the vector relationship and misstates capacity. Significant harmonics can also make the simple triangle inadequate, requiring explicit distinction between fundamental-frequency and total-power definitions before interpreting the result.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-04-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「視在容量與無功」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Apparent capacity and reactive power\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。",
         "以視在減實功估算無功會破壞向量關係，造成錯誤容量判斷；若系統含顯著諧波，簡單三角形本身也可能不足，需明確區分基波及總功率定義。",
         "轉子全部動能都可在不改變轉速下輸出"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
