      {
       "id": "b209-v15-05",
       "title": "轉子旋轉儲能：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Rotor rotational stored energy: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b209-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「轉子旋轉儲能」如何影響溪洛渡水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rotor rotational stored energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiluodu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水輪發電機轉子儲存的旋轉動能可在短時間功率不平衡時交換，但不是可持續供電的水庫能量。轉動慣量乘角速度平方的一半給出動能，若轉速變化小，能量變化仍與初始速度有關。教材用整體等效慣量建立尺度，不推定實際機組慣量常數。 可釋放動能是兩個轉速狀態的能量差，若只用總動能估算支援時間，就等於假設轉子可停轉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉子旋轉儲能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rotor kinetic energy can exchange during brief power imbalance but is not sustained reservoir generation. Half the inertia times angular speed squared gives stored energy, with small energy changes still dependent on initial speed. An assumed equivalent inertia establishes scale without claiming the actual machine inertia constant or allowable speed excursion. Available kinetic release is the energy difference between two speeds; using total stored energy for support duration implicitly assumes that the rotor can stop completely. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rotor rotational stored energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：J=40000000 kg*m2; n=125 rpm; E=0.5*J*(2*pi*n/60)**2/1e9=3.426945973 GJ。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: J=40000000 kg*m2; n=125 rpm; E=0.5*J*(2*pi*n/60)**2/1e9=3.426945973 GJ.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「轉子全部動能都可在不改變轉速下輸出」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"All rotor kinetic energy can be delivered without changing rotational speed.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「轉子旋轉儲能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rotor rotational stored energy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "轉子旋轉儲能",
         "titleEn": "Rotor rotational stored energy",
         "text": "水輪發電機轉子儲存的旋轉動能可在短時間功率不平衡時交換，但不是可持續供電的水庫能量。轉動慣量乘角速度平方的一半給出動能，若轉速變化小，能量變化仍與初始速度有關。",
         "textEn": "Rotor kinetic energy can exchange during brief power imbalance but is not sustained reservoir generation. Half the inertia times angular speed squared gives stored energy, with small energy changes still dependent on initial speed.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-05-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：轉子全部動能都可在不改變轉速下輸出 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: All rotor kinetic energy can be delivered without changing rotational speed. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "關於「轉子旋轉儲能」，下列哪一項敘述正確？",
        "questionEn": "Which statement about \"Rotor rotational stored energy\" is correct?",
        "options": [
         "轉子全部動能都可在不改變轉速下輸出",
         "風機轉速增加一成只會增加一成耗能",
         "水輪發電機轉子儲存的旋轉動能可在短時間功率不平衡時交換，但不是可持續供電的水庫能量。"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
         "All rotor kinetic energy can be delivered without changing rotational speed.",
         "A ten-percent fan speed increase causes only a ten-percent power increase.",
