       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「轉子旋轉儲能」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rotor rotational stored energy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把轉子總動能全當成可用支援，會忽略允許轉速範圍；柔性軸系還可能把能量分配到扭振模態，使平均轉速不足以描述局部動態。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating all rotor kinetic energy as available support ignores the permitted speed range. A flexible shaft can also distribute energy into torsional modes, making mean rotational speed insufficient to describe local dynamics during an electrical or hydraulic disturbance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：可釋放動能是兩個轉速狀態的能量差，若只用總動能估算支援時間，就等於假設轉子可停轉。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Available kinetic release is the energy difference between two speeds; using total stored energy for support duration implicitly assumes that the rotor can stop completely.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「轉子全部動能都可在不改變轉速下輸出」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All rotor kinetic energy can be delivered without changing rotational speed.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-08-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把轉子總動能全當成可用支援，會忽略允許轉速範圍；柔性軸系還可能把能量分配到扭振模態，使平均轉速不足以描述局部動態。",
         "textEn": "Treating all rotor kinetic energy as available support ignores the permitted speed range. A flexible shaft can also distribute energy into torsional modes, making mean rotational speed insufficient to describe local dynamics during an electrical or hydraulic disturbance.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
