       "objective": "說明「風機轉速與耗能」如何影響溪洛渡水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Fan speed and power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiluodu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "發電機通風增加時，風機相似律可估算相同幾何及相似工況下的流量、壓升和軸功率變化。功率對轉速約呈三次方，因此小幅提速可能增加顯著輔機耗能。相似律需配合系統阻力曲線，風道變更、失速或密度改變都可能破壞簡化比例。 風機功率相似通常指軸端，變頻器與馬達損失要另列，才能與電端輔機耗電建立一致比較。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「風機轉速與耗能」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Fan affinity laws estimate changes in flow, pressure and shaft power for unchanged geometry and similar conditions. Power varies approximately with the cube of speed, so a modest increase can raise auxiliary demand substantially. System resistance must also be considered; duct changes, stall and density variation can invalidate the simplified ratio. Fan power similarity usually refers to shaft power; converter and motor losses need separate terms before comparison with electrical auxiliary demand is physically consistent. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fan speed and power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：P1=1 MW; ratioN=1.10 (dimensionless); P2=P1*ratioN**3=1.331 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: P1=1 MW; ratioN=1.10 (dimensionless); P2=P1*ratioN**3=1.331 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「風機轉速增加一成只會增加一成耗能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A ten-percent fan speed increase causes only a ten-percent power increase.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「風機轉速與耗能」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fan speed and power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
