      {
       "id": "b209-v15-15",
       "title": "定子銅損邊界：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Stator copper loss boundary: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b209-v15-14"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「定子銅損邊界」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Stator copper loss boundary” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "量測繞組電阻時記錄溫度並轉換到比較條件，核對相電流及接線方式，再將銅損估算與冷卻熱量比較。若總熱量高於銅損，應補列鐵損及其他熱源，而非把差額全歸於電阻量錯。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Record winding temperature during resistance measurement and convert to comparable conditions, checking phase current and connection. Compare copper-loss estimates with cooling heat. Heat greater than calculated copper loss requires other loss terms rather than assigning the entire difference to an incorrect resistance measurement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：固定電阻把電流提高兩成，重算銅損，再增加熱態電阻比例，分別比較兩項效應並列出現地熱量帳還缺少的損失來源。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Increase current by twenty percent at fixed resistance and recalculate copper loss. Then increase hot resistance, compare both effects separately and list the remaining loss sources required by a field heat account.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：用冷態電阻計算熱態損失會偏低，將線電流直接套到不相容接法也會造成比例錯誤；局部接頭高電阻可能集中發熱，平均每相值不能排除熱點。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Cold resistance understates hot-state loss, and using line current with an incompatible winding connection creates another ratio error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-15-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "量測繞組電阻時記錄溫度並轉換到比較條件，核對相電流及接線方式，再將銅損估算與冷卻熱量比較。若總熱量高於銅損，應補列鐵損及其他熱源，而非把差額全歸於電阻量錯。",
         "textEn": "Record winding temperature during resistance measurement and convert to comparable conditions, checking phase current and connection. Compare copper-loss estimates with cooling heat. Heat greater than calculated copper loss requires other loss terms rather than assigning the entire difference to an incorrect resistance measurement.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
