       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「裂隙開度與滲流」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Fracture aperture and flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "接觸點閉合與局部堵塞會使有效水力開度不同於量得的平均幾何開度；若溫度變化降低黏度，流量也會增加，不能把所有增流都認定為裂隙擴張。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Contact closure and local blockage make hydraulic aperture differ from mean geometric aperture. Warming can also lower viscosity and increase flow, so every rise in seepage cannot be assigned to fracture enlargement without temperature and pressure evidence. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：流路長度與開度可能互相補償產生相同流量，反算參數具有非唯一性，需要獨立幾何或示蹤資料縮小範圍。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Path length and aperture can compensate to produce the same flow, making inverse estimates nonunique; independent geometry or tracer evidence is needed to constrain them.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「滲流量增加就唯一證明裂隙開度增加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An increase in seepage uniquely proves an increase in fracture aperture.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-28-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "接觸點閉合與局部堵塞會使有效水力開度不同於量得的平均幾何開度；若溫度變化降低黏度，流量也會增加，不能把所有增流都認定為裂隙擴張。",
         "textEn": "Contact closure and local blockage make hydraulic aperture differ from mean geometric aperture. Warming can also lower viscosity and increase flow, so every rise in seepage cannot be assigned to fracture enlargement without temperature and pressure evidence.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-28-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「裂隙開度與滲流」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Fracture aperture and flow\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。",
         "接觸點閉合與局部堵塞會使有效水力開度不同於量得的平均幾何開度；若溫度變化降低黏度，流量也會增加，不能把所有增流都認定為裂隙擴張。",
