       ],
       "objective": "說明「通風局部阻力」如何影響溪洛渡水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Ventilation local resistance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiluodu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "地下廠房及廊道通風包含彎頭、格柵和分支等局部阻力，壓損與動壓及阻力係數相關。教材以一個已知係數估算局部壓損，提醒學員係數的參考速度必須明確。這只是正常通風能量帳，不代表火災煙控、逃生條件或所有分支風量均已驗證。 阻力係數使用的參考速度可能位於不同斷面，串接多構件時應換成一致能量帳，不能直接加不相容的係數。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「通風局部阻力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Underground powerhouse ventilation includes local losses at bends, screens and branches, related to dynamic pressure and a loss coefficient. One assumed coefficient estimates local pressure loss, with its reference velocity explicitly stated. This normal-ventilation account does not verify smoke control, escape conditions or flow distribution through every branch of the network. Loss coefficients may use velocities at different sections; connecting several fittings requires a consistent energy account rather than directly adding coefficients with incompatible reference velocities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Ventilation local resistance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：K=2.5 (dimensionless); rho=1.2 kg/m3; v=12 m/s; dp=K*0.5*rho*v*v=216 Pa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: K=2.5 (dimensionless); rho=1.2 kg/m3; v=12 m/s; dp=K*0.5*rho*v*v=216 Pa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「單一構件壓損就是整座風機所需壓升」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The loss across one fitting equals the pressure rise required for the whole fan system.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「通風局部阻力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Ventilation local resistance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "通風局部阻力",
         "titleEn": "Ventilation local resistance",
         "text": "地下廠房及廊道通風包含彎頭、格柵和分支等局部阻力，壓損與動壓及阻力係數相關。教材以一個已知係數估算局部壓損，提醒學員係數的參考速度必須明確。",
         "textEn": "Underground powerhouse ventilation includes local losses at bends, screens and branches, related to dynamic pressure and a loss coefficient. One assumed coefficient estimates local pressure loss, with its reference velocity explicitly stated.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-29-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：單一構件壓損就是整座風機所需壓升 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: The loss across one fitting equals the pressure rise required for the whole fan system. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
