       ],
       "objective": "說明「梯級重複用水發電」如何影響溪洛渡水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Cascade reuse of release water” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Xiluodu Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "同一水量通過上下游兩座電站，可利用兩段不同的落差，並非創造新的水量或把同一位能重複計算。教材以同一流量乘各段淨水頭效率相加求總功率，先確認兩段高程落差不重疊。實際河道傳播、支流與水庫儲存會使兩站瞬時流量不同。 上下游兩段效率各自作用於各段位能，不應把效率連乘套在總落差，因第一段損失不會消滅下游全部落差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「梯級重複用水發電」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The same water can generate through two successive drops without creating water or counting one potential-energy drop twice. Sum each net-head and efficiency contribution at a common assumed discharge, confirming that the elevation intervals do not overlap. Routing, tributaries and storage can make actual instantaneous discharges differ between plants. Each efficiency acts on its own potential-energy drop; multiplying efficiencies over total head misrepresents the stages, because losses upstream do not eliminate the downstream drop. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cascade reuse of release water” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創假想算例，輸入均非本工程操作參數：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=500 m3/s; H1=90 m; eta1=0.91 (dimensionless); H2=70 m; eta2=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(H1*eta1+H2*eta2)/1e6=710.7345 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical example; inputs are not operating parameters of this project: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=500 m3/s; H1=90 m; eta1=0.91 (dimensionless); H2=70 m; eta2=0.90 (dimensionless); P=rho*g*Q*(H1*eta1+H2*eta2)/1e6=710.7345 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「同一水量二次發電就是重複創造水的位能」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Generating twice with the same water creates the same potential energy twice.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「梯級重複用水發電」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cascade reuse of release water”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "梯級重複用水發電",
         "titleEn": "Cascade reuse of release water",
         "text": "同一水量通過上下游兩座電站，可利用兩段不同的落差，並非創造新的水量或把同一位能重複計算。教材以同一流量乘各段淨水頭效率相加求總功率，先確認兩段高程落差不重疊。",
         "textEn": "The same water can generate through two successive drops without creating water or counting one potential-energy drop twice. Sum each net-head and efficiency contribution at a common assumed discharge, confirming that the elevation intervals do not overlap.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-33-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：同一水量二次發電就是重複創造水的位能 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Generating twice with the same water creates the same potential energy twice. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
