      {
       "id": "b209-v15-36",
       "title": "梯級重複用水發電：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Cascade reuse of release water: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-instruments"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b209-v15-35"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「梯級重複用水發電」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Cascade reuse of release water” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "將上游總落差再次列入下游水頭會重複計算位能，忽略流量延遲又會使逐時能量帳不閉合；兩者可能在月平均下被掩蓋，需保留分段基準。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Including the upstream drop again in downstream head double-counts potential energy. Ignoring travel delay also disrupts hourly energy closure. Monthly averages can conceal both errors, so elevation references and interval boundaries must be retained for each stage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：上下游兩段效率各自作用於各段位能，不應把效率連乘套在總落差，因第一段損失不會消滅下游全部落差。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Each efficiency acts on its own potential-energy drop; multiplying efficiencies over total head misrepresents the stages, because losses upstream do not eliminate the downstream drop.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「同一水量二次發電就是重複創造水的位能」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Generating twice with the same water creates the same potential energy twice.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-36-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "將上游總落差再次列入下游水頭會重複計算位能，忽略流量延遲又會使逐時能量帳不閉合；兩者可能在月平均下被掩蓋，需保留分段基準。",
         "textEn": "Including the upstream drop again in downstream head double-counts potential energy. Ignoring travel delay also disrupts hourly energy closure. Monthly averages can conceal both errors, so elevation references and interval boundaries must be retained for each stage.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-36-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「梯級重複用水發電」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Cascade reuse of release water\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "將上游總落差再次列入下游水頭會重複計算位能，忽略流量延遲又會使逐時能量帳不閉合；兩者可能在月平均下被掩蓋，需保留分段基準。",
         "裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。",
