       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「增流邊際功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Marginal power from added flow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "忽略損失導數會高估增流收益，效率若在高流量區下降則偏差更大；把局部最大功率當成允許運轉點，也可能越過汽蝕、振動或電氣限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Ignoring the derivative of head loss overstates added-flow benefit, especially if efficiency falls at higher discharge. A mathematical power maximum may also lie beyond cavitation, vibration or electrical limits and does not establish an authorized operating point. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：損失項隨流量平方增加，功率中的該項則隨流量三次方，因此微分後會出現三倍係數，不能漏算。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Head loss grows with flow squared, but its contribution within power grows with flow cubed; differentiation therefore introduces a factor of three that must be retained.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「平均功率除流量必定等於增流邊際功率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Average power divided by flow always equals marginal power from added flow.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-40-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "忽略損失導數會高估增流收益，效率若在高流量區下降則偏差更大；把局部最大功率當成允許運轉點，也可能越過汽蝕、振動或電氣限制。",
         "textEn": "Ignoring the derivative of head loss overstates added-flow benefit, especially if efficiency falls at higher discharge. A mathematical power maximum may also lie beyond cavitation, vibration or electrical limits and does not establish an authorized operating point.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b209-v15-40-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-xiluodu-voith",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-instruments"
         ]
        }
