    {
     "id": "b210-v15-s1",
     "title": "水文條件、邊界與工程系統",
     "titleEn": "Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「跨季庫容水量帳」與「大湖蒸發與面積」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Seasonal reservoir water balance\" and \"Lake evaporation and surface area\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b210-v15-01",
       "title": "跨季庫容水量帳：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Seasonal reservoir water balance: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-mwri-aswan",
        "v15s-wapda-tarbela",
        "v15s-usbr-filters"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「跨季庫容水量帳」如何影響阿斯旺高壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Seasonal reservoir water balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aswan High Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "阿斯旺案例凸顯長期蓄水必須追蹤入流、放流與損失，單一洪峰並不能描述跨季可靠度。用共同時間窗更新庫存可檢查調節邏輯，但不能忽略水位面積與可用庫容限制；每個水量來源應保留獨立觀測與不確定度。 驗證時應以庫水位容量曲線交叉核對同期流量積分的庫存變化，並辨識以下失效情境：把所有水量殘差當蒸發會掩蓋量測或漏列放流。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨季庫容水量帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Aswan provides context for long-term storage accounting beyond a single flood peak. Update storage from inflow, release and losses over a common window. This bookkeeping does not remove stage-area or usable-storage limits, and each component needs independent observations and uncertainty rather than one balancing adjustment. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Cross-check integrated flows against storage change from the stage-capacity curve. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Assigning every residual to evaporation conceals measurement errors or omitted releases. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Seasonal reservoir water balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：InitialStorage=8 km3; seasonalInflow=5 km3; releases=4 km3; netLoss=0.6 km3; finalStorage=8+5-4-0.6=8.4 km3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: InitialStorage=8 km3; seasonalInflow=5 km3; releases=4 km3; netLoss=0.6 km3; finalStorage=8+5-4-0.6=8.4 km3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只知道洪峰流量就能判定跨季供水可靠度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Peak flood discharge alone determines seasonal supply reliability\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「跨季庫容水量帳」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Seasonal reservoir water balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
