       "objective": "說明「大湖蒸發與面積」如何影響阿斯旺高壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Lake evaporation and surface area” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aswan High Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "乾燥地區的大湖蒸發涉及水面面積與能量交換，蒸發深度不能直接當成水庫降深。湖面積隨水位變動，風場與氣象站代表性也會影響估算；固定面積算例只能說明單位換算，長期水量帳需用一致時間解析度積分。 驗證時應比較湖面氣象與蒸發估法並依逐月水位更新面積，並辨識以下失效情境：直接以單一岸站蒸發量代表全湖可能形成系統偏差。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「大湖蒸發與面積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Large-lake evaporation in an arid setting depends on surface area and energy exchange. Evaporation depth is not automatically reservoir stage decline. Area changes with level and station representativeness matters; a fixed-area calculation illustrates conversion while long-term budgets need consistent temporal integration. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare lake meteorology and evaporation methods and update area from monthly stage. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using one shore station for the entire lake can create systematic bias. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lake evaporation and surface area” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalArea=500 km2; evaporationDepth=1.8 m/year; lossVolume=500e6*1.8/1e9=0.90 km3/year。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalArea=500 km2; evaporationDepth=1.8 m/year; lossVolume=500e6*1.8/1e9=0.90 km3/year.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「蒸發一公尺就表示水庫水位必定下降一公尺」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"One metre of evaporation necessarily lowers reservoir level by one metre\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「大湖蒸發與面積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lake evaporation and surface area”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b210-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "大湖蒸發與面積",
         "titleEn": "Lake evaporation and surface area",
         "text": "乾燥地區的大湖蒸發涉及水面面積與能量交換，蒸發深度不能直接當成水庫降深。湖面積隨水位變動，風場與氣象站代表性也會影響估算；固定面積算例只能說明單位換算，長期水量帳需用一致時間解析度積分。",
         "textEn": "Large-lake evaporation in an arid setting depends on surface area and energy exchange. Evaporation depth is not automatically reservoir stage decline.",
