       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Core seepage resistance in series” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aswan High Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型土石壩的不同土區可形成串聯與並聯流路，不能將各層滲透係數直接算術平均。等面積一維串聯模型以厚度除導水率形成阻力，可顯示低滲層控制作用；裂縫或接觸繞流則可能讓此理想串聯失效。 驗證時應以分層孔壓分配核對主要水頭損失是否位於低滲區，並辨識以下失效情境：沿接觸面繞流可避開原本控制流量的低滲核心。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「防滲核心串聯阻力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Different embankment zones create series and parallel paths, so arithmetic averaging of conductivity is generally inappropriate. Equal-area one-dimensional series resistance illustrates control by a low-permeability layer. Cracks and contact bypasses may defeat that idealization and must be checked independently of laboratory conductivity. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use layered piezometric heads to locate the dominant head loss. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Contact bypass can avoid the low-permeability core that controls the ideal model. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Core seepage resistance in series” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
