       "instructionEn": "Trapped sediment changes storage and delta geometry. Converting dry mass to deposit volume requires compaction and grain-size zoning. Equal mass occupies different bulk volume at different dry densities; repeat bathymetry and layered samples rather than treating grain volume as total deposited volume. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Cross-check bathymetric change and layered dry density against sediment mass. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring consolidation confuses storage change with an equal change in sediment mass. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment storage and dry density” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
