       "objective": "說明「放流輸配與需水」如何影響阿斯旺高壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Release conveyance and demand” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aswan High Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水庫放流經輸配系統到達用水端，取水量與有效供水之間有蒸散、滲漏與回歸水等差異。簡化效率只定義特定邊界的比值，不能把所有損失都視為流域消耗；應先界定取用點與回歸路徑，再計算放流需求。 驗證時應核對水庫出口用水端與回歸水的同時水量帳，並辨識以下失效情境：把回歸水全當消耗會高估流域淨需水。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「放流輸配與需水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Released water passes through a conveyance system before reaching demand. A simplified efficiency belongs to a defined boundary and does not classify every loss as basin consumption; seepage or drainage may return elsewhere. Define delivery points and return paths before converting a service demand into release volume. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Reconcile simultaneous volumes at release, delivery and return-flow boundaries. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Treating all return water as consumption overstates basin net demand. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Release conveyance and demand” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：TargetDeliveredVolume=60 million m3; definedConveyanceEfficiency=0.75; requiredRelease=60/0.75=80 million m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: TargetDeliveredVolume=60 million m3; definedConveyanceEfficiency=0.75; requiredRelease=60/0.75=80 million m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「所有輸配損失都等於流域永久耗水」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every conveyance loss equals permanent basin water consumption\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
