       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Drought sequence and reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aswan High Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "長期蓄水需要面對連續低入流，而非只看平均年供需。以累積短缺估算備援容量可展示序列效應，但假設需求、損失和初始庫容均已界定；實際可靠度還需多種水文序列、操作限制與不確定度分析。 驗證時應比較不同乾旱排列下的最低庫容並保留需求假設，並辨識以下失效情境：只用平均入流會忽略連年不足的累積效應。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「枯水連續與備援」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Carryover storage responds to sequences of low inflow, not just average annual balance. Cumulative deficits illustrate reserve demand for defined demand, losses and initial storage. Reliability still requires multiple hydrological sequences, operating constraints and uncertainty rather than treating one synthetic drought as universal. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare minimum storage under different drought sequences and retain demand assumptions. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Mean inflow alone hides cumulative deficits over consecutive dry years. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drought sequence and reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Three annual deficits=0.4,0.7,0.3 km3; no intervening refill; cumulativeReserveDemand=0.4+0.7+0.3=1.4 km3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Three annual deficits=0.4,0.7,0.3 km3; no intervening refill; cumulativeReserveDemand=0.4+0.7+0.3=1.4 km3.",
