       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Monitoring baseline and anomaly” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Aswan High Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型壩監測應將庫水位與季節溫度造成的可逆反應和持續變化分開。基線殘差能提示不同於歷史關係的訊號，但資料漂移與工況外插也可能造成異常；應用獨立儀器與現場檢查確認，不以重新擬合消除警訊。 驗證時應比較鄰近獨立儀器與人工測量並核對基線適用水位範圍，並辨識以下失效情境：超出歷史水位範圍的外插可能被誤當結構劣化。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「監測基線與異常」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Monitoring separates reversible stage and seasonal effects from persistent change. A baseline residual flags departures from historical relations, but sensor drift and extrapolation also create anomalies. Confirm using independent measurements and inspection rather than erasing a new signal by refitting the baseline to it. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare independent instruments and manual surveys and check the baseline stage range. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Extrapolation beyond historical stages can be mistaken for structural deterioration. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Monitoring baseline and anomaly” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
