       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Layered conductivity and anisotropy” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把水平平均導水率用於垂直流會扭曲滲流分布。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較不同方向的試驗與孔壓反應並繪製連續高滲層，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Using horizontal averaged conductivity for vertical flow distorts the seepage field. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare directional tests and pressure response and map connected high-permeability layers. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
