       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Exit gradient and submerged weight” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "向上滲流可能減少顆粒骨架有效重量，出口梯度需與土的水下重量和拘束比較。臨界梯度簡式用於均勻無黏性土的浮起尺度，不是所有內部沖蝕的起始門檻；局部集中流與反濾失效可能在其他條件下發生。 驗證時應以出口附近密集孔壓量測核對局部梯度並觀察顆粒流失，並辨識以下失效情境：用平均全壩梯度代替局部出口梯度會漏掉集中作用。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出口梯度與有效重量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Upward seepage reduces effective skeleton weight. A critical-gradient expression describes heave of uniform cohesionless soil, not the threshold for every internal-erosion mechanism. Concentrated flow and failed retention can develop under other conditions, so check local gradients and filter function separately. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure local exit gradients with closely spaced piezometers and observe particle loss. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An average whole-dam gradient can conceal concentrated exit effects. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Exit gradient and submerged weight” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：grainSpecificGravity=2.65; voidRatio=0.65; idealHeaveGradient=(2.65-1)/(1+0.65)=1.00 dimensionless。",
