      {
       "id": "b211-v15-29",
       "title": "既有隧道擴建損失：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Existing tunnel conversion losses: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-wapda-tarbela",
        "v15s-worldbank-tarbela",
        "v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit",
        "v15s-usbr-monitoring"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b211-v15-28"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「既有隧道擴建損失」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Existing tunnel conversion losses” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "把既有放水隧道接入新增機組時，流量與壓力邊界改變會影響摩阻和暫態，不能只查隧道直徑是否足夠。局部損失係數乘速度水頭可盤點轉接件作用，還需核對接頭、分岔與下游調節對整體系統的影響。 驗證時應比較改接前後能量線與接頭壓力並核對實際構形，並辨識以下失效情境：新增轉接損失會降低機組可用淨水頭。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「既有隧道擴建損失」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Connecting new generation to an existing release tunnel changes flow and pressure boundaries, affecting friction and transients. Diameter alone is insufficient. A local-loss calculation accounts for one transition, while joints, branching and downstream regulation require a system assessment under the converted operating conditions. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare energy lines and joint pressures before and after connection and verify geometry. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Added connection losses reduce net head available to the generating unit. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Existing tunnel conversion losses” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: AssumedTransitionK=0.35; meanV=9 m/s; localHeadLoss=0.35*9**2/(2*9.81)=1.44495 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Adequate existing diameter removes the need to check conversion head losses\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「既有隧道擴建損失」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Existing tunnel conversion losses”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b211-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "既有隧道擴建損失",
         "titleEn": "Existing tunnel conversion losses",
         "text": "把既有放水隧道接入新增機組時，流量與壓力邊界改變會影響摩阻和暫態，不能只查隧道直徑是否足夠。局部損失係數乘速度水頭可盤點轉接件作用，還需核對接頭、分岔與下游調節對整體系統的影響。",
         "textEn": "Connecting new generation to an existing release tunnel changes flow and pressure boundaries, affecting friction and transients. Diameter alone is insufficient.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-wapda-tarbela",
          "v15s-worldbank-tarbela",
          "v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit",
          "v15s-usbr-monitoring"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b211-v15-29-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：原有隧道直徑足夠就不必檢查改接水頭損失 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
