       "objective": "說明「發電用水與放流協調」如何影響塔貝拉水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Generation flow and release coordination” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "新增發電功能可能利用原有放流水量，但發電時段與灌溉或下游需求的時間尺度不同。能量算例需清楚定義有效出力與時數，不能把裝置容量全年相乘當保證發電；水量與尾水限制需在共同調度邊界核對。 驗證時應以機組電量表與同期放流水量核對發電時窗，並辨識以下失效情境：把停機或缺水時段也當滿載會高估年度電量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「發電用水與放流協調」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "New generation may use existing releases, but its timing can differ from irrigation or downstream needs. Energy requires defined output and duration; nameplate power times a full year is not guaranteed generation. Reconcile water and tailwater constraints within a common scheduling boundary. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare metered energy with release volumes over the same generating window. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Counting outages or water-limited periods as full output overstates annual energy. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Generation flow and release coordination” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: HypotheticalDeliveredPower=450 MW; actualGeneratingDuration=6 h; energy=450*6=2700 MWh.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「裝置容量乘全年時數就是保證可售電量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Nameplate capacity times annual hours equals guaranteed saleable energy\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「發電用水與放流協調」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Generation flow and release coordination”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b211-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "發電用水與放流協調",
         "titleEn": "Generation flow and release coordination",
         "text": "新增發電功能可能利用原有放流水量，但發電時段與灌溉或下游需求的時間尺度不同。能量算例需清楚定義有效出力與時數，不能把裝置容量全年相乘當保證發電；水量與尾水限制需在共同調度邊界核對。",
         "textEn": "New generation may use existing releases, but its timing can differ from irrigation or downstream needs. Energy requires defined output and duration; nameplate power times a full year is not guaranteed generation.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
