       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tarbela Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型低位出口將高水頭轉為高速射流，下游消能與岩床反應必須和洞內壓力一起評估。水力功率給能量速率，不能直接預測沖坑深度；修復前後需以相同流量尾水比較壓力、地形及材料損傷，避免混淆工況改善與構造改善。 驗證時應對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深，並辨識以下失效情境：較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「出口消能與修復證據」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Large low outlets convert head into jets, requiring linked assessment of tunnel pressure, dissipation and the receiving bed. Hydraulic power is an energy rate rather than a scour-depth law. Compare repairs at matching discharge and tailwater using pressures, surveys and damage records to separate operating changes from structural improvement. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
