       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outlet dissipation and repair evidence” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。診斷時應採取以下查核：對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Diagnose it by the following check: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「修復後損傷較少就不必比較前後水力工況」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Less postrepair damage removes the need to compare hydraulic conditions\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b211-v15-40-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "較小洪水後損傷減少不一定證明修復構造更有效。診斷時應採取以下查核：對齊修復前後流量尾水並比較水墊壓力及沖坑測深，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。",
         "textEn": "Less damage after a smaller flood does not by itself prove a better repair. Diagnose it by the following check: Match discharge and tailwater before and after repair and compare pool pressure and scour surveys. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-wapda-tarbela",
          "v15s-worldbank-tarbela",
          "v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit",
          "v15s-usbr-monitoring"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b211-v15-40-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-wapda-tarbela",
          "v15s-worldbank-tarbela",
          "v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit",
