       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Arch action and abutment transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "卡里巴的拱壩背景要求理解水壓如何經曲率傳向壩肩，水平薄環近似只處理一部分受力。實際壩同時具有懸臂、接縫與地基相互作用，不能把一條薄拱環代表全壩；壩肩剛度與節理會改變拱向力分配。 驗證時應以壩體位移及壩肩地質模型核對拱向傳力假設，並辨識以下失效情境：壩肩柔化可能使原本假設的拱向分配失效。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拱作用與壩肩傳力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Kariba provides context for pressure transfer through curvature toward abutments. A thin horizontal ring represents only one component of response. Real behavior includes cantilever action, joints and foundation interaction; one ring cannot stand for the whole dam, and abutment stiffness changes the load distribution. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare dam displacement and abutment geology with assumed arch load transfer. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Abutment softening can invalidate the assumed arch-force distribution. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arch action and abutment transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Ideal thin ring: pressure=0.6 MPa; radius=100 m; thickness=15 m; hoopCompression=0.6*100/15=4 MPa。",
