    {
     "id": "b212-v15-s2",
     "title": "水力機制、材料與定量模型",
     "titleEn": "Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「水舌入池能量」與「水墊展寬與平均壓力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Jet energy entering the pool\" and \"Pool spreading and mean pressure\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b212-v15-09",
       "title": "水舌入池能量：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Jet energy entering the pool: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-zra-history",
        "v15s-zra-pool",
        "v15s-zra-gates",
        "v15s-worldbank-tarbela-audit"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b212-v15-08"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「水舌入池能量」如何影響卡里巴水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Jet energy entering the pool” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "溢流水舌攜帶動能進入水墊，能量率可用流量與落差估尺度，但實際分布受閘門組合與水舌含氣影響。總功率不能決定單一岩塊荷載，需把全系統能量和局部壓力分開量測，才能評估修復目標。 驗證時應同步記錄各孔流量水位與水舌落點並比較池底壓力，並辨識以下失效情境：總流量相同但閘門組合不同可能移動集中沖擊區。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水舌入池能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Spill jets carry energy into the plunge pool, with discharge and head defining a system-level rate. Gate combinations and aeration alter its distribution. Total power does not determine force on one rock block; separate global energy accounting from local pressure measurements when evaluating rehabilitation objectives. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record gate flows, levels and jet footprints together with bed pressures. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Equal total flow with different gate combinations can shift concentrated impact. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Jet energy entering the pool” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Q=200 m3/s; netDrop=60 m; power=1000*9.81*200*60/1e6=117.72 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Q=200 m3/s; netDrop=60 m; power=1000*9.81*200*60/1e6=117.72 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「總流量相同就保證水墊內全部壓力相同」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal total discharge guarantees identical pressures throughout the pool\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水舌入池能量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Jet energy entering the pool”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
