       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Joint pressure and block removal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "岩床沖蝕常受節理塊體控制，脈壓可沿連通裂隙傳到塊底，與頂面壓力形成淨揚力。給定壓差乘面積僅計水力一項，抗力仍含水下重量、咬合與剪阻；完整岩石強度不能代替節理調查。 驗證時應同步量測節理內外壓力並核對岩塊形狀及連通裂隙，並辨識以下失效情境：連通節理可使低平均水面壓力下仍發生局部拔出。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「節理壓差與拔出」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Scour in jointed rock often involves blocks. Pressure pulses transmitted through connected cracks create uplift relative to the block top. Differential pressure times area gives one hydraulic component; submerged weight, interlock and shear provide separate resistance. Intact rock strength cannot replace joint mapping. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure pressures inside and outside joints and map block geometry and connectivity. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Connected joints can enable local plucking despite low mean surface pressure. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint pressure and block removal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：underBlockPressure=90 kPa; topPressure=60 kPa; blockArea=2 m2; netUplift=(90-60)*2=60 kN。",
