       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Cofferdam dewatering balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "既有水工修復的圍堰抽排需要隔離施工區並維持核准水位，抽水能力要與滲入及降雨來源配對。定入流蓄水式只估短時水位變化，不能取代地基隆起、圍堰穩定及停電工況；應同步監測內外水頭與抽排量。 驗證時應記錄抽排量內外水位與地基孔壓並核對停泵反應，並辨識以下失效情境：抽排加快可能增大內外水頭差而改變地基風險。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「圍堰抽排與水量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rehabilitation cofferdams isolate a work area under approved level conditions. Pumping must be matched to seepage and rainfall inputs. A short-interval balance estimates level change only; it does not address heave, cofferdam stability or power failure, which require concurrent head and flow monitoring. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record pumping, inside and outside levels and foundation pressures and examine pump-stop response. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Faster dewatering can enlarge differential head and alter foundation risk. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cofferdam dewatering balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
