       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Sluice deformation and clearance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "長期混凝土變形可能影響閘槽淨距與啟閉，需區分材料膨脹、溫度與結構位移。幾何扣減能示範餘隙消耗，但實際閘門摩擦和扭斜還受支承及止水影響；應沿全行程查核而非只量單一開度。 驗證時應沿槽全高量測淨距並與啟閉負荷及溫度時序比較，並辨識以下失效情境：單一位置淨距正常仍可能在其他行程卡阻。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閘槽變形與淨距」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Long-term concrete deformation can affect gate clearance and travel. Distinguish material expansion from thermal and structural movement. A clearance deduction shows geometric consumption, while friction and skew also depend on supports and seals; inspect the entire travel path rather than one opening. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Survey clearance throughout the slot and compare operating loads and temperature histories. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Normal clearance at one position can coexist with binding elsewhere. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sluice deformation and clearance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：InitialTotalClearance=18 mm; leftIntrusion=4 mm; rightIntrusion=5 mm; remainingClearance=18-4-5=9 mm。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: InitialTotalClearance=18 mm; leftIntrusion=4 mm; rightIntrusion=5 mm; remainingClearance=18-4-5=9 mm.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「某一開度運轉正常就證明整個行程都不會卡阻」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Normal operation at one opening proves the gate cannot bind anywhere\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「閘槽變形與淨距」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sluice deformation and clearance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
