       "objective": "說明「備援隔水與載重」如何影響卡里巴水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Backup isolation and loading” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "備援閘門或隔水構件的用途是建立可維護邊界，其受力取決於隔離後兩側水位，不能把平常低壓差當最不利情境。平均壓差乘面積只算給定分布的合力，導軌、密封與起吊狀態還需依完整工況驗證。 驗證時應將隔離前後水位組合列入荷載表並檢查導軌反力，並辨識以下失效情境：維修側排乾後壓差增加可能超出平常操作荷載。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「備援隔水與載重」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Backup isolation establishes a maintainable boundary. Its load depends on both water levels after isolation, not the low differential during normal operation. Mean pressure times area gives one prescribed resultant; guides, seals and lifting states still need verification across the complete load cases. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: List pre- and post-isolation water levels and check guide reactions. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Dewatering the maintenance side increases differential load beyond normal operation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Backup isolation and loading” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：SpecifiedMeanDifferentialPressure=250 kPa; effectiveArea=20 m2; isolationForce=250*20=5000 kN。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SpecifiedMeanDifferentialPressure=250 kPa; effectiveArea=20 m2; isolationForce=250*20=5000 kN.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「平常低壓差就代表隔水構件永遠只受小荷載」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Normally low differential pressure means isolation components always carry small loads\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「備援隔水與載重」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Backup isolation and loading”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
