       "objective": "說明「修復效益與同工況」如何影響卡里巴水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rehabilitation benefit and matched states” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kariba Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "修復驗證應使用相近水位、流量與閘門組合比較，否則較溫和的工況會被誤認成構造改善。無因次指標可降低部分尺度影響，但不消除地形與材料改變；應把壓力、沖蝕和操作可靠度分別建立證據鏈。 驗證時應用匹配工況資料比較壓力頻譜與空間分布而非只比較均值，並辨識以下失效情境：未匹配流量就計改善百分比可能製造虛假成效。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「修復效益與同工況」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Evaluate rehabilitation at comparable levels, discharge and gate combinations. Milder operation can otherwise masquerade as structural improvement. Dimensionless measures reduce some scaling effects but do not remove geometry or material changes; maintain separate evidence for pressure, scour and operating reliability. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare spectra and spatial pressure distributions at matched conditions, not only means. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: An improvement percentage without matched discharge can be misleading. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rehabilitation benefit and matched states” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Matched conditions: oldPressureRMS=30 kPa; newPressureRMS=24 kPa; relativeReduction=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Matched conditions: oldPressureRMS=30 kPa; newPressureRMS=24 kPa; relativeReduction=(30-24)/30*100=20 percent.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「任意兩次量測相減就能證明修復成效」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Subtracting any two measurements proves rehabilitation performance\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「修復效益與同工況」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rehabilitation benefit and matched states”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b212-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "修復效益與同工況",
         "titleEn": "Rehabilitation benefit and matched states",
