       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「堆石濕陷與水位」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rockfill wetting and settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "堆石壩蓄水可能改變顆粒接觸與破碎，濕潤後變形需與施工壓實沉陷分開。平均軸向應變乘厚度只估均勻壓縮量，不能代表整壩三維沉陷；應以分區材料試驗與蓄水前後測點反應建立對照，避免只看壩頂總量。 驗證時應比對分層沉陷與濕潤前緣孔壓時序並核對材料破碎，並辨識以下失效情境：濕陷集中於局部區帶可能增加核心與壩殼相對變形。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「堆石濕陷與水位」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Wetting can change rockfill contacts and breakage, and its deformation should be separated from construction settlement. Mean axial strain times thickness describes uniform compression only, not the three-dimensional dam. Compare zoned material tests with pre- and postimpoundment markers rather than relying on crest settlement alone. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare layered settlement with wetting-front pressure histories and material breakage. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Localized wetting settlement can increase differential movement between core and shell. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rockfill wetting and settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticLayerThickness=40 m; prescribedWettingStrain=0.004; uniformSettlement=40*0.004=0.16 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「所有蓄水後沉陷都只是施工壓實尚未完成」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every postimpoundment settlement merely reflects unfinished construction compaction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「堆石濕陷與水位」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rockfill wetting and settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
