       "objective": "說明「合成核心應力轉移」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Synthetic core stress transfer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "合成土石壩核心與兩側材料剛度不同時，拱效應可能把部分豎向荷載轉移到較硬區，降低核心局部總應力。單一有效應力差只呈現孔壓餘量，不能直接預報水力劈裂；需評估最小主應力、材料拉伸特性與接觸變形。 驗證時應比較核心內應力與孔壓並檢查相鄰材料變形差，並辨識以下失效情境：用平均覆土重量代替局部最小應力可能漏掉劈裂敏感區。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「合成核心應力轉移」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "In a synthetic zoned dam, stiffness contrast can transfer vertical load away from the core. A scalar effective-stress difference illustrates pressure margin but does not predict hydraulic fracture. Evaluate minimum principal stress, tensile behavior and interface deformation instead of treating average overburden as the complete stress state. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare core stress and pore pressure with deformation differences in adjacent zones. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Average overburden can conceal regions with low local minimum stress. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Synthetic core stress transfer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: PrescribedNormalTotalStress=500 kPa; porePressure=350 kPa; effectiveNormalStress=500-350=150 kPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「平均覆土應力高就保證核心各方向應力都高」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"High average overburden guarantees high stress in every core direction\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「合成核心應力轉移」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Synthetic core stress transfer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b213-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "合成核心應力轉移",
