       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Filter transitions and fines” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "堆石與細粒防滲材料之間需要連續過渡，否則粒徑反差可能讓細土移入大孔隙。示意粒徑比只供辨認幾何尺度，不是所有土類的核准準則；材料分離、施工污染及交界厚度都須以分區取樣與試驗確認。 驗證時應於實際鋪築位置取樣核對界面兩側級配與連續厚度，並辨識以下失效情境：只驗料場級配會漏掉運輸鋪築造成的分離。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「反濾過渡與細粒」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Transitions between rockfill and fine barrier material must remain continuous to prevent fines entering large pores. An illustrative grain-size ratio identifies scale but does not approve every soil type. Verify segregation, contamination and interface thickness through zoned sampling and applicable material tests. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Sample placed material to check both interface gradations and continuous thickness. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Testing only the stockpile misses segregation during transport and placement. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filter transitions and fines” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
