       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Shared equipment and availability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "共用啟閉設備使多個閘門在維修與故障時具有共同依賴，不能把各孔當完全獨立備援。串聯可用率乘積僅適用獨立失效及簡化狀態，現場共因故障需另建事件樹；應檢查設備移動時間、停機及替代方案。 驗證時應以故障維修紀錄分辨共用與獨立設備並核對替代啟閉能力，並辨識以下失效情境：共用啟閉機停機可同時限制多個原本完好的閘門。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「共用設備與可用率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Shared hoisting equipment creates common dependencies among gates. Multiplying availabilities represents an ideal independent series system only; common-cause failures require another model. Examine movement time, outages and alternatives instead of counting every gate as fully independent redundancy merely because the leaves are separate. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Use maintenance records to distinguish shared and independent equipment and check alternative actuation. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A shared hoist outage can constrain several otherwise functional gates. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Shared equipment and availability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Ideal independent gate-and-hoist availability: gate=0.98; hoist=0.95; combined=0.98*0.95=0.931 dimensionless.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「閘門數量多就保證沒有任何共同失效點」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A large number of gates guarantees no common failure point\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「共用設備與可用率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Shared equipment and availability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
