       ],
       "objective": "說明「機組出力與水頭」如何影響阿科松博水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Generating output and hydraulic head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "阿科松博提供水庫發電與放流協調的案例，機組出力需用淨水頭而不是壩高。尾水與進水損失會隨流量改變，效率也受工作點影響；合成定效率算例只是能量量級，不能以裝置容量倒推出未量測的流量。 驗證時應以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍，並辨識以下失效情境：用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「機組出力與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Akosombo provides context for coordinated reservoir generation and releases. Output uses net head rather than dam height; tailwater, losses and efficiency vary with operating point. A constant-efficiency illustration gives an energy scale and does not justify recovering unmeasured flow directly from nameplate capacity. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Generating output and hydraulic head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: rho=1000 kg/m3; Q=200 m3/s; netHead=60 m; efficiency=0.90; power=1000*9.81*200*60*0.90/1e6=105.948 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「裝置容量就是任何水頭下都能維持的出力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Nameplate capacity is output that can be maintained at every head\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「機組出力與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Generating output and hydraulic head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
