       "instructionEn": "Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Match raw observations to the input conditions of this unit and obtain independent evidence for this specific scenario: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. Preserve calibration, location and timing so that unlike operating states are not directly subtracted. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：交接時以以同期電功率流量及上下游水位核對效率範圍作為可追溯證據，保存對應材料、構形與工況版本。針對用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量，由負責工程師設定需補驗的項目與停留點，不能把教學結果當作現場操作許可。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check efficiency using simultaneous electrical power, flow and both water levels. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：用固定最高效率套全年工況會高估發電量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Applying peak efficiency to every operating state overstates generation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
