       "observationEn": "Site practice: At handover, use the following traceable evidence: Check local storage slope using stage-area curves and repeat bathymetry. Record material, geometry and operating-state versions. Address this scenario: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. The responsible engineer defines additional checks and hold points; the teaching result is not field operating authorization.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：固定面積外推大幅洩降會錯估可用庫容。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Constant-area extrapolation over large drawdown misstates usable storage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
