       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Downstream discharge ramping” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "發電調峰會改變下游放流時序，平均日水量相同仍可能造成不同水位變化速度。流量差除時間只是放流變率，不能直接等同下游任一斷面的水位升速；河道儲水、傳播時間與支流入流需用路由與量測評估。 驗證時應同步記錄電廠放流與下游多站水位以辨認傳播延遲，並辨識以下失效情境：把出口流量變率直接當居民區水位升速會混淆量綱。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游流量爬升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Peaking changes release timing even when daily volume is unchanged. Discharge change divided by time is a release ramp, not the water-level rise at every downstream section. Channel storage, travel time and tributaries require routing and observations to determine actual downstream response. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Record plant release and downstream levels at several stations to identify travel delay. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Equating outlet discharge ramp with settlement-area level rise confuses dimensions. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream discharge ramping” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
