       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Drought capacity and annual energy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Akosombo Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "枯水期間可用水量與水頭可能同時下降，使裝置容量與實際年電量差距擴大。容量因數用年能量除額定功率與時數，僅是事後或情境指標，不直接說明停機原因；需分辨水文限制、設備故障與電網需求。 驗證時應將停機紀錄入流與限載原因對照年電量而非只看單一比率，並辨識以下失效情境：容量因數下降可能來自缺水而非機組效率劣化。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「枯水容量與年能量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "During drought both available volume and head may fall, widening the gap between capacity and energy. Capacity factor is a retrospective or scenario ratio, not a diagnosis of why output was limited. Separate hydrological constraints, equipment outages and grid demand before interpreting a lower value. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare outages, inflow and curtailment causes with annual energy rather than one ratio. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A lower capacity factor may reflect water shortage rather than degraded unit efficiency. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drought capacity and annual energy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
