       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Base uplift and drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "底面孔壓降低有效下向接觸力，防滲帷幕與排水需要分別檢查。線性水頭分布僅為明示假設，排水孔附近及節理連通可使實際分布不線性；不能只測單一孔壓就推定整個底面揚力，還需監測排水能力。 驗證時應沿底面廊道孔壓與排水流量核對假設分布，並辨識以下失效情境：排水堵塞會讓既有線性低壓假設失去依據。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「底面揚力與排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Base pressure reduces effective downward contact. Grout curtains and drains need distinct checks. A linear head profile is an explicit assumption; drains and connected joints can make the real distribution nonlinear. One pressure reading cannot determine total uplift, so monitor pressure distribution and drainage performance together. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare gallery piezometers and drainage flow with the assumed base-pressure profile. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Drain blockage invalidates an assumed low-pressure profile. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Base uplift and drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
