       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Resultant eccentricity and contact” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "單寬底面合力的偏心決定線彈性接觸壓力分布，核心範圍判斷須明示底面不能承拉或可承拉的模型。矩形全接觸公式在算出拉應力時已提示假設可能失效，不能保留負接觸壓力繼續當真實地基反力。 驗證時應以完整荷載力矩求合力位置並核對接觸模型是否允許拉力，並辨識以下失效情境：超出全接觸適用範圍仍用線性式會錯估壓縮區。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「合力偏心與接觸」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Resultant eccentricity controls the linear base-pressure distribution. State whether tension can be transferred. A full-contact rectangular formula that predicts tension signals a possible breakdown of its own assumption; negative contact pressure should not simply be retained as a real foundation reaction. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Locate the resultant from all moments and check whether the contact model permits tension. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Using full-contact equations beyond their range misstates the compressed area. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resultant eccentricity and contact” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: SyntheticBaseWidth=60 m; resultantEccentricity=8 m; middleThirdLimit=60/6=10 m; geometricMargin=10-8=2 m.",
