       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b214-v15-24"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「水化熱與拘束」如何影響大迪克桑斯壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Hydration heat and restraint” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大量混凝土的內外溫差與基礎拘束可形成熱應力，澆置分塊及降溫歷程影響開裂。單軸完全拘束且橫向可自由變形的線彈性公式只是應力量級，實際徐變、成熟度與裂縫會鬆弛應力；應用溫度與應變同步紀錄判斷，而非只量表面溫度。 驗證時應比較核心表面溫度與埋設應變並記錄混凝土齡期，並辨識以下失效情境：忽略徐變或拘束差異會使彈性熱應力被誤當實測值。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水化熱與拘束」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Mass concrete develops thermal stress through gradients and restraint. Block placement and cooling history affect cracking. An elastic estimate with full axial restraint and free lateral deformation gives a uniaxial stress scale only; creep, maturity and cracking relax stress. Interpret temperature and strain together rather than using surface temperature as the full thermal state. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare core and surface temperatures with embedded strain and concrete age. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring creep or restraint differences turns an elastic estimate into a false measured stress. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydration heat and restraint” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Uniaxial full axial restraint with free lateral deformation: E=25 GPa; alpha=10e-6 perK; cooling=12 K; elasticStress=25e9*10e-6*12/1e6=3 MPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「完全拘束彈性熱應力就是所有實際位置的應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Fully restrained elastic thermal stress equals stress at every actual location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水化熱與拘束」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydration heat and restraint”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
