       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Curtain testing and permeability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Grande Dixence Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "灌漿帷幕應改變裂隙導水而非只追求灌入量，取芯、壓水與監測資料共同評估效果。前後流量比只能在同壓差及試段條件下比較，不能直接等同整壩滲透率降幅；地下水路重分配需靠廊道孔壓與流量追蹤。 驗證時應保持試段長度壓差一致並比較帷幕上下游孔壓，並辨識以下失效情境：只看灌漿量多會誤把遠處流失當有效封堵。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「帷幕試驗與滲透」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A grout curtain should alter fracture conductance, not merely absorb grout volume. Compare pressure tests, cores and monitoring. A before-and-after flow ratio requires matching test intervals and pressure; it does not directly equal whole-dam permeability reduction because pathways may redistribute through the foundation. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Match interval length and pressure and compare heads on both sides of the curtain. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Large grout take can represent loss elsewhere instead of effective sealing. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Curtain testing and permeability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Matched test pressure: initialWaterTake=20 L/min; finalWaterTake=5 L/min; observedReduction=(20-5)/20*100=75 percent.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「灌漿量越多就必定代表防滲效果越好」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"More injected grout necessarily means better seepage control\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「帷幕試驗與滲透」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Curtain testing and permeability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
