         "textEn": "Mountain snow delays runoff until melting, so an inflow peak can lag temperature rather than follow daily rain. A reservoir control volume separates inflow, release and duration; storage change still needs an area-elevation relationship before it becomes a level change.",
         "sourceIds": [
