       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「融雪脈衝與蓄量帳」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Snowmelt pulses and storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "以同一時鐘對齊入流與出口流量，再逐時積分比較庫容曲線反推的蓄量差。標出量測間隔與缺值補法，若洪峰期間差額變大，先查時間錯位與未入帳支流，不能立刻把殘差判為漏水。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Align inlet and outlet records to one clock, integrate each hourly interval and compare with storage inferred from a capacity curve. Record sampling gaps explicitly. If the mismatch grows near a peak, investigate timing and uncounted tributaries before interpreting the residual as leakage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將入流峰值改成前兩小時三十、後四小時十五立方公尺每秒，分段求蓄量並與平均法比較，說明兩者何時相同、何時因出口變化而不同。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Replace constant inflow with thirty cubic metres per second for two hours and fifteen for four hours. Integrate segments and explain when averaging preserves volume and when a varying outlet invalidates the comparison.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把日平均流量與六小時洪峰混用，會把尖峰放流錯配到整日；即使總水量看似相符，短時最高水位仍可能被平滑掉，失去檢查蓄洪空間的意義。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Mixing a daily mean with a six-hour pulse assigns peak release to the wrong duration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
