       ],
       "objective": "說明「混凝土受拘束溫降」如何影響黑部水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Restrained concrete cooling” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kurobe Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "混凝土冷卻本來會縮短，但岩盤或相鄰塊體若限制收縮，就可能產生拉應力。高山環境的季節溫度與壩內溫度不會同步，完全拘束模型只能用來辨識熱應變的量級，不能忽略徐變及接縫開合。 熱應變本身沒有力的單位，只有與彈性模數及拘束條件結合才形成應力；自由收縮與完全拘束提供兩個理想端點。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土受拘束溫降」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Cooling concrete tends to contract, while restraint by rock or adjoining blocks can create tension. Mountain air and internal concrete temperatures respond on different schedules, so full restraint indicates a thermal strain scale without representing creep or joint opening. Thermal strain has no force unit. Stress emerges only when stiffness and restraint are supplied, making free contraction and full restraint distinct ideal endpoints for interpreting a temperature change. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Restrained concrete cooling” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：E=30000 MPa; alpha=0.00001 1/K; dT=12 K; sigma=E alpha dT=3.6 MPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: E=30000 MPa; alpha=0.00001 1/K; dT=12 K; sigma=E alpha dT=3.6 MPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「每日氣溫變化就是整座壩體的平均溫變」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Daily air-temperature change equals the mean temperature change of the entire dam\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「混凝土受拘束溫降」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Restrained concrete cooling”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-13-k1",
         "title": "混凝土受拘束溫降",
         "titleEn": "Restrained concrete cooling",
         "text": "混凝土冷卻本來會縮短，但岩盤或相鄰塊體若限制收縮，就可能產生拉應力。高山環境的季節溫度與壩內溫度不會同步，完全拘束模型只能用來辨識熱應變的量級，不能忽略徐變及接縫開合。",
         "textEn": "Cooling concrete tends to contract, while restraint by rock or adjoining blocks can create tension. Mountain air and internal concrete temperatures respond on different schedules, so full restraint indicates a thermal strain scale without representing creep or joint opening.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-kurobe-owner",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-13-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：每日氣溫變化就是整座壩體的平均溫變 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Daily air-temperature change equals the mean temperature change of the entire dam Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
