       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「混凝土受拘束溫降」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Restrained concrete cooling” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "直接以每日氣溫降幅代替整塊混凝土溫降，通常誇大深部瞬時應力；若忽略長期徐變的鬆弛，也可能把彈性上限誤讀成持續存在的實際應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Using daily air cooling as the temperature change of an entire block exaggerates immediate interior response. Ignoring long-term creep relaxation can also turn an elastic bound into an incorrect estimate of sustained stress. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：熱應變本身沒有力的單位，只有與彈性模數及拘束條件結合才形成應力；自由收縮與完全拘束提供兩個理想端點。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Stress emerges only when stiffness and restraint are supplied, making free contraction and full restraint distinct ideal endpoints for interpreting a temperature change.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「每日氣溫變化就是整座壩體的平均溫變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Daily air-temperature change equals the mean temperature change of the entire dam\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-16-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "直接以每日氣溫降幅代替整塊混凝土溫降，通常誇大深部瞬時應力；若忽略長期徐變的鬆弛，也可能把彈性上限誤讀成持續存在的實際應力。",
         "textEn": "Using daily air cooling as the temperature change of an entire block exaggerates immediate interior response. Ignoring long-term creep relaxation can also turn an elastic bound into an incorrect estimate of sustained stress.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-kurobe-owner",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-16-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-kurobe-owner",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「混凝土受拘束溫降」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Restrained concrete cooling\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
