       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「長引水管的沿程損失」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Friction in a long conduit” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "用兩個壓力測點及高程差建立總水頭線，校核壓力單位與流量換算速度是否一致。選取穩定流量時段擬合摩擦因子，再檢查不同流量是否維持合理趨勢，避免把閥件損失全塞入沿程係數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Construct the total-head line from two pressure taps and elevations, checking pressure units and velocity inferred from discharge. Fit the friction factor during steady periods and examine its trend across flows rather than absorbing every valve loss into distributed friction. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：保持管徑與粗糙度不變，把速度提高百分之二十，重算水頭損失及增加比例，再列出摩擦因子可能隨雷諾數改變而使簡化比較失準的情況。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Raise velocity by twenty percent at fixed diameter and roughness, recalculate head loss and its percentage increase, then identify circumstances where a changing Reynolds number alters the friction factor and weakens the simple comparison.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把范寧係數誤作達西係數會造成四倍差異；只注意高落差而忽略流速平方項，則會低估增流後的能量損失，甚至錯算可供機組使用的淨水頭。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Confusing Fanning and Darcy factors creates a factor-of-four error. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
