      {
       "id": "b215-v15-21",
       "title": "高水頭水能轉換：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "High head energy conversion: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-kurobe-owner",
        "v15s-usace-arch",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b215-v15-20"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「高水頭水能轉換」如何影響黑部水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “High head energy conversion” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kurobe Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水的位能通量由密度、重力、流量與淨水頭決定，發電效率只是把這股能量轉為電力的比例。黑部案例應先把水路損失從毛水頭扣掉，再談電功率，否則同一耗能會被遺漏或重複扣除。 控制體邊界必須說明是否包含發電機、變壓器與輔機用電，否則兩個看似相同效率可能其實分母分子範圍不同。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高水頭水能轉換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Potential-energy flux depends on density, gravity, discharge and net head; efficiency converts that flux into electric output. In a high-head case, waterway losses must be separated from gross head before applying an efficiency boundary that clearly identifies which equipment is included. The conversion boundary must identify whether generator, transformer and auxiliary consumption are included. Otherwise two apparently comparable efficiencies can refer to different energy inputs and different reported electrical outputs. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “High head energy conversion” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=18 m3/s; Hnet=420 m; eta=0.9; P=rho g Q Hnet eta/1e6=66.74724 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=18 m3/s; Hnet=420 m; eta=0.9; P=rho g Q Hnet eta/1e6=66.74724 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「機組功率乘秒仍可直接標成兆瓦小時」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Power multiplied by seconds can directly be labelled megawatt-hours\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「高水頭水能轉換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “High head energy conversion”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "高水頭水能轉換",
         "titleEn": "High head energy conversion",
         "text": "水的位能通量由密度、重力、流量與淨水頭決定，發電效率只是把這股能量轉為電力的比例。黑部案例應先把水路損失從毛水頭扣掉，再談電功率，否則同一耗能會被遺漏或重複扣除。",
         "textEn": "Potential-energy flux depends on density, gravity, discharge and net head; efficiency converts that flux into electric output. In a high-head case, waterway losses must be separated from gross head before applying an efficiency boundary that clearly identifies which equipment is included.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-kurobe-owner",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
