       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高水頭水能轉換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “High head energy conversion” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "分別核對上游能量、尾水基準與電表邊界，將功率和同一時段流量相配。若估算效率超過一，先查毛淨水頭混淆及千瓦兆瓦換算，再比較壓力與流量儀表的校正紀錄。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Check upstream energy, the tailwater reference and electrical-meter boundary separately, pairing output with simultaneous flow. An efficiency above unity requires checking gross versus net head and power-unit conversions before investigating calibration of pressure and discharge instruments. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：用六小時等功率運行求兆瓦小時，再把淨水頭降低十公尺重算差值，註明效率保持不變是敏感度假設，不是實際機組效率曲線。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Calculate megawatt-hours for six hours at constant output, then reduce net head by ten metres and compare energy. State explicitly that unchanged efficiency is a sensitivity assumption rather than a measured turbine performance curve.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把額定功率當作每小時都能提供的實際功率，會忽略水頭與流量變動；把效率同時包含輸水損失又再扣摩擦，則會把同一能量損失計入兩次。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Treating rated power as continuous achievable output ignores changing head and discharge. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
