       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「高水頭水能轉換」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “High head energy conversion” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把額定功率當作每小時都能提供的實際功率，會忽略水頭與流量變動；把效率同時包含輸水損失又再扣摩擦，則會把同一能量損失計入兩次。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating rated power as continuous achievable output ignores changing head and discharge. An efficiency that already includes waterway losses, followed by another friction deduction, counts the same energy loss twice. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：控制體邊界必須說明是否包含發電機、變壓器與輔機用電，否則兩個看似相同效率可能其實分母分子範圍不同。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Otherwise two apparently comparable efficiencies can refer to different energy inputs and different reported electrical outputs.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「機組功率乘秒仍可直接標成兆瓦小時」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Power multiplied by seconds can directly be labelled megawatt-hours\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-24-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把額定功率當作每小時都能提供的實際功率，會忽略水頭與流量變動；把效率同時包含輸水損失又再扣摩擦，則會把同一能量損失計入兩次。",
         "textEn": "Treating rated power as continuous achievable output ignores changing head and discharge. An efficiency that already includes waterway losses, followed by another friction deduction, counts the same energy loss twice.",
         "sourceIds": [
