    {
     "id": "b215-v15-s4",
     "title": "試驗、量測與監測驗證",
     "titleEn": "Testing, measurement and monitoring",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「快速流速變化與水錘」與「施工湧水的抽排功率」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Rapid velocity change and water hammer\" and \"Pumping energy for tunnel inflow\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b215-v15-25",
       "title": "快速流速變化與水錘：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Rapid velocity change and water hammer: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-kurobe-owner",
        "v15s-usace-arch",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b215-v15-24"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「快速流速變化與水錘」如何影響黑部水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kurobe Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "管中水與管壁都具有彈性，快速改變速度會形成沿管傳播的壓力波。焦科夫斯基關係給出理想快速變化的壓力尺度，與穩流摩擦屬不同物理過程，必須先比較變化時間與波的往返時間。 波速由水與管壁的合成可壓縮性決定，並非水流平均速度；壓力訊息能快速往返，而水體本身位移相對較小。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「快速流速變化與水錘」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Elastic water and pipe walls support a travelling pressure wave when velocity changes rapidly. The Joukowsky relation gives an ideal rapid-change pressure scale, which differs from steady friction and requires comparison of change duration with the wave round-trip time. Wave speed reflects the combined compressibility of water and wall, not mean flow velocity. A pressure signal can travel rapidly back and forth while the water itself moves a comparatively short distance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=1.5 m/s; dp=rho a dv/1e6=1.35 MPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; a=900 m/s; dv=1.5 m/s; dp=rho a dv/1e6=1.35 MPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「一次水錘增量就是整條管線所有位置的最大壓力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"One water-hammer increment is the maximum pressure at every pipeline location\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「快速流速變化與水錘」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rapid velocity change and water hammer”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-25-k1",
         "title": "快速流速變化與水錘",
         "titleEn": "Rapid velocity change and water hammer",
         "text": "管中水與管壁都具有彈性，快速改變速度會形成沿管傳播的壓力波。焦科夫斯基關係給出理想快速變化的壓力尺度，與穩流摩擦屬不同物理過程，必須先比較變化時間與波的往返時間。",
         "textEn": "Elastic water and pipe walls support a travelling pressure wave when velocity changes rapidly. The Joukowsky relation gives an ideal rapid-change pressure scale, which differs from steady friction and requires comparison of change duration with the wave round-trip time.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-kurobe-owner",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-25-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：一次水錘增量就是整條管線所有位置的最大壓力 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: One water-hammer increment is the maximum pressure at every pipeline location Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-kurobe-owner",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
