       "objective": "從症狀倒推「快速流速變化與水錘」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Rapid velocity change and water hammer” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "若局部壓力降到汽化條件，液柱分離及再結合可能改變峰值，簡單線性式不再完整；只把平均壓力加上算得增量也會忽略反射與高程分布。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "If local pressure reaches vapor conditions, column separation and rejoining can alter peaks beyond the simple linear model. Adding one increment to an average pressure also neglects reflections and the elevation-dependent pressure distribution. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：波速由水與管壁的合成可壓縮性決定，並非水流平均速度；壓力訊息能快速往返，而水體本身位移相對較小。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: A pressure signal can travel rapidly back and forth while the water itself moves a comparatively short distance.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「一次水錘增量就是整條管線所有位置的最大壓力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One water-hammer increment is the maximum pressure at every pipeline location\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
