       "objective": "說明「施工湧水的抽排功率」如何影響黑部水壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Pumping energy for tunnel inflow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kurobe Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "黑四施工歷史中的地下水困難提醒工程師，排水是水量、揚程與能源的聯合問題。假想隧道集水坑把來水提升到出口時，所需電功率須除以泵組效率；進水量估計不能只靠某一次乾天觀察。 總揚程包含出口與集水坑的位能差及流動損失，泵的工作點由供能曲線與管路需求曲線交會決定而非單看銘牌。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「施工湧水的抽排功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The historical groundwater difficulty highlights dewatering as a coupled flow, lift and energy problem. A hypothetical tunnel sump must lift inflow to an outlet, so electrical input divides hydraulic power by pump efficiency rather than multiplying by it. Total head contains elevation difference and flow losses. The operating point follows the intersection of pump supply and system demand curves, rather than being fixed by the nameplate flow alone. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pumping energy for tunnel inflow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; H=35 m; eta=0.7; Pin=rho g Q H/eta/1000=122.625 kW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=0.25 m3/s; H=35 m; eta=0.7; Pin=rho g Q H/eta/1000=122.625 kW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「抽水電功率應將水力功率乘上效率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Pumping electrical input equals hydraulic power multiplied by efficiency\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「施工湧水的抽排功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pumping energy for tunnel inflow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "施工湧水的抽排功率",
         "titleEn": "Pumping energy for tunnel inflow",
         "text": "黑四施工歷史中的地下水困難提醒工程師，排水是水量、揚程與能源的聯合問題。假想隧道集水坑把來水提升到出口時，所需電功率須除以泵組效率；進水量估計不能只靠某一次乾天觀察。",
         "textEn": "The historical groundwater difficulty highlights dewatering as a coupled flow, lift and energy problem. A hypothetical tunnel sump must lift inflow to an outlet, so electrical input divides hydraulic power by pump efficiency rather than multiplying by it.",
