       "objective": "從症狀倒推「施工湧水的抽排功率」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Pumping energy for tunnel inflow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把泵額定流量直接視為實際排水能力會忽略揚程工作點；含砂或堵塞造成效率下降時，即使電流升高也不代表排水量增加，水位仍可能持續上升。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Rated pump flow does not establish discharge at the actual head. Abrasion or blockage can reduce efficiency, so rising electrical current may accompany falling water delivery and a continuing increase in sump level. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：總揚程包含出口與集水坑的位能差及流動損失，泵的工作點由供能曲線與管路需求曲線交會決定而非單看銘牌。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: The operating point follows the intersection of pump supply and system demand curves, rather than being fixed by the nameplate flow alone.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「抽水電功率應將水力功率乘上效率」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Pumping electrical input equals hydraulic power multiplied by efficiency\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b215-v15-32-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把泵額定流量直接視為實際排水能力會忽略揚程工作點；含砂或堵塞造成效率下降時，即使電流升高也不代表排水量增加，水位仍可能持續上升。",
         "textEn": "Rated pump flow does not establish discharge at the actual head. Abrasion or blockage can reduce efficiency, so rising electrical current may accompany falling water delivery and a continuing increase in sump level.",
         "sourceIds": [
