       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Downstream buffer storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Kurobe Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "發電放流可能在短時間變動，而下游希望較平順的水量。假想緩衝池以暫時蓄水吸收入出流差額，所需容積由整個時段積分決定，不能只用最大流量相減而忽略持續時間與初始水位。 緩衝所需容積是累積差額曲線的最大與最小之差，若脈衝並非矩形，必須先積分完整歷線才能辨認容量需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「下游緩衝池的時段蓄量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Generating releases can change faster than desired downstream delivery. A hypothetical buffer stores the time integral of the inlet-outlet difference; required volume depends on duration and initial storage, not merely the difference between two peak discharge values. For a repeating cycle, required active storage is the range of the cumulative imbalance curve. Nonrectangular pulses require integration of the complete hydrograph before the relevant volume can be identified. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Downstream buffer storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Qin=24 m3/s; Qout=16 m3/s; dt=1800 s; dV=(Qin-Qout)dt=14400 m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Qin=24 m3/s; Qout=16 m3/s; dt=1800 s; dV=(Qin-Qout)dt=14400 m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「每個放流脈衝都能重新使用緩衝池的全部容量」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every release pulse can reuse the entire buffer capacity from scratch\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「下游緩衝池的時段蓄量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
