       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Thermal movement and joint gap” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "將縫計與附近溫度計同步繪圖，核對量測方向與正負號，再分別辨識日週期與季節週期。以兩側塊體的相對運動重建縫寬，不能把單側絕對位移直接當成開度。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Plot joint and temperature measurements synchronously, checking sensor direction and sign before distinguishing daily from seasonal cycles. Reconstruct gap from the relative motion of both sides rather than treating one block's absolute displacement as joint opening. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：畫兩側等長塊體同時升溫的幾何圖，指定固定端位置後求相對位移，再與單側伸長比較，說明接縫初始間隙對是否接觸的影響。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Sketch two equal blocks warming together, specify their fixed ends and derive relative movement. Compare it with single-block expansion and explain how the initial gap determines whether contact develops.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把自由伸長全數加到縫寬而不考慮方向，可能把閉合預測成張開；若縫面已接觸仍用同一直線關係外推，就會忽略接觸壓力與剛度突然改變。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Adding all free expansion to gap without checking direction can predict opening where closure occurs. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
