       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「水躍共軛水深」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hydraulic jump conjugate depths” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把共軛水深當成保證穩定水躍的尾水設定，可能忽略掃出或淹沒；若又把耗能量當作局部壓力，將無法辨識床面脈動、氣蝕與沖刷的不同機制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "A conjugate depth does not guarantee a stable jump; sweep-out or submergence may occur. Treating dissipated energy as local pressure also obscures distinct mechanisms of fluctuating loads, cavitation and scour. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：躍前與躍後流量相同但速度與水深改變，動量函數相等不代表比能相等，兩斷面的比能差才是耗散的量。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Equal momentum functions do not imply equal specific energies; their specific-energy difference quantifies the mechanical energy dissipated in the transition.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「水躍同時保持動量函數與機械比能不變」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A hydraulic jump conserves both momentum function and mechanical specific energy\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b216-v15-32-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把共軛水深當成保證穩定水躍的尾水設定，可能忽略掃出或淹沒；若又把耗能量當作局部壓力，將無法辨識床面脈動、氣蝕與沖刷的不同機制。",
         "textEn": "A conjugate depth does not guarantee a stable jump; sweep-out or submergence may occur. Treating dissipated energy as local pressure also obscures distinct mechanisms of fluctuating loads, cavitation and scour.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-feitsui-owner",
          "v15s-feitsui-history",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b216-v15-32-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-feitsui-owner",
          "v15s-feitsui-history",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「水躍共軛水深」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Hydraulic jump conjugate depths\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。",
         "濁度數值可以直接當作每立方公尺固體公斤數",
         "把共軛水深當成保證穩定水躍的尾水設定，可能忽略掃出或淹沒；若又把耗能量當作局部壓力，將無法辨識床面脈動、氣蝕與沖刷的不同機制。"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
         "Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.",
         "A turbidity value directly equals kilograms of solids per cubic metre",
         "A conjugate depth does not guarantee a stable jump; sweep-out or submergence may occur."
        ],
