       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「含砂濃度與固體負荷」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Sediment concentration and mass load” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "以單一岸邊樣本代表全斷面會漏掉垂向與橫向濃度梯度；把輸入固體全當作永久沉積，也會忽略排出、再懸浮與密度壓密，使庫容損失估算偏離。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "One bank sample may miss vertical and lateral gradients. Treating all incoming solids as permanent deposition ignores passage, resuspension and compaction, so transported mass cannot directly establish lost reservoir volume. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：質量率積分得到的是運輸量，轉成沉積體積還要知道留下比例與乾容重，因而輸砂與庫容測量應分開設計。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Conversion to deposited volume additionally requires retention and dry bulk density, so sediment transport measurements and reservoir-capacity surveys address related but distinct quantities.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「濁度數值可以直接當作每立方公尺固體公斤數」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A turbidity value directly equals kilograms of solids per cubic metre\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b216-v15-36-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "以單一岸邊樣本代表全斷面會漏掉垂向與橫向濃度梯度；把輸入固體全當作永久沉積，也會忽略排出、再懸浮與密度壓密，使庫容損失估算偏離。",
         "textEn": "One bank sample may miss vertical and lateral gradients. Treating all incoming solids as permanent deposition ignores passage, resuspension and compaction, so transported mass cannot directly establish lost reservoir volume.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-feitsui-owner",
          "v15s-feitsui-history",
