         "textEn": "Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q1=3 m3/s; C1=20 mg/L; Q2=2 m3/s; C2=50 mg/L; Cm=(Q1C1+Q2C2)/(Q1+Q2)=32 mg/L. Applicable boundary: Complete mixing of a hypothetical nonreactive solute, not turbidity or a drinking-water acceptance limit.",
