       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Filter gradation ratio screening” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "繪完整粒徑曲線並標明取樣位置，確認百分之十五與八十五是通過率而非留置率。比較施工前後級配與細料遷移試驗，若局部粗化或離析，應另看局部曲線，不能只用整批平均值。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Plot the complete gradation and sampling locations, confirming that fifteen and eighty-five percent denote passing rather than retained mass. Compare preconstruction and placed material with migration tests, examining local curves where segregation occurs instead of relying on a batch average. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將假想濾料離析成粗細兩區，各自重新計算比值並與合併樣本比較，提出能辨識局部風險的取樣配置，而不要自行訂定現地允許值。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Split hypothetical filter material into coarse and fine segregated zones, calculate each ratio and compare with the blended sample. Propose sampling locations that reveal local risk without inventing field acceptance limits.",
