       ],
       "objective": "說明「含水率與壓實乾密度」如何影響石門水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Water content and compacted density” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shihmen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "土石壩施工控制不能只看每立方公尺濕土多重，因為其中一部分是水。以水重除乾土重定義的含水率可將濕密度換成乾密度，才便於比較固體骨架壓實程度。相同乾密度也不代表相同滲透性，因為土的組成、含水狀態、壓實能量與顆粒排列仍可能不同。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「含水率與壓實乾密度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Wet bulk density alone cannot describe embankment compaction because part of the measured mass is water. Gravimetric water content, defined relative to dry solids, converts wet density to dry density for comparing the solid skeleton. Even equal dry density does not ensure equal permeability, since composition, moisture condition, compactive effort and particle arrangement may still differ substantially between specimens or placed layers. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water content and compacted density” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rhoWet=2100 kg/m3; w=0.12 kg/kg; rhoDry=rhoWet/(1+w)=1875 kg/m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rhoWet=2100 kg/m3; w=0.12 kg/kg; rhoDry=rhoWet/(1+w)=1875 kg/m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「含水率百分之十二可直接以十二代入換算式」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Twelve percent water content can be entered as twelve in the conversion\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「含水率與壓實乾密度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water content and compacted density”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
