       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「含水率與壓實乾密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Water content and compacted density” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "核對濕樣、乾樣與容器重量紀錄，將百分率轉成無因次小數後再換算。以重複試體檢查體積量測偏差，並把現地乾密度與相同材料、相同試驗能量的壓實曲線比較，避免跨材料誤比。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Check wet, dry and container masses, converting percentage to a dimensionless fraction before calculation. Use replicate specimens to assess volume error and compare field dry density with a compaction curve for the same material and test effort rather than a different soil. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：固定濕密度，分別用含水率百分之八與十六計算乾密度，畫出關係並說明這條換算曲線為何不是實際材料的壓實最佳含水率曲線。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: At fixed wet density, calculate dry density for eight and sixteen percent water contents. Plot the conversion and explain why it is not the material's experimental optimum-moisture compaction curve.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把百分之十二直接代入十二會得到不合理低密度；若以濕土質量當含水率分母卻仍用此式，也會系統性偏差，使壓實紀錄看似精確但定義不一致。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Entering twelve instead of zero point one two produces an implausible low density. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
