       "objective": "說明「泥砂收支與占容轉換」如何影響石門水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Sediment budget and occupied storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shihmen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水庫庫容損失來自留下的固體與孔隙空間，而非單純入庫濃度。先用輸入減輸出得到淨沉積質量，再除以沉積乾容重才能估算占容。乾容重會隨顆粒組成、壓密與時間改變，因此每年相同固體質量不必占據相同體積，庫容測量仍是重要獨立證據。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「泥砂收支與占容轉換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Reservoir capacity loss depends on retained solids and their pore space rather than inlet concentration alone. Net deposited mass is incoming minus outgoing solids, and dry bulk density converts that mass to occupied volume. Bulk density changes with grading, consolidation and age, so equal annual solid masses need not occupy equal volumes; bathymetric capacity surveys remain an important independent line of evidence. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sediment budget and occupied storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Min=1800000 kg; Mout=600000 kg; rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; Vdep=(Min-Mout)/rhoDry=1000 m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Min=1800000 kg; Mout=600000 kg; rhoDry=1200 kg/m3; Vdep=(Min-Mout)/rhoDry=1000 m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「入庫泥砂總質量全部等於當期永久庫容損失」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"All incoming sediment mass equals permanent capacity loss in that period\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「泥砂收支與占容轉換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sediment budget and occupied storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
