       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「泥砂收支與占容轉換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Sediment budget and occupied storage” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "將入出庫懸砂與可觀測推移質分開估計，核對每筆質量是乾重還是濕重。以沉積取芯取得乾容重，再與重複水深測量的體積差比較，保留兩者的不確定度及不同測區範圍。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Estimate incoming and outgoing suspended and observable bed loads separately, identifying dry versus wet mass. Obtain dry bulk density from sediment cores and compare with repeated bathymetric volume differences, retaining uncertainty and differences in surveyed coverage. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：把乾容重改為九百與一千五百公斤每立方公尺，計算占容範圍並比較質量不確定度，說明為何單報一個庫容損失數字可能缺乏意義。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Use dry bulk densities of nine hundred and fifteen hundred kilograms per cubic metre to bracket occupied volume. Compare this sensitivity with mass uncertainty and explain why one unqualified capacity-loss number can mislead.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把濕泥密度當乾容重會低估固體對應占容；若排砂輸出與入流統計期間不同，又可能出現虛假的負沉積，誤認庫容已恢復而其實只是資料不同步。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Using wet-mud density as dry bulk density understates occupied volume. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
