       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Local intake orifice discharge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shihmen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "不同高程取水口能選擇不同水層，但流量仍受水頭、孔口面積及收縮損失影響。理想速度由能量式產生，再以流量係數修正局部三維流動。係數與開口形狀、邊緣及上下游條件有關，不能把另一設備的係數直接搬來代表石門現地真實取水口的校準結果。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「取水孔口的局部流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Withdrawal elevation selects a water layer, while flow still depends on head, opening area and contraction losses. An energy-based ideal velocity is corrected by a discharge coefficient representing local three-dimensional effects. That coefficient depends on edge shape, geometry and upstream and downstream conditions, so a value assumed here cannot be transferred directly to a real Shihmen intake or another differently shaped installed structure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Local intake orifice discharge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
