       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Solids export during sluicing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shihmen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排砂效果需要同時知道水量及攜帶固體濃度，只有閘門開度或水流聲音無法衡量輸出。以乾固體質量率積分可比較排砂時段，並與用水量分開記錄。高濃度時顆粒交互作用可能改變流變，簡單稀薄懸浮假設及採樣代表性與乾重定義都需要仔細檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排砂時段的固體輸出」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Sediment export requires both water discharge and carried solids concentration; gate position or visible turbulence alone cannot measure it. Integrating dry-solids flux compares sluicing intervals while keeping water consumption in a separate account. At high concentrations, particle interaction may alter rheology, so dilute-suspension assumptions and sampling representativeness need examination before the simple mass calculation is interpreted as operational performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Solids export during sluicing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=9 m3/s; C=8 kg/m3; dt=2400 s; M=Q C dt/1000=172.8 tonne。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=9 m3/s; C=8 kg/m3; dt=2400 s; M=Q C dt/1000=172.8 tonne.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要放流水量大就能保證排出的泥砂很多」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A large water release guarantees a large exported sediment mass\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「排砂時段的固體輸出」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Solids export during sluicing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
