       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排砂時段的固體輸出」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Solids export during sluicing” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "採樣與流量計必須共用時間區間，對洪砂脈衝增加取樣密度，並標示截面代表方式。把輸出質量與對應放流水量同時報告，再與排砂前後地形比較，避免把輸砂通過誤認為庫底完全清除。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Synchronize sampling and discharge intervals, increase sampling density during pulses and state cross-section representation. Report exported mass alongside water volume and compare with before-and-after bed surveys rather than equating transported material with complete bed clearance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將前後兩個二十分鐘的濃度分設為十二與四公斤每立方公尺，積分質量並比較平均法，再討論流量也改變時需要怎樣的同步資料。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Assign concentrations of twelve and four kilograms per cubic metre to consecutive twenty-minute intervals, integrate export and compare with averaging. Explain the synchronized data needed if discharge changes as well.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：濃度峰值若只維持短時間卻被乘整段放流歷時，會誇大排砂量；取樣管堵塞則可能反向低估粗粒部分，讓看似穩定的濃度紀錄缺少主要固體。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Multiplying a brief concentration peak by the entire release duration exaggerates export. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
