       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「後池吸收放流變化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Afterbay absorption of release changes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "由水位容積曲線計算時段起迄蓄量，與流量差積分互相比較，檢查流量計延遲及回水影響。把下一時段回復所需的出入流差也畫上圖，確認緩衝不是靠不斷累積水量維持。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Calculate endpoint storage from the level-volume curve and compare with integrated flow imbalance, checking meter lag and backwater effects. Plot the subsequent imbalance needed for recovery to confirm that buffering does not depend on indefinitely accumulating water. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：設定可用空間只有兩萬立方公尺，計算一次脈衝後剩餘空間，再增加第二次脈衝並求中間必須恢復的水量，將初始狀態畫入水量帳。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Set available space to twenty thousand cubic metres, calculate the remainder after one pulse and add a second pulse. Determine the intervening recovery volume and include the initial state explicitly in the account.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把後池總容積當作每次都能使用的空間，忽略已有蓄水及水位限制；連續多次脈衝若未恢復，會逐漸耗盡緩衝，即使每次單獨計算都小於總容量。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Using gross volume as newly available space ignores existing storage and level constraints. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
