       "id": "b217-v15-36",
       "title": "後池吸收放流變化：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Afterbay absorption of release changes: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-shihmen-owner",
        "v15s-shihmen-facilities",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b217-v15-35"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「後池吸收放流變化」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Afterbay absorption of release changes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把後池總容積當作每次都能使用的空間，忽略已有蓄水及水位限制；連續多次脈衝若未恢復，會逐漸耗盡緩衝，即使每次單獨計算都小於總容量。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Using gross volume as newly available space ignores existing storage and level constraints. Repeated pulses without recovery progressively consume buffering capacity even when every individual pulse is smaller than the gross basin volume. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：比較容量時應使用可用水位範圍對應的容積，而非整座後池總容量，並明確保留時段開始時的初始蓄量位置。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Capacity comparison must use the volume available within the relevant level range rather than gross basin capacity, while retaining the initial storage position and the duration of subsequent recovery periods.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「每次脈衝都可以重新使用整座後池總容量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Every new pulse can reuse the entire gross afterbay capacity\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b217-v15-36-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把後池總容積當作每次都能使用的空間，忽略已有蓄水及水位限制；連續多次脈衝若未恢復，會逐漸耗盡緩衝，即使每次單獨計算都小於總容量。",
         "textEn": "Using gross volume as newly available space ignores existing storage and level constraints. Repeated pulses without recovery progressively consume buffering capacity even when every individual pulse is smaller than the gross basin volume.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-shihmen-owner",
          "v15s-shihmen-facilities",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
