       "objective": "說明「排水量的水頭正規化」如何影響石門水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Head-normalized drainage conductance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Shihmen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排水量隨庫水頭變化並不必然表示滲流通道劣化，先以水頭差正規化可比較近似達西條件下的導水能力。這個比值仍受降雨入滲、溫度黏度及出口堵塞影響；用石門土石壩背景討論趨勢時，應把量測位置、時滯與水頭定義清楚保留在完整趨勢圖上。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水量的水頭正規化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Drainage increasing with reservoir head does not necessarily indicate deterioration. Dividing flow by head difference compares apparent conductance under roughly Darcy conditions. The ratio remains sensitive to rainfall infiltration, temperature-dependent viscosity and outlet blockage, so trend interpretation must retain measurement location, lag and the definition of hydraulic head rather than presenting one normalized value as a direct measure of erosion or structural condition. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Head-normalized drainage conductance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=0.004 m3/s; dh=20 m; G=Q/dh=0.0002 m2/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=0.004 m3/s; dh=20 m; G=Q/dh=0.0002 m2/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「排水量降低一定表示壩內滲流風險下降」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Lower measured drainage always means reduced internal seepage risk\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「排水量的水頭正規化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Head-normalized drainage conductance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b217-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "排水量的水頭正規化",
