      {
       "id": "b217-v15-39",
       "title": "排水量的水頭正規化：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Head-normalized drainage conductance: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-shihmen-owner",
        "v15s-shihmen-facilities",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b217-v15-38"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「排水量的水頭正規化」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Head-normalized drainage conductance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "將流量與對應時滯後的水頭配對，先標記雨期與清理排水溝日期，再比較乾天穩態區段。以水溫修正黏度影響時保留修正前曲線，並同步檢查排水濁度與細粒是否出現。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Pair discharge with appropriately lagged head, marking rain periods and drain-cleaning dates before comparing dry steady intervals. Retain uncorrected curves when adjusting for viscosity and examine turbidity and any transported fine particles alongside apparent conductance changes. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：設水頭增至二十五公尺而導水能力不變，預測流量，再加入固定雨水流入求表觀比值，展示如何用乾雨時段分組避免錯誤判讀。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Increase head to twenty-five metres at unchanged conductance and predict flow, then add a fixed rainfall contribution and compute apparent conductance. Demonstrate how separating dry and wet periods prevents a misleading trend interpretation.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：出口堵塞可使量到的排水量降低卻讓內部孔壓升高，不能把低流量一律視為改善；相反地雨水混入排水溝會提高比值，但不一定代表心層發生新的滲流通道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Outlet blockage may lower measured drainage while raising internal pressure, so reduced flow is not automatically improvement. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b217-v15-39-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "將流量與對應時滯後的水頭配對，先標記雨期與清理排水溝日期，再比較乾天穩態區段。以水溫修正黏度影響時保留修正前曲線，並同步檢查排水濁度與細粒是否出現。",
         "textEn": "Pair discharge with appropriately lagged head, marking rain periods and drain-cleaning dates before comparing dry steady intervals. Retain uncorrected curves when adjusting for viscosity and examine turbidity and any transported fine particles alongside apparent conductance changes.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-shihmen-owner",
          "v15s-shihmen-facilities",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b217-v15-39-k2",
         "title": "現場實務",
         "titleEn": "Site practice",
         "text": "設水頭增至二十五公尺而導水能力不變，預測流量，再加入固定雨水流入求表觀比值，展示如何用乾雨時段分組避免錯誤判讀。",
         "textEn": "Increase head to twenty-five metres at unchanged conductance and predict flow, then add a fixed rainfall contribution and compute apparent conductance. Demonstrate how separating dry and wet periods prevents a misleading trend interpretation.",
