       "objective": "說明「梯級發電的能量相加」如何影響德基水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Energy addition across a cascade” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deji Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大甲溪梯級背景讓同一股水在不同高程依序釋放位能，每級只能利用其邊界內的淨水頭。功率應逐級計算再相加，不能把同一股串聯流量先相加又乘總落差。若中間有旁通、蓄水或取水，各級流量也未必相同，能量帳必須跟著水量控制體分段，並保留尾水與上游基準高程。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「梯級發電的能量相加」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "In a cascade, the same water releases potential energy at successive elevations, with each stage using only the net head within its boundary. Stage powers are calculated separately and added; adding the same serial flow first and multiplying by combined head double counts water. Bypass, storage and withdrawals can also make stage flows differ, requiring separate water accounts and explicit upstream and tailwater elevation references. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Energy addition across a cascade” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=15 m3/s; H1=200 m; H2=120 m; eta1=0.9; eta2=0.88; P=rho g Q(H1 eta1+H2 eta2)/1e6=42.02604 MW。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: rho=1000 kg/m3; g=9.81 m/s2; Q=15 m3/s; H1=200 m; H2=120 m; eta1=0.9; eta2=0.88; P=rho g Q(H1 eta1+H2 eta2)/1e6=42.02604 MW.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「串聯兩級流量應先相加再乘上總水頭」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Serial stage discharges should be added before multiplying by total head\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「梯級發電的能量相加」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Energy addition across a cascade”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b218-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "梯級發電的能量相加",
         "titleEn": "Energy addition across a cascade",
         "text": "大甲溪梯級背景讓同一股水在不同高程依序釋放位能，每級只能利用其邊界內的淨水頭。功率應逐級計算再相加，不能把同一股串聯流量先相加又乘總落差。",
         "textEn": "In a cascade, the same water releases potential energy at successive elevations, with each stage using only the net head within its boundary. Stage powers are calculated separately and added; adding the same serial flow first and multiplying by combined head double counts water.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v11x-techi",
          "v15s-deji-wra",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b218-v15-01-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：串聯兩級流量應先相加再乘上總水頭 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Serial stage discharges should be added before multiplying by total head Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
