       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「梯級發電的能量相加」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Energy addition across a cascade” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "分別畫每級進出口能量線，檢查中間尾水是否也是下一級上游基準。以各級電表與同時段流量比對，將中間蓄水變化另外入帳，再核對總電能沒有超過共同水流的可用位能。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Draw inlet and outlet energy lines for each stage and check how intermediate tailwater connects to the next inlet. Compare stage electrical meters with synchronized flow, account separately for intermediate storage and verify that total energy stays below the water's available potential. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將第二級效率降至零點八，重算總功率與差額，再設中間暫存使第二級流量少三立方公尺每秒，分開求能量與蓄量變化而不混算。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Lower second-stage efficiency to zero point eight and recalculate total power. Then reduce its flow by three cubic metres per second through intermediate storage, calculating energy and storage changes in separate accounts.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把兩級流量相加後再乘總水頭會重複計入同一水體；若中間水庫正在蓄水卻仍假設流量立即一致，則會錯配發電時間，讓逐時能量帳失去守恆。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Adding serial discharges and multiplying by combined head counts the same water twice. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
