       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Density underflow velocity scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deji Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "含砂較多的入流水可能比庫水密度大，沿底部向前推進形成密度流。以密度差定義約化重力，再與流層厚度組合可估算浮力控制的速度尺度。這個尺度不是底流實際速度，因為坡度、摩擦、混合與顆粒沉降都會改變流體密度及厚度，沿途不一定維持同一狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「濃密入流的底流尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Sediment-rich inflow can be denser than reservoir water and propagate along the bottom as a density current. Reduced gravity combined with current thickness provides a buoyancy velocity scale. It is not the actual underflow speed, because slope, friction, entrainment and particle settling alter density and thickness as the current advances, so conditions need not remain constant along the irregular reservoir floor. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Density underflow velocity scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
