       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Separate diversion water accounting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Deji Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "跨流域引水增加的是實際通過邊界的水，而非來源集水區全部降雨。德基背景的假想日水量帳把本地入流、引入流、機組用水與其他損失分開，避免把同一水量在來源及目的地重複計入。若隧道或中間池有暫存，兩端同時刻流量也可能不一致，需在更小控制體補上蓄量項。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「越域引水的獨立水量帳」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Interbasin diversion adds water that actually crosses a boundary, not all rainfall over the source catchment. A daily account separates local inflow, imported flow, generation release and other losses to avoid counting one transfer twice. Storage in a tunnel or intermediate pool can make simultaneous endpoint flows differ, requiring an additional storage term in the smaller control volume rather than an unexplained balance error. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Separate diversion water accounting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
