       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Local pressure and cavitation index” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：pabs=80000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=18 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5 rho v2)=0.478395。適用邊界：局部絕對壓力與指定蒸氣壓的假想狀態，不給定設備氣蝕臨界值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: pabs=80000 Pa; pv=2500 Pa; rho=1000 kg/m3; v=18 m/s; sigma=(pabs-pv)/(0.5 rho v2)=0.478395. Applicable boundary: A hypothetical local absolute pressure and specified vapor pressure, without assigning an equipment cavitation threshold. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
