      {
       "id": "b218-v15-40",
       "title": "停機發電量與留存水量：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Outage energy and retained water: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v11x-techi",
        "v15s-deji-wra",
        "v15s-usace-arch",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b218-v15-39"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「停機發電量與留存水量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Outage energy and retained water” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "將少發電量全部當永久損失會忽略留水後補發；反之宣稱所有水都可補發又可能忽略溢流、時間限制與下游需求，兩種極端都沒有完成跨時段水能守恆。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Calling all missing generation permanent loss ignores later use of retained water. Claiming complete recovery can instead ignore spill, timing constraints and downstream demand; both extremes fail to close the multi-period water-energy account. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若水位因留存上升，後續淨水頭也可能變動，使固定功率估計只是一階比較。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Retained water may change level and subsequent net head, making constant-power multiplication only a first-order comparison.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「停機時段少發的電能必然全部永久損失」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All generation absent during an outage is necessarily lost permanently\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b218-v15-40-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "將少發電量全部當永久損失會忽略留水後補發；反之宣稱所有水都可補發又可能忽略溢流、時間限制與下游需求，兩種極端都沒有完成跨時段水能守恆。",
         "textEn": "Calling all missing generation permanent loss ignores later use of retained water. Claiming complete recovery can instead ignore spill, timing constraints and downstream demand; both extremes fail to close the multi-period water-energy account.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v11x-techi",
          "v15s-deji-wra",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b218-v15-40-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v11x-techi",
          "v15s-deji-wra",
          "v15s-usace-arch",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「停機發電量與留存水量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Outage energy and retained water\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。",
