      {
       "id": "b219-v15-03",
       "title": "串聯水庫的內部轉水：試驗與驗證",
       "titleEn": "Internal transfers in serial reservoirs: testing and verification",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
        "v15s-tsengwen-history",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b219-v15-02"
       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「串聯水庫的內部轉水」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。以兩池水位庫容變化獨立核對，避免只因合計帳平衡就忽略某一池資料錯誤。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts. If travel crosses the daily boundary, include storage in the conveyance segment. Independently compare both pool level-volume changes so a balanced total does not conceal an error in one reservoir. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將下游需求增加百分之二十，重新求系統與各池蓄量差，再指定內部轉水八十萬立方公尺每天，證明總帳不因轉水名稱而改變。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Increase downstream demand twenty percent and calculate system and individual changes using a transfer of eight hundred thousand cubic metres per day. Show that relabeling internal transfer cannot alter the combined balance.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-03-k1",
         "title": "驗證方法",
         "titleEn": "Verification method",
         "text": "先各寫一份水量表，再把上游轉出與下游收到配對相消；若旅行時間跨日，需在輸水段另列暫存。以兩池水位庫容變化獨立核對，避免只因合計帳平衡就忽略某一池資料錯誤。",
         "textEn": "Write separate balances and cancel matched upper exports and lower receipts. If travel crosses the daily boundary, include storage in the conveyance segment. Independently compare both pool level-volume changes so a balanced total does not conceal an error in one reservoir.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-03-k2",
         "title": "現場實務",
         "titleEn": "Site practice",
         "text": "將下游需求增加百分之二十，重新求系統與各池蓄量差，再指定內部轉水八十萬立方公尺每天，證明總帳不因轉水名稱而改變。",
         "textEn": "Increase downstream demand twenty percent and calculate system and individual changes using a transfer of eight hundred thousand cubic metres per day. Show that relabeling internal transfer cannot alter the combined balance.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
