      {
       "id": "b219-v15-04",
       "title": "串聯水庫的內部轉水：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Internal transfers in serial reservoirs: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
        "v15s-tsengwen-history",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b219-v15-03"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「串聯水庫的內部轉水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Internal transfers in serial reservoirs” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. Checking only combined storage can hide a lower-pool shortage while water remains upstream but cannot be conveyed quickly enough to meet demand. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：兩池總量增加不代表每池都增加，更不表示水可以立即任意調往任何位置。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: A rise in combined storage does not imply that both pools rise, nor that water can move instantly and freely to any location where demand occurs.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「上下游間轉水會增加兩池合計的新水資源」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Transfer between the two reservoirs creates additional combined water resources\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。",
         "textEn": "Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources. Checking only combined storage can hide a lower-pool shortage while water remains upstream but cannot be conveyed quickly enough to meet demand.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-04-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「串聯水庫的內部轉水」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Internal transfers in serial reservoirs\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。",
         "把內部轉水當成系統新供水會虛增資源；只檢查總蓄量而忽略分池庫存，可能掩蓋下游已接近不足、上游卻有水但無法及時輸送的空間限制。",
         "孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
         "Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.",
         "Counting an internal transfer as new system supply inflates resources.",
