       "objective": "說明「壩體孔壓與有效應力」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "土石壩顆粒骨架承擔有效應力，水的孔隙壓力則分擔總法向應力。以總應力減孔壓可說明排水與蓄水變化如何影響骨架受力，但這是單點應力關係，不直接等於整體抗滑能力。若土未飽和或有明顯各向異性，還需要更適當的有效應力描述與材料參數，不能把飽和模型無條件外推。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壩體孔壓與有效應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The soil skeleton carries effective stress while pore water contributes to total normal stress. Subtracting pore pressure illustrates how drainage and reservoir changes affect skeleton loading, but this point relation does not establish whole-slope resistance. Unsaturated conditions or pronounced anisotropy require additional constitutive description and material parameters, so the saturated model cannot be extended indiscriminately to every location or stage of embankment response. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: sigmaTotal=420 kPa; u=170 kPa; sigmaEff=sigmaTotal-u=250 kPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「壩體孔壓與有效應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
