       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「壩體孔壓與有效應力」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "核對土壓計與測壓管是否代表同一位置、方向與時段，再比較水位升降時兩者變化。將量測高程與水壓基準寫清楚，並以多點剖面辨識局部孔壓，避免把一個平均值套到整個壩坡。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Confirm that earth-pressure and pore-pressure measurements represent matching location, direction and time, then compare their changes during level cycles. Record elevation and pressure datum and use multiple points to identify local conditions rather than assigning one average to an entire slope. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：固定總應力，把孔壓提高五十千帕後重算，再畫總應力、孔壓與有效應力三條示意線，說明若總應力也變動時為何不能只看水壓。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Hold total stress fixed and raise pore pressure fifty kilopascals, then sketch total, pore and effective stress. Explain why pressure alone is insufficient when total stress changes at the same time.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
