      {
       "id": "b219-v15-08",
       "title": "壩體孔壓與有效應力：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Embankment pore pressure and effective stress: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
        "v15s-tsengwen-history",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b219-v15-07"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「壩體孔壓與有效應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Embankment pore pressure and effective stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. During drainage blockage, total stress may stay almost unchanged while skeleton stress falls, so total-pressure observations alone can miss the important change. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若土未飽和或有明顯各向異性，還需要更適當的有效應力描述與材料參數，不能把飽和模型無條件外推。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Unsaturated conditions or pronounced anisotropy require additional constitutive description and material parameters, so the saturated model cannot be extended indiscriminately to every location or stage of embankment response.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「孔隙水壓越高就一定讓土粒骨架承受更大壓應力」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Higher pore pressure necessarily increases compression carried by the soil skeleton\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-08-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把孔壓當作額外壓緊土粒的力而相加，會把有效應力方向算反；排水堵塞時總應力可能近似不變而骨架有效應力下降，僅看總壓力會漏掉變化。",
         "textEn": "Adding pore pressure as extra particle clamping reverses the effective-stress relation. During drainage blockage, total stress may stay almost unchanged while skeleton stress falls, so total-pressure observations alone can miss the important change.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-08-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        }
