       "objective": "說明「假想閘下出流量」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Hypothetical gated underflow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "閘下出流把上游水頭轉成高速水流，開口面積與局部收縮共同控制通量。用孔口形式可作量級比較，但真實閘門出流還要分自由與淹沒狀態，並知道上游能量與尾水。曾文案例的教學參數完全是假想，不是現地閘門開度表，計算目的是理解水頭平方根與開口面積的一次關係。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「假想閘下出流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Gated underflow converts upstream head into high-speed flow, with opening area and contraction controlling discharge. An orifice-style relation supports scale comparison, but actual gates require distinction between free and submerged conditions and knowledge of upstream energy and tailwater. All parameters here are hypothetical rather than a Tsengwen gate schedule; the purpose is to distinguish square-root head dependence from linear dependence on opening area. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hypothetical gated underflow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Cd=0.65; b=4 m; opening=0.8 m; g=9.81 m/s2; H=9 m; Q=Cd b opening sqrt(2gH)=27.63975 m3/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「假想閘下出流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hypothetical gated underflow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
