       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「假想閘下出流量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Hypothetical gated underflow” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "畫出開口中心與自由水面，核對水頭定義後用量水設施求實際係數。比較不同開度的係數是否穩定，記錄尾水變化和水面波動，再決定簡單孔口式是否足以描述該測試區間。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Draw opening center and free surface, verify the head definition and infer discharge coefficient from measurements. Compare coefficients across openings while recording tailwater and surface fluctuations before deciding whether a simple orifice relation describes the tested range. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將假想開口高度減半但暫維持中心水頭，求流量變化，再重新加入中心位置改變，說明分步比較有助於分辨面積與水頭兩種效應。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Halve opening height while temporarily holding center head fixed, then account for the changed center elevation. Explain how the two-step comparison separates area effects from the effect of altered hydraulic head.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
