       "objective": "從症狀倒推「假想閘下出流量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Hypothetical gated underflow” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. Retaining a free-discharge equation after submergence can overstate flow and distort the downstream water balance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：曾文案例的教學參數完全是假想，不是現地閘門開度表，計算目的是理解水頭平方根與開口面積的一次關係。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: All parameters here are hypothetical rather than a Tsengwen gate schedule; the purpose is to distinguish square-root head dependence from linear dependence on opening area.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「不論尾水多高都可以使用相同自由出流公式」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The same free-discharge equation applies regardless of tailwater level\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-16-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把開口高度改變造成的中心高程變化完全忽略，會使大幅開度比較不一致；尾水淹沒後仍使用自由出流式，則可能高估通量並錯配下游水量帳。",
         "textEn": "Ignoring the changing opening-center elevation can make comparisons inconsistent over large opening changes. Retaining a free-discharge equation after submergence can overstate flow and distort the downstream water balance.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b219-v15-16-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-tsengwen-owner",
          "v15s-tsengwen-history",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
