       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "靠近底部的取水可能攜帶較濃泥砂，但輸砂效果應用乾固體質量與放流水量共同衡量，而非只說水看起來很濁。質量濃度本身就是每單位水混合物體積攜帶的固體，乘流量才變成質量率。沉積物是否能被帶到入口，還取決於地形與流場，計算輸出不等於證明整個庫底被清除。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「近底取水的輸砂效率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Withdrawal near the bottom may carry more concentrated sediment, but performance requires both dry-solids mass and released water volume rather than visual darkness. Concentration measures solids per mixture volume, and multiplication by flow gives mass rate. Whether deposits reach the inlet depends on bed geometry and flow, so a calculated export does not demonstrate clearance of the entire reservoir floor or uniform sediment removal. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Q=6 m3/s; C=15 kg/m3; dt=3600 s; M=Q C dt/1000=324 tonne.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「原水越濁就一定代表該時段排出總泥砂越多」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Darker water necessarily means more total sediment was exported during the interval\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「近底取水的輸砂效率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Solids concentration in bottom withdrawal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
