       "objective": "說明「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "開放渠道的平均流速受斷面形狀、濕周、坡度及粗糙阻力共同控制。矩形斷面水力半徑是面積除濕周，不等於水深，尤其窄渠道差異顯著。曼寧式可估算均勻流通水量，但回水、閘門控制或急變流會破壞水面坡與底坡近似相同的條件，需要另作水面線分析。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Mean open-channel velocity depends on geometry, wetted perimeter, slope and roughness. For a rectangular section, hydraulic radius is area divided by wetted perimeter, not simply depth, especially in a narrow canal. Manning's relation estimates uniform-flow capacity, while backwater, gates or rapidly varied flow can invalidate the approximation that energy slope follows bed slope and require a water-surface-profile calculation instead. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Manning scale for an irrigation canal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: b=5 m; y=1.2 m; n=0.025 s/m^(1/3); S=0.0004; A=by=6 m2; R=A/(b+2y); Q=A R^(2/3)sqrt(S)/n=4.173697 m3/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「矩形渠道的水力半徑永遠等於水深」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Hydraulic radius of a rectangular canal always equals its depth\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「灌溉明渠的曼寧尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Manning scale for an irrigation canal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
