       ],
       "objective": "說明「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」如何影響曾文水庫大壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Interpreting crest settlement rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "土石壩壩頂高程隨施工後壓密、材料蠕變、水位及量測基準而改變，兩次高程差除時間只給平均沉陷速率。這個速率不代表未來必然維持直線，也不能單靠向下或向上判斷原因。比較不同測點的空間形狀和時間曲線，通常比單一點的總沉陷量更能辨識差異變形與儀器問題。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Crest elevation can change through consolidation, creep, reservoir cycles and reference movement. Dividing the difference between two surveys by elapsed time gives only an average settlement rate, not a guaranteed future linear trend or a diagnosis from movement direction alone. Spatial patterns across several points and the shape of the time history are often more informative than one accumulated displacement for distinguishing differential deformation from measurement problems. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Interpreting crest settlement rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: settlement1=12 mm; settlement2=21 mm; dt=180 day; rate=(21-12)/dt=0.05 mm/day.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「兩次量測求出的平均沉陷速率必定可永久線性外推」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"An average settlement rate from two surveys can always be extrapolated indefinitely\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「壩頂沉陷的速率解讀」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Interpreting crest settlement rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
