       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Net field need and gross withdrawal” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Tsengwen Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "灌溉淨需水深度乘田區面積得到作物端水量，除以整體輸配效率才得到水源端毛需求。效率是同一邊界下有用水與取水的比值，若已涵蓋渠道損失，就不能再扣一次。不同作物、降雨及回歸水會改變真正需求，這個固定深度例子只用來練習單位與邊界，不代表實際配水規則。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「田間淨需水與毛取水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Net irrigation depth times field area gives water needed at the crop boundary, while division by delivery efficiency gives gross source withdrawal. Efficiency must refer to consistent boundaries; canal losses included in it cannot be deducted again. Crop choice, rainfall and return flows alter real demand, so this fixed-depth exercise teaches units and accounting rather than prescribing allocation or representing a measured seasonal irrigation requirement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Net field need and gross withdrawal” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「毛取水量應把田間淨需水乘上輸配效率」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Gross withdrawal equals net field requirement multiplied by delivery efficiency\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「田間淨需水與毛取水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Net field need and gross withdrawal”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
