       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Net field need and gross withdrawal” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3。適用邊界：淨深度已扣有效降雨，效率含假想輸配損失，不再重複扣減。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: depth=0.6 m; area=200 ha=2000000 m2; eta=0.75; Vgross=depth area/eta=1600000 m3. Applicable boundary: Net depth already excludes effective rainfall and efficiency includes assumed conveyance losses, with no second deduction. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：先將公頃換成平方公尺、毫米換成公尺，再分別列淨需水與毛取水，核對效率分子分母。",
       "observationEn": "How to cross-check: Convert hectares to square metres and millimetres to metres, then list net need and gross withdrawal separately with explicit efficiency boundaries.",
