   "workedExample": {
    "title": "原創假想算例與邊界",
    "titleEn": "Original hypothetical example and boundaries",
    "text": "假想一天本地入流五十萬立方公尺，越域進水三十萬、供水六十萬、其他損失四萬，蓄量增加十六萬立方公尺；若越域水源減半，增加量只剩一萬，不能把集水區降雨全部視為可取水。另用上下兩個高程的水面積四與五平方公里、相差兩公尺，以梯形法得區間庫容九百萬立方公尺。若面積曲線中點較線性插值高百分之十，辛普森估值為九百六十萬，提醒粗糙曲線可能低估而不是保證固定庫容。 核驗：Vlocal=500000 m3/day; Vimport=300000 m3/day; Vsupply=600000 m3/day; Vloss=40000 m3/day; dV=160000 m3/day。對齊本地入流、引水出口和供水流量計的累積時段，以庫水位曲線反推蓄量差核對。標記引水中斷或旅行時間跨日的區段，再將管路暫存補入帳，避免把延遲誤判為水量損失。",
    "textEn": "Assume daily local inflow of 0.5 million m3, diversion of 0.3 million, supply of 0.6 million and other losses of 0.04 million. Storage increases by 0.16 million m3; halving diversion leaves only 0.01 million. Catchment rainfall therefore cannot be counted directly as obtainable supply. Separately, water areas of 4 and 5 km2 separated by 2 m give 9 million m3 by trapezoidal integration. If midpoint area is ten percent above the linear midpoint, Simpson integration gives 9.6 million m3, illustrating sensitivity to the shape of the area curve. Verification: Align cumulative intervals for local inflow, diversion outlet and supply meters, then compare storage inferred from reservoir levels. Mark interruptions and transfers crossing a daily boundary, adding conveyance storage so travel delay is not misidentified as a water loss.",
    "assumptions": "數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。",
    "assumptionsEn": "Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.",
    "sourceScope": "原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。",
    "sourceScopeEn": "Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."
