       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Area curve and interval storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Nanhua Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "庫容不是水面積乘整座壩高，而是面積隨高程積分。相鄰兩個水位的面積可用梯形近似區間體積，這隱含中間面積近似線性變化；若谷地擴寬不均或岸坡轉折，較密高程資料可改善估算。每次地形測量還應保留基準、邊界與淤積年代，否則不同版本差異未必全是沉積造成。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水面積曲線與區間庫容」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Storage is the integral of water area over elevation, not one area multiplied by total dam height. Trapezoidal integration between adjacent levels assumes approximately linear area variation. Abrupt valley widening or bank changes require finer elevation spacing. Survey datum, coverage and date must also remain explicit, because differences between capacity-curve versions do not necessarily arise entirely from deposited sediment or represent the same geometric boundary. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Area curve and interval storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
