       "instructionEn": "Imported and local raw water may contain different concentrations of a conservative dissolved constituent. The blend follows summed solute mass flux divided by total flow. This illustrates source-proportion effects but does not guarantee linear mixing of turbidity, disinfectant demand or settling and reactive constituents. Sampling must account for travel time, otherwise a correct equation can be compared with measurements of different water parcels and appear inconsistent. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conservative mixing of two sources” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
