       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Geometric freeboard and wave allowance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Nanhua Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "土石壩壩頂與水面的高程差是幾何超高，但波浪上爬、風壅水與沉陷可能占用這段距離。把假想餘量逐項扣除可練習垂直基準與符號，不能把結果稱為現地允許水位或安全保證。各項未必同時達峰，實際組合需符合適用設計情境，而且壩頂局部低點比平均高程更相關。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「幾何超高與波浪餘量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Geometric freeboard is the elevation difference between crest and water, but wave runup, wind setup and settlement may use part of that distance. Subtracting assumed allowances teaches datum and sign conventions rather than establishing a permitted level or safety guarantee. Peaks need not coincide, actual combinations require an applicable design scenario, and local low crest points matter more than an average elevation when assessing possible overtopping. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Geometric freeboard and wave allowance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
