       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「幾何超高與波浪餘量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Geometric freeboard and wave allowance” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "查明波浪上爬高度是否已包含風壅水，再核對壩頂量測採目前局部低點或設計高程。畫各項垂直距離並對齊基準，若使用未來沉陷預估，需清楚區分已發生沉陷與額外預留量。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Check whether runup already includes wind setup and whether crest data represent a current local low point or design elevation. Draw all vertical distances on one datum and distinguish settlement already observed from an additional future allowance. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將水面升高一公尺而壩頂不變，重算餘量，再比較波浪上爬增加與壩頂沉陷增加的同量效果，註明相同算術結果不代表相同發生機率。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Raise water level one metre at fixed crest, then compare equal increases in runup and settlement. Recalculate the margins and state why identical arithmetic effects do not imply identical occurrence probabilities.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：將已反映在實測壩頂的沉陷再扣一次會重複保守；忽略局部低點則可能反向樂觀。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Subtracting settlement already included in a measured crest double counts it, while ignoring local low points can be unconservative. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
