       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Catchment storm runoff volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Nanhua Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "暴雨總雨量乘集水面積是降到地表的水量，還需扣除截留、入滲與暫存才成為逕流。簡化逕流係數把多種過程合併成比例，適合體積敏感度但不能直接給洪峰流量。南化背景下若土壤前期含水不同，同樣降雨可能產生不同逕流，因此係數不是不變材料常數，也不是可引入水庫的保證比例。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水區暴雨的逕流體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rain depth times catchment area gives precipitation volume, while interception, infiltration and storage reduce runoff. A simplified runoff coefficient combines these processes for volume sensitivity but does not directly produce peak discharge. Antecedent soil moisture can make identical storms yield different runoff, so the coefficient is not an immutable material constant or a guaranteed fraction that can actually be diverted into the reservoir. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment storm runoff volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
