       ],
       "objective": "設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「集水區暴雨的逕流體積」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。",
       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Catchment storm runoff volume” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "用面雨量而非單一雨量站代表整個集水區，記錄前期降雨與土壤狀態，再積分事件出流並扣除基流比較。將體積估算與洪峰量測分開，不可把總立方公尺直接標成每秒立方公尺。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Use areal rainfall rather than one gauge for the entire basin, record antecedent conditions and compare with integrated event discharge after separating baseflow. Keep volume and peak-flow measurements distinct; cubic metres cannot be relabeled as cubic metres per second. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：將係數設為零點三與零點六，求事件體積上下界，再指定不同匯流歷時畫兩條同體積歷線，說明同體積仍可能具有完全不同的洪峰。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Use coefficients of zero point three and zero point six to bracket event volume, then sketch equal-volume hydrographs with different durations. Explain how the same volume can accompany very different peak discharges.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：把總逕流體積當作瞬時流量會遺失時間尺度；若忽略暴雨前土壤已飽和，固定係數可能低估產流，反之乾土情境又可能高估，必須保留假設方向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Treating runoff volume as instantaneous discharge removes the timescale. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
       "check": "提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。",
       "checkEn": "Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.",
       "knowledge": [
