       "objective": "從症狀倒推「集水區暴雨的逕流體積」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Catchment storm runoff volume” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把總逕流體積當作瞬時流量會遺失時間尺度；若忽略暴雨前土壤已飽和，固定係數可能低估產流，反之乾土情境又可能高估，必須保留假設方向。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating runoff volume as instantaneous discharge removes the timescale. A fixed coefficient may underestimate runoff after prior saturation or overestimate it for dry soil, so interpretation must retain the assumed antecedent condition. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：南化背景下若土壤前期含水不同，同樣降雨可能產生不同逕流，因此係數不是不變材料常數，也不是可引入水庫的保證比例。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Antecedent soil moisture can make identical storms yield different runoff, so the coefficient is not an immutable material constant or a guaranteed fraction that can actually be diverted into the reservoir.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「總逕流體積可直接當作暴雨洪峰流量」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Total runoff volume can directly be treated as peak storm discharge\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
