       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Demand adjustment and static supply duration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Nanhua Dam”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "乾旱時以可用水量除每日需求可得到無入流的靜態續供時間，但水位下降可能使取水能力或水質改變，不能把這個商當作保證供水天數。需求削減也要區分可實現的節水與只是帳面假設。比較不同需求情境時應使用同一有效庫存邊界，保留不能動用的水量，而非把總庫容全部拿來相除。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「乾旱需求調整與靜態續供」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Usable water divided by daily demand gives a no-inflow static duration, but falling level can change intake capacity or quality, so the quotient is not guaranteed supply time. Demand reduction must distinguish achievable savings from an accounting assumption. Scenarios need the same usable-storage boundary and should retain unavailable water rather than dividing gross reservoir capacity by demand and ignoring physical access constraints. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Demand adjustment and static supply duration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
