       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Demand adjustment and static supply duration” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：原創教學假設，以下數值不是本工程實測或設備設定：Vusable=12000000 m3; Dbase=500000 m3/day; reduction=0.15; Dnew=Dbase(1-reduction); T=Vusable/Dnew=28.235294 day。適用邊界：無入流、無其他損失且削減比例可實現，僅作靜態比較。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Original teaching assumptions, not project measurements or equipment settings: Vusable=12000000 m3; Dbase=500000 m3/day; reduction=0.15; Dnew=Dbase(1-reduction); T=Vusable/Dnew=28.235294 day. Applicable boundary: No inflow or other losses and an achievable reduction fraction, for static comparison only. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：先核對可用庫存是否已扣除無法取水的部分，再用實際日需求區間重算，不把單日低需求當長期平均。",
