       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「開口流速與收縮」如何影響荷蘭東斯海爾德防潮閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Opening velocity and contraction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Oosterschelde storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "保留潮汐交換需要流通面積，但墩柱壓縮通道使局部速度上升。斷面平均速度不是閘緣噴流速度，動壓與紊流剪應力又隨速度平方變化。比較同一流量的不同開口，才能看見縮窄後的海床代價。 假設總流量6000 m³/s、有效開口3000 m²，平均流速Q/A=2 m/s；局部面積減20%則為2.5 m/s。只比較準穩定斷面，不模擬迴流。 局部高速帶若穿過未保護接縫，平均流速正常仍可能淘空床層。潮向翻轉會把危險區換邊，因此只有單向測線無法確認完整保護範圍。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「開口流速與收縮」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Preserving tidal exchange requires flow area, while piers contract the channels and accelerate local currents. Section-mean velocity differs from the gate-edge jet. Dynamic pressure and turbulent stresses depend on velocity squared, so comparing openings at fixed discharge reveals the seabed consequences of contraction. Assume discharge 6000 m³/s and effective area 3000 m²: Q/A=2 m/s. Reducing area by twenty percent gives 2.5 m/s. This compares quasi-steady sections and excludes recirculation. A narrow fast jet crossing an unprotected joint may erode the bed despite an acceptable average velocity. Tidal reversal moves the vulnerable side, so one-direction transects cannot establish the full protection footprint. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Opening velocity and contraction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設總流量6000 m³/s、有效開口3000 m²，平均流速Q/A=2 m/s；局部面積減20%則為2.5 m/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume discharge 6000 m³/s and effective area 3000 m²: Q/A=2 m/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「開口平均流速相同就能保證閘緣沖刷完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal opening-average velocity guarantees identical gate-edge scour.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「開口流速與收縮」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Opening velocity and contraction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b221-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "開口流速與收縮",
         "titleEn": "Opening velocity and contraction",
         "text": "保留潮汐交換需要流通面積，但墩柱壓縮通道使局部速度上升。斷面平均速度不是閘緣噴流速度，動壓與紊流剪應力又隨速度平方變化。",
         "textEn": "Preserving tidal exchange requires flow area, while piers contract the channels and accelerate local currents. Section-mean velocity differs from the gate-edge jet.",
