       "objective": "說明「潮稜體與生態交換」如何影響荷蘭東斯海爾德防潮閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Tidal prism and ecological exchange” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Oosterschelde storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "潮稜體衡量一個漲潮期間進出的水量，不能直接當成全部水體換新。港灣分支與渦流會保留舊水，同時影響鹽度與棲地。把幾何儲水量和示蹤交換效率分開，可避免以流量總和誤判生態效果。 假設海灣有效面積80 km²、潮差2 m，棱體AΔh=160 million m³；若完全混合且交換率0.3，等效新水為48 million m³，不含河流。 只用固定面積乘潮差可能漏掉潮灘乾濕變化；把同一團回流海水重複計為新水，也會低估污染物停留時間，掩蓋局部缺氧風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「潮稜體與生態交換」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The tidal prism measures water exchanged during a flood tide, but does not mean every parcel is renewed. Branches and recirculation retain older water and influence salinity and habitats. Separating geometric storage from tracer exchange prevents cumulative flow from being mistaken for ecological renewal. Assume effective bay area 80 km² and tidal range 2 m: AΔh=160 million m³. With complete mixing and exchange efficiency 0.3, effective new water is 48 million m³, excluding rivers. A fixed area times tidal range misses wetting and drying of tidal flats. Counting recirculated seawater repeatedly as new inflow underestimates contaminant residence and can conceal localized oxygen depletion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tidal prism and ecological exchange” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設海灣有效面積80 km²、潮差2 m，棱體AΔh=160 million m³；若完全混合且交換率0.3，等效新水為48 million m³，不含河流。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective bay area 80 km² and tidal range 2 m: AΔh=160 million m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「潮汐交換體積大就能保證每個灣角都迅速換水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A large tidal prism guarantees rapid renewal in every bay corner.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「潮稜體與生態交換」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Tidal prism and ecological exchange”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b221-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "潮稜體與生態交換",
         "titleEn": "Tidal prism and ecological exchange",
         "text": "潮稜體衡量一個漲潮期間進出的水量，不能直接當成全部水體換新。港灣分支與渦流會保留舊水，同時影響鹽度與棲地。",
         "textEn": "The tidal prism measures water exchanged during a flood tide, but does not mean every parcel is renewed. Branches and recirculation retain older water and influence salinity and habitats.",
         "sourceIds": [
