       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Differential hydrostatic gate force” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Oosterschelde storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "閘門承受兩側壓力之差，兩邊都濕潤時不能只畫上游三角形。合力大小與作用點分別決定傳遞到支承的剪力及彎矩；潮位反轉時也必須檢查相反方向的接觸與止水。 取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設直立矩形板寬10 m，兩側水深6及4 m，同密度淡水且靜止；F=ρgb(h1²−h2²)/2=981 kN，不含波浪或海水密度差。 測站基準差會造成虛假淨水頭，導致支承反力估計偏移。若忽略波浪瞬時吸力或門體變形，靜水合力相符仍不能證明焊縫與導輪安全。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙側水壓合力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A gate carries the difference between pressures on its two sides, so a single upstream triangle is insufficient when both sides are wet. Resultant magnitude and elevation determine support shear and moment. Reversing the tide also reverses contact and seal demands. Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume a vertical rectangular plate ten metres wide, still fresh water depths 6 and 4 m: F=ρgb(h1²−h2²)/2=981 kN, excluding waves and seawater density differences. A gauge datum mismatch creates false net head and shifts inferred reactions. Ignoring transient wave suction or gate deformation means agreement with hydrostatic force cannot demonstrate weld or guide-wheel adequacy. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Differential hydrostatic gate force” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「兩側都有水時，只用上游水壓就能得到淨荷載。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
