       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Armor mobility and scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Oosterschelde storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "床粒起動受流體剪應力與顆粒有效重量競爭控制。Shields參數把尺寸和密度納入同一比值，但局部亂流、坡度及石塊咬合會改變實際起動。它適合比較候選護床，不直接決定完整海床保護設計。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設床剪應力30 Pa、石密度2650、水密度1000 kg/m³、粒徑0.1 m；θ=30/((2650−1000)9.81×0.1)=0.01853，非通用臨界值。 邊緣保護長度不足會產生淘刷坑，再向墩底倒退侵蝕。即使石塊本身未被搬走，下面的反濾料被抽出仍可能使護床整片下沉。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「護床起動與尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Particle motion reflects competition between fluid shear and submerged particle weight. The Shields parameter includes size and density, but local turbulence, slope and interlocking alter actual initiation. It compares candidate protection materials without determining a complete seabed protection design. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume shear stress 30 Pa, rock and water densities 2650 and 1000 kg/m³, diameter 0.1 m: θ=30/((2650−1000)9.81×0.1)=0.01853. This is not a universal critical value. Insufficient edge protection creates a scour hole that can migrate back toward the pier. Even immobile armor can subside as a sheet when underlying filter material is removed through its voids. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Armor mobility and scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要護床石塊沒有移動，下方基土就一定沒有流失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Stationary armor guarantees that underlying soil has not been lost.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
