       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「護床起動與尺度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Armor mobility and scale” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "邊緣保護長度不足會產生淘刷坑，再向墩底倒退侵蝕。即使石塊本身未被搬走，下面的反濾料被抽出仍可能使護床整片下沉。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Insufficient edge protection creates a scour hole that can migrate back toward the pier. Even immobile armor can subside as a sheet when underlying filter material is removed through its voids. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：即使石塊本身未被搬走，下面的反濾料被抽出仍可能使護床整片下沉。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Even immobile armor can subside as a sheet when underlying filter material is removed through its voids.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「只要護床石塊沒有移動，下方基土就一定沒有流失。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stationary armor guarantees that underlying soil has not been lost.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b221-v15-20-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "邊緣保護長度不足會產生淘刷坑，再向墩底倒退侵蝕。即使石塊本身未被搬走，下面的反濾料被抽出仍可能使護床整片下沉。",
         "textEn": "Insufficient edge protection creates a scour hole that can migrate back toward the pier. Even immobile armor can subside as a sheet when underlying filter material is removed through its voids.",
