       "objective": "說明「腐蝕餘厚與疲勞」如何影響荷蘭東斯海爾德防潮閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Corrosion allowance and fatigue” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Oosterschelde storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "鹽水環境的板件減薄降低截面能力，但焊趾疲勞又取決於局部應力範圍與循環數。均勻腐蝕速率只做餘厚預測，不能替代點蝕量測或裂紋檢查；維護判讀要把材料損失和疲勞機制分列。 假設初厚20 mm、均勻腐蝕0.08 mm/year、經過15 years，餘厚18.8 mm；若截面寬不變，面積損失6%，不據此推定疲勞壽命。 以平均厚度遮蔽單個深坑會高估局部承載能力；反過來把表面粗糙造成的回波誤差當真減薄也會誤導維護。焊趾裂紋可在餘厚足夠時擴展。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「腐蝕餘厚與疲勞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Saline exposure reduces plate section, while weld fatigue depends on local stress range and cycle count. Uniform corrosion rate predicts remaining thickness but cannot replace pitting surveys or crack inspection. Maintenance interpretation must separate material loss from cyclic damage. Assume initial thickness 20 mm and uniform corrosion 0.08 mm/year over 15 years. Remaining thickness is 18.8 mm and area loss is six percent at constant width; fatigue life is not inferred. Average thickness can conceal a deep local pit and overstate resistance, while roughness-related echo error can imitate thinning. Weld-toe cracks may continue growing even where remaining gross thickness appears adequate. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Corrosion allowance and fatigue” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設初厚20 mm、均勻腐蝕0.08 mm/year、經過15 years，餘厚18.8 mm；若截面寬不變，面積損失6%，不據此推定疲勞壽命。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume initial thickness 20 mm and uniform corrosion 0.08 mm/year over 15 years.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要板件餘厚足夠，焊縫就不可能存在疲勞裂紋。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Adequate remaining plate thickness rules out fatigue cracks at welds.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「腐蝕餘厚與疲勞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Corrosion allowance and fatigue”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b221-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "腐蝕餘厚與疲勞",
         "titleEn": "Corrosion allowance and fatigue",
         "text": "鹽水環境的板件減薄降低截面能力，但焊趾疲勞又取決於局部應力範圍與循環數。均勻腐蝕速率只做餘厚預測，不能替代點蝕量測或裂紋檢查；維護判讀要把材料損失和疲勞機制分列。",
         "textEn": "Saline exposure reduces plate section, while weld fatigue depends on local stress range and cycle count. Uniform corrosion rate predicts remaining thickness but cannot replace pitting surveys or crack inspection.",
         "sourceIds": [
