       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b222-v15-03"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「浮運吃水與壓載」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Floating draft and ballast” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "艙內自由液面會削弱穩定性，即使總浮力平衡也可能出現傾斜。若一側進水較快，剛體平均吃水模型便漏掉扭轉與局部碰撞的危險。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Internal free surfaces reduce stability even when total buoyancy balances weight. Unequal filling creates tilt, so a mean-draft model misses twisting and local collision hazards during the transition. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若一側進水較快，剛體平均吃水模型便漏掉扭轉與局部碰撞的危險。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Unequal filling creates tilt, so a mean-draft model misses twisting and local collision hazards during the transition.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「浮力與重量平衡就能保證門體漂浮姿態穩定。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Balanced buoyancy and weight guarantee a stable floating attitude.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b222-v15-04-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "艙內自由液面會削弱穩定性，即使總浮力平衡也可能出現傾斜。若一側進水較快，剛體平均吃水模型便漏掉扭轉與局部碰撞的危險。",
         "textEn": "Internal free surfaces reduce stability even when total buoyancy balances weight. Unequal filling creates tilt, so a mean-draft model misses twisting and local collision hazards during the transition.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-rws-maeslant",
          "v15s-hollandia-maeslant",
          "v15s-rws-east",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
