       "objective": "說明「支臂壓桿穩定」如何影響荷蘭馬仕朗防潮閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Arm compression-member stability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Maeslant storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "細長支臂桿件可能先失穩再達材料降伏，端部拘束決定有效長度。理想歐拉式只說明幾何敏感性，實際彎曲與殘餘應力需另外處理。 假設E=200 GPa、I=0.08 m⁴、鉸支長40 m，Pcr=π²EI/L²=98.696 MN；理想直桿彈性屈曲，未含缺陷或設計折減。 節點腐蝕或鬆動會改變端部拘束，讓先前的有效長度假設失效。若只檢查材料強度，便可能漏掉受壓桿件突然出現的側向失穩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「支臂壓桿穩定」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A slender arm member can buckle before yielding, and end restraint sets effective length. Euler theory illustrates geometric sensitivity but leaves initial curvature and residual stresses to separate assessment. Assume E=200 GPa, I=0.08 m⁴ and pinned length 40 m. Pcr=π²EI/L²=98.696 MN, for an ideal straight elastic member without imperfections or design reductions. Joint corrosion or looseness changes end restraint and invalidates an earlier effective length. Checking material strength alone can miss sudden lateral instability in an otherwise apparently adequate compression member. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arm compression-member stability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=200 GPa、I=0.08 m⁴、鉸支長40 m，Pcr=π²EI/L²=98.696 MN；理想直桿彈性屈曲，未含缺陷或設計折減。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=200 GPa, I=0.08 m⁴ and pinned length 40 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「鋼材尚未降伏時，細長受壓桿件就不可能屈曲。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A slender compression member cannot buckle before its steel yields.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
