       "objective": "說明「曲面門水壓分解」如何影響荷蘭馬仕朗防潮閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Resolving pressure on curved gates” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Maeslant storm-surge barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "曲面水壓應按法向分布積分，水平分量可由垂直投影求得，垂直分量則與上覆假想水體有關。曲面面積不能直接乘最大壓力。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設垂直投影寬20 m、水深5 m、單側靜水密度1025 kg/m³；水平分量ρgbh²/2=2.514 MN，未求曲面垂直分量。 把水壓視為全水平會漏掉浮沉方向荷載，影響壓載與接觸判斷。波浪使壓力隨時間和位置改變，靜水分量不能代表瞬間最大合力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「曲面門水壓分解」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Pressure acts normal to a curved surface. Its horizontal component follows the vertical projection, while its vertical component relates to an imaginary overlying water volume; surface area times maximum pressure is inappropriate. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume vertical projection width 20 m, one-sided depth 5 m and water density 1025 kg/m³. Horizontal force ρgbh²/2=2.514 MN; the curved-surface vertical component remains separate. Treating all pressure as horizontal misses vertical loading that affects ballast and contact. Waves vary pressure in time and space, so the hydrostatic component cannot represent the maximum transient resultant. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Resolving pressure on curved gates” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「曲面門體的靜水壓合力永遠只有水平方向分量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Hydrostatic loading on a curved gate always has only a horizontal component.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「曲面門水壓分解」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Resolving pressure on curved gates”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
