       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b223-v15-28"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「波浪脈衝與反力」如何影響泰晤士河防洪閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Wave impulse and reaction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Thames Barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "波浪撞擊的峰值和持續時間共同決定脈衝，短脈衝對柔性構件的作用不同於同峰值的長載重。靜水壓力不能替代瞬態結構反應。 假設三角形力脈衝峰值2 MN、歷時0.4 s，衝量J=FmaxΔt/2=0.4 MN·s；未由此直接求位移或疲勞。 低取樣率可能完全漏掉撞擊峰值，過度放大峰值而忽略面積與相位也會誤判總力。氣泡含量及局部接觸使相鄰壓力計不一定同步到峰。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波浪脈衝與反力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Wave impact depends on both peak and duration. A short impulse affects a flexible member differently from a sustained load of equal peak, so hydrostatics cannot substitute for transient structural response. Assume a triangular force pulse with peak 2 MN and duration 0.4 s. Impulse J=FmaxΔt/2=0.4 MN·s; displacement and fatigue are not obtained from this alone. Low sampling may miss impact peaks, while multiplying one peak over the entire area misstates total force. Air content and local contact mean adjacent sensors need not peak simultaneously. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave impulse and reaction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形力脈衝峰值2 MN、歷時0.4 s，衝量J=FmaxΔt/2=0.4 MN·s；未由此直接求位移或疲勞。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a triangular force pulse with peak 2 MN and duration 0.4 s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「一個壓力計的瞬間峰值能直接代表整門瞬時合力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"One sensor pressure peak directly represents the instantaneous whole-gate resultant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「波浪脈衝與反力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave impulse and reaction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b223-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "波浪脈衝與反力",
         "titleEn": "Wave impulse and reaction",
         "text": "波浪撞擊的峰值和持續時間共同決定脈衝，短脈衝對柔性構件的作用不同於同峰值的長載重。靜水壓力不能替代瞬態結構反應。",
         "textEn": "Wave impact depends on both peak and duration. A short impulse affects a flexible member differently from a sustained load of equal peak, so hydrostatics cannot substitute for transient structural response.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ea-thames",
          "v15s-ea-thames40",
          "v15s-archives-thames",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b223-v15-29-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：一個壓力計的瞬間峰值能直接代表整門瞬時合力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: One sensor pressure peak directly represents the instantaneous whole-gate resultant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ea-thames",
          "v15s-ea-thames40",
          "v15s-archives-thames",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
