      {
       "id": "b223-v15-37",
       "title": "海平面情境與調適：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Sea-level scenarios and adaptation: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-ea-thames",
        "v15s-ea-thames40",
        "v15s-archives-thames",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b223-v15-36"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「海平面情境與調適」如何影響泰晤士河防洪閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Sea-level scenarios and adaptation” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Thames Barrier”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "長期海平面變化會改變關閉頻率、河流排水窗口和維護時間，而不只提高一道設計水位。情境外推用來比較方案，並非保證未來趨勢。 假設線性相對海平面上升5 mm/year持續40 years，增量0.20 m；另假設加速項0.05 mm/year²，額外0.5at²=0.04 m。 以單一線性速率規劃全部壽命，可能忽略加速、區域沉降與潮汐改變。若只加高牆體而不評估關閉增加，設備疲勞和內河排水需求仍可能失配。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「海平面情境與調適」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Long-term sea-level change affects closure frequency, drainage windows and maintenance time, not only a design level. Scenario extrapolation compares options rather than guaranteeing a future trend. Assume linear relative sea-level rise 5 mm/year over 40 years, giving 0.20 m. An assumed acceleration 0.05 mm/year² adds 0.5at²=0.04 m. One linear rate may miss acceleration, local subsidence and tidal change. Raising walls without examining more frequent closures can leave equipment fatigue and inland drainage demands poorly matched. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sea-level scenarios and adaptation” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設線性相對海平面上升5 mm/year持續40 years，增量0.20 m；另假設加速項0.05 mm/year²，額外0.5at²=0.04 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume linear relative sea-level rise 5 mm/year over 40 years, giving 0.20 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「長期調適只需把海平面增量加到牆頂，其他功能不受影響。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Long-term adaptation only adds sea-level rise to crest height without affecting other functions.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「海平面情境與調適」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Sea-level scenarios and adaptation”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b223-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "海平面情境與調適",
         "titleEn": "Sea-level scenarios and adaptation",
         "text": "長期海平面變化會改變關閉頻率、河流排水窗口和維護時間，而不只提高一道設計水位。情境外推用來比較方案，並非保證未來趨勢。",
         "textEn": "Long-term sea-level change affects closure frequency, drainage windows and maintenance time, not only a design level. Scenario extrapolation compares options rather than guaranteeing a future trend.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ea-thames",
          "v15s-ea-thames40",
          "v15s-archives-thames",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b223-v15-37-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：長期調適只需把海平面增量加到牆頂，其他功能不受影響。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Long-term adaptation only adds sea-level rise to crest height without affecting other functions. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ea-thames",
          "v15s-ea-thames40",
          "v15s-archives-thames",
