       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「浮力翻轉與重心」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Buoyant rotation and centroids” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。上浮不是氣壓直接把整片門推出水面，還必須考慮外部水壓和重心位置。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效排水體積500 m³、海水密度1025 kg/m³、浮力臂3 m，自重3 MN、重心臂4 m；淨復原矩為3.083 MN·m，限靜水姿態。 氣室進水不均會移動重心，改變各鉸座受力。若把完全浸沒的浮力公式沿用到出水後，排水體積與力臂都會錯，進而誤判平衡角度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「浮力翻轉與重心」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge. Rotation is not simply air pressure pushing the entire gate upward; external pressure and centroid positions also matter. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture. Unequal flooding shifts the center of gravity and hinge reactions. Reusing fully submerged buoyancy after emergence gives incorrect displacement and lever arms, leading to a false equilibrium angle. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Buoyant rotation and centroids” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「總浮力大於自重就能直接決定翻板的唯一平衡角。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Buoyancy exceeding weight directly determines the unique flap equilibrium angle.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「浮力翻轉與重心」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Buoyant rotation and centroids”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b224-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "浮力翻轉與重心",
         "titleEn": "Buoyant rotation and centroids",
         "text": "翻板內水被空氣置換後，浮力和自重對鉸軸的力矩改變，門體才會轉動。上浮不是氣壓直接把整片門推出水面，還必須考慮外部水壓和重心位置。",
         "textEn": "Replacing internal water with air changes buoyancy and weight moments about the hinge. Rotation is not simply air pressure pushing the entire gate upward; external pressure and centroid positions also matter.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-mose-test",
          "v15s-venice-first",
          "v15s-abb-mose",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
