         "textEn": "Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume displaced volume 500 m³, seawater density 1025 kg/m³, buoyancy arm 3 m, weight 3 MN and weight arm 4 m. Net restoring moment is 3.083 MN·m for that hydrostatic posture.",
