       "objective": "說明「空氣供應與壓縮功」如何影響威尼斯 MOSE 防潮系統的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Air supply and compression work” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "壓縮機功率取決於壓比、流量、熱交換和效率，注入體積不是同壓力下的自由空氣體積。理想等溫模型提供能耗下界，不能代表真實機組效率。 假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。 壓縮熱若未散去，等溫假設會低估功率；漏氣又使供氣量不等於有效排水量。把氣量和門體位移直接一對一換算，會漏掉可壓縮儲能。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「空氣供應與壓縮功」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Compressor power depends on pressure ratio, flow, heat exchange and efficiency. Delivered volume is not free-air volume at the same pressure. Ideal isothermal work is a lower-bound model, not an actual machine rating. Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa. Ideal isothermal power p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW, excluding mechanical and thermal losses. Incomplete heat rejection makes the isothermal estimate optimistic, and leakage separates supplied air from effective displacement. Equating air volume directly with gate movement ignores compressible energy stored in the system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Air supply and compression work” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設自由空氣流量2 m³/s、入口絕壓100 kPa、出口200 kPa，等溫理想功率p1Q1ln(p2/p1)=138.63 kW；未含機械與熱損失。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume free-air flow 2 m³/s, inlet absolute pressure 100 kPa and outlet 200 kPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「供氣量增加一定等比例增加浮門的排水體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
