       "instructionEn": "Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error. Subtract raw edge-displacement histories directly, compare with the phase formula and quantify sensitivity to timestamp error. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：以相鄰門片相對位移編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。同步量測相鄰門角並換算同一高度的邊緣位移，保留相位資訊；把靜態公差、熱變形與動態間隙分列，檢查時間同步誤差。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for relative motion between gates, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Synchronize adjacent gate angles and convert them to edge displacement at one elevation. Retain phase and separate static tolerance, thermal distortion and dynamic clearance, checking synchronization error.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：兩套感測器若時鐘不一致，可能製造假的反相訊號。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Unsynchronized clocks can create a false out-of-phase response. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
