       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "防潮時海口交換減少，但潟湖降雨和陸域排水仍在加入水量。水面面積使水位對體積敏感度不同，內部風致增水又會打破均勻水位假設。 假設封閉水面100 km²、降雨20 mm且全部直接入水，增量2 million m³、水位上升0.02 m；未含陸域逕流、蒸發或漏流。 將整個流域雨量直接乘潟湖面積會混淆陸地與水面貢獻，地下水和支流也有延遲。只看封閉後平均水位，可能漏掉城市沿岸的局部高水位。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「關閉潟湖降雨收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Reducing inlet exchange does not stop rainfall or land drainage into the lagoon. Surface area controls stage sensitivity to volume, while wind setup can invalidate a uniform water level assumption. Assume isolated surface area 100 km² and direct rainfall 20 mm. Added volume is 2 million m³ and mean rise 0.02 m, excluding land runoff, evaporation and leakage. Multiplying catchment rain by lagoon area confuses land and open-water contributions, while groundwater and tributaries are delayed. Mean lagoon level can miss locally higher levels along urban shores. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rainfall balance in an isolated lagoon” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
