       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Pressure measurement uncertainty” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Venice MOSE flood barriers”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "以壓力反推水深時，密度與感測誤差都進入結果。壓力計精度不是整體水位精度，導壓高程、氣泡和溫度也需要校核。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設壓力標準不確定度500 Pa、密度1025 kg/m³且暫視為精確，uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m；僅此誤差分量，非總誤差。 共同導壓管堵塞會讓多支感測器一致但錯誤，不能用數字吻合當獨立證據。若海水密度變動仍沿用淡水換算，也會產生持續水深偏差。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力量測與不確定度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Inferring depth from pressure involves both density and sensor error. Transducer accuracy is not complete level accuracy because tapping elevation, trapped air and temperature also require checking. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume pressure standard uncertainty 500 Pa and density 1025 kg/m³ treated as exact. uh=up/(ρg)=0.04973 m, representing this component only rather than total error. A shared blocked impulse line can make several sensors agree incorrectly. Agreement is not independence, and using freshwater density for changing seawater creates a persistent inferred-depth bias. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure measurement uncertainty” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「壓力感測器讀數一致就證明共同取壓管沒有問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Matching pressure readings prove the shared impulse connection has no defect.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
