       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「集水區逕流峰值」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Catchment runoff peak” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。合理化公式適合指定的小型集水區條件，不能直接代表整個大型水庫入流歷線。 假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。 短時局部暴雨可能不符合均勻降雨假設，排水瓶頸也會改變峰值時間。把每個分區峰值直接相加，可能錯估各峰不同時到達的真實入流。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水區逕流峰值」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak. The rational method applies to specified small-catchment conditions, not a complete large-reservoir inflow hydrograph. Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time. Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s, excluding channel storage. Brief localized storms violate uniform rainfall assumptions, and drainage bottlenecks alter peak timing. Adding every subcatchment peak directly can misrepresent the actual combined inflow when peaks arrive at different times. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Catchment runoff peak” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設集水區2 km²、C=0.75、雨強60 mm/h且歷時超過集流時間；Q=0.278CiA=25.02 m³/s，未含渠道滯蓄。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume area 2 km², C=0.75 and intensity 60 mm/h lasting beyond concentration time.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「各分區最大流量無須考慮時序就能直接相加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Subcatchment peak discharges can be added directly without considering their timing.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「集水區逕流峰值」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Catchment runoff peak”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b225-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "集水區逕流峰值",
         "titleEn": "Catchment runoff peak",
         "text": "都市不透水面提高快速逕流比例，但降雨空間與集流時間控制峰值。合理化公式適合指定的小型集水區條件，不能直接代表整個大型水庫入流歷線。",
         "textEn": "Impervious surfaces increase rapid runoff, while rainfall distribution and concentration time control the peak. The rational method applies to specified small-catchment conditions, not a complete large-reservoir inflow hydrograph.",
         "sourceIds": [
