       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Low-tide gravity drainage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "庫水高於海水時可由水頭差驅動排水，潮位反轉則可能失去這項能力。閘口流況隨上下游淹沒程度改變，單一係數不能代表全部潮相。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設有效孔口20 m²、Cd=0.65、水頭差0.5 m；Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s，限淹沒孔口準穩定流。 水頭接近零時儀器偏差可能比真實差值更大，造成錯判流向。忽略海側波浪與回流時，即使平均水頭為正，也不能保證瞬間全向外排水。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「低潮重力排水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A positive reservoir-to-sea head can drive gravity drainage, but tidal reversal removes it. Opening hydraulics vary with downstream submergence, so one coefficient does not describe every tide. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective opening 20 m², Cd=0.65 and head difference 0.5 m. Q=CdA√(2gΔh)=40.72 m³/s, for quasi-steady submerged-orifice flow. Near zero head, instrument bias may exceed the real difference and reverse the inferred direction. Waves and return currents can create inward flow even with positive mean outward head. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Low-tide gravity drainage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
