       "objective": "說明「高平均潮位抽水」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Pumping against elevated tide” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "抽水把水量提升到較高海側水位，需要克服靜揚程和管路損失。功率隨流量與揚程變化，不能用固定每立方公尺能耗描述所有潮況。 取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。假設淡水Q=20 m³/s、總揚程3 m、總效率0.8；輸入P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW，不含啟動電流或備援負載。 揚程增加可能使泵流量下降，同時改變效率與振動。只看設備已通電會高估排水能力；忽略輔助設備能耗也會低估整場暴雨的能源需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高平均潮位抽水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Pumping lifts water against sea level and conveyance losses. Power varies with both flow and head, so a fixed energy per cubic metre cannot describe all tidal conditions. Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s². Assume fresh-water flow 20 m³/s, total head 3 m and overall efficiency 0.8. Input P=ρgQH/η=735.75 kW, excluding starting current and auxiliary backup loads. Increasing head may reduce pump flow while changing efficiency and vibration. Energized equipment does not establish drainage capacity, and omitting auxiliary loads understates energy required for the complete storm event. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pumping against elevated tide” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³、g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³ and g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「抽水機已經運轉就表示一定達到額定排水流量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A running pump necessarily delivers its rated drainage flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「高平均潮位抽水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pumping against elevated tide”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
