       "objective": "說明「並聯泵與系統曲線」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Parallel pumps and system curve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。因此兩台流量不是把單台自由出水流量直接相加。 曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。假設單泵H=10−0.01q²、系統H=2+0.005Q²，兩泵相同且Q=2q；解得Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s。 兩台老化程度不同會造成不均分流，甚至低流量機組接近不穩定區。忽略共用管損的加倍估算，通常會高估新增泵帶來的容量提升。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「並聯泵與系統曲線」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Parallel pumps share a discharge system. Adding units increases losses and shifts each operating point, so combined flow is not simply twice a single pump free-discharge rate. For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s. Intercepts 10 and 2 have units m; coefficients 0.01 and 0.005 both have units s²/m⁵. Assume each pump H=10−0.01q² and system H=2+0.005Q², with two identical pumps Q=2q. Solving gives Q=√(8/0.0075)=32.66 m³/s. Unequal ageing creates unequal sharing and may place one unit near an unstable low-flow region. Doubling capacity while ignoring shared losses typically overstates the benefit of adding another pump. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Parallel pumps and system curve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：曲線採H以m、q與Q以m³/s表示；截距10、2的單位為m，係數0.01、0.005的單位均為s²/m⁵。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: For these dimensional curves H is in m and q and Q are in m³/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「並聯兩台相同泵的總流量必定是單台的兩倍。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Two identical parallel pumps always deliver twice the single-pump flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「並聯泵與系統曲線」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Parallel pumps and system curve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b225-v15-17-k1",
         "title": "並聯泵與系統曲線",
         "titleEn": "Parallel pumps and system curve",
         "text": "並聯泵共享同一出水系統，增加機組會提高管損，單機工作點也移動。因此兩台流量不是把單台自由出水流量直接相加。",
         "textEn": "Parallel pumps share a discharge system. Adding units increases losses and shifts each operating point, so combined flow is not simply twice a single pump free-discharge rate.",
         "sourceIds": [
