       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b225-v15-20"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Cavitation margin and suction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。淨正吸入水頭需使用絕對壓力，且和廠商所定試驗條件分開比較。 假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。 低水位與堵塞會同時降低可用吸入水頭，吸入空氣也會產生類似汽蝕的噪音。以冷水汽化壓代表熱天水況，可能誇大實際餘裕。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers. Available net positive suction head uses absolute pressure and must be compared with the manufacturer test definition. Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m. NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m. Low level and blockage both reduce available suction head, while entrained air can imitate cavitation noise. Using cold-water vapor pressure for warm conditions may exaggerate the available margin. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Cavitation margin and suction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設大氣水頭10.3 m、吸水靜高1.5 m、吸管損失0.8 m、汽化水頭0.3 m，NPSHa=10.3+1.5−0.8−0.3=10.7 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume atmospheric head 10.3 m, positive suction static head 1.5 m, suction loss 0.8 m and vapor head 0.3 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「沒有明顯噪音就足以證明吸水條件有足夠餘裕。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Absence of obvious noise proves sufficient suction-head margin.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「汽蝕餘裕與吸水」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Cavitation margin and suction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b225-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "汽蝕餘裕與吸水",
         "titleEn": "Cavitation margin and suction",
         "text": "吸水側壓力若接近水的汽化壓，氣泡形成與崩潰會傷害葉片。淨正吸入水頭需使用絕對壓力，且和廠商所定試驗條件分開比較。",
         "textEn": "Vapor bubbles form and collapse when suction pressure approaches vapor pressure, damaging impellers. Available net positive suction head uses absolute pressure and must be compared with the manufacturer test definition.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-pub-marina",
          "v15s-pub-marina-faq",
          "v15s-pub-marina-book",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
