       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Salt intrusion mass balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "淡水庫的鹽度受微量海水入侵影響，鹽水密度較大會先沿底部擴散。平均混合模型只能估算總鹽量，不能代表取水口短時濃度。 假設淡水體積1 million m³、混入1000 m³海水鹽度35 g/kg，同密度完全混合；平均鹽度35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg。 稀釋後平均值很低仍可能有高鹽舌接近取水口，風浪混合也可能突然把底水抬升。只在表層採樣，會誤認鹽水已完全排除。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鹽水入侵質量平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Small seawater intrusions affect a freshwater reservoir, and denser water can spread along the bottom first. A mean-mixing model estimates total salt but not short-term intake concentration. Assume freshwater volume 1 million m³ and intrusion 1000 m³ at 35 g/kg, equal densities and complete mixing. Mean salinity is 35×1000/1001000=0.03497 g/kg. A low diluted mean can coexist with a saline tongue near an intake. Wind mixing may suddenly lift bottom water, while surface-only sampling can falsely suggest intrusion has been removed. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Salt intrusion mass balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
