    {
     "id": "b225-v15-s5",
     "title": "耐久、維護與工程交接",
     "titleEn": "Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「攔污柵損失與堵塞」與「複合事件與失效組合」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Screen losses and blockage\" and \"Compound events and failure combinations\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b225-v15-33",
       "title": "攔污柵損失與堵塞：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Screen losses and blockage: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-pub-marina",
        "v15s-pub-marina-faq",
        "v15s-pub-marina-book",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b225-v15-32"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「攔污柵損失與堵塞」如何影響新加坡濱海堤壩的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Screen losses and blockage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Marina Barrage”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。損失係數與速度必須使用相容的面積定義，否則會重複計算堵塞影響。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設通過柵格的有效速度1.5 m/s、損失係數K=2，hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；K已對應該速度定義，不再另加堵塞倍數。 堵塞不均會把水流集中到少數開口，引發局部振動與吸氣。差壓增加也可能來自流量增大，因此未正規化的趨勢不能直接當作堵塞程度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「攔污柵損失與堵塞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area. Loss coefficient and velocity must use compatible area definitions to avoid counting the blockage effect twice. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective screen velocity 1.5 m/s and loss coefficient K=2. hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m; K corresponds to that velocity definition, without another blockage multiplier. Uneven blockage concentrates flow through a few openings, promoting vibration and air entrainment. Increased differential head can also reflect increased flow, so an unnormalized trend does not directly measure blockage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Screen losses and blockage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「差壓增加只可能來自攔污柵堵塞，與流量無關。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Higher screen differential head only indicates blockage and is unrelated to flow.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「攔污柵損失與堵塞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Screen losses and blockage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b225-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "攔污柵損失與堵塞",
         "titleEn": "Screen losses and blockage",
         "text": "攔污柵保護設備卻增加水頭損失，堵塞使有效流通面積縮小。損失係數與速度必須使用相容的面積定義，否則會重複計算堵塞影響。",
         "textEn": "Screens protect equipment but consume head, and blockage reduces open area. Loss coefficient and velocity must use compatible area definitions to avoid counting the blockage effect twice.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-pub-marina",
          "v15s-pub-marina-faq",
          "v15s-pub-marina-book",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
