         "textEn": "Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume effective screen velocity 1.5 m/s and loss coefficient K=2. hL=Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m; K corresponds to that velocity definition, without another blockage multiplier.",
