   "contentStatus": "reviewable-educational-curriculum",
   "summary": "本課以巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘為入口，深入節水池耦合、非恆定充洩水與滾動閘門的定量深化。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。",
   "summaryEn": "Using Panama Canal expansion locks as its entry point, this course examines quantitative extension of basin coupling, unsteady filling and rolling-gate mechanics. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.",
   "focus": "節水池耦合、非恆定充洩水與滾動閘門的定量深化",
   "focusEn": "Quantitative extension of basin coupling, unsteady filling and rolling-gate mechanics",
   "scope": "依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。",
   "scopeEn": "Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.",
