       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Equalization between two pools” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "兩個有限面積水體連通時，兩邊水位都會改變，不能把節水池當無限水源。守恆終點只由初始體積與面積決定，達到終點的時間則另受管路控制。 假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。 把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙池水位均衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Connecting two finite pools changes both levels, so a saving basin is not an infinite reservoir. Conservation determines the equilibrium endpoint from initial storage and areas, while conduits separately determine how quickly it is approached. Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas. Equalized level is (20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m. Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equalization between two pools” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設閘室面積20000 m²、水位10 m，池面積10000 m²、水位4 m，同基準且斷面固定；均衡水位(20000×10+10000×4)/30000=8 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume chamber area 20000 m² at level 10 m and basin area 10000 m² at 4 m, common datum and fixed areas.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「雙池水位均衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Equalization between two pools”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
