         "textEn": "Integrate area times level change on each side and check equal opposite exchange volumes. Use valve and flow histories to diagnose slowing near equilibrium instead of comparing endpoints alone. Separately calculate chamber loss and basin gain and verify that the shared endpoint closes both control-volume balances.",
