       "objective": "從症狀倒推「雙池水位均衡」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Equalization between two pools” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "把較小池當固定水頭會高估可回用水量，忽略連通管容積和漏流也會破壞守恆。若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Treating the smaller basin as fixed head overstates recoverable water. Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若兩水位計基準不同，甚至會虛構無法解釋的水量損失。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Conduit storage, leakage and mismatched gauge datums can also break the apparent balance and create fictitious unexplained water losses.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「節水池即使面積有限，交換水量時水位仍保持不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A finite saving basin maintains constant level while exchanging water.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
