      {
       "id": "b226-v15-05",
       "title": "充水歷線與慣性：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Filling hydrograph and inertia: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-acp-open",
        "v7-panama-basins",
        "v7-panama-expanded",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b226-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「充水歷線與慣性」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Filling hydrograph and inertia” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。平均充水時間無法表示瞬時最大流量。 假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。 同一總水量可以由溫和或尖峰歷線達成，船舶受力卻不同。若僅用完成時間驗收，可能漏掉局部流速、壓力振盪和繫纜張力峰值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「充水歷線與慣性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow. Early acceleration and late deceleration also create surface slopes affecting vessels, so average filling time cannot represent peak discharge. Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s. Volume is 180000 m³ and rise over 22500 m² is 8 m, not a site operating hydrograph. Equal total volumes can arise from gentle or peaked hydrographs with different vessel loads. Completion time alone misses local velocities, pressure oscillations and maximum mooring tensions during the filling cycle. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Filling hydrograph and inertia” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設三角形充水歷線峰值300 m³/s、總歷時1200 s，水量0.5Qt=180000 m³；閘面積22500 m²則升8 m，非本站運轉歷線。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular filling hydrograph with peak 300 m³/s over 1200 s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「充水歷線與慣性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Filling hydrograph and inertia”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b226-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "充水歷線與慣性",
         "titleEn": "Filling hydrograph and inertia",
         "text": "船閘水位上升速度取決於當時淨流量，初期加速和末期減速產生的水面坡度又影響船舶受力。平均充水時間無法表示瞬時最大流量。",
         "textEn": "Lock level rises with instantaneous net flow. Early acceleration and late deceleration also create surface slopes affecting vessels, so average filling time cannot represent peak discharge.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-acp-open",
          "v7-panama-basins",
          "v7-panama-expanded",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b226-v15-05-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：充水量和總時間相同就表示所有瞬時水力荷載相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Equal filling volume and total duration imply identical transient hydraulic loads. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-acp-open",
          "v7-panama-basins",
          "v7-panama-expanded",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
