       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Density-exchange front” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "海水與淡水連通時，即使兩側表面水位相同，密度差仍可驅動底層鹽水前進和上層淡水返回。這種交換不能用零淨流量判定不存在。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設密度差25 kg/m³、基準1000 kg/m³、水深5 m，約化重力g′=0.24525 m/s²，速度尺度√(g′h)=1.107 m/s；非精確前緣速度。 表層看似沒有入流時底層仍可向內輸送鹽分，傳感器只設單一深度會漏判。強紊流又會改變界面厚度，使理想兩層模型失效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「密度交換前緣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Connected salt and fresh water can exchange through bottom and surface currents even at equal surface elevations. Zero net discharge therefore does not establish absence of density-driven exchange. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume density difference 25 kg/m³, reference density 1000 kg/m³ and depth 5 m. Reduced gravity is 0.24525 m/s² and √(g′h)=1.107 m/s, a scale rather than an exact front speed. Salt can enter along the bed while the surface appears still, making one-depth sensing inadequate. Strong turbulence thickens the interface and can invalidate an ideal two-layer description of exchange. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Density-exchange front” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
