       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "滾動門靠輪組與浮力共同承受重量，水位改變會重新分配輪載。減輕平均輪載有利移動，但偏心、軌道沉降和門體變形仍可能使個別輪子受力集中。 假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。 某輪懸空會把荷載轉給其他輪，平均公式仍可能看似正常。浮力艙漏水也可能增加荷載而不立即停止運動，所以移動成功不能代替承載檢查。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「閘門浮力與輪載」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rolling gates share weight between buoyancy and wheel groups, with levels changing wheel loads. Lower mean loading aids movement, but eccentricity, rail settlement and deformation can still concentrate reactions on individual wheels. Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels. Mean wheel load is (40−28)/8=1.5 MN, excluding eccentricity, dynamics and rail-level differences. A lifted wheel transfers load to others while the average formula still appears normal. A leaking buoyancy compartment can increase loading without stopping motion, so movement success cannot replace bearing assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gate buoyancy and wheel loads” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設門重40 MN、浮力28 MN、8輪理想均分，平均輪載(40−28)/8=1.5 MN；不含偏心、動力或軌道高差。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume gate weight 40 MN, buoyancy 28 MN and eight equally sharing wheels.",
