       "objective": "說明「混凝土溫差拘束」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Concrete thermal restraint” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型閘室牆體的溫度收縮受底板與相鄰澆塊拘束，裂縫風險取決於拘束和早齡強度發展。只看最高溫度會漏掉冷卻過程的拉應力。 假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。 表面快速冷卻會造成局部裂縫，即使整體平均溫降不大；徐變雖降低短時應力，也不能保證止水接縫保持完整。以成熟度單值代替拉伸能力容易誤判。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「混凝土溫差拘束」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Large lock walls contract against foundations and adjoining blocks. Crack risk depends on restraint and developing early-age strength, so peak temperature alone misses tensile demand during cooling. Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4. Stress REαΔT=1.5 MPa, an elastic estimate without creep relaxation. Rapid surface cooling can crack concrete despite a small mean drop. Creep reduces some stresses but does not guarantee watertight joints, and one maturity value cannot substitute for tensile capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Concrete thermal restraint” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設E=25 GPa、熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、降溫15 K、有效拘束0.4，σ=REαΔT=1.5 MPa；彈性近似，未含徐變鬆弛。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume E=25 GPa, thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K, cooling 15 K and effective restraint 0.4.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「兩澆塊最高溫度相同就表示熱裂縫風險完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
