      {
       "id": "b226-v15-37",
       "title": "故障停航與水源緩衝：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Outage backlog and water reserve: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-acp-open",
        "v7-panama-basins",
        "v7-panama-expanded",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b226-v15-36"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「故障停航與水源緩衝」如何影響巴拿馬運河擴建新船閘的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Outage backlog and water reserve” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Panama Canal expansion locks”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。系統復原應同時盤點通行和水量資源。 假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。 機械最大吞吐量可能遠高於水源允許速率，忽略這點會提出無法實現的復原計畫。若水位下降又增加抽水或通航限制，簡單固定單次需求亦會改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「故障停航與水源緩衝」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time. Recovery therefore requires both transit and water-resource accounting. Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³. Extra demand is 680000 m³; allocation 170000 m³/day requires at least four days, excluding new arrivals. Mechanical throughput can exceed water-limited capacity, making a recovery plan infeasible. Falling levels can introduce further pumping or navigation constraints and change the assumed fixed water demand per transit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Outage backlog and water reserve” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設積壓8次通行、每次教學補水85000 m³，額外需求680000 m³；若可分配水量每日170000 m³，至少需4 days，不含新增需求。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume eight queued transits each needing teaching makeup 85000 m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「設備修復後，積壓通行一定能按機械最大吞吐量完成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"After repair the backlog can always clear at maximum mechanical throughput.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「故障停航與水源緩衝」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Outage backlog and water reserve”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b226-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "故障停航與水源緩衝",
         "titleEn": "Outage backlog and water reserve",
         "text": "容量與水源限制可能交互作用，故障後即使機械恢復，也需要足夠淡水與航道時間清理隊列。系統復原應同時盤點通行和水量資源。",
         "textEn": "Capacity and water availability interact: after mechanical restoration, clearing a backlog also needs freshwater and navigation time. Recovery therefore requires both transit and water-resource accounting.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-acp-open",
          "v7-panama-basins",
          "v7-panama-expanded",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b226-v15-37-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
