       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b227-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「配重不平衡功率」如何影響三峽升船機的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Counterweight imbalance power” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges ship lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "配重抵銷大部分重力，但驅動仍需克服不平衡、摩擦與加速度。把整個提升重量乘高度當成電力耗用，會忽略下降配重釋放的位能。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設不平衡質量100 t、速度0.2 m/s，純重力功率Δmgv=196.2 kW；另有摩擦與效率損失，非整機額定功率。 配重失配可能由漏水或水位偏差引起，單靠驅動電流無法辨認來源。若效率和摩擦隨溫度變動仍視為固定，剩餘荷載的推估便會偏移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「配重不平衡功率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Counterweights offset most gravity, but drives still overcome imbalance, friction and acceleration. Multiplying total lifted weight by height overstates electrical demand by ignoring potential energy released by descending counterweights. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume imbalance mass 100 t and speed 0.2 m/s. Gravity-only power Δmgv=196.2 kW, before friction and efficiency losses and distinct from machine-rated power. Counterweight mismatch may arise from leakage or level error, which current alone cannot distinguish. Temperature-dependent efficiency and friction shift the inferred residual load if incorrectly treated as constant. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Counterweight imbalance power” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「有配重就能完全消除所有重力差所需的驅動功率。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Counterweights completely eliminate drive power required by every gravitational imbalance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「配重不平衡功率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Counterweight imbalance power”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b227-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "配重不平衡功率",
         "titleEn": "Counterweight imbalance power",
         "text": "配重抵銷大部分重力，但驅動仍需克服不平衡、摩擦與加速度。把整個提升重量乘高度當成電力耗用，會忽略下降配重釋放的位能。",
         "textEn": "Counterweights offset most gravity, but drives still overcome imbalance, friction and acceleration. Multiplying total lifted weight by height overstates electrical demand by ignoring potential energy released by descending counterweights.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ctg-trial",
