       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Corner synchronization and caisson tilt” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges ship lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型船廂由多點支承，位置差會轉成傾斜與扭曲，進而改變導向和對接條件。同步控制須比較同基準位置，不能只比較各馬達轉速。 假設橫向支承跨20 m、兩側高差4 mm，小角度θ=0.004/20=0.0002 rad，即0.01146°；剛體近似不含扭曲。 兩側編碼器共同零點漂移會讓同步數字好看卻整體偏離對接高程。只比較速度不能發現先前累積的位置差，也不能排除導向件局部卡阻。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「四角同步與船廂傾斜」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A caisson supported at several points converts position differences into tilt and distortion, affecting guidance and docking. Synchronization requires common-reference positions rather than motor speeds alone. Assume transverse support spacing 20 m and level difference 4 mm. Small-angle θ=0.004/20=0.0002 rad, or 0.01146 degrees, for rigid motion without distortion. Common encoder drift can hide an incorrect docking elevation despite good relative synchronization. Speed comparison misses accumulated position error and does not exclude localized binding in guidance components. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Corner synchronization and caisson tilt” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
