      {
       "id": "b227-v15-21",
       "title": "螺旋機構自鎖判讀：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Self-locking of screw mechanisms: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-ctg-trial",
        "v15s-ctg-function",
        "v15s-ctg-history",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b227-v15-20"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「螺旋機構自鎖判讀」如何影響三峽升船機的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Self-locking of screw mechanisms” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges ship lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "螺旋升降或安全機構的自鎖與導程角、摩擦和牙型有關。靜態幾何比較可解釋反驅趨勢，不能替代實際安全裝置的設計和動態試驗。 假設理想方牙螺旋導程角3°、摩擦係數0.08，tan3°=0.0524小於0.08，靜態模型有自鎖趨勢；未含振動、潤滑變動與其他牙型。 潤滑使摩擦降低可能改變反驅條件，動態衝擊也不服從單純靜摩擦比較。若把自鎖當成不需檢查的永久特性，會忽略磨耗和污染造成的改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「螺旋機構自鎖判讀」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Screw self-locking depends on lead angle, friction and thread form. A static geometric comparison explains back-driving tendency without replacing the design and dynamic verification of a real safety mechanism. Assume an ideal square thread with lead angle three degrees and friction coefficient 0.08. tan3°=0.0524 below 0.08 suggests static self-locking, excluding vibration, lubrication change and other thread forms. Lubrication can lower friction enough to change back-driving behavior, and impacts do not follow a simple static comparison. Treating self-locking as permanent ignores wear and contamination that alter the mechanism. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Self-locking of screw mechanisms” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設理想方牙螺旋導程角3°、摩擦係數0.08，tan3°=0.0524小於0.08，靜態模型有自鎖趨勢；未含振動、潤滑變動與其他牙型。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume an ideal square thread with lead angle three degrees and friction coefficient 0.08. tan3°=0.0524 below 0.08 suggests static self-locking, excluding vibration, lubrication change and other thread forms.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「螺旋機構具有靜態自鎖就保證所有動態情況安全。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Static screw self-locking guarantees safety under every dynamic condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「螺旋機構自鎖判讀」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Self-locking of screw mechanisms”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b227-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "螺旋機構自鎖判讀",
         "titleEn": "Self-locking of screw mechanisms",
         "text": "螺旋升降或安全機構的自鎖與導程角、摩擦和牙型有關。靜態幾何比較可解釋反驅趨勢，不能替代實際安全裝置的設計和動態試驗。",
         "textEn": "Screw self-locking depends on lead angle, friction and thread form. A static geometric comparison explains back-driving tendency without replacing the design and dynamic verification of a real safety mechanism.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ctg-trial",
