       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b227-v15-27"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「對接水位差作用」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Docking head-difference force” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "波動水面可能在平均齊平時仍產生交變荷載，鎖定件間隙又會造成撞擊。若只測一側水位，無法區分船廂升沉和航道自身水位變動。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Fluctuating surfaces create alternating loads even when means match, while locking clearance can cause impact. One-sided level sensing cannot separate caisson movement from changes in the navigation reach itself. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若只測一側水位，無法區分船廂升沉和航道自身水位變動。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: One-sided level sensing cannot separate caisson movement from changes in the navigation reach itself.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「肉眼看到兩側水面齊平就能排除顯著對接荷載。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Visually aligned water surfaces rule out substantial docking forces.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b227-v15-28-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "波動水面可能在平均齊平時仍產生交變荷載，鎖定件間隙又會造成撞擊。若只測一側水位，無法區分船廂升沉和航道自身水位變動。",
         "textEn": "Fluctuating surfaces create alternating loads even when means match, while locking clearance can cause impact. One-sided level sensing cannot separate caisson movement from changes in the navigation reach itself.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ctg-trial",
          "v15s-ctg-function",
          "v15s-ctg-history",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b227-v15-28-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ctg-trial",
          "v15s-ctg-function",
          "v15s-ctg-history",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「對接水位差作用」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Docking head-difference force\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。",
         "波動水面可能在平均齊平時仍產生交變荷載，鎖定件間隙又會造成撞擊。",
         "配重抵銷重量後，船廂與配重的運動慣性也消失。"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
         "Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.",
