      {
       "id": "b227-v15-29",
       "title": "啟停加速度與慣性：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Start-stop acceleration and inertia: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-ctg-trial",
        "v15s-ctg-function",
        "v15s-ctg-history",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b227-v15-28"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「啟停加速度與慣性」如何影響三峽升船機的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Start-stop acceleration and inertia” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges ship lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "即使重量被配重抵銷，船廂和配重的慣性仍需要驅動與制動。加速時兩者動能同時增加，不能將淨重量小誤當總慣性小。 假設兩側總移動質量30 million kg、加速度0.005 m/s²，慣性力ma=150 kN；簡化等效平動質量，未含旋轉件慣量。 直接二次微分雜訊會產生假的加速度峰值，過度平滑又會漏掉衝擊。若不計配重慣性，模型會把正常加速需求誤認為摩擦突然變大。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「啟停加速度與慣性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Counterbalancing weight does not remove caisson and counterweight inertia. Both gain kinetic energy during acceleration, so small net weight does not imply small total inertial demand. Assume total moving mass 30 million kg and acceleration 0.005 m/s². Inertial force ma=150 kN, using equivalent translation and excluding rotating-component inertia. Differentiating noise twice creates false acceleration peaks, while excessive smoothing hides impacts. Omitting counterweight inertia can make ordinary acceleration demand appear to be a sudden increase in friction. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Start-stop acceleration and inertia” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩側總移動質量30 million kg、加速度0.005 m/s²，慣性力ma=150 kN；簡化等效平動質量，未含旋轉件慣量。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total moving mass 30 million kg and acceleration 0.005 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「配重抵銷重量後，船廂與配重的運動慣性也消失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Counterbalancing weight also eliminates caisson and counterweight inertia.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「啟停加速度與慣性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Start-stop acceleration and inertia”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b227-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "啟停加速度與慣性",
         "titleEn": "Start-stop acceleration and inertia",
         "text": "即使重量被配重抵銷，船廂和配重的慣性仍需要驅動與制動。加速時兩者動能同時增加，不能將淨重量小誤當總慣性小。",
         "textEn": "Counterbalancing weight does not remove caisson and counterweight inertia. Both gain kinetic energy during acceleration, so small net weight does not imply small total inertial demand.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-ctg-trial",
          "v15s-ctg-function",
          "v15s-ctg-history",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
