       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Tower temperature and alignment” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges ship lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "高塔受日照與季節溫度變化會伸縮，導軌相對位置因此改變。均勻伸長和橫向溫差彎曲是不同機制，應用獨立幾何量測辨認。 假設有效塔高120 m、混凝土熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、均勻升溫10 K，伸長αLΔT=12 mm；不含溫差彎曲與徐變。 日照不均造成的彎曲可能比平均溫升更影響導向，測站自身也會熱變形。若把可逆日變化當永久沉降，可能誤導對中診斷和維護優先次序。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「塔柱溫度與對中」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Tall towers expand with solar and seasonal temperature changes, shifting guide alignment. Uniform extension differs from curvature caused by transverse thermal gradients and requires independent geometric observations. Assume effective tower height 120 m, concrete thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K and uniform warming 10 K. Extension αLΔT=12 mm, excluding thermal curvature and creep. Uneven solar heating can affect guidance more than mean warming, and survey stations can also deform thermally. Mistaking reversible daily movement for settlement misdirects alignment diagnosis and maintenance priorities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Tower temperature and alignment” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效塔高120 m、混凝土熱膨脹係數10⁻⁵/K、均勻升溫10 K，伸長αLΔT=12 mm；不含溫差彎曲與徐變。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume effective tower height 120 m, concrete thermal expansion 10⁻⁵/K and uniform warming 10 K.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「單一平均塔柱溫度足以描述所有熱變形和對中變化。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
