       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Full-cycle time and capacity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Three Gorges ship lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "提升速度只決定垂直運動的一段時間，通航能力還包含進出船、對接與確認。以單程升降時間推算每日通過量，會高估系統容量。 假設提升100 m、速度0.2 m/s，恆速需500 s；另有進出與對接1300 s，循環1800 s，理想每小時2 cycles，不含停機。 假設所有活動都能重疊會把必要的對接與確認時間刪掉，長船與不同水位也可能改變耗時。以最短一次通過代表全年績效，會隱藏排隊和可用度差異。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「全流程時間與容量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Lift speed controls only the vertical-motion portion of a transit. Entry, exit, docking and confirmation also consume time, so movement time alone overstates daily system capacity. Assume lift 100 m at 0.2 m/s, requiring 500 s at constant speed. Adding 1300 s for entry, exit and docking gives 1800 s and ideal two cycles per hour, excluding outages. Assuming universal overlap removes necessary docking and confirmation time, while vessel length and levels change durations. Using the fastest transit as annual performance hides queues and availability differences. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Full-cycle time and capacity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設提升100 m、速度0.2 m/s，恆速需500 s；另有進出與對接1300 s，循環1800 s，理想每小時2 cycles，不含停機。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume lift 100 m at 0.2 m/s, requiring 500 s at constant speed.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「提升速度最快的設備必定具有最大的全年通航量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"The fastest lifting equipment necessarily has the greatest annual throughput.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「全流程時間與容量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Full-cycle time and capacity”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
