       "objective": "說明「船廂水位與額外質量」如何影響比利時斯特勒比—蒂厄升船機的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Caisson level and extra mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Strepy-Thieu boat lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "浮船排水只在船廂水位固定時保持總質量，水位偏差則直接增加或減少水量。大平面船廂即使小幅水位變化，也會使配重平衡出現明顯差異。 取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³。假設船廂有效面積1200 m²、水位偏高0.03 m，額外淡水質量ρAΔh=36000 kg=36 t；忽略船體水線面排除面積。 若船舶長時間遮蔽部分水面，沿用全空廂面積會高估增量。水位計基準偏差又會使每次循環都出現同方向失配，不能誤判為索具永久伸長。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船廂水位與額外質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Vessel displacement preserves total mass only at a fixed caisson level. A level error directly changes water volume, so even a small change across a large plan area noticeably alters counterweight balance. Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³. Assume effective caisson area 1200 m² and excess level 0.03 m. Added freshwater mass ρAΔh=36000 kg=36 t, neglecting the vessel waterplane exclusion. Using empty-caisson area while a vessel occupies the surface overstates the increment. Gauge datum bias creates same-direction mismatch each cycle and must not be mistaken for permanent rope extension. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Caisson level and extra mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水密度ρ=1000 kg/m³。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater density ρ=1000 kg/m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「浮船船廂總重在任何水位變化下都完全不變。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A floating-vessel caisson keeps identical total mass despite any water-level change.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「船廂水位與額外質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Caisson level and extra mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b228-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "船廂水位與額外質量",
         "titleEn": "Caisson level and extra mass",
         "text": "浮船排水只在船廂水位固定時保持總質量，水位偏差則直接增加或減少水量。大平面船廂即使小幅水位變化，也會使配重平衡出現明顯差異。",
         "textEn": "Vessel displacement preserves total mass only at a fixed caisson level. A level error directly changes water volume, so even a small change across a large plan area noticeably alters counterweight balance.",
         "sourceIds": [
