       "objectiveEn": "Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Caisson level and extra mass” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.",
       "instruction": "比較入廂前後多點水位並平均波動，核對面積是否已扣除船體水線面；另以索力總和反算質量，檢查水位推估和力學量測是否一致。另外檢查船舶進出時水位計受到遮蔽的區段。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。",
       "instructionEn": "Average multiple level readings around entry, checking whether vessel waterplane area is excluded. Independently infer mass from summed tensions and compare the level-based and force-based estimates. Also identify intervals when vessel entry or exit obstructs the level measurement. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：以船廂水位與額外質量編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。比較入廂前後多點水位並平均波動，核對面積是否已扣除船體水線面；另以索力總和反算質量，檢查水位推估和力學量測是否一致。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for caisson level and extra mass, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Average multiple level readings around entry, checking whether vessel waterplane area is excluded. Independently infer mass from summed tensions and compare the level-based and force-based estimates.",
