       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Equalizer lever equilibrium” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Strepy-Thieu boat lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "均衡梁藉槓桿轉動重新分配索力，但臂長、接頭摩擦與行程限制會影響效果。能轉動的機構不一定仍處於有效均衡範圍。 假設總力2 MN、兩臂長0.8與1.2 m，力矩平衡T1×0.8=T2×1.2，T1=1.2 MN、T2=0.8 MN；理想無摩擦鉸接。 軸銷摩擦可讓張力差暫時維持而梁不轉，接近止擋時均衡功能也會退化。只確認梁體沒有裂紋，無法證明整個調平機構仍能有效動作。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「均衡梁槓桿關係」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "An equalizer redistributes tension through lever rotation, with arm length, joint friction and travel limits controlling performance. A movable mechanism is not necessarily still within its effective equalization range. Assume total force 2 MN and lever arms 0.8 and 1.2 m. From T1×0.8=T2×1.2, T1=1.2 MN and T2=0.8 MN, for an ideal frictionless pivot. Pin friction can preserve unequal tension without movement, and approaching a stop degrades equalization. An uncracked beam alone does not establish that the complete leveling mechanism still functions effectively. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Equalizer lever equilibrium” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設總力2 MN、兩臂長0.8與1.2 m，力矩平衡T1×0.8=T2×1.2，T1=1.2 MN、T2=0.8 MN；理想無摩擦鉸接。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume total force 2 MN and lever arms 0.8 and 1.2 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「均衡梁存在就表示兩端張力必定完全相等。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
