       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Counterweight travel and geometric limits” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Strepy-Thieu boat lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "船廂與配重之間的索路幾何決定行程比，不能僅由名稱推定一比一。滑輪組、端部空間與纜索彈伸共同限制可達位置。 假設理想索路長度約束x+2y=constant，船廂上升60 m則配重位移y=−30 m；此為教學滑輪配置，非宣稱本站索路。 把虛構滑輪比例套到實際系統會直接錯估行程，索具伸長也會改變端部餘裕。即使中段運動正常，端部空間不足仍可能成為主要限制。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「配重行程與幾何邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Rope routing determines the travel ratio between caisson and counterweight; it cannot be inferred from terminology alone. Pulley arrangements, endpoint space and rope extension jointly constrain reachable positions. Assume an ideal teaching rope constraint x+2y=constant. A caisson rise of 60 m gives counterweight displacement y=−30 m; this is not a claim about the actual site routing. Applying an assumed pulley ratio to the real system misstates travel, while rope extension changes endpoint clearance. Normal mid-travel motion does not establish adequate space near the ends. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Counterweight travel and geometric limits” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
