       "objective": "說明「制動動能與停止距離」如何影響比利時斯特勒比—蒂厄升船機的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Braking energy and stopping distance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Strepy-Thieu boat lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "制動需吸收整個移動系統的動能，配重不會抵銷動能。停止距離與減速度相關，而不平衡重力可能在同一方向持續加入能量。 假設等效移動質量16 million kg、速度0.15 m/s，動能mv²/2=180 kJ；若恆減速度0.01 m/s²，停止距離v²/(2a)=1.125 m。 反應延遲會在真正減速前增加行程，固定減速度也可能因摩擦溫升而失效。只以低速空載停止測試推論高能量工況，會低估距離與熱負擔。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「制動動能與停止距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Brakes absorb kinetic energy of the moving system, which counterweights do not cancel. Stopping distance depends on deceleration, while imbalance gravity may continue adding energy in the direction of motion. Assume equivalent moving mass 16 million kg and speed 0.15 m/s, giving kinetic energy 180 kJ. Constant deceleration 0.01 m/s² gives stopping distance 1.125 m. Response delay adds travel before deceleration, and heating may invalidate constant braking force. Extrapolating a slow unloaded stop to high-energy conditions understates distance and thermal demand on the braking system. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Braking energy and stopping distance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效移動質量16 million kg、速度0.15 m/s，動能mv²/2=180 kJ；若恆減速度0.01 m/s²，停止距離v²/(2a)=1.125 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent moving mass 16 million kg and speed 0.15 m/s, giving kinetic energy 180 kJ.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「配重平衡後，制動器就不需要吸收系統的動能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Once counterweights balance gravity the brakes need absorb no kinetic energy.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「制動動能與停止距離」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Braking energy and stopping distance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
