    {
     "id": "b228-v15-s5",
     "title": "耐久、維護與工程交接",
     "titleEn": "Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「對接間隙充水體積」與「雙船廂服務與可用度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Docking-gap filling volume\" and \"Two-caisson service and availability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b228-v15-33",
       "title": "對接間隙充水體積：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Docking-gap filling volume: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-wallonia-lift",
        "v15s-sofico-lift",
        "v15s-canal-lift",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b228-v15-32"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「對接間隙充水體積」如何影響比利時斯特勒比—蒂厄升船機的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Docking-gap filling volume” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Strepy-Thieu boat lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "船廂與固定航道之間的間隙需要形成可控水域，間隙體積影響水位變化和密封負荷。幾何體積不是漏水量，兩者應以不同量測辨認。 假設有效對接截面50 m²、間隙長0.25 m，充水體積12.5 m³；若由面積1000 m²船廂供應，理想水位下降12.5 mm。 若把正常間隙填水當成密封漏流，會誤判設備狀況；反之持續漏水被短時大流量掩蓋時也可能漏報。水位解析度不足更會使兩種原因難以區分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「對接間隙充水體積」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The docking gap between caisson and fixed reach forms a controlled water volume. Its geometry influences level change and seal loading, but gap volume is not leakage and requires a separate measurement interpretation. Assume docking cross-section 50 m² and gap length 0.25 m, giving fill volume 12.5 m³. Supplied by a 1000 m² caisson, ideal level reduction is 12.5 mm. Normal gap filling can be mistaken for seal leakage, while large initial flow can conceal sustained leakage. Inadequate level resolution further obscures the distinction between temporary storage and a continuing defect. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Docking-gap filling volume” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效對接截面50 m²、間隙長0.25 m，充水體積12.5 m³；若由面積1000 m²船廂供應，理想水位下降12.5 mm。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume docking cross-section 50 m² and gap length 0.25 m, giving fill volume 12.5 m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「對接時量到的全部進水量都一定是止水失效漏流。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"All water measured during docking must be leakage caused by seal failure.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「對接間隙充水體積」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Docking-gap filling volume”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
