       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Two-caisson service and availability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Strepy-Thieu boat lift”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "兩座獨立船廂可以增加服務彈性，但共用航道與維修資源會形成瓶頸。至少一座可用和兩座同時達到全部容量，是不同的可靠度問題。 假設兩船廂獨立可用度各0.95，至少一座可用為1−0.05²=0.9975；兩座同時可用0.95²=0.9025，未含共同原因。 把至少一座可用率當作完整容量可用率會誇大通行能力，共用航道停用又可能讓兩座正常設備都無法服務。必須先定義成功條件再引用數值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「雙船廂服務與可用度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Two independent caissons improve service flexibility, but shared approaches and maintenance resources can constrain capacity. Availability of at least one differs from simultaneous availability of full two-caisson throughput. Assume independent caisson availability 0.95 each. At least one is available with probability 0.9975, while both are available with probability 0.9025, excluding common causes. Using at-least-one availability as full-capacity availability exaggerates throughput. A closed shared approach can prevent both healthy caissons from serving traffic, so success must be defined before quoting probabilities. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Two-caisson service and availability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
