       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「至少一座船廂可用就代表整個系統完整容量可用。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"At least one available caisson means full system capacity is available.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b228-v15-40-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "把至少一座可用率當作完整容量可用率會誇大通行能力，共用航道停用又可能讓兩座正常設備都無法服務。必須先定義成功條件再引用數值。",
         "textEn": "Using at-least-one availability as full-capacity availability exaggerates throughput. A closed shared approach can prevent both healthy caissons from serving traffic, so success must be defined before quoting probabilities.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-wallonia-lift",
          "v15s-sofico-lift",
          "v15s-canal-lift",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b228-v15-40-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-wallonia-lift",
          "v15s-sofico-lift",
          "v15s-canal-lift",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        }
