    {
     "id": "b229-v15-s2",
     "title": "水力機制、材料與定量模型",
     "titleEn": "Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「船槽水平與齒輪定向」與「旋轉速度與旅程」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Gondola leveling by gearing\" and \"Rotation speed and travel\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b229-v15-09",
       "title": "船槽水平與齒輪定向：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Gondola leveling by gearing: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-sc-wheel",
        "v15s-sc-carbon",
        "v15s-sc-location",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b229-v15-08"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「船槽水平與齒輪定向」如何影響福爾柯克水輪的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Gondola leveling by gearing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。這是運動學約束，不是只靠自由擺動就能保證的結果。 假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。 齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「船槽水平與齒輪定向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground. This is a kinematic constraint rather than a result guaranteed solely by free swinging. Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Ground-referenced change is zero, an ideal opposite one-to-one relation rather than actual site tooth counts. Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gondola leveling by gearing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「船槽水平與齒輪定向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gondola leveling by gearing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b229-v15-09-k1",
         "title": "船槽水平與齒輪定向",
         "titleEn": "Gondola leveling by gearing",
         "text": "船槽需要在主輪轉動時保持接近水平，定向機構抵銷支臂相對地面的旋轉。這是運動學約束，不是只靠自由擺動就能保證的結果。",
         "textEn": "Gondolas remain approximately horizontal by counteracting the arm rotation relative to the ground. This is a kinematic constraint rather than a result guaranteed solely by free swinging.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-sc-wheel",
          "v15s-sc-carbon",
          "v15s-sc-location",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b229-v15-09-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
