       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Gondola leveling by gearing” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設主臂轉過180°，船槽對主臂反轉−180°，對地角度和為0°；理想一比一反向定向，不聲稱本站完整齒輪齒數。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume the main arm rotates 180 degrees and the gondola rotates −180 degrees relative to it. Ground-referenced change is zero, an ideal opposite one-to-one relation rather than actual site tooth counts. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：以地面水平基準同時量主臂和船槽角度，檢查兩角和在全行程是否穩定；將齒隙造成的換向偏差和結構撓曲分開繪製。",
