       "objective": "從症狀倒推「船槽水平與齒輪定向」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Gondola leveling by gearing” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "齒隙會在換向時形成短暫角度誤差，軸承阻力也可能使自由懸吊無法理想跟隨。只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Backlash creates brief reversal errors and bearing resistance prevents ideal free following. Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：只在上下終點檢查水平，可能漏掉中途最大的船槽傾斜。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Checking level only at upper and lower endpoints can miss the largest gondola tilt during intermediate rotation.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「只要船槽自由懸吊，任何摩擦下都會完全保持水平。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A freely suspended gondola stays perfectly level under any amount of friction.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
