       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Free-surface sloshing time scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Falkirk Wheel”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "船槽加速度會激起自由液面晃蕩，運動頻率與水深、槽長共同決定反應。小振幅理論可比較尺度，實際船體和隔板會改變流場。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設矩形槽長20 m、水深2 m，k=π/L，ω²=gk tanh(kh)，第一模態T=2π/ω=9.177 s；無船且小振幅。 船體遮擋會分割水面並改變模態，大幅晃蕩與撞壁亦超出線性理論。若只取槽中央測站，可能恰好位於節點而錯認沒有晃蕩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水面晃蕩時間尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Gondola acceleration excites free-surface sloshing whose response depends on motion frequency, water depth and tank length. Small-amplitude theory compares scales, while vessels and baffles modify the real flow. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume rectangular tank length 20 m and depth 2 m, with k=π/L and ω²=gk tanh(kh). First-mode T=2π/ω=9.177 s, for small motion without a vessel. A hull subdivides the free surface and changes modes, while large sloshing and wall impact exceed linear theory. A central sensor may sit near a node and falsely suggest no motion. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Free-surface sloshing time scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只量船槽中央水位就能可靠捕捉所有晃蕩最大值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
