       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「重現期與壽命風險」如何影響荷蘭三角洲工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Return period and lifetime risk” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Delta Works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "年度超越機率描述每年的事件風險，不代表兩次洪水必須相隔固定年數。跨年累積需說明平穩與獨立假設，氣候及暴露變化可能使它們失效。 假設年超越機率p=0.001且各年獨立平穩，50年內至少一次為1−(1−p)⁵⁰=0.04879，約4.879%；非荷蘭現行標準。 重現期不是保固年限，同一年也可能出現多次高水事件。若把歷史氣候外推成固定未來機率，會讓長壽命設施的累積風險看似比實際更確定。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「重現期與壽命風險」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Annual exceedance probability does not impose a fixed interval between floods. Multi-year accumulation requires stationary and independent years, assumptions that climate and exposure changes can invalidate. Assume annual exceedance p=0.001 with independent stationary years. At least one event in fifty years has probability 1−(1−p)⁵⁰=0.04879, or 4.879 percent, not a Dutch standard. Return period is not a warranty, and several high-water events can occur within one year. Treating historical climate as fixed future probability makes lifetime risk appear more certain than the evidence supports. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Return period and lifetime risk” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設年超越機率p=0.001且各年獨立平穩，50年內至少一次為1−(1−p)⁵⁰=0.04879，約4.879%；非荷蘭現行標準。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual exceedance p=0.001 with independent stationary years.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「千年重現期代表一次洪水後至少一千年不會再發生。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A thousand-year return period prevents another flood for at least one thousand years.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「重現期與壽命風險」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Return period and lifetime risk”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b230-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "重現期與壽命風險",
         "titleEn": "Return period and lifetime risk",
         "text": "年度超越機率描述每年的事件風險，不代表兩次洪水必須相隔固定年數。跨年累積需說明平穩與獨立假設，氣候及暴露變化可能使它們失效。",
         "textEn": "Annual exceedance probability does not impose a fixed interval between floods. Multi-year accumulation requires stationary and independent years, assumptions that climate and exposure changes can invalidate.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-delta",
          "v15s-delta-adapt",
          "v15s-rws-first",
          "v15s-usace-steel",
          "v15s-usace-mechanical"
         ]
