       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Coastal sediment budget” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Delta Works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "海岸維持取決於砂的來源、搬運與流失，而不只是某一斷面的寬度。補砂量應放進區域控制體，避免把移到鄰岸的砂全部當作消失。 假設每年沿岸輸入0.4 million m³、輸出0.7 million m³、補砂0.5 million m³，淨增加0.2 million m³；未含深水交換。 只量乾灘會把移到近岸沙洲的砂當成流失，忽略粒徑差又會誤估補砂持續時間。不同年代測量範圍不一致，可能產生不存在的體積增減。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「沿岸砂量收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Coastal maintenance depends on sediment sources, transport and loss rather than one beach width. Nourishment belongs in a regional control volume so sand moved to a neighboring reach is not all treated as lost. Assume annual input 0.4 million m³, output 0.7 million m³ and nourishment 0.5 million m³. Net gain is 0.2 million m³, excluding deep-water exchange. Dry-beach surveys alone mistake movement to nearshore bars for loss, while grain-size differences alter nourishment persistence. Inconsistent survey footprints can create fictitious volume gains or losses between years. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Coastal sediment budget” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年沿岸輸入0.4 million m³、輸出0.7 million m³、補砂0.5 million m³，淨增加0.2 million m³；未含深水交換。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume annual input 0.4 million m³, output 0.7 million m³ and nourishment 0.5 million m³.",
