       ],
       "objective": "說明「航運代價與關閉頻率」如何影響荷蘭三角洲工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Navigation cost and closure frequency” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Delta Works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "防洪屏障的關閉影響航運時間，長期關閉頻率改變會使等待成本累積。每次平均代價不能代表尖峰供應鏈損失，須區分服務延遲和真實經濟損害。 假設每年12次關閉、每次8艘船各延遲2 h，總192 vessel-hours；假設時間成本1000 currency/h，對應192000 currency/year，非實際損失。 把所有港口延遲都歸於防洪會誇大代價，忽略關閉後隊列消散又會低估代價。若把假設時間價值當作業者實際損失，會產生不當精確感。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「航運代價與關閉頻率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Barrier closures delay navigation and accumulate waiting as their frequency changes. Average event cost does not represent peak supply-chain consequences, requiring service delay to be separated from verified economic loss. Assume twelve closures annually, eight vessels per event and two hours delay each: 192 vessel-hours. At assumed cost 1000 currency/h this is 192000 currency/year, not measured loss. Attributing all port delays to defence exaggerates cost, while omitting post-closure queue recovery understates it. Presenting assumed time values as actual operator losses creates unjustified numerical precision. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Navigation cost and closure frequency” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每年12次關閉、每次8艘船各延遲2 h，總192 vessel-hours；假設時間成本1000 currency/h，對應192000 currency/year，非實際損失。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume twelve closures annually, eight vessels per event and two hours delay each: 192 vessel-hours.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只需關閉歷時乘船數就能精確得到全部經濟損失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Closure duration times vessel count precisely gives all economic losses.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「航運代價與關閉頻率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Navigation cost and closure frequency”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b230-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "航運代價與關閉頻率",
         "titleEn": "Navigation cost and closure frequency",
         "text": "防洪屏障的關閉影響航運時間，長期關閉頻率改變會使等待成本累積。每次平均代價不能代表尖峰供應鏈損失，須區分服務延遲和真實經濟損害。",
         "textEn": "Barrier closures delay navigation and accumulate waiting as their frequency changes. Average event cost does not represent peak supply-chain consequences, requiring service delay to be separated from verified economic loss.",
         "sourceIds": [
