      {
       "id": "b230-v15-29",
       "title": "內外防線蓄洪耦合：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Coupled outer defence and storage: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "b-src-delta",
        "v15s-delta-adapt",
        "v15s-rws-first",
        "v15s-usace-steel",
        "v15s-usace-mechanical"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b230-v15-28"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「內外防線蓄洪耦合」如何影響荷蘭三角洲工程的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Coupled outer defence and storage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Delta Works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "外海屏障降低暴潮進入，卻可能限制內河排水，內部蓄洪空間因此成為系統的一部分。把堤防與蓄水設施各自最佳化可能產生相互衝突。 假設外閘關閉4 h、內河淨入流500 m³/s，需暫存7.2 million m³；若允許平均升水0.3 m，理想有效面積24 km²。 名義庫容若被堤路隔開或入口狹窄，可能在洪峰前無法充分使用。把所有低地直接相加作可用面積，會低估局部最高水位和淹水轉移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「內外防線蓄洪耦合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "An outer barrier excludes surge but can restrict river drainage, making inland storage part of the defence system. Optimizing embankments and storage independently may create conflicting requirements. Assume outer closure four hours with net river inflow 500 m³/s, requiring storage 7.2 million m³. At allowed mean rise 0.3 m, ideal effective area is 24 km². Nominal storage separated by roads or narrow entrances may not fill before the peak. Adding all low ground as usable area understates local maximum levels and the redistribution of flooding. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Coupled outer defence and storage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設外閘關閉4 h、內河淨入流500 m³/s，需暫存7.2 million m³；若允許平均升水0.3 m，理想有效面積24 km²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume outer closure four hours with net river inflow 500 m³/s, requiring storage 7.2 million m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「地圖上所有低窪面積都能立即提供相同蓄洪能力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"All low ground on a map immediately provides equal usable flood storage.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「內外防線蓄洪耦合」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Coupled outer defence and storage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b230-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "內外防線蓄洪耦合",
         "titleEn": "Coupled outer defence and storage",
         "text": "外海屏障降低暴潮進入，卻可能限制內河排水，內部蓄洪空間因此成為系統的一部分。把堤防與蓄水設施各自最佳化可能產生相互衝突。",
         "textEn": "An outer barrier excludes surge but can restrict river drainage, making inland storage part of the defence system. Optimizing embankments and storage independently may create conflicting requirements.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-delta",
