       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Adaptation trigger and lead time” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Delta Works”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "分期調適需要在功能不足前啟動設計施工，監測門檻因此必須包含實施提前量。看到水位達極限才開始準備，可能已錯過調整窗口。 假設剩餘功能裕度0.4 m、情境增加速率0.01 m/year，達限40 years；若實施需15 years，最晚應於25 years前啟動，限線性情境。 海平面加速或施工延期會縮短可用時間，單一速率估算不能當精確倒數。若監測指標與實際失效模式沒有關聯，提早量再長也可能觸發錯誤措施。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「調適門檻與提前量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Staged adaptation must start design and construction before performance becomes inadequate, so monitoring triggers need implementation lead time. Waiting until the limit is reached can miss the available response window. Assume remaining performance margin 0.4 m and scenario change 0.01 m/year: limit in forty years. With fifteen years implementation, initiation is needed by year twenty-five under this linear scenario. Accelerating change or construction delay shortens available time, so one rate is not an exact countdown. A monitoring indicator disconnected from the failure mechanism may trigger the wrong measure despite ample lead time. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adaptation trigger and lead time” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
