       "objective": "說明「絕熱溫升與膠結材」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大體積混凝土內部散熱慢，膠結材水化熱會累積。絕熱溫升把放熱量和材料熱容量連結，但真實澆塊還有表面交換、骨材溫度與時間效應。 假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。 把最終總放熱瞬間施加會錯估早期峰值，忽略表面散熱則會過度保守或失去梯度資訊。相同膠結材用量也不保證不同配方具有相同放熱速率。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「絕熱溫升與膠結材」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Heat accumulates inside mass concrete because dissipation is slow. Adiabatic rise links binder heat to material heat capacity, while actual blocks also exchange heat at surfaces and depend on aggregate temperature and time. Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K). Adiabatic rise is 18.75 K, not the actual peak temperature. Applying ultimate heat instantly misstates early peaks, while neglecting surface loss removes gradient information. Equal binder content also does not guarantee equal heat-release rates across different cementitious formulations. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Adiabatic rise and binder heat” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設膠結材180 kg/m³、累積放熱250 kJ/kg、混凝土體積熱容量2.4 MJ/(m³·K)，絕熱溫升18.75 K；不是實際峰值溫度。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume binder 180 kg/m³, cumulative heat 250 kJ/kg and volumetric heat capacity 2.4 MJ/(m³·K).",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「絕熱溫升就是工地澆塊必定量到的最高溫度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Adiabatic temperature rise is the highest temperature that every placed block must reach.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「絕熱溫升與膠結材」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Adiabatic rise and binder heat”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
