      {
       "id": "b231-v15-05",
       "title": "澆置供應與冷縫風險：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Placement supply and cold joints: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-rcc"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b231-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「澆置供應與冷縫風險」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Placement supply and cold joints” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "分塊澆築要求連續供料與有序覆蓋，供應率不足會延長新舊料接觸時間。總日產量達標不代表每一局部層面都在可接受條件下接續。 假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。 同一停機時間在不同溫度下會產生不同接縫狀態，盲目加水恢復工作性又會改變材料品質。若只補足少澆的方量，已形成的弱層不會自動消失。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「澆置供應與冷縫風險」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Block placement needs continuous supply and orderly coverage. Insufficient delivery prolongs local intervals between layers, so meeting daily output does not establish acceptable continuity at every local interface. Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h. Placement requires eight hours, or 9.5 h with a 1.5 h outage, excluding local compaction and coverage sequence. The same interruption produces different interface states at different temperatures, and adding water to restore workability changes material quality. Making up missing volume does not automatically remove an already formed weak layer. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Placement supply and cold joints” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設澆塊600 m³、有效供應率75 m³/h，純澆置需8 h；若停機1.5 h則9.5 h，未計振實和局部覆蓋順序。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume block volume 600 m³ and effective supply 75 m³/h.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要最後總澆置方量正確，局部冷縫就不會影響壩體。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Correct final placed volume means local cold joints cannot affect the dam.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「澆置供應與冷縫風險」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Placement supply and cold joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "澆置供應與冷縫風險",
         "titleEn": "Placement supply and cold joints",
         "text": "分塊澆築要求連續供料與有序覆蓋，供應率不足會延長新舊料接觸時間。總日產量達標不代表每一局部層面都在可接受條件下接續。",
         "textEn": "Block placement needs continuous supply and orderly coverage. Insufficient delivery prolongs local intervals between layers, so meeting daily output does not establish acceptable continuity at every local interface.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-rcc"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-05-k2",
