       "objective": "說明「層面剪力與有效正應力」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水平施工層面傳遞剪力，黏聚、摩擦與孔壓共同控制可動員阻力。層面清理和骨材嵌固影響黏結，不能用完整混凝土強度直接代表接縫。 假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。 漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「層面剪力與有效正應力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Horizontal lift joints transfer shear through cohesion and friction under effective normal stress. Cleaning and aggregate interlock affect bond, so intact-concrete strength cannot directly represent the interface. Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6. Resistance cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN, using assumed peak parameters. Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設層面面積100 m²、總正力30 MN、上浮10 MN、c=0.1 MPa、μ=0.6，阻力cA+μ(N−U)=22 MN；參數為假設峰值。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume interface area 100 m², normal force 30 MN, uplift 10 MN, c=0.1 MPa and μ=0.6.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「層面剪力與有效正應力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lift-joint shear and effective stress”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-09-k1",
         "title": "層面剪力與有效正應力",
         "titleEn": "Lift-joint shear and effective stress",
         "text": "水平施工層面傳遞剪力，黏聚、摩擦與孔壓共同控制可動員阻力。層面清理和骨材嵌固影響黏結，不能用完整混凝土強度直接代表接縫。",
         "textEn": "Horizontal lift joints transfer shear through cohesion and friction under effective normal stress. Cleaning and aggregate interlock affect bond, so intact-concrete strength cannot directly represent the interface.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-rcc"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-09-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-rcc"
