      {
       "id": "b231-v15-12",
       "title": "層面剪力與有效正應力：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Lift-joint shear and effective stress: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-rcc"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b231-v15-11"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「層面剪力與有效正應力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Lift-joint shear and effective stress” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「接縫剪力能力可以直接等同完整混凝土的強度。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A construction-joint shear capacity directly equals intact-concrete strength.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-12-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "漿皮或污染使層面黏結降低，孔壓增加又削弱摩擦項。若在可能開裂的接縫仍無條件保留黏聚力，會高估滑動後阻力並掩蓋排水功能的重要性。",
         "textEn": "Laitance or contamination reduces bond, while pore pressure reduces friction. Retaining cohesion unconditionally after possible cracking overstates post-movement resistance and obscures the importance of drainage performance.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-rcc"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-12-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
