       ],
       "objective": "說明「上浮折減與抗滑」如何影響混凝土重力壩分塊澆築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Uplift reduction and sliding” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Block-by-block concrete gravity-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "重力壩的自重提供摩擦抗滑，但基底上浮降低有效正向力。排水效果需由孔壓驗證，不能因設計有排水孔就自動採取最大折減。 假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。 排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「上浮折減與抗滑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Gravity-dam weight provides frictional resistance, but uplift reduces effective normal force. Drainage effectiveness requires pressure evidence rather than an automatic maximum reduction because drains appear on drawings. Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m. Friction-only ratio μ(W−U)/H=1.575, excluding cohesion and earthquake loading. Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Uplift reduction and sliding” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「上浮折減與抗滑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Uplift reduction and sliding”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b231-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "上浮折減與抗滑",
         "titleEn": "Uplift reduction and sliding",
         "text": "重力壩的自重提供摩擦抗滑，但基底上浮降低有效正向力。排水效果需由孔壓驗證，不能因設計有排水孔就自動採取最大折減。",
         "textEn": "Gravity-dam weight provides frictional resistance, but uplift reduces effective normal force. Drainage effectiveness requires pressure evidence rather than an automatic maximum reduction because drains appear on drawings.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-rcc"
         ]
        },
