      {
       "id": "b231-v15-34",
       "title": "上浮折減與抗滑：定量估算",
       "titleEn": "Uplift reduction and sliding: quantitative estimate",
       "estimatedMinutes": 30,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-rcc"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b231-v15-33"
       ],
       "objective": "以數值模型估算「上浮折減與抗滑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。",
       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Uplift reduction and sliding” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設每米壩段重量12 MN/m、上浮3 MN/m、μ=0.7、水平推力4 MN/m，純摩擦比μ(W−U)/H=1.575；未含黏聚與地震。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume per-metre weight 12 MN/m, uplift 3 MN/m, μ=0.7 and horizontal force 4 MN/m. Friction-only ratio μ(W−U)/H=1.575, excluding cohesion and earthquake loading. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：沿基底量測孔壓並積分上浮，對照排水量和庫位變化；確認滑動面位置、材料參數與荷載組合一致，再比較排水減弱時的敏感度，而非只驗一個數字。",
       "observationEn": "How to cross-check: Integrate measured basal pressure into uplift and compare drainage and reservoir changes.",
       "failure": "計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。",
       "failureEn": "Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.",
       "check": "依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。",
       "checkEn": "Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.",
