       "objective": "從症狀倒推「上浮折減與抗滑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Uplift reduction and sliding” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "排水量變小可能代表堵塞而非更防水，孔壓升高會讓摩擦比降低。若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Lower drainage may indicate clogging rather than improved impermeability, and rising pressure lowers frictional reserve. Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若把排水孔附近低壓當整個基底均值，會過度樂觀估計有效重量與抗滑能力。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Extrapolating low pressure beside drains across the whole base overstates effective weight and sliding resistance.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「圖面有排水孔就能不量孔壓而忽略全部基底上浮。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Drains shown on drawings allow all foundation uplift to be ignored without pressure measurements.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
