   "stages": [
    {
     "id": "b232-v15-s1",
     "title": "水文條件、邊界與工程系統",
     "titleEn": "Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「鋪層體積與供料節拍」與「壓實度與參考密度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Lift volume and supply rhythm\" and \"Compaction and reference density\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b232-v15-01",
       "title": "鋪層體積與供料節拍：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Lift volume and supply rhythm: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-rcc",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「鋪層體積與供料節拍」如何影響碾壓混凝土壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Lift volume and supply rhythm” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Roller-compacted-concrete dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "碾壓混凝土以薄層連續鋪築形成大體積結構，層面暴露時間由面積和供料節拍共同決定。設備名義產能不等於可持續有效供料，需考慮運輸與等待。 假設鋪層面積5000 m²、厚0.3 m，體積1500 m³；有效供料250 m³/h需6 h，未含邊緣修整和局部停頓。 大面積整層平均完成很快仍可能有角落長時間未覆蓋，臨時道路交錯也會造成局部延遲。若以最高一小時產量推算全日，便會低估冷縫風險。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鋪層體積與供料節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "RCC forms mass structures through thin successive lifts. Lift exposure depends on area and delivery rhythm, while rated plant capacity differs from sustainable placement because transport and queuing intervene. Assume lift area 5000 m² and thickness 0.3 m, giving 1500 m³. Effective supply 250 m³/h requires six hours, excluding edge work and local interruptions. A fast average lift cycle can conceal long exposure in corners, while crossing haul routes cause local delays. Extrapolating the best production hour to a full day understates cold-interface risk. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Lift volume and supply rhythm” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設鋪層面積5000 m²、厚0.3 m，體積1500 m³；有效供料250 m³/h需6 h，未含邊緣修整和局部停頓。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume lift area 5000 m² and thickness 0.3 m, giving 1500 m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「拌合廠額定產能就是每個澆築位置可持續取得的供料率。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Rated batching capacity equals sustainable delivery at every placement location.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「鋪層體積與供料節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Lift volume and supply rhythm”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b232-v15-01-k1",
