    {
     "id": "b232-v15-s4",
     "title": "試驗、量測與監測驗證",
     "titleEn": "Testing, measurement and monitoring",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「層狀滲透異向性」與「上下游面層協調」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Layered permeability anisotropy\" and \"Facing and RCC compatibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b232-v15-25",
       "title": "層狀滲透異向性：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Layered permeability anisotropy: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-rcc",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b232-v15-24"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「層狀滲透異向性」如何影響碾壓混凝土壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Layered permeability anisotropy” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Roller-compacted-concrete dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "薄層界面可能沿水平方向形成較易滲流的通道，垂直試體低滲透不代表整壩各方向相同。層狀介質的等效滲透率須依平行或垂直流向計算。 假設等厚兩層k1=10⁻⁸、k2=10⁻⁶ m/s，平行ke=(k1+k2)/2=5.05×10⁻⁷ m/s，垂直調和平均1.9802×10⁻⁸ m/s。 單一方向芯樣可能避開連續弱層，低試驗水頭也未必揭露開裂後通道。若把實驗室完整小試體結果直接代表整壩，會低估尺度與界面影響。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「層狀滲透異向性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Lift interfaces can create easier horizontal seepage paths, so low vertical specimen permeability does not establish isotropy. Equivalent permeability of layers differs for flow parallel and perpendicular to them. Assume equal layers with k1=10⁻⁸ and k2=10⁻⁶ m/s. Parallel permeability is 5.05×10⁻⁷ m/s and perpendicular harmonic mean is 1.9802×10⁻⁸ m/s. A specimen orientation may miss continuous weak layers, and low head may not reveal post-cracking paths. Directly extrapolating intact small specimens to the dam understates scale and interface effects. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Layered permeability anisotropy” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等厚兩層k1=10⁻⁸、k2=10⁻⁶ m/s，平行ke=(k1+k2)/2=5.05×10⁻⁷ m/s，垂直調和平均1.9802×10⁻⁸ m/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equal layers with k1=10⁻⁸ and k2=10⁻⁶ m/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「垂直芯樣滲透率很低就證明水平層面也同樣不透水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Low vertical-core permeability proves equally low permeability along horizontal lift interfaces.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「層狀滲透異向性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Layered permeability anisotropy”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b232-v15-25-k1",
         "title": "層狀滲透異向性",
         "titleEn": "Layered permeability anisotropy",
         "text": "薄層界面可能沿水平方向形成較易滲流的通道，垂直試體低滲透不代表整壩各方向相同。層狀介質的等效滲透率須依平行或垂直流向計算。",
         "textEn": "Lift interfaces can create easier horizontal seepage paths, so low vertical specimen permeability does not establish isotropy. Equivalent permeability of layers differs for flow parallel and perpendicular to them.",
         "sourceIds": [
