      {
       "id": "b232-v15-32",
       "title": "上下游面層協調：失效診斷",
       "titleEn": "Facing and RCC compatibility: failure diagnosis",
       "estimatedMinutes": 25,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-rcc",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b232-v15-31"
       ],
       "objective": "從症狀倒推「上下游面層協調」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Facing and RCC compatibility” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "面層過早變硬可能拘束後續RCC收縮，缺乏黏結則可能形成漏流路徑。若只要求兩種材料各自強度達標，仍無法證明接合區能共同工作。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "An early-stiffening facing can restrain later RCC shrinkage, while poor bond creates leakage paths. Separate strength compliance of both materials does not establish that their interface acts compatibly under service conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若只要求兩種材料各自強度達標，仍無法證明接合區能共同工作。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Separate strength compliance of both materials does not establish that their interface acts compatibly under service conditions.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「面層和內部材料各自強度合格就代表接合區必然可靠。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Separate strength compliance of facing and RCC guarantees a reliable interface.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b232-v15-32-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "面層過早變硬可能拘束後續RCC收縮，缺乏黏結則可能形成漏流路徑。若只要求兩種材料各自強度達標，仍無法證明接合區能共同工作。",
         "textEn": "An early-stiffening facing can restrain later RCC shrinkage, while poor bond creates leakage paths. Separate strength compliance of both materials does not establish that their interface acts compatibly under service conditions.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-rcc",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b232-v15-32-k2",
         "title": "根因確認",
         "titleEn": "Root-cause confirmation",
         "text": "根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。",
         "textEn": "Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-rcc",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "在「上下游面層協調」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？",
        "questionEn": "When \"Facing and RCC compatibility\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?",
        "options": [
         "補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。",
         "邊緣弱帶占總體積很小就不可能影響整壩防滲功能。",
         "面層過早變硬可能拘束後續RCC收縮，缺乏黏結則可能形成漏流路徑。"
