       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Edge compaction and restricted zones” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Roller-compacted-concrete dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "大型碾輪難以接近模板、廊道和埋件，邊緣區可能需要不同設備與工法。中部試驗成果不能直接代表受限空間，幾何可達性是品質控制的一部分。 假設長100 m的邊緣未充分覆蓋帶寬0.4 m、層厚0.3 m，受影響體積12 m³；占1500 m³一層的0.8%，不代表可忽略。 體積占比小但若沿上游形成連續通道，可能主導滲流而非平均強度。以隨機中部取樣代表全部工程，會系統性漏掉可達性不足造成的缺陷。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「邊緣壓實與死角」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Large rollers cannot fully approach forms, galleries and embedded items, so restricted zones need different equipment or methods. Central trial results do not represent these areas, making geometric access part of quality control. Assume a poorly covered edge band 100 m long, 0.4 m wide and 0.3 m thick. Volume is 12 m³, or 0.8 percent of a 1500 m³ lift, not necessarily negligible. A small-volume band can dominate seepage if continuous near the upstream face. Random sampling confined to central areas systematically misses defects caused by restricted equipment access along the structure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Edge compaction and restricted zones” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
