      {
       "id": "b233-v15-05",
       "title": "拱與懸臂分擔：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Arch and cantilever load sharing: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-arch-2",
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b233-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「拱與懸臂分擔」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Arch and cantilever load sharing” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "壩體可由水平拱與豎向懸臂共同分擔水壓，兩者變形必須相容。分擔比例由剛度與邊界形成，不是可任意指定以降低應力的設計選項。 假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。 一條路徑剛度被高估會把荷載過度導向該路徑，整體平衡仍可能成立。只校準壩頂位移而忽略局部應變，可能得到錯誤卻看似吻合的內力分配。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「拱與懸臂分擔」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Horizontal arches and vertical cantilevers share pressure while maintaining compatible movement. Relative stiffness and boundaries determine sharing; the proportions cannot be arbitrarily chosen to make stresses smaller. Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN. Displacement is 2 mm, with arch share 6 MN and cantilever share 4 MN, a spring analogy only. Overstated stiffness attracts too much load to one path even while global equilibrium holds. Calibrating only crest displacement can produce a misleadingly good fit with incorrect local force distribution. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Arch and cantilever load sharing” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩平行線性路徑剛度ka=3 GN/m、kc=2 GN/m，共受10 MN，位移2 mm，拱分6 MN、懸臂分4 MN；僅教學彈簧類比。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume parallel linear paths ka=3 GN/m and kc=2 GN/m under total 10 MN.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「拱與懸臂分擔」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Arch and cantilever load sharing”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b233-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "拱與懸臂分擔",
         "titleEn": "Arch and cantilever load sharing",
         "text": "壩體可由水平拱與豎向懸臂共同分擔水壓，兩者變形必須相容。分擔比例由剛度與邊界形成，不是可任意指定以降低應力的設計選項。",
         "textEn": "Horizontal arches and vertical cantilevers share pressure while maintaining compatible movement. Relative stiffness and boundaries determine sharing; the proportions cannot be arbitrarily chosen to make stresses smaller.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b233-v15-05-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：拱和懸臂的荷載比例可以任意指定而不影響位移相容。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Arch and cantilever shares can be chosen arbitrarily without affecting displacement compatibility. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
