    {
     "id": "b233-v15-s2",
     "title": "水力機制、材料與定量模型",
     "titleEn": "Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「岸坡推力方向」與「楔體滑動抗力」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Abutment thrust direction\" and \"Wedge sliding resistance\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b233-v15-09",
       "title": "岸坡推力方向：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Abutment thrust direction: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-arch-2",
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b233-v15-08"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「岸坡推力方向」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Abutment thrust direction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "拱推力到達岸坡時需要分解到岩面法向與剪向，方向與大小同樣重要。大壓力若指向易滑節理組合，仍可能形成不利楔體受力。 假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。 角度定義混淆會交換法向與剪向分量，直接改變摩擦判讀。若把整個岸坡用單一平面代表，可能漏掉由兩組節理交線控制的三維運動方向。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岸坡推力方向」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Arch thrust must be resolved normal and tangential to abutment surfaces, making direction as important as magnitude. Large compression can still destabilize a wedge when directed unfavorably relative to joints. Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal. Normal component is 17.3205 MN and tangential component 10 MN, a planar illustration rather than a complete wedge force system. Confusing angle definitions swaps normal and tangential components and changes friction assessment. Representing the whole abutment by one plane can miss three-dimensional movement controlled by intersecting joint sets. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Abutment thrust direction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設推力20 MN與岩面法向夾角30°，法向17.3205 MN、剪向10 MN；平面向量示例，不代表三維楔體完整力系。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume thrust 20 MN at thirty degrees to the rock-surface normal.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「岸坡承受的總推力越大就必定越穩定，方向不重要。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Greater total abutment thrust always improves stability regardless of its direction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「岸坡推力方向」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Abutment thrust direction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b233-v15-09-k1",
         "title": "岸坡推力方向",
         "titleEn": "Abutment thrust direction",
         "text": "拱推力到達岸坡時需要分解到岩面法向與剪向，方向與大小同樣重要。大壓力若指向易滑節理組合，仍可能形成不利楔體受力。",
         "textEn": "Arch thrust must be resolved normal and tangential to abutment surfaces, making direction as important as magnitude. Large compression can still destabilize a wedge when directed unfavorably relative to joints.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
