       "instructionEn": "Map continuity and daylighting of the sliding surface and locate pore pressures relative to it. Separate peak and residual friction and check whether wedge movement and crack observations support the assumed mechanism. Check whether the potential wedge genuinely has an outward movement surface. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
