       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Joint water-pressure distribution” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水沿岩體節理傳遞到岸坡內部，裂隙開度與排水會使壓力分布不同於外部庫水線性內插。水壓合力及作用點都會影響楔體穩定。 假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。 出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂隙水壓分布」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Water transmits through abutment joints, with aperture and drainage producing pressure distributions different from a simple interpolation of reservoir level. Both resultant and location influence wedge stability. Assume joint area 200 m² with pressure rising linearly from zero to 0.4 MPa. Resultant is 40 MN at two-thirds length from the low-pressure edge, for a linear distribution. Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Joint water-pressure distribution” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設矩形節理面200 m²，壓力由上緣0線性增到底部0.4 MPa，水壓合力40 MN，作用點距低壓邊2/3長度；限線性分布。",
