       "objective": "從症狀倒推「裂隙水壓分布」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Joint water-pressure distribution” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「裂隙出水很少就能證明整個岸坡節理水壓很低。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Small joint discharge proves low water pressure throughout all abutment discontinuities.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b233-v15-20-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "出水量小可能因通道堵塞而水壓更高，不等於岸坡變乾。只用一個低壓測點代表整個滑面，會低估未排水區的合力和不利力矩。",
         "textEn": "Low discharge can indicate blockage with higher pressure rather than drier rock. Extending one low-pressure point over the full slip plane understates force and adverse moment in undrained portions.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
