      {
       "id": "b233-v15-37",
       "title": "水溫荷載與監測殘差：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-arch-2",
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b233-v15-36"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「水溫荷載與監測殘差」如何影響雙曲拱壩拱座分析的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Abutment analysis for double-curvature arch dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "拱壩位移同時受庫水位、溫度和時間影響，異常診斷需先扣除可解釋的正常反應。統計模型只能在已驗證範圍內描述資料，不直接證明結構安全。 線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。假設教學位移模型d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm，ΔH=10 m、ΔT=5 K，預測2 mm；觀測2.6 mm則殘差0.6 mm，非警戒值。 高度相關的水位與溫度會讓係數難以識別，模型也可能把長期損傷吸收為時間趨勢。重新訓練前若未檢查原因，異常可能被數學上消除卻仍存在。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水溫荷載與監測殘差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Arch displacement responds to water level, temperature and time, so anomaly interpretation first removes explainable normal behavior. Statistical models describe validated data ranges rather than independently proving structural safety. The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively. Assume teaching displacement d=0.1ΔH+0.2ΔT mm with ΔH=10 m and ΔT=5 K. Prediction is 2 mm; observation 2.6 mm leaves residual 0.6 mm, not an alarm threshold. Correlated level and temperature make coefficients difficult to identify, and a time trend can absorb deterioration. Retraining without investigating causes may mathematically erase an anomaly while its physical source remains. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：線性係數分別為0.1 mm/m與0.2 mm/K。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: The linear coefficients are 0.1 mm/m and 0.2 mm/K, respectively.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要重新擬合後殘差變小，就證明原先結構異常已消失。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A smaller residual after refitting proves the original structural anomaly has disappeared.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水溫荷載與監測殘差」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b233-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "水溫荷載與監測殘差",
         "titleEn": "Hydrothermal effects and monitoring residuals",
         "text": "拱壩位移同時受庫水位、溫度和時間影響，異常診斷需先扣除可解釋的正常反應。統計模型只能在已驗證範圍內描述資料，不直接證明結構安全。",
         "textEn": "Arch displacement responds to water level, temperature and time, so anomaly interpretation first removes explainable normal behavior. Statistical models describe validated data ranges rather than independently proving structural safety.",
         "sourceIds": [
