   "id": "b234",
   "title": "混凝土面板堆石壩施工",
   "titleEn": "Concrete-face rockfill dam construction",
   "category": "water",
   "kind": "course",
   "status": "guided",
   "contentStatus": "reviewable-educational-curriculum",
   "summary": "本課以混凝土面板堆石壩施工為入口，深入堆石變形、混凝土面板與周邊接縫的相容。十個單元各自對應不同的荷載路徑、能量交換或監測問題，從守恆式建立量化估算，再檢查量測配置是否能辨認真正失效原因。工程史實只採用列明範圍的公開一手資料；所有模型輸入另標為教學假設，成果是可追溯的工程判讀紀錄。",
   "summaryEn": "Using Concrete-face rockfill dam construction as its entry point, this course examines compatibility of rockfill deformation, concrete facing and perimeter joints. Ten units address different load paths, energy exchanges or monitoring questions, starting with conservation-based estimates and testing whether observations distinguish failure causes. Historical statements use scoped primary evidence. Numerical model inputs are separately identified as teaching assumptions, producing a traceable engineering interpretation record.",
   "focus": "堆石變形、混凝土面板與周邊接縫的相容",
   "focusEn": "Compatibility of rockfill deformation, concrete facing and perimeter joints",
   "scope": "依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、開挖、注漿或受限空間作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。",
   "scopeEn": "Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, excavation, grouting or confined-space permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.",
   "subcategory": "water-systems",
   "subcategoryTitle": "防潮、航運與大壩施工",
   "subcategoryTitleEn": "Tidal barriers, navigation and dam construction",
   "learningTrack": "water",
   "learningSubdiscipline": "water-systems",
   "learningTags": [
    "water",
    "water-systems",
    "water"
