      {
       "id": "b234-v15-05",
       "title": "分層壓縮與壩頂沉降：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Layer compression and crest settlement: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usbr-embankment",
        "v15s-usbr-construction",
        "v15s-usbr-filters",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b234-v15-04"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「分層壓縮與壩頂沉降」如何影響混凝土面板堆石壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Layer compression and crest settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Concrete-face rockfill dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "堆石壩沉降是不同高程層壓縮的累積，局部大應變不一定出現在壩頂。分層量測能辨認填築、蓄水與長期作用各自造成的位移。 假設兩填築層厚30及50 m、豎向應變0.003及0.002，總壓縮30×0.003+50×0.002=0.19 m；一維分層近似。 只看壩頂總沉降可能把某一薄層的大應變平均掉，面板卻對局部曲率敏感。若基礎基準也沉降，所有相對儀器可能低估絕對位移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分層壓縮與壩頂沉降」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Crest settlement accumulates compression across layers, while the largest local strain need not occur at the crest. Layered measurements distinguish placement, impoundment and long-term contributions to movement. Assume layers 30 and 50 m thick with vertical strains 0.003 and 0.002. Total compression is 0.19 m, a one-dimensional layered approximation. Crest settlement can average out severe strain in a thin layer, while the face responds to local curvature. A settling reference foundation can make relative instruments understate absolute movement throughout the section. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Layer compression and crest settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設兩填築層厚30及50 m、豎向應變0.003及0.002，總壓縮30×0.003+50×0.002=0.19 m；一維分層近似。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume layers 30 and 50 m thick with vertical strains 0.003 and 0.002.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「壩頂沉降量很小就能排除任何局部填築層的大變形。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Small crest settlement rules out large deformation in every individual fill layer.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「分層壓縮與壩頂沉降」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Layer compression and crest settlement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b234-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "分層壓縮與壩頂沉降",
         "titleEn": "Layer compression and crest settlement",
         "text": "堆石壩沉降是不同高程層壓縮的累積，局部大應變不一定出現在壩頂。分層量測能辨認填築、蓄水與長期作用各自造成的位移。",
         "textEn": "Crest settlement accumulates compression across layers, while the largest local strain need not occur at the crest. Layered measurements distinguish placement, impoundment and long-term contributions to movement.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usbr-embankment",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "v15s-usbr-filters",
