      {
       "id": "b234-v15-13",
       "title": "周邊接縫位移分量：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Perimeter-joint movement components: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usbr-embankment",
        "v15s-usbr-construction",
        "v15s-usbr-filters",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b234-v15-12"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「周邊接縫位移分量」如何影響混凝土面板堆石壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Perimeter-joint movement components” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Concrete-face rockfill dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "面板與趾板交界會發生張開、沉降和剪移，止水需對應三方向變形。單一合位移大小相同，不表示止水受力和漏水風險相同。 假設接縫張開8 mm、沿縫剪移6 mm，平面合位移√(8²+6²)=10 mm；分量仍須保留，不能當成等效容許張開。 法向張開與剪向錯動對銅片或橡膠止水的影響不同，反覆循環也會累積疲勞。若只記錄合位移，可能把危險張開誤當較可容受的滑移。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「周邊接縫位移分量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The face-plinth interface experiences opening, settlement and shear, requiring waterstops to accommodate three components. Equal resultant displacement does not imply equal waterstop loading or leakage risk. Assume opening 8 mm and along-joint shear 6 mm. Planar resultant is 10 mm, but components remain necessary and this is not an equivalent allowable opening. Opening and shear act differently on metal or elastomeric waterstops, and cycles accumulate damage. Recording only a resultant can disguise critical opening as a more tolerable sliding movement. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Perimeter-joint movement components” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設接縫張開8 mm、沿縫剪移6 mm，平面合位移√(8²+6²)=10 mm；分量仍須保留，不能當成等效容許張開。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume opening 8 mm and along-joint shear 6 mm.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要接縫合位移相同，止水承受的變形模式就完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal resultant joint displacement means an identical deformation mode for the waterstop.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「周邊接縫位移分量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Perimeter-joint movement components”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b234-v15-13-k1",
         "title": "周邊接縫位移分量",
         "titleEn": "Perimeter-joint movement components",
         "text": "面板與趾板交界會發生張開、沉降和剪移，止水需對應三方向變形。單一合位移大小相同，不表示止水受力和漏水風險相同。",
         "textEn": "The face-plinth interface experiences opening, settlement and shear, requiring waterstops to accommodate three components. Equal resultant displacement does not imply equal waterstop loading or leakage risk.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usbr-embankment",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "v15s-usbr-filters",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b234-v15-13-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：只要接縫合位移相同，止水承受的變形模式就完全相同。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Equal resultant joint displacement means an identical deformation mode for the waterstop. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usbr-embankment",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
