       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Leakage and water-balance closure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Concrete-face rockfill dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "漏水量需與庫位、降雨和排水系統一起判讀，總量增減不能單獨定位面板裂縫。分區量測與水質示蹤可區分壩體、基礎和外部集水。 假設量測出水120 L/s、可辨識降雨集水30 L/s、儀器零偏5 L/s，校正滲流85 L/s；各來源穩定且可相加，未含儲水延遲。 突增可能來自排水管清通而非新增裂縫，減少也可能是堵塞。未校正外部雨水便比較兩次蓄水，會把不同環境條件誤當面板性能改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漏流與水量閉合」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Leakage must be interpreted with reservoir level, rain and drainage. Total change alone cannot locate face cracks; sectional measurement and water-quality tracing distinguish embankment, foundation and external collection. Assume measured outflow 120 L/s, identified rain collection 30 L/s and instrument offset 5 L/s. Corrected seepage is 85 L/s, with steady additive sources and no storage lag. An increase may follow drain clearing rather than a new crack, and a decrease may mean blockage. Comparing impoundments without rainfall correction confuses environmental differences with changes in face performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Leakage and water-balance closure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設量測出水120 L/s、可辨識降雨集水30 L/s、儀器零偏5 L/s，校正滲流85 L/s；各來源穩定且可相加，未含儲水延遲。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume measured outflow 120 L/s, identified rain collection 30 L/s and instrument offset 5 L/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「排水量減少必定表示面板防水性能改善而無其他可能。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Reduced drain discharge necessarily means improved face watertightness with no other explanation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
