       "objective": "說明「含水調整與乾土質量」如何影響心牆土石壩分區填築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Moisture adjustment on dry mass” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Zoned placement in earth-core rockfill dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "心牆含水量以水重除乾土重定義，施工加水須先區分乾土與濕土基準。含水量影響壓實、滲透和施工孔壓，不能只追求最大乾密度。 假設乾土1000 t、初始含水率12%、目標16%，需加水(0.16−0.12)×1000=40 t；未含蒸發和混合損失，不是工地配方。 表面灑水可能使上濕下乾，平均含水正確仍有弱層；誤用濕土重量會算錯補水量。材料濕側施工也可能提高短期孔壓，需與穩定需求共同評估。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「含水調整與乾土質量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Core water content is water mass divided by dry-soil mass, so water addition requires a clear dry versus wet basis. Moisture affects compaction, permeability and construction pore pressure rather than density alone. Assume dry soil 1000 t, initial water content twelve percent and target sixteen percent. Added water is forty tonnes, excluding evaporation and mixing losses and not a field recipe. Surface wetting can leave wet tops and dry bottoms despite a correct mean. Using wet mass miscalculates additions, and wetter placement can raise short-term pore pressure, requiring evaluation with stability needs. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Moisture adjustment on dry mass” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設乾土1000 t、初始含水率12%、目標16%，需加水(0.16−0.12)×1000=40 t；未含蒸發和混合損失，不是工地配方。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume dry soil 1000 t, initial water content twelve percent and target sixteen percent.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「用濕土總重量乘含水率差就一定得到正確補水量。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Wet total soil mass times the moisture difference always gives the correct water addition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「含水調整與乾土質量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Moisture adjustment on dry mass”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
