       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Core arching and differential settlement” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Zoned placement in earth-core rockfill dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "較軟心牆與較硬壩殼變形不同，界面剪力可把部分豎向荷載轉移到兩側。這有時降低心牆壓應力，不能把荷載轉移一律視為有利。 假設原豎向應力600 kPa、側向界面轉移比例0.25，剩餘450 kPa；此為量化荷載分配假設，不是普遍拱效應係數。 窄谷或陡峭岸坡容易形成複雜三維拱效應，單一二維係數可能不足。若只以心牆壓力降低當作減載好處，會忽略裂縫與水力劈裂敏感性提高。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「心牆拱效應與沉降差」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A softer core and stiffer shells settle differently, allowing interface shear to transfer vertical load sideways. Reduced core compression can be unfavorable, so load transfer is not automatically beneficial. Assume original vertical stress 600 kPa and side-interface transfer fraction 0.25. Remaining stress is 450 kPa, an assumed load split rather than a universal arching coefficient. Narrow valleys and steep abutments create three-dimensional arching beyond one two-dimensional coefficient. Viewing reduced core stress only as beneficial unloading overlooks increased sensitivity to cracking and hydraulic fracture. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Core arching and differential settlement” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設原豎向應力600 kPa、側向界面轉移比例0.25，剩餘450 kPa；此為量化荷載分配假設，不是普遍拱效應係數。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume original vertical stress 600 kPa and side-interface transfer fraction 0.25.",
