       "objective": "說明「排水帶流量與水頭」如何影響心牆土石壩分區填築的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Drain flow and hydraulic head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Zoned placement in earth-core rockfill dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排水帶需把滲流導出而不累積高孔壓，其能力取決於滲透率、斷面和水力坡降。出水端堵塞或尾水升高也會改變系統，不能只看材料試驗k值。 假設排水k=0.01 m/s、通流面積2 m²、坡降0.05，Q=kiA=0.001 m³/s=1 L/s；穩定飽和達西流，未含出口損失。 高流量時粗料可能出現非達西效應，出口被淹也會降低實際坡降。若把設計名義斷面當永遠有效，會高估經沉降與細料遷移後的排水能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水帶流量與水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A drain must transmit seepage without building high pore pressure. Capacity depends on permeability, area and gradient, while outlet blockage or tailwater changes the system beyond the material permeability value. Assume drain k=0.01 m/s, flow area 2 m² and gradient 0.05. Q=0.001 m³/s=1 L/s, for steady saturated Darcy flow without outlet loss. Coarse drains can become non-Darcy at high flow, and submerged outlets reduce gradients. Treating nominal section as permanently effective overstates capacity after settlement and fines migration alter the flow paths. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drain flow and hydraulic head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設排水k=0.01 m/s、通流面積2 m²、坡降0.05，Q=kiA=0.001 m³/s=1 L/s；穩定飽和達西流，未含出口損失。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume drain k=0.01 m/s, flow area 2 m² and gradient 0.05.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「排水料滲透係數很高就保證任何出口條件下都能充分排水。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"High drain permeability guarantees sufficient drainage under every outlet condition.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「排水帶流量與水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drain flow and hydraulic head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b235-v15-25-k1",
         "title": "排水帶流量與水頭",
         "titleEn": "Drain flow and hydraulic head",
         "text": "排水帶需把滲流導出而不累積高孔壓，其能力取決於滲透率、斷面和水力坡降。出水端堵塞或尾水升高也會改變系統，不能只看材料試驗k值。",
         "textEn": "A drain must transmit seepage without building high pore pressure. Capacity depends on permeability, area and gradient, while outlet blockage or tailwater changes the system beyond the material permeability value.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usbr-embankment",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "v15s-usbr-filters",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
