       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Zone volumes and boundary contamination” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Zoned placement in earth-core rockfill dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "分區填築的空間邊界維持不同材料的功能，推土機越界和運輸掉料可能造成混雜。總材料量正確不能證明反濾帶厚度或心牆連續性正確。 假設一層心牆長200 m、寬6 m、厚0.25 m，方量300 m³；兩側各混入0.1 m寬帶則受影響10 m³，占3.333%。 局部混料占比小仍可能沿整條反濾帶形成堵塞，心牆被粗粒貫穿也可增加缺陷。若只按各料區進場重量驗收，空間錯位會被總量平衡掩蓋。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「分區方量與邊界污染」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Zoned placement preserves distinct material functions through spatial boundaries. Equipment crossing and spillage mix materials, so correct total quantities do not establish filter thickness or core continuity. Assume core lift length 200 m, width 6 m and thickness 0.25 m, giving 300 m³. Mixed bands 0.1 m wide on both sides affect 10 m³, or 3.333 percent. A small mixed fraction can clog a continuous filter strip, while coarse intrusion damages the core. Acceptance based only on incoming material mass allows spatial misplacement to hide behind a correct total balance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Zone volumes and boundary contamination” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
