       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Air voids and connectivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Asphalt-core embankment-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "低孔隙是防滲的重要條件，但總孔隙量不等於連通孔隙量。密度法可檢查壓實狀態，仍須用滲透和界面檢驗排除連續缺陷。 假設理論最大密度2500 kg/m³、實測體積密度2450 kg/m³，空隙率1−2450/2500=2%；非任何專案接受上限。 少量連通孔隙可能比較多封閉孔隙更影響漏流，取芯損傷又可能製造人工裂縫。只看空隙百分比，無法分辨施工缺陷與取樣過程造成的通道。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「體積孔隙與連通性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Low void content supports impermeability, but total void volume differs from connected voids. Density checks compaction while permeability and interface evidence remain necessary to exclude continuous defects. Assume theoretical maximum density 2500 kg/m³ and measured bulk density 2450 kg/m³. Air void content is two percent, not a project acceptance limit. A small connected void fraction can transmit more flow than many isolated voids, and coring damage can create artificial cracks. Void percentage alone cannot distinguish construction defects from sampling-induced pathways. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Air voids and connectivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
