       "objective": "說明「熱收縮與相鄰材料」如何影響瀝青混凝土心牆壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Thermal contraction and neighboring materials” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Asphalt-core embankment-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "瀝青心牆冷卻時會收縮，而兩側過渡料限制其自由變形。變形相容與黏結同樣重要，不能只看心牆材料自身能承受多大拉應變。 假設有效長10 m、熱膨脹係數15×10⁻⁶/K、降溫20 K，自由收縮3 mm；材料係數為假設，不含黏彈鬆弛與拘束。 局部快速冷卻可能產生集中拉伸，而高溫黏性又會讓應力鬆弛。若直接用彈性拘束公式跨越整個溫度範圍，可能誇大或低估真正的接縫需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「熱收縮與相鄰材料」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Cooling contracts the asphalt core while transition material restrains free movement. Compatibility and bonding matter alongside the material tensile strain capacity, especially where geometry changes or the core meets concrete. Assume length 10 m, expansion coefficient 15×10⁻⁶/K and cooling twenty kelvin. Free contraction is 3 mm, with assumed coefficient and no viscoelastic relaxation or restraint. Local rapid cooling concentrates tension, while warm viscous behavior relaxes stress. Applying one elastic restraint formula across the whole temperature range can either exaggerate or understate actual joint demand. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Thermal contraction and neighboring materials” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設有效長10 m、熱膨脹係數15×10⁻⁶/K、降溫20 K，自由收縮3 mm；材料係數為假設，不含黏彈鬆弛與拘束。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume length 10 m, expansion coefficient 15×10⁻⁶/K and cooling twenty kelvin.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「自由熱收縮量就是心牆接頭實際必然張開的寬度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Free thermal contraction is exactly the opening that must occur at the core connection.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「熱收縮與相鄰材料」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Thermal contraction and neighboring materials”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
