       "objective": "說明「層間黏結與剪切」如何影響瀝青混凝土心牆壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Interlift bond and shear” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Asphalt-core embankment-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "瀝青層之間的黏結受表面潔淨、熱歷程和壓實影響，整體材料延性不能補救未黏結界面。接縫試驗需保留載重方向與溫度條件。 假設接縫試體剪力峰值12 kN、面積0.02 m²，名義剪應力0.6 MPa；不含應力集中且只代表該溫度速率下試驗。 試體可能在完整材料先破壞而無法量得真正接縫能力，也可能因取芯熱損傷改變結果。若只報最大剪力不記錄破壞面，便無法判讀層間品質。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「層間黏結與剪切」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Asphalt interlift bonding depends on cleanliness, thermal history and compaction. Bulk ductility cannot repair an unbonded interface, and joint tests must preserve loading direction and temperature conditions. Assume joint specimen peak shear 12 kN over 0.02 m². Nominal shear stress is 0.6 MPa, excluding concentration and applying only at the tested temperature and rate. Failure in intact material may prevent measuring joint capacity, while coring heat can alter results. Reporting peak force without the failure surface leaves the interlift quality interpretation incomplete and potentially misleading. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Interlift bond and shear” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設接縫試體剪力峰值12 kN、面積0.02 m²，名義剪應力0.6 MPa；不含應力集中且只代表該溫度速率下試驗。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint specimen peak shear 12 kN over 0.02 m².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「瀝青材料具有延性就能保證所有施工層面完全黏結。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Ductile asphalt material guarantees complete bonding at every construction interface.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「層間黏結與剪切」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Interlift bond and shear”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b236-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "層間黏結與剪切",
         "titleEn": "Interlift bond and shear",
         "text": "瀝青層之間的黏結受表面潔淨、熱歷程和壓實影響，整體材料延性不能補救未黏結界面。接縫試驗需保留載重方向與溫度條件。",
         "textEn": "Asphalt interlift bonding depends on cleanliness, thermal history and compaction. Bulk ductility cannot repair an unbonded interface, and joint tests must preserve loading direction and temperature conditions.",
