    {
     "id": "b236-v15-s4",
     "title": "試驗、量測與監測驗證",
     "titleEn": "Testing, measurement and monitoring",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「趾板接觸與有效壓力」與「過渡區剪應變相容」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Plinth contact and effective pressure\" and \"Transition-zone shear compatibility\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b236-v15-25",
       "title": "趾板接觸與有效壓力：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Plinth contact and effective pressure: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-asphalt-quxue",
        "v15s-asphalt-rate",
        "v15s-asphalt-model",
        "v15s-usbr-embankment",
        "v15s-usbr-construction"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b236-v15-24"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「趾板接觸與有效壓力」如何影響瀝青混凝土心牆壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Plinth contact and effective pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Asphalt-core embankment-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "心牆與混凝土趾板需要在變形下維持密封，接觸壓力和水壓之差影響張開傾向。幾何粗糙、黏結與黏彈行為使此差值只能作初步指標。 假設總接觸壓力300 kPa、接面水壓220 kPa，差80 kPa；若變形降低接觸壓力100 kPa，差為−20 kPa，不直接判定必然失效。 接觸壓力下降可能只在小區域發生，平均土壓計會漏掉；黏結損傷也可在仍受壓時形成優先通道。單一壓差不能代表接頭完整的密封狀態。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「趾板接觸與有效壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "The core-plinth connection must remain sealed during deformation. Contact compression minus water pressure indicates opening tendency, but roughness, bond and viscoelastic behavior make it only a preliminary measure. Assume contact compression 300 kPa and interface water pressure 220 kPa, leaving eighty kPa. A hundred-kPa reduction gives −20 kPa, without directly declaring inevitable failure. Loss of compression can be localized and missed by averaged pressure measurements, while damaged bond can create paths even under compression. One pressure difference cannot establish the complete sealing condition of the connection. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Plinth contact and effective pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設總接觸壓力300 kPa、接面水壓220 kPa，差80 kPa；若變形降低接觸壓力100 kPa，差為−20 kPa，不直接判定必然失效。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume contact compression 300 kPa and interface water pressure 220 kPa, leaving eighty kPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要平均接觸壓力大於水壓，接頭就不可能存在漏流。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Mean contact pressure above water pressure makes leakage through the connection impossible.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「趾板接觸與有效壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Plinth contact and effective pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b236-v15-25-k1",
         "title": "趾板接觸與有效壓力",
         "titleEn": "Plinth contact and effective pressure",
         "text": "心牆與混凝土趾板需要在變形下維持密封，接觸壓力和水壓之差影響張開傾向。幾何粗糙、黏結與黏彈行為使此差值只能作初步指標。",
         "textEn": "The core-plinth connection must remain sealed during deformation. Contact compression minus water pressure indicates opening tendency, but roughness, bond and viscoelastic behavior make it only a preliminary measure.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-asphalt-quxue",
          "v15s-asphalt-rate",
          "v15s-asphalt-model",
          "v15s-usbr-embankment",
          "v15s-usbr-construction"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b236-v15-25-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：只要平均接觸壓力大於水壓，接頭就不可能存在漏流。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Mean contact pressure above water pressure makes leakage through the connection impossible. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-asphalt-quxue",
          "v15s-asphalt-rate",
          "v15s-asphalt-model",
          "v15s-usbr-embankment",
          "v15s-usbr-construction"
