       "instructionEn": "Compare interface movement, pressure and leakage over the same period and verify instrument representativeness. Use connection-specific tests across temperatures and shear paths instead of substituting generic asphalt specimens for the actual contact geometry. Check whether interface water pressure is spatially uniform. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.",
       "observation": "現場實務：以趾板接觸與有效壓力編製可交接的證據頁，註明資料時間、單位、模型適用範圍與審查者。核對接面位移、壓力和漏流在同一時段的關係，檢查儀器是否代表實際接觸區；利用接頭專屬試驗比較不同溫度和剪移路徑，避免以一般瀝青試體代替接面。檢查接觸面水壓是否均勻。",
       "observationEn": "Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for plinth contact and effective pressure, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Compare interface movement, pressure and leakage over the same period and verify instrument representativeness. Use connection-specific tests across temperatures and shear paths instead of substituting generic asphalt specimens for the actual contact geometry. Check whether interface water pressure is spatially uniform.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：接觸壓力下降可能只在小區域發生，平均土壓計會漏掉；黏結損傷也可在仍受壓時形成優先通道。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Loss of compression can be localized and missed by averaged pressure measurements, while damaged bond can create paths even under compression. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
