       "objective": "說明「材料老化與保留試樣」如何影響瀝青混凝土心牆壩施工的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Material ageing and retained specimens” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Asphalt-core embankment-dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "瀝青材料隨熱氧化與時間改變，硬化可能提高短時剛度卻降低延性。比較需使用相同試驗溫度和速率，不能把較高強度自動解讀為更好密封能力。 假設相同試驗條件下模數由120升到180 MPa，剛度比1.5；同時破壞應變由0.04降0.025，降低37.5%，不代表真實老化速率。 保留試樣的氧氣暴露可能與深埋心牆不同，不能直接把其老化年限當現地壽命。若只檢查峰值強度，延性降低與界面脆化可能被視為性能改善而漏判。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「材料老化與保留試樣」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Asphalt changes with thermal oxidation and time. Hardening can raise short-term stiffness while reducing ductility, requiring comparisons at equal temperature and rate rather than treating higher strength as automatically better sealing. Assume modulus rises from 120 to 180 MPa under matched tests, a ratio 1.5, while failure strain falls from 0.04 to 0.025, a 37.5 percent reduction, not an actual ageing rate. Retained specimens may see different oxygen exposure from a buried core, preventing direct conversion to service life. Peak strength alone can make reduced ductility and interface embrittlement appear to be improved performance. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Material ageing and retained specimens” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同試驗條件下模數由120升到180 MPa，剛度比1.5；同時破壞應變由0.04降0.025，降低37.5%，不代表真實老化速率。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume modulus rises from 120 to 180 MPa under matched tests, a ratio 1.5, while failure strain falls from 0.04 to 0.025, a 37.5 percent reduction, not an actual ageing rate.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「老化後模數提高就表示心牆密封能力與延性必定一起提高。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"An ageing-related modulus increase necessarily improves both core sealing and ductility.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「材料老化與保留試樣」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Material ageing and retained specimens”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b236-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "材料老化與保留試樣",
         "titleEn": "Material ageing and retained specimens",
         "text": "瀝青材料隨熱氧化與時間改變，硬化可能提高短時剛度卻降低延性。比較需使用相同試驗溫度和速率，不能把較高強度自動解讀為更好密封能力。",
         "textEn": "Asphalt changes with thermal oxidation and time. Hardening can raise short-term stiffness while reducing ductility, requiring comparisons at equal temperature and rate rather than treating higher strength as automatically better sealing.",
