   "stages": [
    {
     "id": "b237-v15-s1",
     "title": "水文條件、邊界與工程系統",
     "titleEn": "Hydrology, boundaries and engineering system",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「裂隙開度與流量」與「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Fracture aperture and flow\" and \"Particle size and groutability\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b237-v15-01",
       "title": "裂隙開度與流量：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Fracture aperture and flow: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-grout",
        "b-src-water",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-gravity"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「裂隙開度與流量」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Fracture aperture and flow” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "薄裂隙的層流流量對水力開度高度敏感，微小張開可造成大流量變化。平行板立方律只是理想模型，粗糙、接觸點與通道化會改變實際通水性。 假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。 把水力開度當作幾何平均寬度會錯估可灌性，壓力上升也可能改變裂隙本身。若只用一次流量反算唯一開度，會掩蓋多通道等效結果的不唯一性。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「裂隙開度與流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Laminar flow through a thin fracture is highly sensitive to hydraulic aperture. The parallel-plate cubic law is idealized; roughness, contacts and channeling change actual conductivity and can dominate the measured response. Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient. Ideal flow ratio is 3.375 for laminar Newtonian flow, not directly for particle-bearing grout. Hydraulic aperture is not geometric mean width, and pressure can change the fracture itself. Inferring one unique aperture from one flow measurement hides the nonuniqueness of several equivalent conducting channels. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Fracture aperture and flow” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同壓差下開度由0.1增至0.15 mm，理想流量比(0.15/0.1)³=3.375；牛頓流體層流，不直接代表含顆粒漿液。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume aperture rises from 0.1 to 0.15 mm at equal pressure gradient.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「水試反算的水力開度就是所有裂隙的實際幾何寬度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Water-test hydraulic aperture equals the actual geometric width of every fracture.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「裂隙開度與流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Fracture aperture and flow”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "裂隙開度與流量",
         "titleEn": "Fracture aperture and flow",
         "text": "薄裂隙的層流流量對水力開度高度敏感，微小張開可造成大流量變化。平行板立方律只是理想模型，粗糙、接觸點與通道化會改變實際通水性。",
         "textEn": "Laminar flow through a thin fracture is highly sensitive to hydraulic aperture. The parallel-plate cubic law is idealized; roughness, contacts and channeling change actual conductivity and can dominate the measured response.",
