       ],
       "objective": "說明「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Particle size and groutability” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水能通過的裂隙未必能讓水泥顆粒通過，顆粒架橋與濾餅會限制滲入。粒徑與開度比只能做篩選，還需考慮聚集、形狀和流變。 假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。 細度證書不能代表混合後沒有團聚，孔口濾堵可能讓壓力上升卻沒有深部填充。若把高注入壓力當成帷幕密實證據，便可能掩蓋入口附近的局部封堵。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A water-conducting fracture may exclude cement grains. Bridging and filter-cake formation limit penetration, while particle-to-aperture ratio is only screening evidence because agglomeration, shape and rheology also matter. Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five. This is not a universal groutability limit or a prediction of field reach. A fineness certificate does not exclude agglomeration after mixing. Entrance filtration can raise pressure without deep filling, so high injection pressure alone can conceal a locally blocked entrance rather than a continuous curtain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Particle size and groutability” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設裂隙開度0.2 mm、顆粒d95=0.04 mm，開度粒徑比5；不將此數字當通用可灌門檻，也不推定現地可達距離。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fracture aperture 0.2 mm and particle d95=0.04 mm, giving aperture-to-particle ratio five.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要岩體能透水，同一裂隙就必定能讓任何水泥漿通過。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Any water-conducting fracture necessarily admits every cement grout mixture.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「顆粒尺寸與可灌性」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Particle size and groutability”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "顆粒尺寸與可灌性",
         "titleEn": "Particle size and groutability",
         "text": "水能通過的裂隙未必能讓水泥顆粒通過，顆粒架橋與濾餅會限制滲入。粒徑與開度比只能做篩選，還需考慮聚集、形狀和流變。",
         "textEn": "A water-conducting fracture may exclude cement grains. Bridging and filter-cake formation limit penetration, while particle-to-aperture ratio is only screening evidence because agglomeration, shape and rheology also matter.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
         ]
