       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Yield stress and penetration length” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "含顆粒漿液常有降伏應力，壓力梯度不足時不會像水一樣持續流動。平行裂隙中的門檻量級可解釋為何低黏度仍可能停止，但實際材料也有時變性。 假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。 等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「降伏應力與滲入距離」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Particle-bearing grout often has yield stress and will not flow like water below a sufficient pressure gradient. An ideal fracture threshold explains arrested penetration despite low plastic viscosity, with real materials also changing over time. Assume Bingham yield stress 5 Pa, aperture 0.5 mm and length 10 m. Threshold scale 2τyL/b=200 kPa, for ideal parallel plates and not a field injection setting. Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Yield stress and penetration length” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設Bingham漿降伏應力5 Pa、裂隙開度0.5 mm、長10 m，最低壓差尺度2τyL/b=200 kPa；理想平行板，非現地注入設定。",
