       "objective": "從症狀倒推「降伏應力與滲入距離」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Yield stress and penetration length” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「漿液塑性黏度低就代表不需要壓力梯度也能無限滲入。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Low plastic viscosity means grout can penetrate indefinitely without a pressure gradient.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-12-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "等待時間改變漿液結構，實際降伏值可能不同於初拌值；裂隙分叉和漏失也使壓力分配改變。只用泵表壓除距離，不能得到真正前緣壓力梯度。",
         "textEn": "Waiting changes grout structure and yield stress, while branching and losses redistribute pressure. Pump gauge pressure divided by distance does not establish the actual gradient at the advancing front within the fracture network.",
         "sourceIds": [
