         "textEn": "Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume gauge pressure 500 kPa, twenty-metre descending grout column at 1500 kg/m³, line loss 50 kPa and groundwater pressure 200 kPa. Effective difference is 544.3 kPa, a head-correction example.",
