       "objective": "說明「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "注入壓力若推開節理會改變岩體結構，吸漿量增加不一定代表成功填充。抬動應與原位應力、覆蓋及孔壓共同判讀，不能由固定深度比例推定全部條件。 假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。 高壓造成新通道可能短期增加吸漿量，卻把漿液帶到非目標區。若只追求耗漿量而不查抬動和回流，可能損害既有接觸或鄰近構造。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Injection can open joints and change rock structure, so increased take is not automatically successful filling. Jacking interpretation requires in-situ stress, cover and pore pressure rather than one universal depth rule. Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa. Added pressure 300 kPa leaves 100 kPa, excluding bond and three-dimensional redistribution. Pressure-created paths can increase take while diverting grout away from its target. Pursuing consumption without checking movement and returns can damage existing contacts or adjacent structures instead of improving the intended barrier. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設某面總正應力600 kPa、原孔壓200 kPa，有效壓縮400 kPa；若額外孔壓升300 kPa，剩100 kPa，忽略黏結與三維應力重分配。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「吸漿量突然增加就必定表示帷幕填充效果變得更好。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A sudden increase in grout take necessarily indicates improved curtain filling.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「岩體抬動與壓力邊界」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Rock jacking and pressure boundaries”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
