         "textEn": "Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume joint total normal stress 600 kPa and initial pore pressure 200 kPa, leaving effective compression 400 kPa. Added pressure 300 kPa leaves 100 kPa, excluding bond and three-dimensional redistribution.",
