       ],
       "objective": "說明「耗漿量與孔隙估算」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Grout take and void estimate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "耗漿量包含管內存量、回流、漏失和實際填充，不能全當成岩體孔隙。帷幕幾何的等效孔隙估算可做量級比較，但裂隙分布通常高度不均。 假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。 漿液流入大空洞或遠端通道會消耗大量材料而不形成連續帷幕，析水又使硬化體積小於注入體積。總耗漿相符仍不能證明目標裂隙全部被封住。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「耗漿量與孔隙估算」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Grout consumption includes line storage, returns, losses and actual filling. A geometric equivalent-void estimate compares scales, but fracture distribution is usually uneven and consumption cannot all be assigned to rock voids. Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01. Ideal volume is 60 m³; delivery 90 m³ leaves 30 m³ requiring source accounting rather than proving improvement. A cavity or distant channel consumes material without forming a continuous curtain, while bleeding reduces hardened volume. Matching total take therefore does not prove that all targeted flow paths have been sealed. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grout take and void estimate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設處理區100×20×3 m、等效可填孔隙率0.01，理想填充60 m³；實際供漿90 m³與其差30 m³須分解來源，非自動灌得更好。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume treatment zone 100×20×3 m with equivalent fillable void fraction 0.01.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「供漿總體積就是硬化後留在目標裂隙中的有效填充體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Total supplied grout equals the hardened effective volume retained in targeted fractures.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「耗漿量與孔隙估算」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grout take and void estimate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "耗漿量與孔隙估算",
         "titleEn": "Grout take and void estimate",
         "text": "耗漿量包含管內存量、回流、漏失和實際填充，不能全當成岩體孔隙。帷幕幾何的等效孔隙估算可做量級比較，但裂隙分布通常高度不均。",
         "textEn": "Grout consumption includes line storage, returns, losses and actual filling. A geometric equivalent-void estimate compares scales, but fracture distribution is usually uneven and consumption cannot all be assigned to rock voids.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
         ]
