       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Water-test normalization” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "孔段長度與試驗壓力不同時，流量需標準化才能初步比較。比例換算假設近似線性流動，裂隙張開或紊流會破壞這個關係。 假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。 同樣標準化數值可能來自不同裂隙幾何和各向異性，不能直接換成唯一k值。封塞旁漏或孔壁損傷也會提高讀數，需用獨立證據區分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓水試驗標準化」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Different stage lengths and test pressures require normalized flow for preliminary comparison. Proportional scaling assumes nearly linear flow, which joint opening and turbulence can invalidate. Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa. Linear normalization to 1 MPa gives 2.5 L/(min·m), not a permeability coefficient directly. Equal normalized values can arise from different fracture geometries and anisotropy and do not determine a unique k. Packer bypass and drilling damage also raise readings and require separate evidence to distinguish. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Water-test normalization” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量10 L/min、孔段5 m、有效試壓0.8 MPa，線性換算到1 MPa為10/5×1/0.8=2.5 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 10 L/min, stage length 5 m and effective pressure 0.8 MPa.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「標準化壓水值可不經幾何假設直接視為岩體滲透係數。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Normalized water-test flow directly equals rock permeability without geometric assumptions.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「壓水試驗標準化」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Water-test normalization”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
