       "objective": "說明「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "深孔會偏離設計線，孔口間距相符不代表深部間距相符。帷幕連續性依實際孔跡與可達處理範圍判讀，不能只按平面鑽孔圖驗收。 假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。 兩孔朝相反方向偏移會在深部拉開大缺口，同向偏移則可能讓整排偏離目標。僅看平均偏斜角，會漏掉局部曲折造成的最近或最遠間距。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「鑽孔偏斜與帷幕連續」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Deep holes deviate from design lines, so correct collar spacing does not establish spacing at depth. Curtain continuity depends on actual trajectories and treatment reach rather than the plan of drill collars alone. Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees. Horizontal offset Lsin2°=2.094 m, a straight-deviation example rather than a curved real trajectory. Opposing deviations open deep gaps, while common-direction deviation shifts the row away from its target. Mean deviation angle misses local curvature controlling the closest and widest spacing between treatment paths. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Borehole deviation and curtain continuity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設孔深60 m、固定偏斜角2°，水平偏移Lsin2°=2.094 m；直線偏孔示例，實際孔跡可能彎曲且方向變化。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume hole length 60 m and constant deviation two degrees.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「孔口間距完全符合設計就能保證深部帷幕一定連續。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Correct collar spacing guarantees a continuous curtain at every depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
