    {
     "id": "b237-v15-s5",
     "title": "耐久、維護與工程交接",
     "titleEn": "Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「序列孔耗量趨勢」與「獨立驗證與統計分布」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Successive-hole take trends\" and \"Independent verification and distributions\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b237-v15-33",
       "title": "序列孔耗量趨勢：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Successive-hole take trends: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-grout",
        "b-src-water",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-gravity"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b237-v15-32"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「序列孔耗量趨勢」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Successive-hole take trends” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "逐次縮小孔距常用來觀察處理後剩餘可灌性，但耗量下降也可能受材料、壓力和孔段條件改變。趨勢必須在可比較條件下解讀，不能單獨作完成證明。 假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。 先前孔堵住入口會使後續孔吸漿少，卻可能留下更遠通道；濃漿用量的重量與稀漿體積也不可直接比較。只追求下降曲線會導致錯誤完工判讀。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「序列孔耗量趨勢」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Successive spacing reduction can reveal remaining groutability, but declining take also reflects changed mixtures, pressures and stages. Trends require comparable conditions and cannot alone establish completion of a hydraulic barrier. Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m. Final take is eighty percent below initial, a trend indicator rather than an eighty-percent permeability reduction. Earlier entrance blockage lowers later take while leaving distant paths, and dense-grout mass cannot directly compare with dilute-grout volume. Pursuing a falling curve alone can therefore lead to an incorrect completion assessment. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Successive-hole take trends” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設可比較孔段的單位耗量由30降至12再到6 kg/m，最後相對初始下降80%；只是趨勢指標，不等同滲透率下降80%。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume comparable unit takes fall from 30 to 12 to 6 kg/m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「序列孔耗量趨勢」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Successive-hole take trends”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "序列孔耗量趨勢",
         "titleEn": "Successive-hole take trends",
         "text": "逐次縮小孔距常用來觀察處理後剩餘可灌性，但耗量下降也可能受材料、壓力和孔段條件改變。趨勢必須在可比較條件下解讀，不能單獨作完成證明。",
         "textEn": "Successive spacing reduction can reveal remaining groutability, but declining take also reflects changed mixtures, pressures and stages. Trends require comparable conditions and cannot alone establish completion of a hydraulic barrier.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-33-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：後續孔耗漿量下降百分之八十就代表滲透率必定下降八成。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: An eighty-percent decline in later-hole take guarantees an eighty-percent permeability reduction. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
         ]
