       "objective": "說明「獨立驗證與統計分布」如何影響壩基帷幕灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Independent verification and distributions” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation curtain grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "帷幕驗證應以水力性能與空間覆蓋為主，不能只重用施工過程數據。裂隙岩體常有偏態分布，平均值會被少數高透水段支配，需保留位置。 假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。平均(1+1+2+3+20)/5=5.4 L/(min·m)，中位2 L/(min·m)；非直接滲透係數，異常高值不能因中位低而刪除。 低中位值可能掩蓋穿越整個帷幕的單一高透水帶，而高值也可能是測試漏流。缺乏位置與原始曲線時，統計不能分辨真正缺口和儀器假象。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「獨立驗證與統計分布」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Curtain verification prioritizes hydraulic performance and coverage rather than reusing process records. Fractured rock commonly has skewed results, so a few conductive stages dominate means and locations must remain visible. Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m). Mean (1+1+2+3+20)/5 is 5.4 L/(min·m) and median is 2 L/(min·m). These are not direct permeability coefficients; the high value cannot be discarded because the median is low. A low median can hide one permeable band crossing the curtain, while a high value can reflect test leakage. Without location and raw curves, statistics cannot distinguish a real gap from an instrumentation artifact. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Independent verification and distributions” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設五孔段在近似線性流況下，按1 MPa有效試壓標準化的單位孔長流量為1、1、2、3、20 L/(min·m)。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume five stage flows per unit length, linearly normalized to effective test pressure 1 MPa under approximately linear flow, are 1, 1, 2, 3 and 20 L/(min·m).",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「獨立驗證與統計分布」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Independent verification and distributions”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "獨立驗證與統計分布",
         "titleEn": "Independent verification and distributions",
         "text": "帷幕驗證應以水力性能與空間覆蓋為主，不能只重用施工過程數據。裂隙岩體常有偏態分布，平均值會被少數高透水段支配，需保留位置。",
         "textEn": "Curtain verification prioritizes hydraulic performance and coverage rather than reusing process records. Fractured rock commonly has skewed results, so a few conductive stages dominate means and locations must remain visible.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b237-v15-37-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：驗證結果中位數很低就能忽略少數高透水孔段。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: A low verification median allows highly permeable individual stages to be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity"
         ]
