       "objective": "說明「水力阻力與廊道水頭」如何影響壩基排水廊道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Hydraulic resistance and gallery head” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation drainage galleries”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排水不是把壩基孔壓直接設為零，而是建立通向較低水頭邊界的有限導水路徑。岩體入流與排水出口共同決定節點水頭，出口淹沒會抬高整個系統的基準。 假設上游水頭50 m、出口10 m，入流導度0.002、排出導度0.008 m²/s，穩態節點水頭(0.002×50+0.008×10)/0.01=18 m；線性集總模型。 若只看排出流量，出口淹沒與排水阻塞可能產生相似結果，但內部壓力未必相同。非線性裂隙、暫態儲水和旁通通道會使單節點模型不足以定位異常。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水力阻力與廊道水頭」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Drainage does not simply set foundation pressure to zero. It provides finite conductance toward a lower-head boundary, while rock inflow and outlet conditions jointly establish the internal node head and submerged outlets raise that reference. Assume upstream head 50 m, outlet head 10 m and conductances 0.002 and 0.008 m²/s. Steady node head is 18 m in a linear lumped network. Outlet submergence and obstruction can produce similar flow changes with different internal pressures. Nonlinear fractures, transient storage and bypass paths can make a single-node model inadequate for locating the cause of deterioration. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Hydraulic resistance and gallery head” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設上游水頭50 m、出口10 m，入流導度0.002、排出導度0.008 m²/s，穩態節點水頭(0.002×50+0.008×10)/0.01=18 m；線性集總模型。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume upstream head 50 m, outlet head 10 m and conductances 0.002 and 0.008 m²/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要設置排水孔，壩基所有位置的孔隙水壓都會變成零。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Installing drain holes makes pore pressure zero at every foundation location.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水力阻力與廊道水頭」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Hydraulic resistance and gallery head”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
