       ],
       "objective": "說明「揚壓分布與合力」如何影響壩基排水廊道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Uplift distribution and resultant” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation drainage galleries”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "揚壓是沿底面的空間分布，排水位置的低壓點不能代表全底面。把量測頭換成壓力並積分，可以看出排水前後抗滑法向力的變化，但必須保留未量測區域的不確定性。 取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。假設每米壩長底寬40 m，水頭在x=0、10、40 m為40、10、5 m，分段線性積分水頭面積475 m²，揚力9.81×475=4659.75 kN/m。 測點間可能有局部高透水裂隙，線性插值會低估壓力峰值。若把不同高程儀器的原始壓力直接相連，還會把安裝高差誤認為真正的水頭梯度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「揚壓分布與合力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Uplift is a spatial pressure distribution, not the low value at one drain. Converting measured heads to pressure and integrating reveals changes in sliding normal force while retaining uncertainty between and beyond measurement points. Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³. Assume base width 40 m and heads 40, 10 and 5 m at x=0, 10 and 40 m. Piecewise-linear head area 475 m² gives uplift 4659.75 kN/m. Conductive fractures between instruments can produce pressure peaks missed by linear interpolation. Joining raw pressures from different elevations also confuses installation height with hydraulic gradient, producing an incorrect resultant despite apparently consistent readings. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Uplift distribution and resultant” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取淡水單位重γw=9.81 kN/m³。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use freshwater unit weight γw=9.81 kN/m³.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「單一排水孔附近的低壓讀值足以代表整個壩底的揚壓。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"One low pressure reading beside a drain represents uplift across the entire base.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「揚壓分布與合力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Uplift distribution and resultant”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b238-v15-05-k1",
         "title": "揚壓分布與合力",
         "titleEn": "Uplift distribution and resultant",
         "text": "揚壓是沿底面的空間分布，排水位置的低壓點不能代表全底面。把量測頭換成壓力並積分，可以看出排水前後抗滑法向力的變化，但必須保留未量測區域的不確定性。",
         "textEn": "Uplift is a spatial pressure distribution, not the low value at one drain. Converting measured heads to pressure and integrating reveals changes in sliding normal force while retaining uncertainty between and beyond measurement points.",
         "sourceIds": [
