       "objective": "從症狀倒推「揚壓分布與合力」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Uplift distribution and resultant” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "測點間可能有局部高透水裂隙，線性插值會低估壓力峰值。若把不同高程儀器的原始壓力直接相連，還會把安裝高差誤認為真正的水頭梯度。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Conductive fractures between instruments can produce pressure peaks missed by linear interpolation. Joining raw pressures from different elevations also confuses installation height with hydraulic gradient, producing an incorrect resultant despite apparently consistent readings. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若把不同高程儀器的原始壓力直接相連，還會把安裝高差誤認為真正的水頭梯度。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Joining raw pressures from different elevations also confuses installation height with hydraulic gradient, producing an incorrect resultant despite apparently consistent readings.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「單一排水孔附近的低壓讀值足以代表整個壩底的揚壓。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One low pressure reading beside a drain represents uplift across the entire base.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b238-v15-08-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "測點間可能有局部高透水裂隙，線性插值會低估壓力峰值。若把不同高程儀器的原始壓力直接相連，還會把安裝高差誤認為真正的水頭梯度。",
         "textEn": "Conductive fractures between instruments can produce pressure peaks missed by linear interpolation. Joining raw pressures from different elevations also confuses installation height with hydraulic gradient, producing an incorrect resultant despite apparently consistent readings.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-joints",
          "b-src-water"
         ]
