    {
     "id": "b238-v15-s2",
     "title": "水力機制、材料與定量模型",
     "titleEn": "Hydraulics, materials and quantitative models",
     "description": "本階段聚焦「排水孔間距與覆蓋」與「導水能力的趨勢比較」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。",
     "descriptionEn": "This stage covers \"Drain spacing and coverage\" and \"Conductance trend comparison\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.",
     "steps": [
      {
       "id": "b238-v15-09",
       "title": "排水孔間距與覆蓋：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Drain spacing and coverage: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usace-gravity",
        "v15s-usbr-joints",
        "b-src-water"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b238-v15-08"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「排水孔間距與覆蓋」如何影響壩基排水廊道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Drain spacing and coverage” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation drainage galleries”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "孔數增加只有在與導水裂隙相交時才可能改善排水，均勻孔口間距不代表均勻影響範圍。覆蓋概念可先做幾何篩選，再用水力回應驗證相互影響是否連續。 假設一維等效影響半徑2.5 m、孔距6 m，相鄰影響帶留下6−2×2.5=1 m缺口；半徑為教學假設，不是岩體固有常數。 實際裂隙各向異性可能讓影響區狹長而非圓形，兩孔接近也未必相通。單一試驗水位得到的範圍可能隨裂隙開合改變，不能永久視為固定覆蓋圖。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「排水孔間距與覆蓋」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Additional drains help only where they intercept conducting fractures. Uniform collar spacing does not ensure uniform influence, so geometric coverage is preliminary screening that requires hydraulic response evidence to establish continuity. Assume one-dimensional influence radius 2.5 m and spacing 6 m. Adjacent influence zones leave a one-metre gap; this radius is an assumed teaching parameter, not a rock constant. Anisotropic fractures create elongated rather than circular influence regions, and close drains may remain disconnected. Coverage observed at one reservoir level can change as fractures open or close and is not a permanent geometric guarantee. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Drain spacing and coverage” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設一維等效影響半徑2.5 m、孔距6 m，相鄰影響帶留下6−2×2.5=1 m缺口；半徑為教學假設，不是岩體固有常數。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume one-dimensional influence radius 2.5 m and spacing 6 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「排水孔口等距排列就能保證深部各處具有相同的排水效果。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equally spaced drain collars guarantee equal drainage effectiveness throughout the foundation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「排水孔間距與覆蓋」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Drain spacing and coverage”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b238-v15-09-k1",
         "title": "排水孔間距與覆蓋",
         "titleEn": "Drain spacing and coverage",
         "text": "孔數增加只有在與導水裂隙相交時才可能改善排水，均勻孔口間距不代表均勻影響範圍。覆蓋概念可先做幾何篩選，再用水力回應驗證相互影響是否連續。",
         "textEn": "Additional drains help only where they intercept conducting fractures. Uniform collar spacing does not ensure uniform influence, so geometric coverage is preliminary screening that requires hydraulic response evidence to establish continuity.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usace-gravity",
          "v15s-usbr-joints",
          "b-src-water"
