       ],
       "objective": "說明「導水能力的趨勢比較」如何影響壩基排水廊道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Conductance trend comparison” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation drainage galleries”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排水流量必須與驅動水頭一起比較，因為庫水位降低本來就會減少流量。以流量除水頭差得到的表觀導度，可篩選退化趨勢，但仍需辨認岩體入流邊界的改變。 假設同一孔初始Q=0.004 m³/s、Δh=20 m，後來0.003 m³/s、Δh=25 m，表觀導度由0.0002降至0.00012 m²/s，下降40%；穩態線性假設。 流量下降同時伴隨水頭升高通常比單獨流量變化更值得調查，但仍不能僅憑比值定位沉積位置。管路漏失或量測分流也可能造成表觀導度下降而非孔內堵塞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導水能力的趨勢比較」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Drain flow must be compared with its driving head because a lower reservoir naturally reduces discharge. Apparent conductance screens deterioration trends but still requires distinction from changes in rock inflow and outlet conditions. Assume flow and head change from 0.004 m³/s at 20 m to 0.003 m³/s at 25 m. Apparent conductance declines from 0.0002 to 0.00012 m²/s, or forty percent. Lower flow with higher head is more informative than flow alone, but the ratio does not locate deposits. Leakage in collection pipes or unmeasured diversions can reduce apparent conductance without an obstruction inside the drain. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Conductance trend comparison” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設同一孔初始Q=0.004 m³/s、Δh=20 m，後來0.003 m³/s、Δh=25 m，表觀導度由0.0002降至0.00012 m²/s，下降40%；穩態線性假設。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow and head change from 0.004 m³/s at 20 m to 0.003 m³/s at 25 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「排水流量減少總是表示滲漏減少，因此排水性能必然改善。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Decreasing drain discharge always means less leakage and therefore improved drainage performance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「導水能力的趨勢比較」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Conductance trend comparison”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b238-v15-13-k1",
         "title": "導水能力的趨勢比較",
         "titleEn": "Conductance trend comparison",
         "text": "排水流量必須與驅動水頭一起比較，因為庫水位降低本來就會減少流量。以流量除水頭差得到的表觀導度，可篩選退化趨勢，但仍需辨認岩體入流邊界的改變。",
         "textEn": "Drain flow must be compared with its driving head because a lower reservoir naturally reduces discharge. Apparent conductance screens deterioration trends but still requires distinction from changes in rock inflow and outlet conditions.",
         "sourceIds": [
