       "objective": "說明「廊道熱量與通風尺度」如何影響壩基排水廊道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Gallery heat and ventilation scale” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation drainage galleries”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "設備散熱、濕空氣與岩體熱交換共同影響廊道環境。簡單顯熱平衡只能估通風尺度，不能取代氣體、濕度與局部氣流評估，也不能作為人員進入許可依據。 假設設備顯熱12 kW、空氣密度1.2 kg/m³、比熱1005 J/(kg·K)、容許教學溫升5 K，Q=12000/(1.2×1005×5)=1.990 m³/s；忽略潛熱與岩體交換。 總風量符合估算仍可能有局部停滯區，濕氣凝結會影響設備與表面耐久。只用平均溫度判斷環境充分性，會漏掉獨立的氣體風險和人員活動需求。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「廊道熱量與通風尺度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Equipment heat, moisture and rock heat exchange shape gallery conditions. A sensible-heat balance estimates ventilation scale but cannot replace gas, humidity or local-airflow assessment and does not establish personnel-entry authorization. Assume sensible heat 12 kW, air density 1.2 kg/m³, heat capacity 1005 J/(kg·K) and teaching rise 5 K. Flow is 1.990 m³/s, excluding latent heat and rock exchange. Adequate total airflow can coexist with stagnant zones, and condensation affects equipment and surface durability. Average temperature alone overlooks separate gas hazards and occupancy requirements, so the heat calculation cannot establish overall environmental suitability. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Gallery heat and ventilation scale” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設設備顯熱12 kW、空氣密度1.2 kg/m³、比熱1005 J/(kg·K)、容許教學溫升5 K，Q=12000/(1.2×1005×5)=1.990 m³/s；忽略潛熱與岩體交換。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume sensible heat 12 kW, air density 1.2 kg/m³, heat capacity 1005 J/(kg·K) and teaching rise 5 K.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要顯熱通風計算合格，就不必再評估廊道氣體與濕度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Passing the sensible-heat ventilation calculation removes any need to assess gallery gases or humidity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「廊道熱量與通風尺度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Gallery heat and ventilation scale”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b238-v15-25-k1",
