       "objective": "說明「析出沉積與質量收支」如何影響壩基排水廊道的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Precipitation deposits and mass balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam-foundation drainage galleries”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "排水通道的沉積可來自化學析出或攜帶顆粒，外觀相似但成因與趨勢不同。溶質濃度差乘流量只能估潛在沉積通量，仍需確認採樣位置、混合與其他反應路徑。 假設流量2 L/s、進出溶解物差20 mg/L且全轉為沉積，日質量2×20×86400/10⁶=3.456 kg/day；非指定礦物且忽略旁路與再溶解。 不同比例水源混合會造成濃度降低而沒有沉積，採樣瓶內反應也會改變結果。即使總質量小，局部狹窄處的沉積仍可能主導水力阻力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「析出沉積與質量收支」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Drain deposits can arise from chemical precipitation or transported particles with similar appearance but different causes. Concentration difference times flow estimates potential deposition only after accounting for sampling locations, mixing and alternative reaction paths. Assume flow 2 L/s and dissolved-mass decrease 20 mg/L, entirely retained as deposits. Daily mass is 3.456 kg/day, without specifying mineral composition and excluding bypass or redissolution. Mixing different waters lowers concentration without deposition, and reactions inside sample bottles alter results. Even small total deposit mass can dominate hydraulic resistance when concentrated at a narrow section rather than distributed uniformly. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Precipitation deposits and mass balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設流量2 L/s、進出溶解物差20 mg/L且全轉為沉積，日質量2×20×86400/10⁶=3.456 kg/day；非指定礦物且忽略旁路與再溶解。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume flow 2 L/s and dissolved-mass decrease 20 mg/L, entirely retained as deposits.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「出水溶解物濃度比進水低，就能確定全部差值都沉積在排水孔內。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Lower outlet concentration proves that the entire dissolved-mass difference deposited inside the drain.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「析出沉積與質量收支」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Precipitation deposits and mass balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
