       "objective": "從症狀倒推「析出沉積與質量收支」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Precipitation deposits and mass balance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "不同比例水源混合會造成濃度降低而沒有沉積，採樣瓶內反應也會改變結果。即使總質量小，局部狹窄處的沉積仍可能主導水力阻力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Mixing different waters lowers concentration without deposition, and reactions inside sample bottles alter results. Even small total deposit mass can dominate hydraulic resistance when concentrated at a narrow section rather than distributed uniformly. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：即使總質量小，局部狹窄處的沉積仍可能主導水力阻力。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Even small total deposit mass can dominate hydraulic resistance when concentrated at a narrow section rather than distributed uniformly.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「出水溶解物濃度比進水低，就能確定全部差值都沉積在排水孔內。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Lower outlet concentration proves that the entire dissolved-mass difference deposited inside the drain.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
