       "observationEn": "Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for compartment grout-volume balance, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconcile integrated supply, collected returns and line storage by compartment, converting measurement uncertainty to volume bounds. Compare high-take regions with aperture maps and boundary-seal records to distinguish geometry, escape and metering discrepancies. Cross-check delivered volume by independent weighing.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：耗量超過理論空隙可能是外漏或鄰區串通，少於理論量也可能是入口濾堵。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Excess take can indicate escape or communication with another compartment, while low take can reflect entrance blockage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
