       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Residual channels and cubic sensitivity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam contraction-joint grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "少量未填通道可能控制整個接縫的滲漏，因薄縫層流對開度呈立方敏感。封堵體積百分比與水力改善百分比沒有固定對應，連通路徑比平均孔隙更重要。 假設相同寬度、長度和壓差的平行縫，開度0.3降至0.1 mm，理想水流比(0.1/0.3)³=0.03704，減少96.296%；牛頓層流且無旁通。 局部裂縫紊流、粗糙與壓力張開都會偏離立方律，旁路還可能繞過已填區。若把理想降幅當成材料保證，會漏掉真正控制滲漏的最薄弱連通段。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「殘留通道與立方敏感性」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A small unfilled channel can control joint leakage because laminar thin-gap flow scales with aperture cubed. Filled-volume percentage does not have a fixed relationship to hydraulic improvement; connectivity matters more than average void fraction. Assume equal width, length and pressure difference with aperture reduced from 0.3 to 0.1 mm. Ideal flow ratio is 0.03704, a 96.296-percent reduction for Newtonian laminar flow without bypass. Turbulence, roughness and pressure-induced opening violate the cubic idealization, while bypasses avoid treated regions. Treating the ideal reduction as a material guarantee misses the weakest connected segment that actually governs leakage. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Residual channels and cubic sensitivity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設相同寬度、長度和壓差的平行縫，開度0.3降至0.1 mm，理想水流比(0.1/0.3)³=0.03704，減少96.296%；牛頓層流且無旁通。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equal width, length and pressure difference with aperture reduced from 0.3 to 0.1 mm.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「填滿接縫體積百分之九十，就一定能把滲漏流量降低百分之九十。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Filling ninety percent of joint volume necessarily reduces leakage by ninety percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
