         "textEn": "Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equal width, length and pressure difference with aperture reduced from 0.3 to 0.1 mm. Ideal flow ratio is 0.03704, a 96.296-percent reduction for Newtonian laminar flow without bypass.",
