      {
       "id": "b239-v15-13",
       "title": "漿柱水頭與分區壓力：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Grout-column head and compartment pressure: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-arch-2",
        "v15s-usace-grout",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-joints"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b239-v15-12"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「漿柱水頭與分區壓力」如何影響大壩接縫灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Grout-column head and compartment pressure” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam contraction-joint grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "同一接縫內不同高程的漿壓不相同，密度與靜水頭必須和管損分開。儀表位置高於分區時，下部壓力可能大於表壓，不能把單一讀值當整片接縫受壓。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設靜止漿體密度1800 kg/m³、高差10 m，壓力差ρgΔz=176.58 kPa；若有流動、屈服或堵塞，不再等同單純靜水分布。 高黏度或正在凝結的漿體可形成非靜水壓差，分區堵塞又會隔離儀器。若僅提高泵端壓力追求讀值一致，可能在未量測區造成不預期的開縫與串漿。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「漿柱水頭與分區壓力」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Grout pressure varies with elevation inside a joint, and hydrostatic head must be separated from line losses. A gauge above a compartment can underrepresent pressure lower down, so one reading cannot describe loading over the whole interface. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume stationary grout density 1800 kg/m³ over ten metres. Hydrostatic difference is 176.58 kPa; flow, yield behavior or blockage can invalidate the simple hydrostatic distribution. Viscous or setting grout can develop nonhydrostatic pressure differences, and obstruction isolates instruments. Increasing pump pressure merely to equalize readings can create unexpected joint opening or cross-compartment flow in unmonitored regions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Grout-column head and compartment pressure” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「位於不同高程的接縫灌漿壓力計應該不經修正讀到完全相同壓力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Joint-grout gauges at different elevations should read identical pressure without correction.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「漿柱水頭與分區壓力」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Grout-column head and compartment pressure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b239-v15-13-k1",
         "title": "漿柱水頭與分區壓力",
         "titleEn": "Grout-column head and compartment pressure",
         "text": "同一接縫內不同高程的漿壓不相同，密度與靜水頭必須和管損分開。儀表位置高於分區時，下部壓力可能大於表壓，不能把單一讀值當整片接縫受壓。",
         "textEn": "Grout pressure varies with elevation inside a joint, and hydrostatic head must be separated from line losses. A gauge above a compartment can underrepresent pressure lower down, so one reading cannot describe loading over the whole interface.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
