       "objective": "說明「析水與硬化後空隙」如何影響大壩接縫灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Bleeding and hardened voids” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam contraction-joint grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "灌入時連續的漿體可能因析水、沉降與體積變化在上緣留下空隙。新拌材料體積並不等於硬化填充體積，分區上部尤其需要獨立證據而非只看出漿顏色。 假設新拌填充體積2.4 m³、自由析水比例5%，分離水量0.12 m³；若均集中在面積20 m²的上部水平面，等效空層6 mm，僅幾何極端示例。 小型量筒的析水比例不一定可直接放大到受限薄縫，泌水又可能沿通道外排。忽略拘束與水路會把最壞幾何空隙誤當實際缺陷，或相反漏掉局部空洞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「析水與硬化後空隙」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Initially continuous grout can leave upper voids through bleeding, settlement and volume change. Fresh volume is not hardened filled volume, and upper compartment regions require independent evidence rather than relying on the appearance of returns. Assume fresh fill 2.4 m³ and free bleeding five percent, producing 0.12 m³ water. Concentrated over an upper horizontal area 20 m², this corresponds to six millimetres of void, a geometric extreme. Cylinder bleeding does not scale directly to confined thin joints, and bleed water can leave through channels. Ignoring confinement and drainage can mistake an extreme geometric void for actual damage or overlook a localized unfilled pocket. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Bleeding and hardened voids” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設新拌填充體積2.4 m³、自由析水比例5%，分離水量0.12 m³；若均集中在面積20 m²的上部水平面，等效空層6 mm，僅幾何極端示例。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume fresh fill 2.4 m³ and free bleeding five percent, producing 0.12 m³ water.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只要新拌漿液充滿接縫，硬化後就不可能再形成任何空隙。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Once fresh grout fills a joint, no void can develop during hardening.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「析水與硬化後空隙」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Bleeding and hardened voids”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
