       ],
       "objective": "說明「溫度與材料反應速率」如何影響大壩接縫灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Temperature and reaction rate” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam contraction-joint grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "灌漿材料的可用時間和強度發展受溫度影響，固定鐘錶時間不能代表相同反應程度。簡化反應速率可比較溫度敏感性，但實際配方、摻料與早期反應需要試驗校正。 假設表觀活化能40 kJ/mol，R=8.314 J/(mol·K)，以293.15 K為基準，303.15 K速率比exp[(40000/8.314)(1/293.15−1/303.15)]=1.718；非凝結時間保證。 材料反應不是全程單一速率，外加劑可改變誘導期，桶內發熱也會讓試體失去代表性。直接用理論倍率縮短施工等待時間，可能誤判材料可操作性與承載能力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「溫度與材料反應速率」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Temperature changes grout working time and strength development, so equal clock time does not imply equal reaction progress. A simplified rate model compares sensitivity but requires calibration for mixture composition, admixtures and early-age reactions. Assume activation energy 40 kJ/mol and R=8.314 J/(mol·K). Relative rate at 303.15 K versus 293.15 K is 1.718, an idealized comparison rather than a setting-time guarantee. Reaction does not follow one rate throughout; admixtures alter induction and self-heating changes sample representativeness. Scaling waiting times directly by a theoretical ratio can misjudge workability and load-transfer capacity despite correct arithmetic. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Temperature and reaction rate” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設表觀活化能40 kJ/mol，R=8.314 J/(mol·K)，以293.15 K為基準，303.15 K速率比exp[(40000/8.314)(1/293.15−1/303.15)]=1.718；非凝結時間保證。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume activation energy 40 kJ/mol and R=8.314 J/(mol·K).",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「溫度提高十度後，所有灌漿配方的凝結時間都會固定縮短一半。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"A ten-degree temperature increase halves setting time for every grout mixture.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「溫度與材料反應速率」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Temperature and reaction rate”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b239-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "溫度與材料反應速率",
         "titleEn": "Temperature and reaction rate",
         "text": "灌漿材料的可用時間和強度發展受溫度影響，固定鐘錶時間不能代表相同反應程度。簡化反應速率可比較溫度敏感性，但實際配方、摻料與早期反應需要試驗校正。",
         "textEn": "Temperature changes grout working time and strength development, so equal clock time does not imply equal reaction progress. A simplified rate model compares sensitivity but requires calibration for mixture composition, admixtures and early-age reactions.",
         "sourceIds": [
