       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b239-v15-32"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「壓力衰減與漏失辨識」如何影響大壩接縫灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Pressure decay and loss diagnosis” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam contraction-joint grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "封閉試驗中的壓力衰減同時受洩漏導度與系統可壓縮儲量控制。衰減快未必表示大裂縫，空氣泡、軟管和結構變形都會改變儲量，需先辨認量測系統。 假設線性儲量C=0.0005 m³/kPa、漏失導度G=0.00001 m³/(s·kPa)，時間常數C/G=50 s，半衰時間50ln2=34.657 s；固定邊界與單一儲量。 壓力計漂移、閥漏與漿材凝結會產生非水力衰減，單一半衰時間無法分開導度和儲量。若不獨立量測其中一項，就存在多組參數都能符合相同曲線。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「壓力衰減與漏失辨識」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Pressure decay in a closed test depends on leakage conductance and compressible storage. Rapid decay does not uniquely identify a large crack, because entrained air, flexible hoses and structural deformation change the system response. Assume linear storage C=0.0005 m³/kPa and leakage conductance G=0.00001 m³/(s·kPa). Time constant is fifty seconds and half-life 34.657 seconds, with fixed boundaries and one storage compartment. Gauge drift, valve leakage and setting introduce nonhydraulic decay, while one half-life cannot separate storage from conductance. Without independent measurement, multiple parameter combinations fit the same curve and do not uniquely establish joint tightness. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Pressure decay and loss diagnosis” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設線性儲量C=0.0005 m³/kPa、漏失導度G=0.00001 m³/(s·kPa)，時間常數C/G=50 s，半衰時間50ln2=34.657 s；固定邊界與單一儲量。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume linear storage C=0.0005 m³/kPa and leakage conductance G=0.00001 m³/(s·kPa).",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「只量到一個壓力半衰時間，就能唯一算出接縫的滲漏導度。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"One measured pressure half-life uniquely determines the leakage conductance of a joint.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「壓力衰減與漏失辨識」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Pressure decay and loss diagnosis”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b239-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "壓力衰減與漏失辨識",
         "titleEn": "Pressure decay and loss diagnosis",
         "text": "封閉試驗中的壓力衰減同時受洩漏導度與系統可壓縮儲量控制。衰減快未必表示大裂縫，空氣泡、軟管和結構變形都會改變儲量，需先辨認量測系統。",
         "textEn": "Pressure decay in a closed test depends on leakage conductance and compressible storage. Rapid decay does not uniquely identify a large crack, because entrained air, flexible hoses and structural deformation change the system response.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-joints"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b239-v15-33-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：只量到一個壓力半衰時間，就能唯一算出接縫的滲漏導度。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: One measured pressure half-life uniquely determines the leakage conductance of a joint. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "v15s-usace-grout",
