      {
       "id": "b239-v15-34",
       "title": "壓力衰減與漏失辨識：定量估算",
       "titleEn": "Pressure decay and loss diagnosis: quantitative estimate",
       "estimatedMinutes": 30,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-arch-2",
        "v15s-usace-grout",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-joints"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b239-v15-33"
       ],
       "objective": "以數值模型估算「壓力衰減與漏失辨識」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、水頭、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。",
       "objectiveEn": "Estimate the key quantities of “Pressure decay and loss diagnosis” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, water head, load or material parameters move.",
       "instruction": "依下列模型逐步重算：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設線性儲量C=0.0005 m³/kPa、漏失導度G=0.00001 m³/(s·kPa)，時間常數C/G=50 s，半衰時間50ln2=34.657 s；固定邊界與單一儲量。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。",
       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume linear storage C=0.0005 m³/kPa and leakage conductance G=0.00001 m³/(s·kPa). Time constant is fifty seconds and half-life 34.657 seconds, with fixed boundaries and one storage compartment. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
       "observation": "如何核對：先用已知密閉容積校正設備儲量，記錄溫度、含氣與閥件漏失，再擬合多時段壓力曲線；比較流量收支與壓力模型殘差，確認單指數衰減是否足以描述資料。",
       "observationEn": "How to cross-check: Calibrate equipment storage with a known sealed volume and record temperature, entrained air and valve leakage before fitting pressure segments.",
       "failure": "計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。",
       "failureEn": "Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.",
       "check": "依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。",
       "checkEn": "Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.",
