      {
       "id": "b239-v15-37",
       "title": "波速檢測與接觸證據：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Wave velocity and contact evidence: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-arch-2",
        "v15s-usace-grout",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-joints"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b239-v15-36"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「波速檢測與接觸證據」如何影響大壩接縫灌漿的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Wave velocity and contact evidence” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Dam contraction-joint grouting”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "彈性波走時可協助辨認不連續區，但波可能繞行裂縫，也受含水率與溫度影響。接縫黏結與抗剪傳力不能僅由高波速推定，需與幾何和力學證據交叉查核。 假設路徑2 m、完整材料波速4000 m/s，走時500 microseconds；接縫使走時增加20 microseconds，表觀速度2/0.00052=3846.15 m/s，非黏結強度換算。 首波拾取偏差可與小接縫延遲同量級，濕裂縫也可能傳波而不傳剪。將單一路徑速度直接換成全接縫黏結百分比，會把訊號品質與材料行為混為一談。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「波速檢測與接觸證據」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Elastic-wave travel time helps identify discontinuities, but waves can bypass cracks and respond to moisture and temperature. High apparent velocity alone does not establish bond or shear transfer, requiring geometric and mechanical corroboration. Assume a two-metre path at 4000 m/s, giving 500 microseconds. Added joint delay twenty microseconds reduces apparent velocity to 3846.15 m/s, without providing a bond-strength conversion. First-arrival picking error can rival the joint delay, and a wet crack may transmit waves without shear capacity. Converting one velocity into a whole-joint bonded percentage confuses signal quality with actual mechanical behavior. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Wave velocity and contact evidence” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設路徑2 m、完整材料波速4000 m/s，走時500 microseconds；接縫使走時增加20 microseconds，表觀速度2/0.00052=3846.15 m/s，非黏結強度換算。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume a two-metre path at 4000 m/s, giving 500 microseconds.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「接縫超音波速度很高就足以證明其黏結強度和抗剪能力完全恢復。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"High ultrasonic velocity alone proves full restoration of joint bond strength and shear capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「波速檢測與接觸證據」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Wave velocity and contact evidence”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b239-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "波速檢測與接觸證據",
         "titleEn": "Wave velocity and contact evidence",
         "text": "彈性波走時可協助辨認不連續區，但波可能繞行裂縫，也受含水率與溫度影響。接縫黏結與抗剪傳力不能僅由高波速推定，需與幾何和力學證據交叉查核。",
         "textEn": "Elastic-wave travel time helps identify discontinuities, but waves can bypass cracks and respond to moisture and temperature. High apparent velocity alone does not establish bond or shear transfer, requiring geometric and mechanical corroboration.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-joints"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b239-v15-37-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：接縫超音波速度很高就足以證明其黏結強度和抗剪能力完全恢復。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: High ultrasonic velocity alone proves full restoration of joint bond strength and shear capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-arch-2",
          "v15s-usace-grout",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-joints"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "關於「波速檢測與接觸證據」，下列哪一項敘述正確？",
        "questionEn": "Which statement about \"Wave velocity and contact evidence\" is correct?",
        "options": [
         "接縫超音波速度很高就足以證明其黏結強度和抗剪能力完全恢復。",
         "彈性波走時可協助辨認不連續區，但波可能繞行裂縫，也受含水率與溫度影響。",
         "用當日外氣溫度就能直接推定整塊混凝土的接縫開度。"
        ],
        "optionsEn": [
