      {
       "id": "b240-v15-13",
       "title": "入口局部損失與堵塞：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Entrance loss and obstruction: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-coffer",
        "v15s-usbr-construction",
        "b-src-water",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b240-v15-12"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「入口局部損失與堵塞」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Entrance loss and obstruction” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。漂流物改變收縮和有效面積，速度增加又會放大損失，形成非線性的能力下降。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設原入口流速3 m/s、損失係數K=0.5，局部損失Kv²/(2g)=0.2294 m；同流量下有效面積減20%，速度3.75 m/s，若K不變損失增56.25%。 漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。偏流造成單側壓力與沖刷，即使總流量尚可，也可能已影響入口結構或鄰近岸坡。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「入口局部損失與堵塞」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "An entrance redistributes river flow into a tunnel or channel, with losses controlled by more than area. Debris changes contraction and effective opening, increasing velocity and amplifying losses nonlinearly as capacity declines. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume entrance velocity 3 m/s and loss coefficient 0.5, giving loss 0.2294 m. At constant discharge, twenty-percent area reduction raises velocity to 3.75 m/s and loss by 56.25 percent if K is unchanged. Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. Asymmetric flow creates one-sided pressure and scour even while total discharge appears adequate, affecting the entrance and adjacent banks. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Entrance loss and obstruction” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「入口局部損失與堵塞」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Entrance loss and obstruction”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-13-k1",
         "title": "入口局部損失與堵塞",
         "titleEn": "Entrance loss and obstruction",
         "text": "入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。漂流物改變收縮和有效面積，速度增加又會放大損失，形成非線性的能力下降。",
         "textEn": "An entrance redistributes river flow into a tunnel or channel, with losses controlled by more than area. Debris changes contraction and effective opening, increasing velocity and amplifying losses nonlinearly as capacity declines.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-coffer",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-13-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Reducing entrance area by twenty percent always raises head loss by only twenty percent. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-coffer",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        }
       ],
       "quiz": {
        "question": "關於「入口局部損失與堵塞」，下列哪一項敘述正確？",
        "questionEn": "Which statement about \"Entrance loss and obstruction\" is correct?",
        "options": [
         "入口有效面積減少百分之二十，水頭損失也一定只增加百分之二十。",
         "入口把河道動能重新分配到隧洞或渠道，局部損失不只由截面大小決定。",
         "圍堰只是臨時構造，所以抗滑計算可以不扣除基底揚壓。"
