       "observationEn": "Site practice: Prepare a reviewable evidence sheet for entrance loss and obstruction, recording data time, units, model applicability and reviewer. Reconstruct head loss from upstream and downstream levels and local velocity, recording debris coverage and approach angle. Compare different blockage patterns rather than total area alone, identifying asymmetric flow, vortices and air entrainment. Check whether blockage patterns shift vortex locations.",
       "failure": "注意干擾：漂流物會同時改變K與面積，固定係數估算可能低估實際損失。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、水頭與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。",
       "failureEn": "Watch for interference: Debris changes both loss coefficient and area, so a fixed coefficient can understate deterioration. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, water head and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.",
