       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Contraction flow and scour similarity” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "導流造成的急流與回流會重新分配河床剪力，水深弗勞德數只能描述重力慣性比例。沖刷還取決於顆粒、尾水與流況歷程，不能只憑一個無因次數直接推定深度。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設局部流速5 m/s、水深2 m，Fr=v/sqrt(gy)=1.129；教學自由水面尺度，未給粒徑與持續時間，因此不推算沖刷深度。 平均斷面流速可能漏掉貼岸高速射流，護底本身又會把沖刷轉移到末端。以某一瞬間無明顯變化判定穩定，可能忽略長時間淘刷或洪水退水期的破壞。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「收縮流與沖刷相似」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Diversion-induced jets and recirculation redistribute bed stress. Depth Froude number describes inertia relative to gravity, while scour also depends on sediment, tailwater and duration and cannot be predicted from one dimensionless number alone. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume local velocity 5 m/s and depth 2 m. Froude number is 1.129 for a free-surface scale; sediment size and duration are unspecified, so scour depth is not inferred. Section-average velocity misses bank-attached jets, while protection can shift scour to its downstream edge. Apparent short-term stability does not exclude cumulative erosion or failure during recession when support and hydraulic conditions change. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Contraction flow and scour similarity” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s².",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「兩個河道的弗勞德數相同，就能保證最終沖刷深度完全相同。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Equal Froude numbers in two channels guarantee identical final scour depth.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
