       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Closure-gap velocity amplification” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "截流過程使剩餘缺口逐步縮小，局部流速和水面差會隨分流比例共同變動。固定流量除面積可示範敏感性，但實際河水可能轉入導流通道或上游暫存。 取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。假設瞬間缺口流量120 m³/s、水深4 m、寬由12降至8 m且分流暫不變，平均速度由2.5增至3.75 m/s；動能水頭由0.3186增至0.7167 m。 缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「截流缺口的流速放大」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Closure progressively narrows the remaining gap, changing velocity and head difference together with flow partition. Constant discharge divided by area illustrates sensitivity, while actual water may shift into diversion works or upstream storage. Use gravitational acceleration g=9.81 m/s². Assume instantaneous gap flow 120 m³/s at depth four metres and width reducing from twelve to eight metres without repartition. Mean velocity rises from 2.5 to 3.75 m/s and velocity head from 0.3186 to 0.7167 m. Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Closure-gap velocity amplification” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：取重力加速度g=9.81 m/s²。",
