       "objective": "從症狀倒推「截流缺口的流速放大」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Closure-gap velocity amplification” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「截流缺口縮小時，河道流量分配和水深必定保持原值不變。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"During gap closure, discharge partition and water depth necessarily remain unchanged.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-28-k1",
         "title": "失效模式",
         "titleEn": "Failure mode",
         "text": "缺口縮窄也會抬高水頭並改變導流分配，流速未必按面積倒數持續上升。只使用上一階段的水深與流量，可能低估局部射流、床面變形和材料受力。",
         "textEn": "Narrowing raises head and changes diversion partition, so velocity need not continue increasing inversely with area. Reusing previous-stage depth and flow can misrepresent local jets, bed changes and forces on closure materials.",
         "sourceIds": [
