       "objective": "說明「洪峰暫存與水位上升」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Flood storage and stage rise” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "導流設施的瞬時出流小於洪峰時，差額會累積在上游暫存區。容量檢核需積分整個超額歷線，不能只比較洪峰差，也不能假定所有可見河谷空間都可用於儲洪。 假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。 出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「洪峰暫存與水位上升」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "When diversion outflow falls below inflow, excess accumulates upstream. Storage checks integrate the full excess hydrograph rather than peak difference alone and cannot assume all visible valley space is available flood storage. Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s. Required storage is 216000 m³; constant effective surface area 120000 m² gives stage rise 1.8 m, excluding changing outlet capacity. Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Flood storage and stage rise” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設超過導流能力的流量歷線為底寬2 h、峰值60 m³/s三角形，所需暫存0.5×7200×60=216000 m³；若有效面積120000 m²恆定，水位升1.8 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume triangular excess flow lasting two hours and peaking at 60 m³/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「洪峰暫存與水位上升」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Flood storage and stage rise”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-29-k1",
         "title": "洪峰暫存與水位上升",
         "titleEn": "Flood storage and stage rise",
         "text": "導流設施的瞬時出流小於洪峰時，差額會累積在上游暫存區。容量檢核需積分整個超額歷線，不能只比較洪峰差，也不能假定所有可見河谷空間都可用於儲洪。",
         "textEn": "When diversion outflow falls below inflow, excess accumulates upstream. Storage checks integrate the full excess hydrograph rather than peak difference alone and cannot assume all visible valley space is available flood storage.",
         "sourceIds": [
