       "objective": "從症狀倒推「洪峰暫存與水位上升」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Flood storage and stage rise” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "出流能力通常隨水位上升改變，固定能力三角示例可能高估或低估暫存。洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Outflow capacity usually changes with stage, making the fixed-capacity triangle potentially conservative or unconservative. Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：洪水期間地形被沖淤改變也會改寫容量，不能把一次測量曲線當作永遠有效。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Erosion and deposition can also alter storage during a flood, so one surveyed relation is not permanently valid.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「洪峰流量減去導流能力的差值，就是洪水所需的暫存體積。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Peak inflow minus diversion capacity directly equals the required flood-storage volume.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-32-k1",
