       "objective": "說明「基坑降水與滲流供給」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "圍堰內基坑降水會增加外側水體的水頭差，抽水需求可能隨開挖深度增加。達西估算提供連續介質量級，但岩體裂隙、各向異性與河床補注需要專門辨認。 假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。 抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「基坑降水與滲流供給」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Dewatering inside a cofferdam increases head difference from the river, so pumping demand can grow with excavation depth. Darcy estimates provide a continuum scale, while fractures, anisotropy and riverbed recharge require distinct evidence. Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres. One-dimensional steady Darcy flow is 0.003 m³/s or three litres per second, excluding concentrated fractures. Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設等效透水係數2×10⁻⁵ m/s、過流面積300 m²、水頭差10 m、路徑20 m，Q=kAΔh/L=0.003 m³/s即3 L/s；一維穩態且無集中裂隙。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「基坑降水與滲流供給」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-33-k1",
         "title": "基坑降水與滲流供給",
         "titleEn": "Excavation dewatering and seepage supply",
         "text": "圍堰內基坑降水會增加外側水體的水頭差，抽水需求可能隨開挖深度增加。達西估算提供連續介質量級，但岩體裂隙、各向異性與河床補注需要專門辨認。",
         "textEn": "Dewatering inside a cofferdam increases head difference from the river, so pumping demand can grow with excavation depth. Darcy estimates provide a continuum scale, while fractures, anisotropy and riverbed recharge require distinct evidence.",
