       "instructionEn": "Recalculate step by step: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume equivalent permeability 2×10⁻⁵ m/s, area 300 m², head difference ten metres and path twenty metres. One-dimensional steady Darcy flow is 0.003 m³/s or three litres per second, excluding concentrated fractures. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.",
