       "objective": "從症狀倒推「基坑降水與滲流供給」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Excavation dewatering and seepage supply” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "抽水流量增加可能來自裂隙被開挖接通或施工水混入，未必是整體k變大。若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Higher pumping can reflect newly exposed fractures or process water rather than increased bulk permeability. Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：若只提高抽排量而不查孔壓與細料，可能掩蓋基底有效應力或侵蝕條件的改變。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: Focusing on discharge without pressures and transported fines can conceal changes in base effective stress or internal-erosion conditions.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「基坑抽水量增加必定代表整片地基的透水係數同步增加。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Increasing excavation pumping always means permeability increased uniformly throughout the foundation.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
       "check": "完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。",
       "checkEn": "Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.",
       "knowledge": [
