      {
       "id": "b240-v15-37",
       "title": "導流切換與關鍵工期：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Diversion transitions and critical duration: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "v15s-usace-coffer",
        "v15s-usbr-construction",
        "b-src-water",
        "v15s-usbr-manuals"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b240-v15-36"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「導流切換與關鍵工期」如何影響大壩施工導流的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Diversion transitions and critical duration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “River diversion during dam construction”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "導流切換把水工能力和施工排程連在一起，某項延誤會讓高暴露階段跨入不同水文季節。關鍵路徑需表示真正的前置關係，並與可回復狀態和監測交接共同審查。 假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。 名義平行的工作可能共享設備或通道，隱藏資源限制會使計算工期過短。若把驗證當成可壓縮空檔，可能在尚未證明新通道能力時就失去原來的導流冗餘。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「導流切換與關鍵工期」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Diversion transitions couple hydraulic capacity with scheduling, and delays can carry vulnerable stages into a different hydrologic season. Critical paths must represent actual dependencies and be reviewed with recoverable states and monitoring handover requirements. Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days. Duration is 26 days; four-day entrance delay increases it to thirty days. Nominally parallel tasks may share equipment or access, so hidden resource constraints shorten calculated duration unrealistically. Treating verification as expendable slack can remove previous diversion redundancy before the new route has demonstrated capacity. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Diversion transitions and critical duration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：教學假設，非地標實測值或操作設定：假設入口工程18 days、隧洞檢查12 days可平行，兩者完成後切換5 days，再驗證3 days，總期max(18,12)+5+3=26 days；入口延誤4 days使總期30 days。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Teaching assumptions, not landmark measurements or operating settings: Assume entrance work eighteen days and tunnel checks twelve days run in parallel, followed by transition five days and verification three days.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「導流切換與關鍵工期」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Diversion transitions and critical duration”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-37-k1",
         "title": "導流切換與關鍵工期",
         "titleEn": "Diversion transitions and critical duration",
         "text": "導流切換把水工能力和施工排程連在一起，某項延誤會讓高暴露階段跨入不同水文季節。關鍵路徑需表示真正的前置關係，並與可回復狀態和監測交接共同審查。",
         "textEn": "Diversion transitions couple hydraulic capacity with scheduling, and delays can carry vulnerable stages into a different hydrologic season. Critical paths must represent actual dependencies and be reviewed with recoverable states and monitoring handover requirements.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-coffer",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b240-v15-37-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：兩項工作只要畫在平行排程列，就一定能完全同時完成而不受共享資源限制。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Tasks drawn in parallel schedule rows can always finish concurrently without shared-resource constraints. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "v15s-usace-coffer",
          "v15s-usbr-construction",
          "b-src-water",
          "v15s-usbr-manuals"
         ]
        }
