       "prerequisiteIds": [],
       "objective": "說明「總水頭與共同基準」如何影響壩體滲流監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Total head and common datum” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seepage monitoring in dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "孔壓計讀到的是量測位置的壓力，必須加上測點高程才能與庫水位比較；換用不同高程基準會製造假的水力坡降。先辨認壓力是否為表壓並扣除大氣補償，再確認管線氣泡與感測器零點，低水頭不必然代表低孔隙壓力。 驗證時應將測點水準成果與同日人工水位管讀值交叉比較，並辨識以下失效情境：壓力基準或高程更新未同步會使整組水頭產生固定偏移。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「總水頭與共同基準」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A piezometer measures pressure at its own elevation; add elevation head before comparing it with reservoir stage. Mixing vertical datums creates a false gradient. Identify gauge versus absolute pressure and atmospheric compensation, then inspect trapped air and zero offsets; low total head does not necessarily mean low local pore pressure. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare surveyed sensor elevations against same-day manual standpipe readings. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Unsynchronized pressure or elevation references produce a persistent offset across the head series. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Total head and common datum” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：z=142 m; gaugePressure=196.2 kPa; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; totalHead=142+196.2/9.81=162 m。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: z=142 m; gaugePressure=196.2 kPa; gammaWater=9.81 kN/m3; totalHead=142+196.2/9.81=162 m.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「孔壓數值可以直接與不同高程的水位相比」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Pressure values can be compared directly with water level at any elevation\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「總水頭與共同基準」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Total head and common datum”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b241-v15-01-k1",
         "title": "總水頭與共同基準",
         "titleEn": "Total head and common datum",
         "text": "孔壓計讀到的是量測位置的壓力，必須加上測點高程才能與庫水位比較；換用不同高程基準會製造假的水力坡降。先辨認壓力是否為表壓並扣除大氣補償，再確認管線氣泡與感測器零點，低水頭不必然代表低孔隙壓力。",
         "textEn": "A piezometer measures pressure at its own elevation; add elevation head before comparing it with reservoir stage. Mixing vertical datums creates a false gradient.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-monitoring",
          "v15s-fema-seepage",
          "v15s-usbr-embankment-history"
