       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Darcy discharge and gradient” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seepage monitoring in dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "穩定飽和滲流的流量同時受導水截面、滲透係數與水力坡降控制。排水量增加可能只是庫水頭提高，不能單憑流量認定內部沖蝕；反之通道面積改變或排水截流也會改變量測。應先建立同水位工況的比較，再檢查非線性及地下邊界。 驗證時應以同時水頭差與集水流量建立分水位區間的散點圖，並辨識以下失效情境：把降雨旁流併入滲流會誇大推估導水能力。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「達西流量與梯度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Steady saturated flow depends jointly on conducting area, hydraulic conductivity and gradient. Higher drainage may merely reflect higher reservoir head and does not by itself prove internal erosion. Changing pathway area or drain interception also changes measured flow; compare like stages before interpreting nonlinearity or subsurface boundaries. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Plot simultaneous head difference and collected discharge in separate reservoir-stage bands. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Including rainfall bypass in seepage exaggerates inferred hydraulic conductance. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Darcy discharge and gradient” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：k=0.00002 m/s; A=500 m2; deltaHead=12 m; L=50 m; Q=k*A*deltaHead/L=0.0024 m3/s。",
