       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “V-notch weir calibration” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seepage monitoring in dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "量水堰藉控制斷面把上游水頭轉成流量，三角堰指數使小水頭誤差被放大。堰尖沉積、未通氣水舌及尾水淹沒都會破壞既有率定；水深必須在適當上游位置量取，不能以貼近堰口的抽降水面代替。 驗證時應以容積計時法抽驗率定曲線並攝錄水舌與尾水高度，並辨識以下失效情境：尾水淹沒時繼續套自由溢流曲線將造成系統流量誤差。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「三角堰率定水深」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A measuring weir converts upstream head into discharge through a controlled section, and the exponent amplifies small head errors. Deposits at the notch, an unventilated nappe or submerged tailwater invalidate calibration. Measure head at the specified upstream station rather than within the local drawdown beside the notch. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Check the rating by timed-volume collection and record nappe ventilation and tailwater. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Applying a free-flow rating during submergence creates systematic discharge error. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “V-notch weir calibration” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
