      {
       "id": "b241-v15-13",
       "title": "集水分區水量平衡：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Zoned drainage water balance: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-monitoring",
        "v15s-fema-seepage",
        "v15s-usbr-embankment-history"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b241-v15-12"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「集水分區水量平衡」如何影響壩體滲流監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Zoned drainage water balance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seepage monitoring in dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "量測槽可同時接收壩體滲水、地表逕流與維護排水，只有辨認來源才能推估穿越壩體的部分。用相同時間窗做分區平衡並檢查儲水變化；若集水坑水位持續上升，出流並不等於入流，短時事件更需保留集水系統的滯留量。 驗證時應獨立量測地表截水溝與維護排放並核對集水坑水位穩定，並辨識以下失效情境：省略集水坑蓄水變化會把抽水週期誤讀為壩體滲流脈動。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「集水分區水量平衡」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "A collection channel may receive embankment seepage, surface runoff and maintenance water. Separate these sources within a common observation window and include storage change. When sump level rises, discharge is not equal to inflow; transient events require the collection system retention term rather than a simple subtraction of unmatched readings. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Meter surface interception and maintenance releases independently and verify steady sump level. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Ignoring sump storage turns pump cycling into an apparent seepage pulse. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Zoned drainage water balance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Steady sump: measured=18 L/s; rainfallRunoff=5 L/s; maintenance=2 L/s; inferredSeepage=18-5-2=11 L/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Steady sump: measured=18 L/s; rainfallRunoff=5 L/s; maintenance=2 L/s; inferredSeepage=18-5-2=11 L/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「所有集水槽流量都是穿越壩體的地下水」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Every collected drainage flow is groundwater passing through the dam\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「集水分區水量平衡」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Zoned drainage water balance”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b241-v15-13-k1",
         "title": "集水分區水量平衡",
