      {
       "id": "b241-v15-21",
       "title": "水溫黏度與流量：機制與系統路徑",
       "titleEn": "Temperature viscosity and discharge: mechanism and system paths",
       "estimatedMinutes": 20,
       "simulationOnly": true,
       "sourceIds": [
        "b-src-water-manuals",
        "v15s-usbr-monitoring",
        "v15s-fema-seepage",
        "v15s-usbr-embankment-history"
       ],
       "prerequisiteIds": [
        "b241-v15-20"
       ],
       "objective": "說明「水溫黏度與流量」如何影響壩體滲流監測的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。",
       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Temperature viscosity and discharge” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seepage monitoring in dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "水的動黏度變化會影響同一孔隙結構的水力傳導，季節流量漂移不全代表材料劣化。以固定密度近似時導水率與動力黏度成反比；若介質不飽和、裂隙開度改變或水化反應發生，單一溫度修正不能恢復可比性。 驗證時應同步量測出水溫度並將同水頭的流量按黏度比正規化，並辨識以下失效情境：未補償水溫就提高警戒線可能掩蓋真正導水通道增長。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水溫黏度與流量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Water viscosity changes hydraulic conductivity even when pore geometry remains unchanged, so seasonal drift need not indicate deterioration. At approximately fixed density, conductivity varies inversely with dynamic viscosity. Temperature normalization cannot restore comparability if saturation, fracture aperture or chemical alteration has also changed; those require separate observations. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Measure outlet temperature simultaneously and normalize like-head discharge by the viscosity ratio. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Raising triggers without temperature correction can conceal genuine pathway growth. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Temperature viscosity and discharge” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
       "observation": "量級提示：原創教學假設：Same head and geometry; Qcold=8 L/s; muCold=1.30 mPa*s; muWarm=1.00 mPa*s; Qwarm=8*1.30/1.00=10.4 L/s。",
       "observationEn": "Order-of-magnitude cue: Original teaching assumptions: Same head and geometry; Qcold=8 L/s; muCold=1.30 mPa*s; muWarm=1.00 mPa*s; Qwarm=8*1.30/1.00=10.4 L/s.",
       "failure": "常見誤解：「季節流量增加就表示孔隙已被沖大」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。",
       "failureEn": "Common misconception: \"Seasonal flow growth proves that soil pores have enlarged\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.",
       "check": "系統圖標明「水溫黏度與流量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。",
       "checkEn": "The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Temperature viscosity and discharge”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.",
       "knowledge": [
        {
         "id": "b241-v15-21-k1",
         "title": "水溫黏度與流量",
         "titleEn": "Temperature viscosity and discharge",
         "text": "水的動黏度變化會影響同一孔隙結構的水力傳導，季節流量漂移不全代表材料劣化。以固定密度近似時導水率與動力黏度成反比；若介質不飽和、裂隙開度改變或水化反應發生，單一溫度修正不能恢復可比性。",
         "textEn": "Water viscosity changes hydraulic conductivity even when pore geometry remains unchanged, so seasonal drift need not indicate deterioration. At approximately fixed density, conductivity varies inversely with dynamic viscosity.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-monitoring",
          "v15s-fema-seepage",
          "v15s-usbr-embankment-history"
         ]
        },
        {
         "id": "b241-v15-21-k2",
         "title": "誤解辨析",
         "titleEn": "Misconception check",
         "text": "誤解：季節流量增加就表示孔隙已被沖大 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。",
         "textEn": "Misconception: Seasonal flow growth proves that soil pores have enlarged Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.",
         "sourceIds": [
          "b-src-water-manuals",
          "v15s-usbr-monitoring",
