       "objectiveEn": "Explain how “Head-normalized hydraulic conductance” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Seepage monitoring in dams”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.",
       "instruction": "將出流除以有效水頭差可得到整體導水指標，適合在幾何與邊界相近的工況比較。此量是流路網路的集中表現，不等於單一材料滲透係數；尾水改變、排水孔啟閉與流路重分配都能改變指標，需配合分區孔壓判讀。 驗證時應比較同季節不同水位的導水指標並核對下游水頭實測，並辨識以下失效情境：誤用固定下游水頭會在尾水升高時製造假導水變化。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「水頭正規化導水」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Dividing outflow by effective head difference gives a bulk conductance indicator for comparable boundaries. It represents a network of pathways, not an individual material conductivity. Tailwater changes, drain operation and pathway redistribution can alter the indicator without changing soil properties, so interpret it alongside zoned pore-pressure measurements. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Compare conductance across stage bands in one season and verify measured downstream head. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: Assuming fixed downstream head creates false conductance change when tailwater rises. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Head-normalized hydraulic conductance” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
