       "objective": "從症狀倒推「水頭正規化導水」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。",
       "objectiveEn": "Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Head-normalized hydraulic conductance” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.",
       "instruction": "誤用固定下游水頭會在尾水升高時製造假導水變化。診斷時應採取以下查核：比較同季節不同水位的導水指標並核對下游水頭實測，確認異常是否同時出現在相關量測；未釐清原因就調整門檻，會使真正的機制變化被資料處理掩蓋。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。",
       "instructionEn": "Assuming fixed downstream head creates false conductance change when tailwater rises. Diagnose it by the following check: Compare conductance across stage bands in one season and verify measured downstream head. Establish whether related measurements corroborate the anomaly; changing thresholds before identifying the cause can conceal a real change in the governing mechanism. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.",
       "observation": "連結機制：這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。",
       "observationEn": "Link to the mechanism: That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid.",
       "failure": "誤判風險：若相信「整體導水指標就是土樣本身的滲透係數」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。",
       "failureEn": "Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Bulk hydraulic conductance equals the conductivity of a soil specimen\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.",
