       "instruction": "資料記錄頻率限制最早能看見事件的時間，通訊延遲則在此之外再增加反應時間。等間隔抽樣的平均等待只適用事件發生時相均勻且訊號持續存在；短脈衝可能完全漏記，因此應以失效發展時間與備援記錄規劃監測。 驗證時應以已知時間的測試訊號量測本地記錄到控制室顯示的延遲，並辨識以下失效情境：共同電源失效會使兩套共用電源的感測器同時失去證據。這有助於確認模型的水流、受力或量測邊界是否仍成立。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「採樣時距與偵測」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。",
       "instructionEn": "Logging frequency limits the earliest observable change, while communication latency adds further delay. The average wait for periodic sampling assumes a uniformly distributed event phase and a persistent signal. Brief pulses may be missed entirely; choose monitoring intervals using failure-development times and independent backup logging rather than a convenient data volume. Test this interpretation with the following evidence: Inject a timestamped test signal and measure latency from local logging to control-room display. In particular, distinguish this failure mechanism: A shared power failure removes evidence from both nominally redundant sensors. That distinction determines whether the model boundary or measurement assumption remains valid. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Sampling interval and detection” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.",
